const MOVIES_BASE = [{"num":1,"t":"My Neighbor Totoro","y":"1988","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Gentle and whimsical, but not emotionally weightless. The girls' mother is ill and hospitalized (nothing graphic, but real worry), and there's a tense sequence where the younger sister goes missing. A mother scolds her son harshly early on. Totoro himself and the \"dust sprites\" might look odd but are quickly shown to be friendly, not scary. A nonsexual bathing scene shows a family in a soaking tub with brief partial nudity (bare shoulders/chests/legs). Strong themes of sibling bonds, courage, and compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-neighbor-totoro","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":2,"t":"Finding Nemo","y":"2003","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"No traditional villain, but real tension: the opening shows Nemo's mother and siblings-to-be killed by a predator (quick, not graphic, but a gut-punch for sensitive kids). Nemo is separated from his father and nearly dies more than once; Marlin faces sharks, jellyfish, and an anglerfish in genuinely scary scenes. Themes of overprotection, letting go, and perseverance run throughout. Fine for many 5-6 year olds, but the shark and jellyfish sequences catch some kids off guard.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/finding-nemo","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":3,"t":"A Bug's Life","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"More intense than its G rating suggests. Grasshoppers led by Hopper menace and threaten the ant colony with real bullying and violence; there's fire, rain, and predatory birds. Not gory, but the sustained threat and aggressive language surprise some parents. Positive messages about teamwork, individuality, and standing up to bullies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-bugs-life","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":4,"t":"Toy Story","y":"1995","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"Tense/scary moments played mostly for humor: toys get knocked around, dismembered-arm slapstick, a squeaky alien toy torn apart by Sid's dog. Sid himself mutilates and reassembles toys into unsettling \"mutant\" hybrids that can frighten younger or sensitive kids, and Scud the dog is genuinely menacing. A dad is shown asleep next to beer cans. Core messages: courage, teamwork, humility, and outgrowing rivalry for friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/toy-story","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Toy Story","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":5,"t":"Paddington","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM recommends this warm live-action/CGI comedy for age 6+. Concerns: some peril (a taxidermist villain wants to stuff Paddington), slapstick, and mild scares; very little language, no sex, minimal substances. Positive themes: kindness, family, welcoming immigrants and outsiders, politeness, and that \"in London everyone is different, so anyone can fit in.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paddington","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":6,"t":"Charlotte's Web","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM praises this adaptation as unusually respectful of E.B. White's classic. The chief concern is the death of a central character (Charlotte), handled with appropriate mourning and recovery, plus references to the farmer's plan to slaughter Wilbur. Templeton the rat models selfishness. No language/sex/substance issues. Positive: friendship, loyalty, the cycle of life, selflessness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/charlottes-web-2006","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Comedy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":7,"t":"Shaun the Sheep Movie","y":"2015","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Tons of barn-animal fun in sweet stop-motion adventure,\" told with no dialogue. Appropriate for older preschoolers mature enough to handle brief mild peril (a cruel animal-control officer with an electrified claw device). Some potty humor (fart, burp, poop jokes) and a gag where a man flirts with two sheep in disguise. Positive: teamwork, friendship, fixing your mistakes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shaun-the-sheep-movie","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Aardman","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":8,"t":"The Good Dinosaur","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Young dino braves nature in lovely but intense adventure.\" CSM's 8+ is well above the list's 6+: it flags many scenes of peril, trauma, and loss — including the death of Arlo's father, flash floods, and animal attacks — plus a hallucination sequence after characters eat rotten fruit. Likely to frighten younger/sensitive viewers. Positive: courage, family, loyalty, facing fears.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-good-dinosaur","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":9,"t":"Ponyo","y":"2008","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Miyazaki's stunning adventure is geared to younger kids\" — one of his most kid-friendly films. Concerns: fantasy peril during tsunami/flood sequences and moments when Sosuke fears Ponyo is lost; a slightly scary wizard father. Minimal language, no sex or substances. Positive: strong female characters, loyalty, love, environmental balance, a 5-year-old modeling responsibility.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ponyo","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":10,"t":"Inside Out","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Creative, clever story about big feelings has peril, scares.\" CSM notes some peril and scary moments (e.g., a frightening subconscious sequence, the loss of an imaginary friend) and heavy themes about sadness/depression that can overwhelm younger kids. A passing mention of a mom's former boyfriend. Positive: all emotions matter; empathy, family, and honest feelings.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/inside-out","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":11,"t":"Encanto","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Vibrant visuals, catchy songs, moving messages.\" Concerns are mild: some thematic elements and peril (the off-screen murder of a man in front of his wife in backstory, frightening visions, a crumbling house), plus a kid drinking coffee and a family toast. No real language or sex. Positive: family, self-acceptance, generational healing, Colombian culture.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/encanto","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":12,"t":"Luca","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Sweet fish-out-of-water story about friendship, adventure.\" Concerns: near-attacks on sea monsters with harpoons, some peril, rude humor, and mild name-calling; some parents flag disobedience themes. No sex; minimal substances. Positive: courage, curiosity, empathy, perseverance, teamwork, and friendship on the Italian Riviera.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/luca","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":13,"t":"Zootopia","y":"2016","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Charming buddy-animal story promotes teamwork, perseverance.\" CSM's 8+ reflects several scenes of danger and tension, predators who \"go savage\" (including a frightening black jaguar), and mature commentary on prejudice, policing, and sexism. Also flags a fatphobic portrayal of one officer. Minimal language/sex/substances. Positive: teamwork, tolerance, perseverance, questioning stereotypes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zootopia","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":14,"t":"How to Train Your Dragon","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Thrilling adventure sends brains-over-brawn message.\" Concerns: scary-looking dragons, destruction, and battle sequences; characters drink from mugs in a bar-style setting; a crush/date subplot. Limb differences in central characters are handled sensitively. Positive: compassion, integrity, perseverance, and that strategy and empathy beat brute force.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-to-train-your-dragon","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":15,"t":"Over the Moon","y":"2020","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Dreamy, China-set musical fairy tale has positive lessons.\" The fantasy violence is only mildly scary; the heavier material is a dying mother and a \"Chamber of Exquisite Sadness,\" which resolve into growth. Some flirting/romance between the father and his new partner. No language/substances. Positive: processing grief, girls in STEM, family, that loving new people doesn't erase old love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/over-the-moon","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":16,"t":"March of the Penguins","y":"2005","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Stunning, loving documentary; some intense peril.\" CSM flags occasionally disturbing imagery of penguins walking, mating, and dying, including chicks and eggs lost to cold and predators. No language/sex/substances. Positive: perseverance, devoted parenting, teamwork, and reverence for nature.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/march-of-the-penguins","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":17,"t":"March of the Penguins 2: The Next Step","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Another beautiful, fascinating penguin docu; some peril,\" narrated by Morgan Freeman. Concerns: birds of prey attack and try to kill young Emperor penguins; discussion of climate change and possible penguin extinction, handled without heavy-handedness. Positive: cooperative parenting, perseverance, reverence for nature, the cycle of life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/march-of-the-penguins-2-the-next-step","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":18,"t":"The LEGO Movie","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Hilarious toy tale plugs product but is nonstop fun.\" Concerns: nonstop cartoonish action (chases, explosions aimed at plastic minifigures), a crush/love-triangle subplot with mild jealousy, and — most notably — heavy consumerism, since the film doubles as a LEGO commercial. Minimal language/substances. Positive: teamwork, creativity, individuality, that anyone can be \"special.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lego-movie","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":19,"t":"Mary Poppins","y":"1964","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM says this classic musical is \"a fine movie for children of any age,\" listing it 6+ mostly for full plot comprehension. Only a handful of chaotic moments may briefly scare younger kids; death is mentioned; the father drinks sherry and mentions a pipe, and minor characters smoke. A married couple kisses. Positive: a strong, independent, caring nanny; family, imagination, compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mary-poppins","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":139,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":20,"t":"Mary Poppins Returns","y":"2018","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Blunt is a delight in sweet, nostalgic, toe-tapping sequel.\" Concerns: a few suspenseful scenes and the significant thematic weight that Michael's wife has died a year earlier (the children sing about missing her). Off-screen tie-in merchandise. No real language/sex/substances. Positive: hope, family, grief and healing, finding joy; educational nods to the Great Depression.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mary-poppins-returns","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":131,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":21,"t":"Penguins","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Funny narration makes Arctic docu particularly kid-friendly,\" narrated by Ed Helms. Concerns: predator peril (leopard seals, killer whales, skua birds threaten an Adélie penguin), but softened by comedic narration. No language/sex/substances. Positive: teamwork, perseverance, devoted parenting, nature appreciation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/penguins","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":22,"t":"Up","y":"2009","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Pixar's stunning adventure is an upper for everyone.\" CSM's PG-level concerns: a band of trained talking dogs menacing the heroes, near-falls from a floating house, and some gunfire; violence stays mild. Most notable is the deeply moving opening montage depicting a wife's death and the couple's inability to have children. Two adults sip champagne. Positive: love, loyalty, adventure at any age, found family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/up","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":23,"t":"Vivo","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Touching Lin-Manuel Miranda animated musical. Concerns: some peril and scary scenes with a hungry giant snake and dogs chasing a small animal, plus a non-graphic death (a limp hand indicating a character has died). No language/sex/substances. Positive: family, love, following through on promises; strong Cuban/Latino representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/vivo","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":24,"t":"Smallfoot","y":"2018","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Animated musical about yetis. Concerns: lots of slapstick falls from heights (all survived), dart guns with sedatives, a plane crash, and a fear-driven flashback with weapons; mild flirting; a minor character drinks at a bar; infrequent \"crap\"/\"stupid.\" Positive: questioning authority, seeking truth, honesty, and understanding those who are different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/smallfoot","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":25,"t":"Terra Willy","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"French animated space-survival adventure (also called Astro Kid). Concerns: mild peril, a child emotionally separated from his parents, a few slightly scary aliens, and brief potty humor. No sex, language, or substances. Positive: curiosity, learning, emotional resilience, empathy, teamwork, and problem-solving.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/terra-willy","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":26,"t":"Migration","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Funny animated adventure is just ducky; some peril, threats.\" Concerns: action/peril, a menacing chef who threatens the ducks, and mild rude humor; brief flirting. Little other iffy content. Positive: family togetherness, courage, and opening yourself to new experiences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/migration","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":27,"t":"Muppets Most Wanted","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Amusing Muppets sequel ups the gags, as well as the action.\" Concerns: comic action with some guns, a Siberian gulag storyline, and a villain (Constantine) that some younger kids find intense; mild language (\"hell\"/\"suck\"). Positive: teamwork, friendship, being yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/muppets-most-wanted","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":28,"t":"Singin' in the Rain","y":"1952","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM recommends this classic MGM musical comedy for about age 6+. Concerns are very mild: some slapstick, mild romantic flirting and kissing, and social drinking/smoking typical of its era. No real violence or crude content. Positive: perseverance, friendship, integrity (exposing a fraud), and joyful artistry.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/singin-in-the-rain","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":29,"t":"The Sound of Music","y":"1965","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM recommends this beloved musical for about age 6+. Concerns: the looming Nazi threat and the family's tense escape from Austria, plus some romantic content (kissing, an older teen romance) and social drinking. Positive: courage, family, standing up to tyranny, love, and music as resilience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sound-of-music","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":174,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":30,"t":"The Wizard of Oz","y":"1939","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"One of the best family films ever made; has scary moments.\" It flags several scenes of peril, almost all involving the green-skinned Wicked Witch of the West and her band of creepy flying monkeys, plus a tornado and threatening imagery. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: courage, friendship, resourcefulness, and \"there's no place like home.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wizard-of-oz","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":31,"t":"Paddington in Peru","y":"2025","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"The third Paddington film. Concerns: adventure action and some intense scenes that may disturb younger viewers, mild rude humor, a spider, and peril; a box of martini glasses/alcohol appears as \"emergency supplies,\" plus a suggestive one-liner. Positive: family, faith in yourself and loved ones, finding where you belong, kindness, courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paddington-in-peru","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":32,"t":"The Boy, the Mole, the Fox and the Horse","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM recommends this gentle Oscar-winning animated short for age 7+. Concerns: mild tension — the fox threatens to kill the mole, a character nearly drowns, and there's a winter storm. No language/sex/substances. Positive: kindness, self-worth, love, and friendship; the idea that \"home\" isn't a place.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-boy-the-mole-the-fox-and-the-horse","genre":["Animation","Drama","Fantasy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":34,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":33,"t":"The Secret of Kells","y":"2009","la":"8+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Magical animated adventure is intense but beautiful.\" CSM's 10+ is well above the list's 8+: Viking/barbarian invaders terrorize and kill villagers with swords and axes, villages burn, red-eyed wolves snarl, and an evil pagan serpent god (Crom Cruach) appears. Positive: light overcomes darkness, the value of art and knowledge, and standing up for beliefs; rich Irish folklore.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-secret-of-kells","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":34,"t":"Wreck-It Ralph","y":"2012","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Game-themed movie mixes potty humor with strong messages.\" Concerns: a first-person-shooter game comes to life with alien bugs, some peril, a character pours a martini, a wedding kiss, and potty humor. Positive: perseverance, integrity, self-acceptance, teamwork, and \"there's no wrong side to be on.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wreck-it-ralph","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":35,"t":"Onward","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Original, heartfelt sibling adventure about love and loss.\" Concerns: fantasy action/peril, a few mild scares (a Manticore, a monster), goofy/rude humor, and the heavy theme of grieving a dead father. Minimal language. Positive: brotherhood, teamwork, perseverance, and resilience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/onward","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":36,"t":"E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial","y":"1982","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM recommends Spielberg's classic for about age 7+, though its parents' guide notes the film \"features surprisingly strong language and scenes that may not be suitable for young viewers,\" leading some families to hold it until closer to 10. Concerns: intense scenes (E.T. appears near death, menacing government agents in hazmat suits), the emotional weight of a broken family and near-loss, and notable mild profanity for its era. Positive: friendship, empathy, childhood wonder, and loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/et-the-extra-terrestrial","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":37,"t":"A Greyhound of a Girl","y":"2024","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM recommends this \"sweet animated adaptation about losing a grandparent\" for age 7+. The central theme is death and grief — a grandmother approaching the end of her life. Mild Irish slang (\"eejit\") and \"Jesus\" as an exclamation. No sex/substances. Positive: adapting to loss, multi-generational family love, and that love endures.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-greyhound-of-a-girl","genre":["Animation","Drama","Fantasy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":38,"t":"My Father's Dragon","y":"2022","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Runaway finds courage in colorful cartoon fantasy adventure.\" Concerns: Elmer runs away distressed after his mother yells at him, some \"shut up\" and threats, and mild peril. No sex/substances. Positive: that a friend can see you through scary times; courage, resourcefulness, and friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-fathers-dragon","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":39,"t":"Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone","y":"2001","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM recommends the first Harry Potter for about age 7+. Concerns: fantasy peril and scary moments (a mountain troll, a three-headed dog, Voldemort emerging from the back of a head, a tense final confrontation) and the backstory of Harry's murdered parents. Minimal language/sex/substances. Positive: friendship, courage, loyalty, and standing up for what's right.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-sorcerers-stone","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":152,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":40,"t":"Felix and the Hidden Treasure","y":"2021","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"Canadian animated seafaring/sci-fi adventure. Concerns: mild cartoon violence, a mysterious cult subplot, a couple kissing, and the emotional weight of a father missing at sea. Positive: strong role models, determination, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/felix-and-the-hidden-treasure","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Felix and the Treasure of Morgäa","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":41,"t":"Mighty Joe Young","y":"1998","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this adventure about a giant gorilla for about age 8+. Concerns: action violence and peril (poachers with guns, a mother killed protecting her baby gorilla in the opening, a fire-filled climax) that can frighten younger kids. Mild language. Positive: conservation, courage, loyalty, protecting the vulnerable.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mighty-joe-young-1998","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":42,"t":"Peter Pan (Broadway Musical)","y":"2000","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This filmed 2000 stage production (the Cathy Rigby Broadway musical) has a full Common Sense Media review. Concerns: staged battles among pirates, Native Americans, and children; Peter being wounded; Captain Hook's self-sacrificial leap to the crocodile; and dated Native American stereotyping plus Wendy's gendered caregiving role, both worth a parent's conversation. Positive: imagination, bravery, friendship, and the bittersweet theme of growing up.","srcUrl":"https://broadwaymusicalhome.com/shows/peterpan.htm","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":43,"t":"Strike","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"British stop-motion about a mole who dreams of playing soccer but is destined to be a coal miner. Concerns: potty humor (burps/farts), slapstick, a cartoonishly evil villain, and a tragic mine-accident thread. Positive: pursuing your dreams, community, and brave, smart kids in non-traditional roles.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/strike","genre":["Animation","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":44,"t":"The Princess Diaries","y":"2001","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this Disney comedy for about age 8+. Concerns: mild teen romance and kissing, some mean-girl bullying and social-status pressure, and light rude humor. Minimal substances. Positive: self-confidence, being true to yourself, responsibility, and inner beauty over appearances.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-princess-diaries","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":45,"t":"Yes Day","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this family comedy for about age 8+. Concerns: chaotic slapstick and some risky stunts (a theme-park ride, a car wash with windows down, a messy food fight), mild language, and a scene at a music festival. Positive: family bonding, trust, empathy between parents and kids, and balancing rules with fun.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/yes-day","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":46,"t":"Ron's Gone Wrong","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Animated comedy about a boy and his malfunctioning robot. Concerns: bullying, social-media/tech themes, some peril and crude humor (\"poop\"), a reference to vodka, and adults with sparkling wine. Positive: real vs. online friendship, being yourself, and healthy technology use.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rons-gone-wrong","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":47,"t":"The Bad Guys","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Book-based animated heist is so fun, it's criminal.\" Concerns: cartoon violence (characters hit by a car, explosions, self-defense fighting) and momentary peril; cocktail/champagne glasses at a gala. Positive: the harm of stereotypes, redemption, teamwork, and choosing to do good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-bad-guys","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":48,"t":"Raya and the Last Dragon","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Fantasy adventure has girl power, action, emotion.\" CSM's 8+ reflects scary sequences and intense fights against relentless plague-like Druun monsters that turn people to stone, plus a major theme of grief and broken trust. Some name-calling. Positive: trust, teamwork, courage, perseverance, and Southeast Asian representation (with the caveat that cultures are blended non-specifically).","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/raya-and-the-last-dragon","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":49,"t":"Soul","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Amazing animation, serious themes in thoughtful dramedy.\" Concerns: a man nearly dies (his body appears dead/dying), heavy existential themes about death, the afterlife, and life's meaning; some mild language and a kiss. Positive: purpose, living in the moment, mentorship; Pixar's first Black lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/soul","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":50,"t":"Abominable","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Funny, heartwarming adventure has some peril, scares.\" Concerns: a yeti and three kids pursued by armed adults in vehicles, some peril/scares, grief over a father's death, and mild rude humor. Positive: teamwork, compassion, friendship, and healing from grief; Chinese setting and characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/abominable","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":51,"t":"Wish Dragon","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"China-set animated comedy has great messages, some scares.\" Concerns: lots of animated fights and falls from great heights, characters who die and are revived, kung-fu chases; adults drink wine/champagne, a woman flirts and kisses; mild insults and a toilet gag. Positive: friendship earned, humility, compassion, and that wealth and fame don't bring happiness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wish-dragon","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":52,"t":"Spies in Disguise","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Animated spy buddy comedy. Concerns: action violence (fighting, weapons, some injuries and at least two deaths, a reference to an officer killed in the line of duty), a brief partial-nudity gag, and mild language. Positive: teamwork, accepting help, and promoting non-lethal, non-violent ways to stop criminals.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spies-in-disguise","genre":["Animation","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Blue Sky Studios","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":53,"t":"The Mitchells vs. the Machines","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Animated robot-apocalypse comedy. Concerns: lots of cartoonish action (robots crushed/impaled, oil as \"blood\"), a groin-kick gag, a brief obscured-nudity joke, and mild language. Positive: family unity, understanding differences, and appreciating others' perspectives; features positive LGBTQ+ representation (a lesbian teen protagonist).","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-mitchells-vs-the-machines","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Mitchells vs. the Machines","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":54,"t":"Wolfwalkers","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Lush, lyrical Irish folktale has dark moments, peril.\" Concerns: sequences of violence and scary images — wolves bite and scratch people, characters are shot with crossbows (some mild blood), a character falls to their death, and villagers threaten wolves with cannons and swords; brief \"bloody hell\" and religious exclamations. Positive: empathy, courage, tolerance, environmentalism, and standing up to authority.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wolfwalkers","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":55,"t":"The Sea Beast","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Swashbuckling adventure has kid role model, monster attacks.\" Concerns: animated action violence, scary giant sea-monster attacks that destroy ships, and some peril; monster hunters share flasks of alcohol; mild insults. Positive: questioning official history and propaganda, that there's more than meets the eye, courage; a Black girl lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sea-beast","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":56,"t":"The One and Only Ivan","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Big-hearted adaptation should please fans of the book.\" Concerns: mild thematic elements — circus animals in captivity, the death of an elephant, and some sadness (softened from the book). A car-brand product placement. Positive: loyal friendship, teamwork, empathy, perseverance, redemption, and animal welfare.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-one-and-only-ivan","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":57,"t":"Flora & Ulysses","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Comedy about a girl and a superhero squirrel. Concerns: action played for humor (a squirrel causes mayhem, an animal-control agent fires tranquilizer darts, a cat attack leaves bloody scratches, a near car crash), divorced/separated parents, adults drinking wine, and sensual romance-novel covers on a wall. Positive: hope in hard times, family, friendship, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flora-ulysses","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":58,"t":"The Biggest Little Farm","y":"2018","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this acclaimed farming documentary for about age 8+. Concerns: real farm life including animal death (predator attacks, animals that don't survive) and some peril that may upset sensitive kids. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: ecological harmony, resilience, perseverance, sustainable agriculture, and following a dream.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-biggest-little-farm","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":59,"t":"The Biggest Little Farm: The Return","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"An Earth Day mini-documentary follow-up. Concerns: real farm life including animal death (e.g., piglets that don't survive) and animals in peril, which may upset sensitive kids. Positive: nature's ecosystems, resilience, perseverance, sustainable farming, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-biggest-little-farm-the-return","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":30,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":60,"t":"Jane","y":"2017","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this documentary about Jane Goodall for about age 8+. Concerns: some real footage of chimpanzee aggression, illness (a polio outbreak among the chimps), and death in the wild; mature discussion of Goodall's marriage and career sacrifices. No language/substance issues. Positive: perseverance, scientific curiosity, conservation, and a groundbreaking female scientist as a role model.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jane","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary","Biography"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":61,"t":"Dream Big: Engineering Our World","y":"2017","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"IMAX STEM documentary narrated by Jeff Bridges. Concerns are essentially none — no violence, language, or sex; a couple of engineers reference difficult pasts. Positive: strong STEM/educational value, engineering as a force for good, and inspiring female-engineer role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dream-big-engineering-our-world","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":42,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":62,"t":"Paper Planes","y":"2014","la":"8+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Thoughtful, inspired look at grief soars.\" CSM's 10+ exceeds the list's 8+: concerns include a boy pushing another down stairs, mild bullying, a mother killed in a car accident (grief), a boy stealing from his dad, a hungover father, and mild language (\"hell,\" \"sucks\"). Positive: perseverance, standing up to bullies, sportsmanship, and processing grief at your own pace.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paper-planes","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Paper Planes (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":63,"t":"The Eagle Huntress","y":"2016","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this inspiring documentary about 13-year-old Aisholpan, the first female eagle hunter in her Mongolian Kazakh family, for age 8+. Concerns: some real hunting sequences (a sheep's throat is slit, foxes are hunted), edited for tension. Positive: girl power, dedication, perseverance, discipline, and a remarkable father-daughter relationship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-eagle-huntress","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":64,"t":"Elemental","y":"2023","la":"8+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Heartfelt, romantic fable about immigrant experience.\" Concerns: mild peril (explosive fire bursts, a climactic flood), discriminatory comments toward fire people (\"go back to Fireland\"), insults, and swearing stand-ins (\"lazy ash\"); more romance than usual for Pixar (a young-adult couple flirt and kiss). Positive: the immigrant experience, acceptance, breaking down prejudice, family, and cross-cultural love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elemental","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Romance"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":65,"t":"We Can Be Heroes","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Robert Rodriguez superhero-kids adventure. Concerns: mild fantasy/action violence (kids and adults fighting aliens/monsters), an alien-invasion premise with captured parents that may scare young kids, one brief cleavage shot, and mild language. No substances/sex. Positive: teamwork, child empowerment, and discovering your strengths.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/we-can-be-heroes","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":66,"t":"A Beautiful Planet","y":"2016","la":"8+","ca":"6+","full":"IMAX documentary of Earth filmed from the International Space Station, narrated by Jennifer Lawrence. Concerns are minimal — no violence, language, or sex; the film discusses climate change and human environmental impact, which is thematically mature but not frightening. Positive: strong educational/STEM value, environmental stewardship, and global perspective.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-beautiful-planet","genre":["Live-Action","Documentary"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":46,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":67,"t":"Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory","y":"1971","la":"8+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM lists this musical classic for about age 6+, though it flags genuinely unsettling moments: the psychedelic, nightmarish boat-tunnel scene, bratty children meeting alarming fates, and a generally dark undertone. Some mild peril and scares. Positive: honesty, humility, and that good character is rewarded over greed.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/willy-wonka-the-chocolate-factory","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":68,"t":"Finding 'Ohana","y":"2021","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Fun Hawaii adventure celebrates culture; peril, language.\" Concerns: treasure-hunt peril (venomous spider bites, caves and skeletons, a near-drowning requiring CPR, \"Night Marchers\" spirits), language (\"stupid,\" \"sucks,\" anatomical/potty references), and tween flirting/a kiss. Positive: family ('ohana), Hawaiian language, culture, and heritage, identity, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/finding-ohana","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":69,"t":"Kubo and the Two Strings","y":"2016","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Stop-motion fantasy set in ancient Japan. Concerns: dark thematic elements including death, scary images (a tentacled sea monster, sinister evil Sisters, the Moon King), and action/peril; a mother's sacrifice and death. Positive: storytelling, family, memory, resilience, and honoring loved ones.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kubo-and-the-two-strings","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Laika","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":70,"t":"The Princess Bride","y":"1987","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Witty, winsome fairy tale has violence, language.\" Recommended for about age 8+. Concerns: swordfighting, a torture machine, R.O.U.S. (rodents of unusual size), some peril and mild scares, and a bit of innuendo; brief kissing and some mild language. Positive: true love, loyalty, friendship, courage, and wit over brawn.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-princess-bride","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":71,"t":"The Sandlot","y":"1993","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Lighthearted tween baseball comedy has language, sexism.\" Recommended for age 9+. Concerns: period-typical strong language and insults, kids chewing tobacco and getting sick, a mild sexual reference/a lifeguard kiss ruse, and a menacing dog. Positive: friendship, belonging, teamwork, and childhood adventure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sandlot","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":72,"t":"Zarafa","y":"2012","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Enchanting African fable with some scares and sadness\" (French, subtitled). Concerns: an orphaned boy, a slavery/slave-trader pursuit, some peril and sadness, and a man disoriented while smoking a long pipe. Positive: that personal freedom is worth fighting for, keeping promises, loyalty, and compassion; historical and cultural value.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zarafa","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":73,"t":"The Colors Within","y":"2025","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Moving coming-of-age story about friendship and music\" (Japanese anime by Naoko Yamada). Concerns: very little iffy content — a teen is briefly knocked down in dodgeball, teens are disciplined for a sleepover, and there's gossip about a girl leaving school. No language/substances. Positive: found family, art and music, honesty, and staying true to yourself; synesthesia representation and Catholic-school prayer themes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-colors-within","genre":["Animation","Drama","Musical"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":74,"t":"Dog Man","y":"2025","la":"9+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Amusing adaptation is true to book's silly humor, slapstick.\" Concerns: cartoon violence (Dog Man is surgically created from an officer and his dog, with brief stitches shown), the catchphrase \"See you later, suckers!,\" and mild potty/rude humor; two adults briefly express romantic feelings. Heavy off-screen merchandising. Positive: kindness and character strengths; a fairly diverse human cast.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dog-man","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":75,"t":"Elio","y":"2025","la":"9+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Moments of peril in heartfelt adventure about lonely boy\" (Pixar). Concerns: sci-fi violence/peril (camp bullying, an alien emperor threatening destruction, a punch, a briefly scary toothy alien, a lava-pool threat, a bloody nose), the heavy theme of an orphaned boy grieving his parents, and mild language (\"stupid,\" \"butt\"); an adult drinks wine. Positive: courage, empathy, and being true to yourself; a diverse boy-of-color lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elio","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":76,"t":"How to Train Your Dragon (live-action)","y":"2025","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM recommends the live-action remake for age 9+. Concerns: sequences of intense fantasy action and peril — dragons breathe fire into crowds, Vikings are thrown and smashed, weapons abound, a major character is injured, and there's a terrifying giant dragon (the Red Death); mild romance/a kiss, a \"breast hat\" joke, and \"bloody.\" Positive: friendship, courage, acceptance, and challenging tradition and prejudice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-to-train-your-dragon-2025","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":77,"t":"Liyana","y":"2017","la":"9+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Inspiring, unique film tells two stories of perseverance.\" CSM's 11+ is well above the list's 9+: this documentary about Swazi (eSwatini) orphans creating a fairy tale incorporates their real experiences of child abuse, alcoholic fathers, HIV, and armed men abducting children at night, plus scary animated elements. Positive: resilience, creativity, perseverance, hope — \"you write your own ending.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/liyana","genre":["Documentary","Animation"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":78,"t":"The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind","y":"2019","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM recommends this true-story drama (set in Malawi) for about age 11+. Concerns: a harrowing famine, desperation and a near-riot over food, some violence, a dog's death, and mature themes of poverty and political corruption; some language. Positive: perseverance, ingenuity, education, family, and using science (a wind turbine) to save a community.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-boy-who-harnessed-the-wind","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Biography"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":79,"t":"If You Build It","y":"2013","la":"10+","ca":"13+","full":"Inspiring documentary in which two designer-educators teach rural North Carolina high-schoolers to design and build a farmers' market. Concerns are very mild — a few scenes of adults drinking beer and some mild bickering; no swearing, smoking, drugs, sex, or violence. Positive: teamwork, perseverance, empowering youth, hands-on education, and community.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/if-you-build-it","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:If You Build It","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":80,"t":"Queen of Katwe","y":"2016","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this Disney true-story drama about a Ugandan chess prodigy for about age 10+. Concerns: mature themes of extreme poverty, illness, a difficult childbirth, some peril and a near-assault, and family hardship. Minimal language. Positive: perseverance, education, self-belief, family, and breaking out of poverty through talent and mentorship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/queen-of-katwe","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Biography"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":82,"t":"Girl Rising","y":"2013","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM recommends this documentary about girls' education in the developing world for about age 11+. Concerns: mature real-world themes including child slavery, forced marriage, sexual abuse, and extreme poverty, presented seriously though not graphically. Positive: girls' empowerment, the transformative power of education, resilience, and global awareness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/girl-rising","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":83,"t":"Chasing Coral","y":"2017","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this Netflix environmental documentary about coral-reef bleaching for about age 10+. Concerns: no violence/language/sex; the mature, potentially distressing theme is the large-scale death of coral reefs due to climate change. Positive: strong STEM/environmental value, scientific perseverance, and urgency about climate action.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chasing-coral","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":84,"t":"He Named Me Malala","y":"2015","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this documentary about Malala Yousafzai for about age 10+. Concerns: the Taliban's shooting of Malala and its aftermath, discussion of terrorism and oppression of girls, and some disturbing news footage. Positive: courage, girls' education and rights, activism, family, and standing up to extremism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/he-named-me-malala","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action","Biography"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":85,"t":"Science Fair","y":"2018","la":"10+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Compelling, entertaining docu about teen science geniuses.\" Concerns: minimal — a brief description of microcephaly with footage of an affected baby may disturb some, and younger kids may not grasp the science. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: STEM inspiration, perseverance, curiosity, thinking big, and a globally diverse group of student competitors.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/science-fair","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":86,"t":"My Octopus Teacher","y":"2020","la":"10+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM recommends this Oscar-winning nature documentary for about age 8+. Concerns: the \"circle of life\" in the kelp forest — a shark attacks and injures the octopus, and the octopus eventually dies (which can sadden viewers); some non-sexual nudity as the diver free-dives. Positive: nature connection, mindfulness, perseverance, empathy for other species, and environmental appreciation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-octopus-teacher","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":87,"t":"Night of the Zoopocalypse","y":"2025","la":"10+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Fun 'starter' horror flick has scary parts, positive themes.\" Concerns: zombie-like glowing-eyed mutant animals, many chases and frightening moments (a zombified grandmother tries to bite and turn her granddaughter, and is punched), and tranquilizer darts; insults (\"stupid,\" \"numbskull\"). Notably, no animals actually die. Positive: teamwork, courage, compassion, found family, and tolerance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/night-of-the-zoopocalypse","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Horror"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":88,"t":"Back to the Future","y":"1985","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM's guide notes this \"1980s time-travel favorite includes scenes in which main character Marty McFly and his friends are in physical jeopardy.\" Concerns: an attempted sexual assault played partly for comedy (Marty's mother's unwitting romantic interest in her own son), some violence including terrorists shooting a character, mild-to-moderate language, and teen drinking/smoking typical of the era. Positive: family, self-confidence, ingenuity, and standing up to bullies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/back-to-the-future","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":89,"t":"School of Rock","y":"2003","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this Jack Black comedy for about age 10+. Concerns: frequent mild language and insults, a con-artist adult lying to kids and their school, rock-and-roll references to partying, and some rude humor. Positive: creativity, self-expression, teamwork, confidence, and mentorship (with the caveat that the hero starts as a liar).","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/school-of-rock","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":90,"t":"The Karate Kid","y":"1984","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"1980s classic has fighting but still fun for older tweens.\" Recommended for age 10+. Concerns: significant bullying and martial-arts violence (a gang of teens repeatedly beats up the hero, a near-strangling), some strong language, and teen romance/drinking. Positive: discipline, mentorship, perseverance, self-defense over aggression, and balance in life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-karate-kid","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":91,"t":"The Kid Who Would Be King","y":"2019","la":"10+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM recommends this Arthurian adventure for about age 9+. Concerns: fantasy action and scary imagery — flaming skeletal knights, a demonic sorceress (Morgana), and some peril; mild language and bullying. Positive: leadership, courage, teamwork, chivalry (\"a knight's code\"), and that ordinary kids can be heroes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-kid-who-would-be-king","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":92,"t":"Holes","y":"2003","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Gritty adaptation of bestselling novel has violence.\" Recommended for age 11+. Violent flashbacks include the lynching of a Black man and men trying to force themselves onto women; other concerns include a harsh juvenile detention camp, cruelty by adults, deadly yellow-spotted lizards, gunfire, racism, and some language. Positive: friendship, loyalty, justice, breaking a family \"curse,\" and standing up to cruelty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/holes","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":117,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":93,"t":"Hidden Figures","y":"2016","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this acclaimed true-story drama for about age 10+. Concerns: pervasive 1960s racism and segregation (slurs and discrimination), some tense workplace and historical moments, and mild language. Positive: perseverance, education, dignity, civil rights, and three Black women mathematicians as powerful STEM role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hidden-figures","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Biography"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":94,"t":"Little Women","y":"2019","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends Greta Gerwig's adaptation for about age 10+. Concerns: the emotional weight of a sister's terminal illness and death, Civil War-era peril, some romance and heartbreak, and social drinking. Minimal language. Positive: sisterhood, female independence and ambition, family, artistic passion, and resilience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/little-women-2019","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":135,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":95,"t":"Mixtape","y":"2021","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Serious themes, language in poignant tween dramedy.\" Concerns: mature themes — a 7th-grader's parents died in a car crash, ongoing grief, middle-school bullying, some fighting, a child not wearing a seatbelt treated casually, and some language. Positive: processing loss, self-discovery, connecting with family history, and friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mixtape","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":96,"t":"Ride Like a Girl","y":"2020","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Woman gallops through boundaries in inspiring sports drama\" (a Michelle Payne biopic). Concerns: a parent has died off-screen and another character dies during the film; sexism and one instance of sexual harassment (advancement offered for sex); and disordered-eating imagery (an orange for dinner, plastic-wrap sweating to make weight). Positive: courage, perseverance, and breaking gender barriers; a respectful portrayal of a character with Down syndrome.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ride-like-a-girl","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":97,"t":"Rainbow (Dhanak)","y":"2016","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Sweet Hindi road-trip fable in which a 10-year-old girl takes her blind younger brother across Rajasthan seeking a movie star to fund his eye surgery. Concerns: the threat of physical violence, a kidnapping, tense moments, smoking, alcohol, and parental death (the children are orphans). Positive: sibling love, faith, determination, kindness, and cross-cultural understanding.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rainbow-dhanak","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":98,"t":"Wonder","y":"2017","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this adaptation about a boy with facial differences for about age 10+. Concerns: significant bullying and cruelty, emotional distress, a pet dog's death, and some mild language. Positive: kindness (\"choose kind\"), empathy, inclusion, family, and seeing past appearances — one of the strongest pro-social messages on the list.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Lionsgate","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":99,"t":"The Personal History of David Copperfield","y":"2020","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM recommends this Dickens adaptation for about age 10+. Concerns: an abusive stepfather, child labor and poverty, some peril and period cruelty, a character's death, and social drinking. Minimal strong language. Positive: resilience, self-invention, kindness, found family, and the redemptive power of storytelling; a notably diverse, colorblind-cast production.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-personal-history-of-david-copperfield","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":119,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":100,"t":"The Water Man","y":"2021","la":"10+","ca":"9+","full":"David Oyelowo's directorial debut. Concerns: thematic content, scary images, and peril — a seriously ill mother (leukemia), a boy finding his mom's prescription morphine, two kids in danger in the woods, and an intense climax; touches on death and grief. Positive: honesty, courage, compassion, and strong parent-child bonds.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-water-man","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"}];
const MOVIES_RT = [{"num":101,"t":"Beauty and the Beast","y":"1991","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"CSM rates the animated original 5+ (and notes it may suit some 4-year-olds). The Beast has frightening angry outbursts—yelling and smashing furniture—and a pack of fierce wolves attacks Belle and Maurice; the climactic castle battle and Gaston's fall can scare younger kids. Language is limited to insults (\"idiot,\" \"fool,\" \"crazy,\" \"hag\"), there's a raucous tavern scene with beer, and Lumiere comically flirts with a maid. Strong messages dominate: look past appearances, don't fear the unknown, brains over brawn, and be true to yourself. Belle is an intelligent, independent role model who values kindness and individuality over popularity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/beauty-and-the-beast","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":102,"t":"Chicken Run","y":"2000","la":"1-5","ca":"7+","full":"Despite its G rating, CSM reviewer Nell Minow rates Chicken Run 7+ and warns it \"may be too scary or hard to follow for younger or sensitive kids\"—well above RT's toddler bracket. A hen is killed off-screen with an axe, the chickens face execution and a terrifying pie-machine sequence, and the birds are in peril throughout. Language is very mild (\"flippin'\"), and Rocky briefly acts drunk. There's no sex and only slapstick stop-motion violence. Themes of teamwork, perseverance, and courage are strong—but the sustained life-or-death stakes catch sensitive preschoolers off guard, so parents should preview.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chicken-run","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Aardman","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":103,"t":"Frozen","y":"2013","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"CSM rates Frozen 5+ (and notes it may suit kids as young as 2, depending on the child). As in many Disney films the parents die (at sea), and there are a few violent moments involving men who attack Elsa, plus a scary wolf chase and an icy peril climax. Romance is gentle (Anna's crush, a kiss), with no real language or substance concerns. The heart of the film is sisterly love, self-acceptance, and the idea that an act of true love need not be romantic; courage, self-control, and compassion run throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/frozen-0","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":104,"t":"Kiki's Delivery Service","y":"1989","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"This gentle Miyazaki/Studio Ghibli coming-of-age tale is one of his least frightening; CSM rates it 5+ and calls it ideal for the whole family. There's no villain and virtually no violence—just a mildly tense storm and a climactic dirigible rescue, plus an aggressive crow that may startle. A boy, Tombo, flirts with and pursues Kiki; there's no language or substance content. Kiki is a wonderfully selfless, generous role model, and the film celebrates independence, perseverance, empathy, and the normal self-doubt that comes with growing up.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kikis-delivery-service","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":105,"t":"A Little Princess","y":"1995","la":"1-5","ca":"7+","full":"CSM rates this acclaimed adaptation of Frances Hodgson Burnett's novel 7+—older than RT's 1-5 bracket—largely for emotional intensity and scary moments, with \"war violence, including images of war with dead men strewn about trenches and explosions.\" Sara believes her father died in WWI, and she's stripped of everything and forced into cruel servitude by headmistress Miss Minchin. Little girls sneak a taste of the headmistress's alcohol; otherwise content is clean. Sara is an exceptionally kind, imaginative heroine who befriends the marginalized, and the film's themes—compassion, empathy, gratitude, and inner worth regardless of circumstance—are strong. The loss and mistreatment can distress sensitive young children.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-little-princess","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":106,"t":"The Muppet Movie","y":"1979","la":"1-5","ca":"6+","full":"CSM rates the first Muppet feature 6+. It's a gentle road-trip romp, but the villain (Doc Hopper) repeatedly threatens Kermit with a gun and even tries to have him \"brainwashed,\" and there's slapstick throughout (Miss Piggy's karate). An early scene is set in a bar; Kermit and Piggy sip drinks, and Rowlf sings about having a couple of beers. Romance is limited to Kermit-and-Piggy smooches. Themes of following your dreams, friendship, perseverance, and teamwork carry the film, and the gunplay is comic rather than graphic.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-muppet-movie","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":107,"t":"The Red Balloon","y":"1956","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"This nearly wordless 34-minute French classic earns CSM's 5+ and is suitable for all ages. A lonely Paris boy befriends a magical balloon; the only distress comes when a gang of bullies chases the pair and finally pops the balloon—a gut-punch before an uplifting, fantastical finale. There's no language, sex, or substances, and no real violence beyond the bullying. CSM notes the film offers wonder and imagination more than an overt moral, and its allegory about beauty, cruelty, and resilience invites discussion. The slow pace and subtitle-free minimalism may or may not hold modern toddlers' attention.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-red-balloon","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":34,"runtimeSourceId":"websearch-snippet-2026-09","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-22"},{"num":108,"t":"Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs","y":"1937","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"Disney's first feature earns CSM 5+ (possibly younger, depending on the child). Its scares are real for little ones: the Wicked Queen is genuinely creepy, especially as the Old Hag; she orders the huntsman to cut out Snow White's heart, and Snow White's flight through the enchanted forest is nightmarish. Violence is bloodless and there's no language or substance content; the Prince's kiss is chaste. CSM flags dated messaging—Snow White is a passive damsel and the film prizes beauty and youth (colorism/ageism)—but positive notes remain: kindness, optimism, and finding family in the dwarfs.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/snow-white-and-the-seven-dwarfs","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q134430","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":109,"t":"WALL-E","y":"2008","la":"1-5","ca":"5+","full":"CSM rates this Pixar gem 5+. The largely dialogue-free love story is gentle, but there's sci-fi action—robot-on-robot laser fire, a rogue autopilot, and some peril—and the bleak, garbage-buried Earth may unsettle sensitive kids. There's no language, sex, or substance content. CSM specifically flags that the film's satire of consumerism leans fatphobic/ableist, using overweight, hoverchair-bound humans as shorthand for laziness. Still, the themes are powerful and positive: environmental stewardship, love, perseverance, and human connection over mindless consumption.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wall-e","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q104905","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":110,"t":"Babe","y":"1995","la":"6-9","ca":"7+","full":"CSM rates this Oscar-winning barnyard fable 7+. It's charming but has genuinely upsetting moments: wild dogs attack the sheep and kill one (shown with a bloody wound), a duck is implied to be slaughtered, and there are frequent references to animals becoming food; the farmer nearly shoots Babe by mistake. Language is minimal and there's no sex; a dog bites a man's hand in a fight. Babe himself is an exemplary role model—kind, humble, and non-discriminatory—and the film champions the idea that \"a kind and steady heart can mend a sorry world,\" along with teamwork and believing in yourself. The themes of separation and slaughter can distress tender kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/babe","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q720724","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":111,"t":"Coco","y":"2017","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates this vibrant Pixar tribute to Día de los Muertos 8+—a touch above RT's 6-9 bracket—largely for emotional and thematic weight. Death is central: there's a murder (a poisoning) revealed in the plot, skeletons losing limbs, a startling spirit-creature (Pepita), and a tearjerker finale about a great-grandmother's fading memory. There's mild romance and some peril, but no language. Coco delivers powerful, positive messages about family, remembrance, perseverance, gratitude, and following your dreams, and features an all-star Latino voice cast. Sad moments hit hardest for kids who've lost a loved one.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/coco","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q5815826","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":112,"t":"Elf","y":"2003","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates this Will Ferrell holiday comedy 8+, mostly for mild language and humor. Expect potty humor and words like \"pissed,\" \"hell,\" and \"damn,\" plus some crude jokes; there's mild slapstick and a comic fight with a department-store \"Santa.\" Romance is light (Buddy and Jovie), with a brief shower duet, and adults are seen drinking. CSM notes the film can complicate Santa belief and has some adoption references. At its core it's warm and family-friendly, celebrating curiosity, kindness, honesty, and finding your family, with an infectiously earnest hero.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elf","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q949879","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":113,"t":"Fantastic Mr. Fox","y":"2009","la":"6-9","ca":"7+","full":"Wes Anderson's dry, stop-motion Roald Dahl adaptation earns CSM 7+, and CSM notes much of its humor and themes fly over kids' heads. Farmers try to kill Mr. Fox with guns, explosives, and digging—he loses his tail to gunfire—and there's a knife-wielding rat and real peril, though the violence is stylized. Adult animals drink cider, wine, and champagne (not to excess); Mr. and Mrs. Fox kiss; and swears are replaced with the word \"cuss.\" Mr. Fox lies and steals but ultimately shares his bounty. Themes of family, identity, cleverness, and community give the offbeat film heart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-mr-fox","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q465275","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":114,"t":"The Goonies","y":"1985","la":"6-9","ca":"10+","full":"CSM reviewer Charles Cassady Jr. rates this Spielberg-produced treasure hunt 10+—notably older than RT's 6-9 bracket—noting \"kids are in constant peril, as they're being hunted by thieves\" and \"death and torture are constantly threatened and implied.\" There are hideous skeletons and booby traps, and the tone is intense. Language is salty for a PG (frequent mild profanity and crude jokes), there's kissing and an off-color gag about a nude statue, and product placement (Pepsi, Baby Ruth, Domino's) appears. Underneath the mayhem are genuine messages about friendship, loyalty, teamwork, and being yourself (\"Goonies never say die\"). Best previewed for sensitive younger kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-goonies","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Goonies","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":115,"t":"Home Alone","y":"1990","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates this John Hughes holiday hit 8+. The famous final act is heavy slapstick—burglars are burned, shocked, and clobbered with heavy objects—which is played for laughs but is genuinely violent; a real threat of home invasion may scare some kids. There's sibling name-calling (\"puke,\" \"little jerk\"), mild language, an adult kiss, and Kevin briefly finds an old Playboy. The film ultimately affirms family, love, and forgiveness, and Kevin models bravery, resourcefulness, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/home-alone","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q105031","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":116,"t":"The Iron Giant","y":"1999","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"Brad Bird's Cold War–era classic earns CSM 8+. There's cartoon action—a giant robot under attack, futuristic weapons, crashing vehicles, a boat lost in a storm—and a paranoid, ruthless government villain who briefly knocks a boy unconscious; a deer is shot and killed, which upsets some young viewers. Some scatological humor and a government agent's smoking appear; no real sex or language concerns. The film carries beautiful messages about friendship, choosing who you want to be (\"You are who you choose to be\"), courage, and the tragedy of gun violence. Young hero Hogarth is resourceful, curious, and compassionate.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-iron-giant","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q867283","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":117,"t":"Little Manhattan","y":"2005","la":"6-9","ca":"10+","full":"CSM rates this sweet \"When Harry Met Sally for tweens\" 10+, above RT's 6-9 bracket. It's a gentle, realistic story of 10-year-old Gabe's first crush; content is very mild, with a few crude moments and some mild language, plus the backdrop of Gabe's parents divorcing. There's innocent romance (hand-holding, a chaste kiss) but nothing explicit and no violence or substances. The film is refreshingly honest about the ache and awkwardness of first love, and it wisely lets the kids stay kids. Themes of resilience, self-awareness, and grand-versus-small gestures of love resonate with preteens.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/little-manhattan","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Romance","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2341849","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":118,"t":"Matilda","y":"1996","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"Danny DeVito's surreal Roald Dahl adaptation earns CSM 8+. It's full of cartoonish but genuinely menacing violence, nearly all from the child-hating principal Miss Trunchbull—kids are locked in the nail-and-glass-lined \"Chokey,\" flung by pigtails, and hurled out windows; Matilda's parents are neglectful and berating. Language is limited (one \"hell\"), adults drink beer, and there's some product placement (dented Budweiser cans, Cheerios). Matilda is a brilliant, brave role model who loves books, stands up for others, and stays positive, and she finds a loving kindred spirit in Miss Honey. The film celebrates intelligence, kindness, and resilience triumphing over cruelty—though the mean adults can scare sensitive kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/matilda","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q280400","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":119,"t":"The Neverending Story","y":"1984","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates this fantasy 8+. It has scary images and one famously traumatic scene—Atreyu's horse Artax sinking to his death in the Swamp of Sadness—plus a snarling wolf-creature (Gmork), the world-devouring \"Nothing,\" bullies who throw a boy in a dumpster, and brief charred remains. Language is very mild (name-calling, one \"wench\"); a pair of sphinx statues have bare breasts; an adult briefly smokes a pipe. The film richly promotes imagination, hope, perseverance, courage, and the love of reading, with brave heroes in Bastian and Atreyu.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-neverending-story","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The NeverEnding Story (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":120,"t":"Paddington 2","y":"2017","la":"6-9","ca":"6+","full":"CSM rates this beloved sequel 6+ and highlights how it inspires compassion. There's some peril—chases, a climactic runaway-train sequence, a sword-fighting villain, and a scene where Paddington nearly drowns—plus a genuinely sad stretch when Paddington, wrongly imprisoned, believes his family has abandoned him. Language is essentially absent (mild insults like \"coward\"), romance is limited to married-couple hugs, and there are no substance concerns. The film's messages are exceptionally warm: kindness, empathy, treating everyone with respect, found family, and community. Paddington's habit of seeing the best in everyone anchors it.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paddington-2","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27590871","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":121,"t":"Spirited Away","y":"2001","la":"6-9","ca":"9+","full":"CSM reviewer Liz Perle rates Miyazaki's masterpiece 9+—older than RT's 6-9 bracket—noting it is \"widely considered an animated masterpiece, but not one that was made for children alone\" and \"can be creepy and frightening at times.\" Chihiro's parents are transformed into pigs, the dragon Haku is shown bloodied, the spirit No-Face and witch Yubaba are menacing, and a character's mouth is zippered shut. There's no language; a giant baby's bare bottom is visible, and a character smokes. The film is a profound coming-of-age story about courage, selflessness, humility, hard work, and faith in oneself, with Chihiro growing from a sulky girl into a brave heroine. Its dreamlike intensity is best for the older end of this bracket.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spirited-away","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q155653","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":122,"t":"Spy Kids","y":"2001","la":"6-9","ca":"7+","full":"Robert Rodriguez's family spy adventure earns CSM 7+. Action is fantasy-style and comedic—fights, chases, crashes, and explosions with \"head-bonking\" slapstick, plus some mutant creatures and fumbling henchmen that could scare little kids, though almost no one is hurt. Language is minimal (a \"shiitake mushroom\" gag substitutes for a swear), there's no sex, and adults are briefly seen with wine. The film strongly celebrates family, teamwork, courage, and perseverance, with resourceful kid heroes and a diverse Latino cast.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spy-kids","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q550581","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":123,"t":"Star Wars: Episode IV – A New Hope","y":"1977","la":"6-9","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates the original Star Wars 8+. Sci-fi violence is frequent: blaster and lightsaber fights, dogfights, minor characters killed, Darth Vader choking victims, the destruction of Alderaan and its billions, Luke's guardians left as burnt skeletons, and Obi-Wan slicing off an alien's arm. Language is light (\"damn,\" \"hell\"), romance is a flirtation and a good-luck kiss, and the cantina features aliens drinking and smoking. The film is a clear good-versus-evil epic promoting courage, sacrifice, teamwork, and hope, with an assertive, intelligent Princess Leia and a hero's-journey arc for Luke.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-iv-a-new-hope","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Action"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":121,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q17738","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":124,"t":"The 400 Blows","y":"1959","la":"10-12","ca":"13+","full":"CSM reviewer Charles Cassady Jr. rates François Truffaut's French New Wave landmark 13+, calling it a \"landmark French drama of restless, troubled boyhood,\" older than RT's placement—though its concerns are thematic rather than graphic. Twelve-year-old Antoine, neglected by distracted parents and harsh teachers, lies, steals, skips school, and is sent to an observation center; he's slapped once but there's little violence. Some subtitled translations include \"s--t\" and \"a--hole\"; a psychologist asks the boy about sex, there's a reference to a near-abortion, and the family smokes heavily while Antoine smokes and drinks underage. There's no tidy moral—Antoine is neither hero nor villain—making it a rich but mature film best suited to thoughtful older tweens/teens and worth watching with an adult.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-400-blows","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":1,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q162331","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":125,"t":"Akeelah and the Bee","y":"2006","la":"10-12","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates this inspiring spelling-bee drama 8+. Content is relatively mild: two girls bully and shove Akeelah, and there are sober references to a father killed by neighborhood gun violence and a coach's daughter who died. Language is stronger than you might expect (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"hell,\" \"damn,\" plus put-downs), a positive character smokes and another drinks whiskey, and there's a Starbucks tie-in. The film delivers uplifting messages about being yourself, community support, self-control, and perseverance, with strong role models in Akeelah, coach Dr. Larabee, and her friend Javier.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/akeelah-and-the-bee","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Lionsgate","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2529557","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":126,"t":"Au Revoir, les Enfants","y":"1987","la":"10-12","ca":"12+","full":"CSM rates Louis Malle's semi-autobiographical WWII drama 12+, at the top of RT's bracket. Set in a Catholic boarding school hiding Jewish boys from the Nazis, its tension is emotional and historical: the Gestapo searches the school, a boy is made to prove he isn't circumcised (off-camera), and the true-story ending—revealed in final text—is heartbreaking. Subtitled schoolboy language includes swears and antisemitic slurs (\"yids\"), there are hints of boys' curiosity about sex, and students sneak cigarettes. The film powerfully conveys war's tragedy, moral courage, and self-sacrifice, with clergy who risk their lives to protect children. Its subtitles and somber subject fit mature tweens.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/au-revoir-les-enfants","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","War"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Au revoir les enfants","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":127,"t":"Hugo","y":"2011","la":"10-12","ca":"8+","full":"CSM rates Martin Scorsese's love letter to early cinema 8+. It has real emotional weight—Hugo's father dies in a fire, leaving him an orphan hiding in a train station—and some peril: a station inspector sics his Doberman on stray children, a boy's hand is crushed in a door, and there's a frightening train-crash dream. Language is limited to insults, and a drunken uncle drinks from a flask. The film beautifully champions resilience, friendship, purpose, and the magic of movies (introducing kids to pioneer filmmaker Georges Méliès). Its themes of loss and orphanhood are its most mature elements.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hugo","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Mystery"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q206576","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":128,"t":"Napoleon Dynamite","y":"2004","la":"10-12","ca":"11+","full":"CSM rates this deadpan cult comedy 11+. Violence is minor and comic—clumsy teen scuffles, a bully's headlock and locker-shove, an off-screen beating of Uncle Rico, and a school bus stopping as a farmer shoots a cow (implied, not shown). Language sticks to insults and substitute swears (\"frickin',\" \"crap,\" \"retarded\") plus a breast-enhancement subplot; romance is very mild and there are no drugs or alcohol. The film celebrates nonconformity and the idea that everyone has value, with dignity found through friendship—though the clueless adults show some prejudice toward Pedro, a Mexican newcomer.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/napoleon-dynamite","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1133772","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":129,"t":"Pee-wee's Big Adventure","y":"1985","la":"10-12","ca":"7+","full":"CSM rates Tim Burton's debut 7+—actually younger than RT's 10-12 placement. It's mostly whimsical, but has cartoonish chases and pratfalls plus some genuinely scary bits: nightmare sequences with menacing clowns, devils, and dinosaurs, a jealous boyfriend waving a gun (no one hurt), and the ghost trucker \"Large Marge,\" who frightens many young kids. Language is very mild (\"crap,\" a \"burn in hell\" in a music video, Pee-wee's \"I know you are, but what am I?\"), romance is a declined flirtation, and there's a brief biker-bar scene. Themes of perseverance and resilience carry the day, though Pee-wee can be bratty before learning to treat friends better.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pee-wees-big-adventure","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Pee-wee's Big Adventure","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":130,"t":"Raiders of the Lost Ark","y":"1981","la":"10-12","ca":"11+","full":"CSM rates Indiana Jones's first adventure 11+. It's action-packed with a high body count: fists, whips, swords, and lots of gunplay (including a point-blank shooting), a man's head hit by a plane propeller, a pit of snakes, giant spiders, and the climactic melting/exploding faces and vengeful ghosts. Language is moderate (one \"s--t,\" plus \"goddamn,\" \"hell,\" \"bastard\"), there's implied sex and flirtation, and Marion wins a heavy-drinking contest. Positive notes include perseverance, courage, teamwork, and standing up to Nazis—but CSM flags dated, troubling portrayals of people of color as barbaric and Marion as a frequent damsel.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/indiana-jones-and-the-raiders-of-the-lost-ark","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q174284","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":131,"t":"Romeo and Juliet","y":"1968","la":"10-12","ca":"14+","full":"CSM reviewer Scott G. Mignola rates Franco Zeffirelli's Shakespeare adaptation 14+, well above RT's bracket, tagging it \"wonderful, but a little too mature for some kids.\" The feuding leads to deadly swordplay—Mercutio and Tybalt are killed—and the famous double suicide of the teenage lovers. There's a tasteful wedding-night scene with a glimpse of a nude male backside and breasts, and passionate kissing; there's no strong language or substance use. As CSM puts it: \"Romeo and Juliet take their own lives, disobey their parents, and Romeo even commits murder. Romantic and heart-breaking? Absolutely! Role model worthy? Definitely not!\" The romanticized suicide is worth discussing with teens, and the film's maturity makes it a stretch for the youngest in this bracket.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/romeo-and-juliet","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Romance"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":4,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":138,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q517265","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":132,"t":"Rudy","y":"1993","la":"10-12","ca":"11+","full":"CSM rates this real-life underdog sports drama 11+. Content is fairly grounded: a fiery steel-plant explosion kills Rudy's best friend, and football scenes show bloody wounds and bruises along with crushing disappointment. Language is heavier than the PG suggests (\"bullsh--t,\" \"ass,\" \"goddamn,\" \"pissed off\"), there's mild girl-chasing and kissing, and Rudy gets drunk enough at a bar to blurt out something that costs him. The film is a stirring celebration of perseverance, hard work, and heart against long odds (dyslexia, small stature, poverty) as Rudy chases his dream of playing for Notre Dame.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rudy","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3107519","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":133,"t":"Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse","y":"2018","la":"10-12","ca":"9+","full":"CSM rates this acclaimed animated Spider-Man 9+. Action is intense and large-scale—destruction, explosions, and close-up fighting, mostly with superpowers but also a gun that injures/kills—and, notably, one Spider-Man (Peter Parker) is killed early and another key character dies later, with references to lost loved ones. Language is mild (\"crap,\" \"hell,\" a cut-off \"What the...\"), romance is limited to flirting and hugs, and there's some product placement (Marvel, Nike, Coca-Cola). The film delivers rich messages about friendship, mentorship, perseverance, teamwork, and \"with great power comes great responsibility,\" anchored by Afro-Latino hero Miles Morales and supportive parents; it's widely praised for diverse representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse","source":"RT","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":117,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":134,"t":"Time Bandits","y":"1981","la":"10-12","ca":"9+","full":"Terry Gilliam's fantasy earns CSM 9+. Its humor is dark and its peril real: lots of cartoonish battle violence, some genuinely frightening imagery, and a famously bleak ending in which young Kevin's parents touch a lump of pure Evil and are blown up, leaving him alone. Language is mild (\"hell,\" \"damn\"), romance is limited to light innuendo, and the bandits frequently drink wine, martinis, and champagne and smoke cigars (never shown drunk). History-loving Kevin is curious and good-hearted, and the film satirizes greed and materialism, though the treasure-hunting bandits are bickering, larcenous mixed role models. The unsettling ending is its biggest caution for younger tweens.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/time-bandits","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Other","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1426318","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":135,"t":"West Side Story","y":"1961","la":"10-12","ca":"11+","full":"CSM rates the classic musical 11+. Despite the songs and dancing, it's violent: a rumble leaves Riff and Bernardo stabbed to death, a gang physically abuses and attempts to sexually assault Anita, and Tony is shot and killed. Language includes \"hell,\" \"s--t,\" and ethnic slurs (\"spic,\" \"Polack\"); there are references to sex work, drinking, drugs, and period smoking. The film tackles racism, immigration, and social injustice, with Maria as an inspirational voice against violence—but CSM flags that nearly all the \"Puerto Rican\" roles are played by non-Hispanic white actors (except Rita Moreno) with stereotyped accents.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/west-side-story","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":150,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q273704","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":136,"t":"The Witches","y":"1990","la":"10-12","ca":"9+","full":"Nicolas Roeg's Roald Dahl adaptation earns CSM 9+ (many kid reviewers say 10+). It's genuinely creepy: the witches reveal clawed hands, bald scalps, and hideous true faces, children are turned into mice, a baby in a carriage is pushed toward a cliff (rescued), and Luke's parents are killed off-screen in a car crash. There's no language, sex, or substance content. The tone is deliberately twisted, which some kids love and others find disturbing, so it best suits the older, braver end of RT's 10-12 bracket. Its simple, positive message is to be brave, and Luke is exceptionally courageous.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-witches","source":"RT","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1616747","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_DCOM = [{"num":137,"t":"The Magic Faraway Tree","y":"2026","la":"N/A","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's parent guide flags mild threat rather than real danger — kids risk getting stuck in fantastical lands, climb a towering ladder into the sky, and endure a scary plane flight in bad weather. Parents kiss on the lips a few times and a character practices kissing on a broom; light branded mentions (a tractor brand, a marmalade candy). The MPAA rates it PG for rude humor, mild action, and brief language, while the BBFC gives it a U (suitable for all ages), with Australia's Children and Media council recommending guidance for kids under 7. Positive themes are strong: appreciating nature, unplugging from technology, creativity, imagination, and reconnecting as a family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-magic-faraway-tree","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Magic Faraway Tree (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":138,"t":"Northern Lights","y":"1997","la":"DCOM","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No dedicated Common Sense Media review exists for this title. Per Wikipedia and Disney Channel Wiki, this is an adult-facing drama starring Diane Keaton as a childless woman who inherits her orphaned 9-year-old nephew after her estranged brother's death; Keaton's character is a heavy smoker, and the tone is more mature drama than kids' adventure. Disney Channel itself doesn't count this as an official DCOM (crediting Under Wraps as the first). Given the adult themes and lack of CSM coverage, preview before showing to young kids.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Lights_(1997_film)","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2279315","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":139,"t":"Under Wraps","y":"1997","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"\"Disney monster adventure has violence, scary scenes.\" CSM flags a bold, intense opening and real scares as three kids reanimate and befriend a 3,000-year-old mummy, plus references to a recent parental divorce and a scared character called a \"wuss.\" No language/sex/substance concerns of note. Positive: compassion, courage, teamwork, and friendship; widely considered the first official DCOM.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/under-wraps-1997","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1607657","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":140,"t":"High School Musical","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"\"Feel-good musical has positive messages for tweens.\" CSM flags flirting and an almost-kiss in the final scene, plus a character who screams in anger when food is spilled on her; its sanitized depiction of high school won't ring true for older teens. No language/substance concerns of note. Positive: be true to yourself, chase your dreams even when it's scary, support friends who want to change, plus themes of acceptance and empathy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/high-school-musical","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q53110","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":141,"t":"High School Musical 2","y":"2007","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Staying true to its predecessor, CSM notes this sequel spends more time on music than romance — only sweet kisses at the very end, plus a boy calling a girl a \"little hottie.\" A character manipulates others before realizing her mistake and making amends. No language/violence/substance concerns. Positive: empathy, humility, and that being true to yourself and considering friends' feelings matters more than personal ambition.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/high-school-musical-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q53113","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":142,"t":"Halloweentown","y":"1998","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"CSM flags a reptilian-faced warlock villain with an angry, bellowing voice, plus unusual creatures that can frighten younger viewers; in the most intense scene, the villain zaps beloved adults in front of the kids. The heroine defies her mother but also shows healthy, growing independence. No language/sex/substance issues. Positive: family bonds across generations, self-acceptance, courage, and the value of being different — a beloved Halloween franchise-starter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/halloweentown","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Halloweentown (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":143,"t":"Halloweentown II: Kalabar's Revenge","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"CSM flags mildly scary scenes — a young warlock villain popping up unexpectedly and taunting the heroes, and the normally kind mom transforming into an angry, frightening witch — plus non-graphic magic-based \"violence\" (a zap that's quickly recovered from). The heroine resists peer pressure from an attractive but untrustworthy villain and works with friends to solve problems creatively. Positive: family teamwork, sticking to your principles, and creative problem-solving.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/halloweentown-ii-kalabars-revenge","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q259357","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":144,"t":"Zenon: Girl of the 21st Century","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"CSM calls this \"suitable for all ages\" but notes it will appeal most to tweens, since younger kids may not follow the futuristic storyline. No violence, language, sex, or substance concerns are flagged — this is one of the cleanest entries in the whole franchise. Positive: Zenon is courageous, confident, and values family, friendship, and teamwork; a strong, independent female lead for its era.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zenon-girl-of-the-21st-century","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q189717","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":145,"t":"Zenon: The Zequel","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"CSM calls this sequel \"a harmless space caper\" with no violence, very little peril, and zero bad language, sex, drugs, or drinking — safe for all ages, though the plot is admittedly thin and corny. Positive: courage, self-confidence, determination, and the value of friendship and sticking together, embodied by a feisty, relatable heroine.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zenon-the-zequel","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2420454","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":146,"t":"Zenon: Z3","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"CSM notes this third installment skews slightly older than the first two: 17-year-old Zenon now navigates a coming-of-age romance subplot (flirting, a gentle kiss) alongside teen environmental activism, with a Moon Goddess threatening to destroy Earth as the only real \"scary\" content. No language or substance concerns. Positive: strong female friendships, environmental awareness, and continued courage and confidence from its now-teenage heroine.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zenon-z3","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2128187","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":147,"t":"Descendants","y":"2015","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"\"Energetic Disney movie's villains make likable role models.\" CSM flags a scary scene where a woman transforms into a menacing dragon, plus teen flirting and a couple of kisses; one character flirts heavily and breathily. The teenage children of Disney villains face pressure from their parents toward trickery, lying, and stealing before choosing their own path. Positive: found family, choosing good over inherited expectations, and second chances.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/descendants","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q17278086","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":148,"t":"Descendants 2","y":"2017","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"CSM notes this sequel is \"decidedly darker than the first,\" with a lengthy sword battle over a kingdom's fate and a character transforming into a dragon amid real suspense; a happy ending isn't guaranteed. The heroine wrestles with serious inner-demon themes and tense emotional moments. Positive: friendship, self-acceptance, and choosing your own identity over a villainous legacy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/descendants-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q26154237","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":149,"t":"Descendants 3","y":"2019","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"In this trilogy finale, CSM flags a villain hitting the heroine and her friends with laser blasts and knocking them down, with one character injured; the film assumes familiarity with the prior two movies. Continues the franchise's themes of found family and choosing good over a villainous upbringing. Positive: loyalty, courage, and self-determination, wrapping up the Auradon story on a hopeful note.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/descendants-3","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q48967619","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":150,"t":"Camp Rock","y":"2008","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"\"Disney turns out a fun, clean, surefire tween hit.\" CSM flags only infrequent mild language (\"jerk,\" \"stupid,\" \"loser,\" \"shut up\"), some flirting between the two leads, and a few pratfalls and shouting matches; no violence, drinking, or drugs. The film is also part of a large marketing campaign. Positive: like High School Musical before it, strong messages about being yourself and pursuing your passions.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/camp-rock","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q217250","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":151,"t":"Camp Rock 2: The Final Jam","y":"2010","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"CSM notes this sequel is \"bound to be another must-see for tweens,\" with the same ultra-clean tone as the original and little more than an occasional well-meaning prank. It's part of a huge marketing campaign with many product tie-ins. Positive: strong messages about loyalty, friendship, individuality, and being happy with who you are.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/camp-rock-2-the-final-jam","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q276279","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":152,"t":"The Cheetah Girls","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"CSM flags that the girls' diva personas and material wants (wardrobe, gadgets, attitude) are likely to be imitated by tween and younger viewers, which can create real-world friction with parents. No violence, language, or substance concerns of note. Positive: self-respect, loyalty to friends and family, accepting responsibility, and anti-prejudice, cultural-acceptance themes woven through the group's music.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-cheetah-girls","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q261704","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":153,"t":"The Cheetah Girls 2","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"CSM notes this sequel is \"more mature and much less hyper than the original,\" with the girls' drama giving way to introspective decision-making; content stays mild (occasional \"Oh, my God,\" a few mild kissing scenes and flirtatious exchanges). Positive: navigating new relationships without hurting existing friendships, and balancing individual dreams with team loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-cheetah-girls-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q587876","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":154,"t":"The Cheetah Girls: One World","y":"2008","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"\"Big tween fun as the Cheetahs take on Bollywood.\" CSM flags very light romance and flirting with one kiss, and a girl who starts a relationship over the phone with someone she's never met in person; jealousy among the group resolves into loyalty. Positive: teamwork, cross-cultural respect (a friendly Bollywood dance-off replaces conflict), and staying loyal to friends under pressure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-cheetah-girls-one-world","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1068911","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":155,"t":"Cadet Kelly","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"CSM praises this military-school comedy for handling a friendly divorce and blended-family adjustment in a warm, comforting way, with a well-liked, free-spirited heroine learning to respect people who first seem very different from her. The heroine is repeatedly called a \"maggot\" by her drill instructor, and there's one suspenseful training scene; the villain is one-dimensional but ultimately learns from her mistakes. Positive: teamwork, creativity, compromise, and adapting to major life changes with empathy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cadet-kelly","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q921922","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":156,"t":"Teen Beach Movie","y":"2013","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"\"Heavily marketed musical is wholesome fun for tweens.\" CSM flags no violence, no scary content, and only innocent romance (crushes, hand-holding) as two modern teens get pulled into a 1960s beach movie. It's part of a large Disney marketing push. Positive: breaking down gender-role stereotypes from the film-within-a-film, staying true to yourself, and valuing real connection over a scripted romance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teen-beach-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2708392","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":157,"t":"You Lucky Dog","y":"1998","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Kirk Cameron plays a dog \"psychiatrist\" who can read a wealthy pooch's mind and gets pulled into a scheme over a $64 million fortune. CSM flags moments of peril and slapstick, with guns handled and fired (bullets and tranquilizers) on several occasions, plus mild insults (\"moron,\" \"numskull\"). The plot revolves around money, with shopping sprees shown, so greed/consumerism is a theme the movie ultimately criticizes. Little to no sex or romance. Generic but harmless family fun.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/you-lucky-dog","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1152617","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":158,"t":"Brink!","y":"1998","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Andy \"Brink\" Brinker joins a sponsored inline-skating team for money, going against his morals and friends. CSM notes only mild verbal and physical exchanges; skaters wear proper protective gear despite falls, and there's mild flirting. Strong positive threads around integrity, resisting \"sell-out\" peer pressure, and a character (Gabriella) who challenges gendered language. A solid, wholesome sports movie.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/brink","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1132450","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":159,"t":"Can of Worms","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A lonely teen broadcasts a plea into space asking aliens to take him away — and some actually show up. CSM calls it \"harmless Disney sci-fi fun\" with witty extraterrestrials; the aliens and a scary zoo-keeper villain are cheesy rather than genuinely frightening, though the TV-PG tone is slightly edgier than earlier G-rated DCOMs. Positive messages about appreciating what you have and self-acceptance. Minimal language, sex, or substances.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/can-of-worms","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1762954","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":160,"t":"The Thirteenth Year","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A star teen swimmer starts growing scales and fins when he turns 13 and discovers his birth mother is a mermaid. CSM calls it a wholesome, far-fetched-but-fun coming-of-age comedy that gently touches on first love and puberty. Very little iffy content. Themes of self-acceptance, family, and embracing what makes you different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-thirteenth-year","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2419762","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":161,"t":"Smart House","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A tech-whiz teen wins an automated \"smart house\" whose AI mother-figure, PAT, becomes possessive and eventually traps the family. CSM notes the AI's turn is mildly scary (PAT shocks a bully, projects ghostly holograms, and holds the family hostage in a tornado-like tantrum). It addresses the emotions kids feel after losing a parent and encourages communication. No real language, sex, or substance concerns.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/smart-house","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q670646","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":162,"t":"Johnny Tsunami","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A Hawaiian surfing teen is uprooted to Vermont, where he takes up snowboarding and gets caught in a prep-school-vs-public-school rivalry. CSM says there's little sex, violence, or language to worry about. Strong positive messages about family, friendship, patience, and forgiveness, with a Native Hawaiian lead. A DCOM classic that's fine for most grade-schoolers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/johnny-tsunami","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q921889","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":163,"t":"Genius","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A 14-year-old prodigy (Trevor Morgan, with a young Emmy Rossum) invents a rebellious alter ego to make friends and impress a girl. CSM highlights positive messages, strong role models, and essentially no iffy content beyond some teasing/insults (\"jerk\"), a sexist use of \"ladies,\" and one gentle kiss. Themes of friendship and being yourself; content skews to tweens.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/genius-0","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2712269","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":164,"t":"P.U.N.K.S.","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Bullied teens (including a young Jessica Alba) steal a super-strength suit from an evil corporation to save a father with a heart condition. CSM notes insults (\"nerd,\" \"dumb\"), a crotch grab, a woman smoking in a bar, and kids sneaking into a bar (no alcohol consumed); adults are bumbling or greedy. Positive notes on ethnic diversity and a smart, brave girl teammate. Message: stand up to bullies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/punks","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1481619","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":165,"t":"Don't Look Under the Bed","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"10+","full":"A logical teen teams with an imaginary friend to defeat a vengeful boogeyman (Steve Valentine) framing her for town pranks. This is famously one of Disney Channel's scariest films and only the second DCOM to earn a TV-PG for scary content; per Wikipedia/Disney Fandom, Disney Channel ceased its annual October rebroadcasts after 2006 \"due to complaints from parents who found the film to be too scary for young children,\" and director Kenneth Johnson told EW \"everybody thought we had hit it until they started getting derogatory mail after it aired.\" CSM flags real scares and a suitably frightening boogeyman \"too scary for some,\" with no gore; the film also notably includes an interracial kiss (leads Erin Chambers and Ty Hodges) that Disney was hesitant to keep but retained. Themes of growing up, faith, and sibling love — best for tweens, not little kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dont-look-under-the-bed","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Horror"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1432475","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":166,"t":"Horse Sense","y":"1999","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A spoiled rich 20-something (Joey Lawrence) is sent to his younger cousin's Montana ranch and learns humility and hard work. CSM calls it heartfelt but predictable, with only mild language (\"butt,\" \"darn\") and no real concerns. Themes of empathy, humility, family, and the value of hard work. Inoffensive fish-out-of-water fare.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/horse-sense","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q739115","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":167,"t":"Up, Up and Away","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The one non-superpowered kid in a family of superheroes has to save the day. CSM says it has heart but lacks style; content is very mild with cheesy effects. Themes of self-acceptance, family teamwork, and racial/gender diversity within the superhero family. Little to no iffy content.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/up-up-and-away","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q82913","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":168,"t":"The Color of Friendship","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"10+","full":"Based on Piper Dellums' autobiographical story \"Simunye,\" an African American congressman's daughter hosts a white South African exchange student during apartheid in 1977. This is one of the most substantive and awarded DCOMs — it won the 2000 Primetime Emmy for Outstanding Children's Program, the Humanitas Prize, a WGA Award (Paris Qualles), and a 2001 NAACP Image Award — and the heaviest in content: CSM flags racially charged language including racist slurs, depictions of apartheid-era racism, and references to activist Steve Biko's death in custody. Powerful positive messages about racial equality, challenging prejudice, and finding common ground; Congressman Ron Dellums is a strong role model. Best for older kids/tweens who can process the themes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-color-of-friendship","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":4,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1762748","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":169,"t":"Alley Cats Strike!","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Retro-styled outcast teens who love bowling are thrust into an inter-school tiebreaker with the popular jock (an early Kaley Cuoco role). CSM praises its strong positive messages: don't judge others, kindness and community over winning, and loyalty over popularity. Some characters read as stereotypes. No meaningful violence, language, sex, or substances.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alley-cats-strike","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Alley Cats Strike","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":170,"t":"Rip Girls","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A 13-year-old (Camilla Belle) visits Hawaii, learns to surf, and must decide whether to sell the plantation she inherited. CSM calls it a good-vibes coming-of-age surf movie with strong role models and only one chaste teen kiss. Kids learn about Hawaiian culture. Themes of courage, following your convictions, and environmental stewardship of the land.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rip-girls","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1551056","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":171,"t":"Miracle in Lane 2","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Frankie Muniz plays Justin Yoder, the real first child with a disability to race in the All-American Soap Box Derby; per CSM, the film is \"inspired by the real life of Justin Yoder, the first disabled child to drive a soapbox in the All-American Soap Box Derby.\" (Yoder, 1986–2024, had spina bifida and hydrocephalus and in 1996 successfully challenged the rules to allow a hand brake, now called the \"Justin Brake\" in his honor.) CSM notes a racing crash and hospitalization, sibling rivalry, and a subplot involving a family's past losses; parents kiss and a character takes medicine. Strong themes challenging perceptions of disability, plus fairness, perseverance, and faith. Emotionally moving for all ages.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/miracle-in-lane-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q580814","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":172,"t":"Stepsister from Planet Weird","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A girl resists her mom's engagement to a man whose daughter turns out to be from another planet. CSM calls it a gentle alien comedy with essentially no iffy content. Themes of blended families, coping with divorce/parent loss, empathy, communication, and self-acceptance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/stepsister-from-planet-weird","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3611778","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":173,"t":"Ready to Run","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A girl who can communicate with horses becomes a jockey. CSM flags racing falls and injuries, a reference to horses being put down, mild words (\"loser,\" \"butt\"), light flirting, and a cigar. Themes of perseverance, hard work, believing in yourself, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ready-to-run","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4003728","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":174,"t":"Quints","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A girl's world is upended when her parents have quintuplets and sign the babies to a manager for money and gifts. CSM notes a brief touch on where babies come from, a fire-breathing scene, and consumerism (parents cashing in on the babies). No violence, strong language, or substances. Themes about parental attention and pressure on kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/quints","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4004186","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":175,"t":"The Other Me","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A lazy student accidentally clones himself before a big science project. CSM highlights integrity and honesty as central themes; content is mild with clownish villains. Wholesome and low-stakes. Message about doing your own work and being yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-other-me","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1171765","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":176,"t":"Mom's Got a Date with a Vampire","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Kids scheme to ruin their single mom's date after realizing her suitor is a vampire. CSM calls it a dated comedy-horror with mild vampire scares and peril but little bite. Themes of family and honesty (the kids scheme, then do the right thing). Mild for the genre.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/moms-got-a-date-with-a-vampire","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q935745","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":177,"t":"Phantom of the Megaplex","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A teen managing a huge movie theater on a big premiere night must cope with a mysterious \"phantom\" and malfunctioning equipment. CSM notes little real violence but a creepy edge and mild scares, plus a brief dating reference. Themes of hard work, friendship, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/phantom-of-the-megaplex","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Mystery","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3793908","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":178,"t":"The Ultimate Christmas Present","y":"2000","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Two LA girls find a weather machine and accidentally bury the city in snow before Christmas. CSM notes minimal iffy content — mild peril and weather-machine hijinks. Themes of friendship, responsibility, and family. Light holiday fun.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-ultimate-christmas-present","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1171651","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":179,"t":"Motocrossed","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A cheerleader secretly races motocross disguised as her injured twin brother (a loose Twelfth Night update). CSM notes sexist language (\"chick\"), teasing, and mild leering/suggestive comments, plus racing spills and a mild teen romance. Strong themes of gender equality, empathy, perseverance, and challenging stereotypes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/motocrossed","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1763851","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":180,"t":"The Luck of the Irish","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A teen (Ryan Merriman) discovers he's part leprechaun and must recover a lucky charm from an evil leprechaun. CSM rates it 3/5, noting good intentions about celebrating heritage undermined by heavy Irish stereotypes; content is otherwise very safe with only mild fantasy battles and alcohol references, and no scary scenes. Themes of cultural identity, family heritage, and self-acceptance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-luck-of-the-irish","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2713787","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":181,"t":"Hounded","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"An overachiever is tormented by a rich rival's small dog. CSM says it makes little sense and flags mild violence — a snarling dog attacks played for laughs that may scare some young kids — plus cheating and poor decisions. Message that cheating doesn't pay.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hounded","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3629136","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":182,"t":"Jett Jackson: The Movie","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A teen TV action star magically swaps places with his spy character. CSM notes mild action and peril, a diverse cast, and many positive role models, including supportive separated parents. Themes of appreciating your own life, family, and identity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jett-jackson-the-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"imdb:tt0272606","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":183,"t":"The Jennie Project","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A family takes in a chimpanzee raised to use sign language. CSM flags some distressing violence against animals. Themes of animal welfare and rights, communication, and respect. Thoughtful for its age group.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-jennie-project","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1763791","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":184,"t":"Jumping Ship","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A sequel to Horse Sense in which cousins are stranded and must survive after pirates attack their yacht. CSM notes comedic moments of peril (pirates, castaway survival). Themes of responsibility, teamwork, and maturity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jumping-ship","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1763592","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":185,"t":"The Poof Point","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Parents' time machine backfires, causing them to age backward toward infancy. CSM flags characters in danger of \"disappearing,\" lab explosions, and parents who flirt/hug/kiss with \"going steady\" mentions. Celebrates science; themes of empathy and communication.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-poof-point","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3926966","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":186,"t":"'Twas the Night","y":"2001","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A boy and his con-artist uncle borrow Santa's sleigh on Christmas Eve. CSM calls it formulaic but unthreatening fun with mild threat and a \"naughty\" uncle. Themes of family, honesty, redemption, and Christmas spirit.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/twas-the-night","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1708277","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":187,"t":"Double Teamed","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"The true story of twin sisters Heidi and Heather Burge, who became pro basketball players. CSM rates it 3/5 and notes sibling rivalry and sabotage, bullying, and parental pressure. Positive themes of teamwork, perseverance, and supporting family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/double-teamed","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q645907","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":188,"t":"Tru Confessions","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A girl dreams of her own TV show while caring about her twin brother (Shia LaBeouf), who has a developmental disability. CSM notes it's emotional and tearjerking with a sensitive, positive portrayal of disability. Themes of family, acceptance, empathy, and self-understanding.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tru-confessions","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2901990","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":189,"t":"Get a Clue","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A posh Manhattan teen (Lindsay Lohan) turns detective when a teacher disappears. CSM notes very mild teen flirting and crushes and a heroine who's occasionally impudent to adults; multicultural friends work together. A clean teen mystery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/get-a-clue","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Mystery","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1467511","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":190,"t":"Gotta Kick It Up!","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A teacher inspires an underdog Latina dance team. CSM flags mild teasing/bullying and derogatory terms (\"dumb,\" \"loser\") but no violence, strong language, or sex. Celebrates cultural diversity, being yourself, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/gotta-kick-it-up","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Gotta Kick It Up!","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":191,"t":"A Ring of Endless Light","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"9+","full":"A teen (Mischa Barton) with a telepathic bond to dolphins copes with her grandfather's terminal illness. CSM notes it deals with death and dying plus a teen romance/love triangle. Strong environmental and dolphin-conservation themes. More mature emotional content.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-ring-of-endless-light","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2355488","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":192,"t":"The Scream Team","y":"2002","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Kids team up with friendly ghosts to help their late grandfather move on. CSM notes death and afterlife themes handled lightly and humorously, with friendly ghosts but one fire-throwing \"evil\" ghost that may scare the very young. Themes of family and not fearing what you don't understand.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-scream-team","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2481055","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":193,"t":"You Wish!","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A boy wishes his annoying little brother out of existence and must set things right. CSM notes simulated war-play with \"goo\" guns, bullies, and teen crushes (a kiss on the cheek). Classic \"be careful what you wish for\" message about appreciating family and friends.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/you-wish","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2358690","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":194,"t":"Right on Track","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The true story of sisters Erica and Courtney Enders breaking into junior drag racing. CSM calls it empowering, tackling sexism in a male-dominated sport. Themes of perseverance, gender equality, and family. Racing action is the main \"peril.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/right-on-track","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1763398","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":195,"t":"The Even Stevens Movie","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The Stevens family is secretly filmed for a prank reality show on a remote island (Shia LaBeouf). CSM notes tween-friendly mild slapstick. Themes of family and good clean fun. Very low content concern.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-even-stevens-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q659953","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":196,"t":"Eddie's Million Dollar Cook-Off","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A star baseball player would rather be a gourmet chef, defying his coach and dad. CSM rates it 4/5 and notes slapstick/food fights plus bullying and prejudice over a boy who cooks. Strong messages about defying gender stereotypes, family, and following your passion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/eddies-million-dollar-cook-off","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3718959","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":197,"t":"Full-Court Miracle","y":"2003","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Inspired by a true story, a Jewish school's basketball team is coached by a former college player during Hanukkah. CSM notes sports content and themes of faith, perseverance, teamwork, and cross-cultural friendship. Family expectations feature prominently.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/full-court-miracle","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q627403","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":198,"t":"Pixel Perfect","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A teen creates a holographic pop-star to help his friend's band, sparking jealousy. CSM notes somewhat muddled messages (controlling behavior brushed over) but mild content overall. Themes of friendship, identity, and jealousy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pixel-perfect","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q731789","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":199,"t":"Going to the Mat","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A blind teen moves to a new school and joins the wrestling team. CSM notes rudeness, snobbery, and bullying before growth. Strong themes of disability, acceptance, and fitting in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/going-to-the-mat","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q945952","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":200,"t":"Stuck in the Suburbs","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Two girls accidentally swap phones with a pop star and see his controlled life. CSM calls it clichéd but very mild, with a positive message critiquing consumerism and image, and staying down-to-earth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/stuck-in-the-suburbs","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2373456","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":201,"t":"Tiger Cruise","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"9+","full":"A teen visiting her father's Navy ship is aboard during the September 11 attacks. CSM notes real Twin Towers footage, a relative missing/presumed dead, and the term \"army brat,\" but no strong language. Themes of courage, empathy, family, and stepping up. Best for older kids/tweens given the 9/11 content.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tiger-cruise","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Tiger Cruise (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":202,"t":"Halloweentown High","y":"2004","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Marnie brings Halloweentown creatures to the human world in this third franchise entry. CSM calls it ho-hum but fine for older kids, with very mild monster/mall chaos. Themes of tolerance and acceptance of differences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/halloweentown-high","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q369986","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":203,"t":"Now You See It…","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A teen TV producer discovers a contestant on a young-magician reality show has real powers. CSM notes mild jump scares and villain peril, with relatable, good-values teens. Themes of teamwork, friendship, and good vs. evil.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/now-you-see-it","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Mystery","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"disneyplus:entity-0b1923f8-bfe4-48f5-9cf4-9cae7a07e3a3","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":204,"t":"Buffalo Dreams","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A boy befriends a Navajo peer and learns to respect Native traditions. CSM flags a buffalo stampede, a dangerous bike race (a stick in the spokes), and vandalism of a sacred site. Themes of Navajo culture, nature/environment, respect, and making amends.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/buffalo-dreams","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3646583","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":205,"t":"Kim Possible Movie: So the Drama","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The animated teen spy faces off with Dr. Drakken while navigating a real crush. CSM notes one kiss, skimpy cheerleading costumes, and cartoonish fights, explosions, and peril (all mild). A strong female role model; themes of friendship, family, loyalty, and determination.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kim-possible-movie-so-the-drama","source":"DCOM","genre":["Animation","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2294224","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":206,"t":"Go Figure","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A figure skater joins a hockey team to earn a skating scholarship. CSM flags name-calling (\"Tonya\"), betting, and some stereotypes (a clichéd Russian character). Themes of perseverance, teamwork, not judging by appearance, and putting others first.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/go-figure","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2005934","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":207,"t":"Life Is Ruff","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A slacker trains a stray dog for a big show to win money. CSM notes derogatory terms (\"doofus,\" \"mutt\") and a manipulative but likable lead. Themes of pet responsibility, selflessness, and empathy; it examines dog-show ethics.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/life-is-ruff","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2629495","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":208,"t":"The Proud Family Movie","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The animated Proud family is targeted by a mad scientist's cloning scheme. CSM flags non-stop parental insults and sarcasm/rudeness from Penny, and notes a concern that the darkest-complexioned characters are portrayed most negatively. Themes of family love, loyalty, and balancing protection with independence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-proud-family-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2042834","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":209,"t":"Twitches","y":"2005","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Separated twin witches (Tia and Tamera Mowry) reunite on their birthday to fight a dark force. CSM notes scary moments that may be much for little kids, sad parent-loss themes, and frequent shopping references (consumerism). Themes of sisterhood, family, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/twitches","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q244511","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":210,"t":"Cow Belles","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Spoiled rich sisters (Aly & AJ Michalka) must work at the family dairy and grow up. CSM notes very mild content and a strong message about being responsible with money, thinking of others, and admitting mistakes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cow-belles","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1753186","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":211,"t":"Wendy Wu: Homecoming Warrior","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A popularity-obsessed teen (Brenda Song) learns she's a reincarnated warrior destined to fight an evil spirit. CSM notes mild kung-fu action and a teen romance, with loving parents. Themes of heritage, Chinese culture, priorities, and self-discovery; a strong Asian American female lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wendy-wu-homecoming-warrior","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q951101","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":212,"t":"Read It and Weep","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A girl's private diary is accidentally published, bringing overnight fame (Kay Panabaker). CSM notes it's very clean with mild popularity/peer-pressure themes. Messages about friendship, self-confidence, and being yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/read-it-and-weep","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1505940","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":213,"t":"Return to Halloweentown","y":"2006","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Marnie heads to Witch University and confronts a plot to seize dark power. CSM notes fantasy violence, spells, and dark-power/possession themes. Messages about not misusing power and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/return-to-halloweentown","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1571871","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":214,"t":"Jump In!","y":"2007","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A young boxer (Corbin Bleu) secretly takes up competitive Double Dutch. CSM notes minor boxing/jump-rope action and one kiss, with a multicultural cast and a devoted widowed dad. Themes of family, self-respect, and the courage to be different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jump-in","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q765579","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":215,"t":"Johnny Kapahala: Back on Board","y":"2007","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The Johnny Tsunami sequel finds a now-17-year-old Johnny mentoring a rebellious 12-year-old (Jake T. Austin) in Hawaii. CSM notes a tween who's rude to adults and his mentor before shaping up, with peer pressure a dominant theme; action-packed mountain-boarding scenes. Themes of respect and following your own instincts.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/johnny-kapahala-back-on-board","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1966378","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":216,"t":"Twitches Too","y":"2007","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"The twin witches search for their missing father and again battle the dark force. CSM notes suspense and brief fantasy violence (fiery spells, a shadowy figure) unlikely to upset most viewers. Themes of family, courage, faith, and sisterhood.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/twitches-too","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q244514","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":217,"t":"Minutemen","y":"2008","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Three outcasts build a time machine to stop classmates' embarrassing moments. CSM rates it 3/5, noting heavy jock/nerd stereotypes that the film ultimately subverts, plus an anti-bullying message. Themes of friendship and everything-happens-for-a-reason.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/minutemen","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1342998","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":218,"t":"Dadnapped","y":"2009","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A girl's famous author dad is \"kidnapped\" by overzealous fans. CSM notes the comedic kidnapping isn't a real threat, with no violence or scares. Themes of communication, family, and self-confidence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dadnapped","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1165290","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":219,"t":"Hatching Pete","y":"2009","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A shy teen secretly becomes the school mascot while his friend takes the credit. CSM notes it's very clean. Themes of self-respect, self-confidence, friendship, honesty, and being yourself; a positive teen romance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hatching-pete","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1313586","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":220,"t":"Princess Protection Program","y":"2009","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A princess (Demi Lovato) hides out with an ordinary teen (Selena Gomez) after a military coup. CSM rates it 4/5, noting a mild takeover premise and no romance subplot. Great messages about integrity, friendship, inner beauty, and self-reliance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/princess-protection-program","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q549859","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":221,"t":"Wizards of Waverly Place: The Movie","y":"2009","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The Russo siblings' magic strands their family on vacation, forcing Alex (Selena Gomez) to fix her mistake. CSM notes mild flirting, a brief married-couple kiss, \"dang it\" as the worst language, and a rebellious Alex who learns her lesson. Themes of family ties and self-confidence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wizards-of-waverly-place-the-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18948","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":222,"t":"Starstruck","y":"2010","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"An ordinary girl unexpectedly falls for a self-absorbed pop star. CSM notes it's squeaky-clean with no sexual content and celebrity-crush/fan themes. A modern Cinderella about being true to your feelings rather than fame.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/starstruck","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q830555","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":223,"t":"Den Brother","y":"2010","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A self-centered hockey player takes over his little sister's scout troop. CSM notes no iffy content and a brief touch on parent death and a dad's heavy workload. Themes of responsibility, integrity, accountability, and sibling love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/den-brother","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2272891","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":224,"t":"Avalon High","y":"2010","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A new student realizes her classmates are reincarnated figures from Arthurian legend. CSM notes mild fantasy and great messages about destiny, the greater good, courage, and selflessness, with an educational tie to the legend.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/avalon-high","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q722888","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":225,"t":"The Suite Life Movie","y":"2011","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Zack and Cody join a twin-bonding science experiment that goes awry. CSM calls it a no-surprises tween movie with some peril and a discussion-worthy subliminal-advertising/product-placement subplot. Themes of the sibling bond.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-suite-life-movie","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q139825","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":226,"t":"Lemonade Mouth","y":"2011","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Five misfits form a band that becomes a voice for student rights. CSM flags bullying/harassment by adults and teens, a pizzeria fight, teens lying to and fighting with parents, some suggestive (non-sexual) dancing, and mild name-calling. Strong themes of friendship, standing up for yourself, honest parent-kid communication, and self-expression.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lemonade-mouth","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q950535","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":227,"t":"Phineas and Ferb the Movie: Across the 2nd Dimension","y":"2011","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The animated stepbrothers travel to an alternate dimension ruled by an evil Doofenshmirtz. CSM flags animated action violence — laser blasts destroying robots, falls, fistfights, electrocution, and monster peril — plus heavy franchise marketing. Themes of loyalty, friendship, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/phineas-and-ferb-across-the-2nd-dimension","source":"DCOM","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1300140","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":228,"t":"Geek Charming","y":"2011","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A popular girl becomes the subject of a nerdy classmate's documentary. CSM notes mean-girl/popularity pressure. Themes of friendship, mutual respect, self-confidence, and rejecting stereotypes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/geek-charming","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q865193","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":229,"t":"Good Luck Charlie, It's Christmas!","y":"2011","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"The Duncan family's holiday road trip goes hilariously wrong. CSM notes true-to-life family bickering and holiday stress but a focus on togetherness over commercialism. Warm humor with happy outcomes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/good-luck-charlie-its-christmas","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1573500","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":230,"t":"Frenemies","y":"2012","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Three interwoven stories explore friendships that flip between friend and enemy. CSM notes oversimplified teen relationships and some stereotypes. Messages about friendship, individuality, and social priorities.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/frenemies","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q830459","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":231,"t":"Radio Rebel","y":"2012","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A shy teen (Debby Ryan) becomes a secretly influential radio DJ. CSM calls it sweet and very mild. Themes of self-expression, overcoming shyness and fear, anti-bullying, and authenticity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/radio-rebel","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Radio Rebel","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":232,"t":"Let It Shine","y":"2012","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A shy, church-raised teen ghostwrites rap lyrics for a friend to win a girl's heart (a hip-hop Cyrano). CSM notes mild name-calling/put-downs and mild rebellion (breaking a dad's rules). Themes of self-confidence, friendship, artistic integrity, and staying true to yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/let-it-shine","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q129822","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":233,"t":"Girl vs. Monster","y":"2012","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A teen (Olivia Holt) discovers she's from a family of monster hunters and must face her fears on Halloween. CSM notes monster hunters, ray guns, and scares that may be too much for the youngest, plus disobeying parents with consequences. Themes of facing fears, friendship, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/girl-vs-monster","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2701590","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":234,"t":"Cloud 9","y":"2014","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Two snowboarders (Dove Cameron, Luke Benward) team up to compete. CSM notes snowboarding crashes and falls, one kiss, and an innocent romance, with no language or substances. Positive role models and messages about believing in yourself, hard work, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cloud-9","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q12108188","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":235,"t":"Zapped","y":"2014","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A girl (Zendaya) gets an app that lets her control boys and dogs. CSM notes mild content but somewhat mixed messaging about manipulation and control. Themes of blended families.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zapped","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16334727","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":236,"t":"How to Build a Better Boy","y":"2014","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Two tech-savvy friends accidentally build a \"perfect\" robot boyfriend (a teen Weird Science). CSM notes very mild content and some social-caste setup. Feel-good messages about self-acceptance, not conforming, and girl-power in STEM.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/how-to-build-a-better-boy","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16251603","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":237,"t":"Bad Hair Day","y":"2015","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A teen's prom day collides with a jewel-heist detective plot. CSM awarded it the Common Sense Seal (age 6), noting a mild caper, chase, and theft. Themes of being yourself, plus discussion hooks about internet safety/cyberbullying and intergenerational friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/bad-hair-day","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18636702","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":238,"t":"Teen Beach 2","y":"2015","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"The characters from the surf-musical cross into the real world. CSM gave it the Common Sense Seal (age 8), noting it's very safe with no violence, scares, or language issues, though heavy on merchandising. Themes of friendship, staying true to yourself, and female empowerment.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teen-beach-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19516295","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":239,"t":"Invisible Sister","y":"2015","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"A science experiment accidentally turns a girl's popular older sister invisible. CSM calls it funny and feel-good with very mild content and excellent messages. Themes of sisterhood, friendship, and stepping out of a sibling's shadow.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/invisible-sister","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18758155","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":240,"t":"Adventures in Babysitting","y":"2016","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"Two rival babysitters (Sabrina Carpenter, Sofia Carson) chase their charges across the city. CSM notes some rough play (slapping, leg-swipes) and occasional appearance comments, but no sex, strong language, or drugs. Themes of teamwork, cooperation, and responsibility.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/adventures-in-babysitting","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q21197880","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":241,"t":"The Swap","y":"2016","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A boy and girl magically swap bodies via text and gain new empathy. CSM rates it 3/5, noting no violence or language and one unreciprocated flirtation; the source book has puberty talk that the movie softens. Positive messages about empathy, family, and appreciating others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-swap","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q26060355","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":242,"t":"Tangled: Before Ever After","y":"2017","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"This bridge to the series finds Rapunzel chafing at royal duties as her magic hair returns. CSM calls it an enjoyable follow-up; Rapunzel kisses Eugene and there's mild fantasy peril. Themes of independence, freedom vs. duty, self-determination, and partnership.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tangled-before-ever-after","source":"DCOM","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":54,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28804247","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":243,"t":"Zombies","y":"2018","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A zombie boy and a cheerleader fall for each other in a segregated town. CSM notes zombie transformations (darkening eyes/veins) and mean exchanges between humans and zombies, serving as a strong metaphor for prejudice. Themes of tolerance, individuality, self-acceptance, and resisting peer pressure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zombies","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q42404224","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":244,"t":"Freaky Friday","y":"2018","la":"DCOM","ca":"6+","full":"A musical remake of the mother-daughter body-swap story. CSM gave it the Common Sense Seal (age 6), noting a clean body-swap musical. Themes of empathy, mother-daughter understanding, and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/freaky-friday-2018","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q54214396","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":245,"t":"Kim Possible","y":"2019","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"The live-action reboot of the teen-spy franchise. CSM notes realistic emotions — jealousy, low confidence, an identity crisis — a mean classmate, brief grief over an apparent loss, and mild cartoonish action. A courageous role-model lead who seeks help from mentors (her mom and grandmother).","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kim-possible","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q54801207","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":246,"t":"Zombies 2","y":"2020","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Werewolves join the mix, testing the town's fragile tolerance. CSM notes prejudice and mistrust among humans, zombies, and werewolves and minimal kissing. Prominent themes of positive body image, identity, friendship, tolerance, and acceptance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zombies-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Zombies 2","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":247,"t":"Upside-Down Magic","y":"2020","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Kids with \"wonky,\" non-standard magic navigate a magical school. CSM notes a brief dark-magic possession/shadow monster (mild, may scare sensitive 6-year-olds), some poop humor, and a mean prank that endangers a kid. Themes of embracing differences and respecting uniqueness, with a biracial lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/upside-down-magic","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q88799614","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":248,"t":"Spin","y":"2021","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"An Indian American teen discovers a passion for DJing while balancing family and culture. Per Entertainment Tonight, Spin was \"the network's first original TV film featuring an Indian American lead,\" premiering Aug. 13, 2021, starring Avantika Vandanapu as Rhea Kumar (directed by Manjari Makijany). CSM rates it 3/5, noting the lead's mother has died (grief), a teen crush with nothing beyond hand-holding, and brief mistrust. It celebrates Indian culture; a warm coming-of-age story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/spin","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q108184943","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":249,"t":"Under Wraps","y":"2021","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"Three kids befriend a reanimated mummy and race to return him before Halloween. CSM rates it 4/5, noting initial spooky scares (the mummy comes to life and chases the kids), peril/chases, and thugs with clubs — nothing violent or gory — with no sex, language, or substances. A diverse cast; themes of friendship and standing up to bullies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/under-wraps","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Under Wraps (2021 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":250,"t":"Christmas…Again?!","y":"2021","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"A girl relives Christmas in a Groundhog Day–style loop until she learns to appreciate her family. CSM notes a bully who pushes kids (a repeating plot beat), mild profanity (\"jerk,\" \"butt,\" \"heck\"), verbal hostility from the rude lead, and some adult kissing, plus a consumerism note. Themes of kindness, personal growth, and empathy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/christmas-again","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Christmas...Again?!","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":251,"t":"Zombies 3","y":"2022","la":"DCOM","ca":"7+","full":"Aliens arrive as the monster community pursues acceptance. CSM notes it's wholesome — dancing and singing, minimal cheek-kissing/nose-nuzzling, and very mild interspecies taunting/threats \"not meant to be scary.\" Themes of diversity, equality, and inclusion, plus environmental/anti-pollution messages.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zombies-3","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106142567","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":252,"t":"Under Wraps 2","y":"2022","la":"DCOM","ca":"8+","full":"The mummy returns as an old rival threatens the friends' Halloween. CSM calls it goofy, spooky fun with mildly spooky moments and a few jump scares (more humorous than scary, may frighten the very young) and a wedding/kiss. A diverse cast including queer representation; themes of friendship, family, love, and loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/under-wraps-2","source":"DCOM","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q114766543","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_DISNEY = [{"num":253,"t":"Pinocchio","y":"1940","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM calls this Disney masterpiece \"darker than you may remember,\" recommending it for about age 6+. Concerns: Pinocchio is kidnapped, caged, and threatened with destruction, boys get into fights and destroy property, and a character fires a gun. Most startling to modern parents, Pinocchio gets drunk on beer and smokes cigars during the Pleasure Island sequence. Positive: Jiminy Cricket models conscience and guidance, Geppetto shows selfless love, and the story explores honesty, courage, and unselfishness through real consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pinocchio","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4341553","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":254,"t":"Fantasia","y":"1940","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Breathtaking animation feat -- with some creepy visuals.\" Recommended for about age 6+. Concerns: the pairing of dark, ominous music with unsettling imagery -- flooding caused by out-of-control broomsticks, dinosaurs locked in deadly battle, and a finale full of skeletons, graves, and ghosts -- can frighten young or sensitive kids; mythological centaurs drink wine and one deity gets tipsy. Positive: music, color, and movement are shown as deeply connected, and Mickey Mouse's Sorcerer's Apprentice segment models curiosity, courage, and the consequences of overreaching.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantasia","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q943192","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":255,"t":"Dumbo","y":"1941","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Sweet Disney classic is still lovely, despite stereotypes.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: cruel circus kids torment Dumbo, his mother is imprisoned and separated from him after defending him, and the collapsing circus tent is a genuinely scary set piece; silhouetted clowns are shown drinking, and Dumbo and Timothy get accidentally drunk, triggering the trippy \"Pink Elephants on Parade\" sequence. CSM also flags the crow characters, originally written with racist speech patterns and a character named Jim Crow, as dated and controversial. Positive: unconditional maternal love, that differences make you special, and that bullying is wrong.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dumbo","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":64,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q40895","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":256,"t":"Bambi","y":"1942","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Disney's original circle-of-life story.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: hunters fatally shoot Bambi's mother off-screen, and the film has other intense sequences -- a raging forest fire, a thunderstorm, a quail shot out of the sky, and hunting dogs chasing terrified animals. No language or substance content. Positive: Bambi's mother models total selflessness, and the film builds strong themes of environmental stewardship, friendship, and community, portraying humans as a real threat to the forest.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bambi","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":69,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q43051","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":257,"t":"Saludos Amigos","y":"1942","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"CSM reviews this together with The Three Caballeros as the \"Classic Caballeros Collection,\" calling them Walt Disney's love letter to 1940s Latin America, and recommends the pair for about age 4+. In this shorter, gentler travelogue, a caballero fires his guns into the air and a mail plane nearly crashes, but there's little else to flag. Positive: CSM highlights that, for the era, the film's genuine celebration of Latin American art, music, dance, and tradition is a pleasant surprise rather than caricature.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/saludos-amigos","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Documentary"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":43,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q842306","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":258,"t":"The Three Caballeros","y":"1944","la":"6+","ca":"4+","full":"Reviewed by CSM alongside Saludos Amigos as the \"Classic Caballeros Collection\" (recommended about age 4+ for the pair), this segment is livelier and riskier: Donald gets drunk off a single cocktail, Jose Carioca smokes a cigar throughout, Donald and a llama nearly fall from a high bridge, and Donald repeatedly whistles at and ogles Latina women in a way that reads as dated. Dated song lyrics use period slang like \"three gay caballeros.\" Positive: as with its companion film, CSM credits it with real affection for Latin American culture, music, and art rather than mockery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/saludos-amigos","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q736731","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":259,"t":"Make Mine Music","y":"1946","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"This 1940s Disney musical anthology does not have a Common Sense Media review, so this entry draws on Wikipedia and other sources. Concerns: the \"Martins and Coys\" feuding-families segment includes gunplay (edited out of some home releases), Peter and the Wolf involves wolf-hunting peril, and the finale has a whale harpooned and killed; the film carries general 1940s-era cultural stereotypes throughout. Positive: pursuing your dreams against the odds, romantic devotion, and artistic and musical expression across its ten short segments. Substitute assessment -- no direct CSM page exists for this title.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Make_Mine_Music_(1946_film)","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q754736","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":260,"t":"Fun and Fancy Free","y":"1947","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM recommends this Disney package film -- Bongo the circus bear and Mickey's Jack and the Beanstalk -- for about age 5+. Concerns: real peril throughout, including a much bigger, angrier bear chasing Bongo, lightning storms, cliff and waterfall dangers, and a giant who kidnaps Mickey and friends; one musical number oddly plays bears hitting each other as affection. Minimal language (\"stupid\"), no substances. Positive: Mickey's resourcefulness in rescuing his caged friends, Jiminy Cricket's sunny outlook, and the message to take life in stride rather than worrying about the future.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fun-and-fancy-free","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q853718","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":261,"t":"Melody Time","y":"1948","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Peril, outdated cultural references in '40s Disney cartoon.\" Recommended for about age 7+. Concerns are significant by modern standards: a heroic cowboy shoots up a town, Native Americans are portrayed as savages facing unprovoked violence, buzzards attack a dying colt, a baby is abandoned to be raised by coyotes, a smoking cowboy is framed as heroic, and women are largely shown as passive and appearance-focused. Positive: CSM credits the era's animation as innovative and spectacular even while noting its dated biases; largely a historical artifact rather than a straightforward pick for today's kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/melody-time","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q869741","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":262,"t":"The Adventures of Ichabod and Mr. Toad","y":"1949","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Two classic stories told in the best Disney style.\" Recommended for about age 6+. Concerns: the Headless Horseman repeatedly attempts to behead Ichabod Crane with a sword, a sequence genuinely scary for sensitive kids since the horseman is never unmasked as the town bully; cartoon weasels are shown passed-out drunk with bottles nearby, and characters smoke cigars and pipes. CSM notes \"very little\" in the way of positive role modeling, critiquing how men scheme and compete to win a woman characterized as a flirt. Positive: an appreciation for two classic pieces of literature.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-adventures-of-ichabod-and-mr-toad","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":68,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q863963","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":263,"t":"Cinderella","y":"1950","la":"5+","ca":"4+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Sweet fairy-tale classic has bullying, tense chase scenes.\" Recommended for about age 4+. Concerns: a clawed cat named Lucifer menacingly chases Gus and the other mice, Cinderella is pursued by shadowy steeds, and her stepfamily cruelly tears apart her ball gown; opening narration mentions a parent's death, and a king briefly smokes a cigar. Mild insults like \"stupid\" and \"pompous windbag.\" Positive: kindness, teamwork, and finding hope in hard circumstances, though CSM flags Cinderella's passivity and reliance on rescue as worth a conversation about gender roles.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cinderella","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q191753","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":264,"t":"Alice in Wonderland","y":"1951","la":"6+","ca":"4+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Surreal animated Disney classic with mild peril.\" Recommended for about age 4+. Concerns: Alice nearly drowns in a pool of her own tears, oysters are eaten by the Walrus and Carpenter, flowers throw Alice out of the garden, and the Queen of Hearts repeatedly shrieks \"Off with her head!\"; the Caterpillar smokes a hookah in every scene, and two other characters smoke pipes. Mild insults like \"stupidest,\" \"fat,\" and \"barbarian.\" Positive: Alice's curiosity and perseverance carry her through Wonderland, and she learns the value of actually following her own good advice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alice-in-wonderland","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Alice in Wonderland (1951 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":265,"t":"Peter Pan","y":"1953","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Stereotypes and violence mar Disney adventure stalwart.\" Recommended for about age 7+. Concerns: very frequent peril, with Captain Hook pointing his hook and sword and firing guns at people, children kidnapped, threats of throat-slitting, and a forced walk of the plank; the film's offensive racial slurs (\"Red Man,\" \"savages,\" \"Injuns\") and dated gender stereotyping (\"girls talk too much!\") are significant concerns for modern viewers; kids smoke a ceremonial pipe, and adults drink. Positive: imagination and freedom are celebrated, but the film also stresses that maturity and responsibility matter -- though Peter tends to solve conflict with violence rather than negotiation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/peter-pan","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q270470","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":266,"t":"Lady and the Tramp","y":"1955","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Classic Disney dogs paw their way into hearts of all ages.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: Lady is muzzled by an unkind human and chased by fierce dogs, a secondary character briefly appears to be killed, and the climax has a rat threatening a baby. CSM also flags the Siamese cats as racist caricatures of Asian people and other stereotypical portrayals worth discussing with kids. Positive: loyalty, being a good friend, protecting the vulnerable, standing up for what's right, and not judging others by their status.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lady-and-the-tramp","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Romance","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q172284","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":267,"t":"Sleeping Beauty","y":"1959","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Disney classic is delightful but sometimes scary.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: an intense sword fight between the prince and a fire-breathing dragon (Maleficent transformed), the prince nearly falls from a cliff, Maleficent kidnaps and beats him (mostly shown in shadow) and rains boulders down via her goons; she also uses words like \"fools,\" \"idiots,\" and \"imbeciles\" and there's a passing reference to hell. Kings toast with wine and a minstrel drinks himself unconscious. Positive: love conquering evil, and both Aurora and Philip standing up for choosing who they marry; the good fairies model resourcefulness and loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sleeping-beauty","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q215617","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":268,"t":"One Hundred and One Dalmatians","y":"1961","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Lovable cartoon classic with cute dogs and a mean villain.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: Cruella De Vil can be genuinely frightening, the puppies are in real peril from her fur-coat scheme, her henchmen threaten the dogs, and there are tense high-speed chases; Cruella smokes cigarettes in nearly every scene, other adults drink, and Roger smokes a pipe. Cruella's insults include \"idiot\" and \"imbecile.\" Positive: the cruelty of greed and animal mistreatment, teamwork, and compassion, as the Dalmatian parents and their humans take in 84 additional puppies beyond their own litter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/101-dalmatians","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q165512","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":269,"t":"The Sword in the Stone","y":"1963","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Delightful classic brings King Arthur legend to life.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: young Wart is often punished by his guardian and bullied by Kay, there's some peril during his and Merlin's magical adventures (including a spooky forest), and the witch Madam Mim can be a bit frightening; wine is served with meals. Very mild language (\"Blast me to Bermuda!\"). Positive: bullying doesn't make you a bully, the value of education, and that courage, love, and intelligence matter more than brute strength -- with young Arthur modeling strong character even before he becomes king.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sword-in-the-stone","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q204662","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":270,"t":"The Jungle Book","y":"1967","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Jaunty animation, jazzy songs, iffy representation.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: the climactic battle between Baloo and Shere Khan isn't graphic but includes some upsetting moments, and a burning branch is tied to the tiger's tail as he flees; CSM specifically flags King Louie and the monkeys as drawing on racist minstrelsy imagery, worth a conversation with kids. Positive: friendship, responsibility, and finding family in unexpected places, with generous, caring characters succeeding while selfish or evil ones don't, and Mowgli's friends showing courage and teamwork to protect him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-jungle-book-1967","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q199839","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":271,"t":"The Aristocats","y":"1970","la":"5+","ca":"4+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Jazz and hijinks make this Disney cat tale meow.\" Recommended for about age 4+. Concerns: the butler Edgar spikes the cats' milk with sleeping pills and kidnaps and abandons Duchess and her kittens in the country, and a pitchfork chase creates brief injury scares; a goose gets comically drunk after a restaurant meal. CSM flags a Siamese cat character built on racist stereotypes, including exaggerated features. Positive: that friendship and family can form anywhere, loyalty, and the value of shared adventure -- with Duchess staying graceful through new experiences and the wrongdoing butler facing consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-aristocats","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q184701","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":272,"t":"Robin Hood","y":"1973","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Clever animated take on the folktale has some violence.\" Recommended for about age 5+. Concerns: frequent cartoon violence with characters fighting using bows, flaming arrows, swords, and axes, plus references to hanging and a noose; a character stumbles out of a tavern visibly drunk, and one disguise scene draws wolf whistles with suggestive costuming. Positive: Robin Hood and his Merry Men model empathy for the poor and stand against economic injustice, while the vain, greedy Prince John shows the costs of selfishness and poor self-control.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/robin-hood","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19090","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":273,"t":"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh","y":"1977","la":"4+","ca":"3+","full":"\"Remains faithful to A.A. Milne's beloved classic stories.\" A few mild-peril moments — Pooh chased by a swarm of bees, Rabbit lost and disoriented in the woods, and a dream sequence where Pooh is shot at with a toy pop gun — might startle very sensitive kids, and Eeyore's gloomy self-criticism runs throughout. Positive: warm messages about friendship and looking out for one another, with an ensemble of characters modeling compassion and empathy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-many-adventures-of-winnie-the-pooh","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q498434","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":274,"t":"The Rescuers","y":"1977","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Great adventure, but too dark for preschoolers.\" Concerns: a dark plot involving a kidnapped orphan girl held for ransom by the villainous Madame Medusa, who wields a shotgun; scenes of near-drowning and dangerous falls in the bayou; and an unsettling shot of a diamond glinting inside a human skull. Positive: teamwork, courage, and compassion, as the mouse heroes model helping those in need while greed gets its comeuppance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-rescuers","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q39722","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":275,"t":"The Fox and the Hound","y":"1981","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Heartwarming tale of friendship, but expect some peril.\" The film opens with the off-screen shooting death of Tod's mother, and later includes hunting imagery (traps, gunfire) and an intense bear attack that ends in a cliffside plunge. Positive: loyalty across social divides, as Tod and Copper's friendship survives the world's insistence that a fox and a hound must be enemies, plus a gentle message about turning grief into hope.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-fox-and-the-hound","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q40302","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":276,"t":"The Black Cauldron","y":"1985","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"Dark Disney fantasy adventure with real peril: frightening creatures, skeleton imagery, repeated mortal danger, and a temporary self-sacrifice death drive much of the story. A brief witch-seduction gag adds some body-focused comedy, and minor drunken behavior appears among the villain's followers. No meaningful language concern. Positive: courage, self-sacrifice, and standing up to evil even when afraid.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Cauldron_(film)","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q329316","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":277,"t":"The Great Mouse Detective","y":"1986","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Clever Sherlock Holmes tribute mixes wit, peril.\" Though rated G, the plot involves the kidnapping of a toymaker mouse and a scheme to kill the reigning Mouse Queen, carried out by the menacing Professor Ratigan and his creepy bat henchman; there's a pub brawl, a duel, and background drinking/smoking. Positive: intelligence over brute force, as Basil's cleverness defeats Ratigan's plotting, plus strong father-daughter devotion and teamwork between Basil and Dr. Dawson.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-great-mouse-detective","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Mystery","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q334132","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":278,"t":"Oliver & Company","y":"1988","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Can't compete with Disney classics, but still fun.\" Loosely based on Oliver Twist, the film has some scary moments as the orphaned kitten Oliver falls in with a gang of street dogs and their down-on-their-luck owner Fagin, who owes money to a menacing loan shark. Positive: Oliver learns self-reliance, and the dogs model loyalty and mutual care for each other and their human friend, with the pack's makeup reflecting different NYC neighborhoods.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/oliver-company","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q216929","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":279,"t":"The Little Mermaid","y":"1989","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Superb, entertaining animated musical has some scary stuff.\" Concerns: a genuinely frightening climax where the sea witch Ursula grows to giant size and wields a trident, a chef who chases Sebastian with a cleaver, and a storyline in which Ariel trades away her voice for a chance at romance, worth a conversation about self-worth. Positive: Ariel models curiosity, adventurousness, and perseverance, and Sebastian's loyalty holds even when he disagrees with her choices.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-little-mermaid","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q190135","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":280,"t":"The Rescuers Down Under","y":"1990","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A rare sequel that improves on the original.\" Concerns: young Cody is threatened with being eaten by a crocodile more than once and spends much of the film in real jeopardy alongside a golden eagle and her eggs, and the villain McLeach is swept over a waterfall to his death. Positive: courage, teamwork, and helping those in need, with an anti-poaching, conservation message running throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-rescuers-down-under","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q202371","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":281,"t":"Aladdin","y":"1992","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A magic carpet ride of a movie from Disney.\" Concerns: the sorcerer Jafar and his mind control can be scary for younger kids, chase scenes involve armed henchmen and mythological monsters, and the film leans on cultural stereotyping of its Middle Eastern setting alongside some potty humor and mild name-calling. Positive: love, loyalty, and honesty win out, and Aladdin's arc about not pretending to be someone else pairs with Jasmine's spirited independence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/aladdin","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Aladdin (1992 Disney film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":282,"t":"The Lion King","y":"1994","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Musical king-of-the-beasts blockbuster is powerful, scary.\" Concerns: Mufasa's death in the wildebeest stampede is both sad and frightening, hyenas menace as a militaristic threat, there's an eerie elephant graveyard, and some reviewers flag villains drawing on Black, gay, and disabled stereotypes. Positive: family, sacrifice, and responsibility — Simba learns that running from your problems isn't the answer, and his parents model selfless love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lion-king-1994","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q36479","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":283,"t":"Pocahontas","y":"1995","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fine for kids; just don't expect a history lesson.\" Concerns: three people are shot (one fatally), settlers use slurs like \"savages\" and \"heathens\" toward Indigenous characters, partial nudity during a swimming scene, and the film romanticizes a relationship between an adult Pocahontas and John Smith despite the real Pocahontas being a preteen. Positive: Pocahontas models bravery and moral courage as a peacemaker between two hostile groups, and her father Chief Powhatan is a caring leader who values her counsel.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pocahontas","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Pocahontas (1995 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":284,"t":"The Hunchback of Notre Dame","y":"1996","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Touching but dark Disney tale cheers on the outcasts.\" Concerns: sword fights and an arrow injury, disturbing demonic imagery, and Judge Frollo's menacing pursuit of Esmeralda carries an uncomfortable undertone that goes over most kids' heads but not all parents'. Positive: it's okay to be different — Esmeralda fights for justice and defends outcasts, and Quasimodo's kindness and loyalty are rewarded; CSM recommends previewing before showing to kids under 9.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-hunchback-of-notre-dame-1996","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Hunchback of Notre Dame (1996 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":285,"t":"Hercules","y":"1997","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Lighthearted, but scary stuff is too much for littlest kids.\" Concerns: a lot of gore and intensity for a G-rated film, including the fanged, terrifying Hades, a hydra that gets decapitated, glimpses of dead and dying people in the underworld, and apocalyptic flood/fire imagery near the end. Positive: the film's real theme is that true heroism is about character, not fame, and Meg is written as tougher and braver than the usual damsel in distress.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hercules","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q271189","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":286,"t":"Mulan","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Disneyfied but dignified tale of Chinese warrior.\" Concerns: scary, intense battle scenes with weapons and explosions, a genuinely menacing villain in Shan Yu, and the off-screen destruction of villages; gender stereotypes are played for laughs in ways worth discussing. Positive: perseverance, integrity, and courage, as Mulan works hard, stays honest, and challenges gender expectations to save her family and country.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mulan","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q537407","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":287,"t":"Tarzan","y":"1999","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Kids will be drawn to Disney's fast-paced version.\" Concerns: a baby gorilla and Tarzan's parents are killed by a rampaging leopard, with aftermath scenes of grieving and bloody paw prints; there's also a burning ship, an animal rampage, gunfire, and a climactic villain death. Positive: acceptance across difference — \"hearts are the same\" — with Kala modeling devoted adoptive parenting and Jane written as a capable scientist rather than a damsel in distress.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tarzan","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Tarzan (1999 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":288,"t":"Fantasia 2000","y":"1999","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Delightful, but may scare more sensitive kids.\" Concerns: dark, scary imagery paired with ominous music across several segments, including an overpowering jack-in-the-box with glaring eyes and sharp teeth, marauding rats, threatening eagles, raging fires and giant waves, plus a Penn & Teller segment involving an axe. Positive: music as storytelling, with several segments modeling heroism and perseverance, and an accessible introduction to symphonic music for kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantasia-2000","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q30937","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":289,"t":"Dinosaur","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Stunning, but can be dark and scary in places.\" Concerns: battles to the death between vicious predators and heroes frequently in danger, plus intense imagery — landslides, a meteor strike, tsunamis, cave collapses, and fire — heightened by spooky music and very dark settings; not for very young or easily frightened kids. Positive: teamwork and standing together, as the loyal, brave hero dinosaur risks himself for the less fortunate, modeling that the best leaders truly care about those who follow them.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dinosaur","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q476329","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":290,"t":"The Emperor's New Groove","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fun, goofy cartoon misrepresents Incan culture.\" Concerns: mostly comic peril, including a creepy nighttime jungle chase, and a sarcastic protagonist whose attitude could rub off on young viewers; despite the Incan setting, none of the principal voice cast is Latino, a real gap in representation. Positive: people can change — spoiled Emperor Kuzco learns humility and redemption through his friendship with Pacha, who keeps faith in him despite repeated mistreatment.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-emperors-new-groove","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q223163","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":291,"t":"Atlantis: The Lost Empire","y":"2001","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Entertaining but intense adventure for tweens and up.\" Scarier and more violent than most Disney animated fare: mass-destruction sequences with tidal waves, a sea monster, and lava; extensive weapons use (guns, explosives) with numerous character deaths; betrayal among the expedition crew; and background smoking/drinking. Positive: CSM notes the positive messaging is thin here — Milo's genuine wish to preserve Atlantean culture stands out against companions driven by greed, though the ensemble does model multicultural teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/atlantis-the-lost-empire","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q318975","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":292,"t":"Lilo & Stitch","y":"2002","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Great characters, life lessons in Hawaii-set Disney film.\" Concerns: sci-fi laser battles, gunfire, and explosions; a scene where a bullied Lilo punches and bites a classmate back; Stitch's fanged, destructive behavior; and insults like \"stupidhead\" and \"abomination\" played for laughs; Lilo and Nani's parents died in a car accident, referenced once. Positive: family can form in the most strained circumstances, and every character — even Stitch — gets a redemption arc built on compassion, courage, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lilo-stitch-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q36092","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":293,"t":"Treasure Planet","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Outer-space pirate treasure hunt has fun, intense battles.\" This sci-fi spin on Treasure Island packs in near-constant action: ship chases, laser-blast battles, explosions, and falls, plus a loyal character's tragic death after a betrayal. Language stays mild (\"stupid,\" \"shut up,\" an exclamatory \"oh my God\"), and background drinking and a pipe-smoking character round out the concerns. Positive messages carry real weight, though: Jim Hawkins grows from reckless troublemaker into someone honest and brave, mentored by the morally complicated John Silver, while Captain Amelia models sharp, confident leadership.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/treasure-planet","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q392530","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":294,"t":"Brother Bear","y":"2003","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Cute bear tale has some peril.\" A young man named Kenai kills a bear in anger after his brother is fatally mauled protecting him, and the spirits transform Kenai into a bear himself as a lesson — two character deaths and several tense, perilous scenes may unsettle sensitive kids, and the spiritual return of deceased loved ones could raise questions. There's light bathroom humor but nothing on language, substances, or sexual content. The story's real strength is its message of empathy: Kenai learns to see the world through another's eyes, make amends, and lean on family, with a talkative cub named Koda along for the journey.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/brother-bear","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q215365","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":295,"t":"Home on the Range","y":"2004","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Not a classic, but cute and fun for families.\" A trio of dairy cows sets out to catch an outlaw and save their farm from foreclosure, with mostly comic peril, a rollercoaster-style chase that might spook the youngest viewers, mild language, and a brief cross-dressing joke. No one actually gets hurt despite the cartoonish action. The film leans on wit and heart more than any explicit moral lesson, with its animal heroes working together and taking real initiative to protect their home.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/home-on-the-range","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q936194","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":296,"t":"Chicken Little","y":"2005","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Cute, sometimes-frantic movie has peril, potential scares.\" After Chicken Little's false alarm about the sky falling gets him mocked by his whole town, an actual alien invasion arrives, bringing pounding music, zapping alien machines, and a panicked-citizens opening that can run intense for younger kids; ongoing bullying and a bit of suggestive humor (including a scene of Chicken Little in his underwear) round out the concerns. Positive: the story rewards persistence and honesty, as Chicken Little is ultimately proven right, and his small circle of loyal friends stands by him even when the rest of town doesn't.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chicken-little","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q270940","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":297,"t":"Meet the Robinsons","y":"2007","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Clever but sometimes scary time-travel adventure.\" Orphan inventor Lewis travels to the future and tangles with a villain whose robotic bowler hat wreaks havoc, plus a genuinely startling T-Rex chase and several comic-but-loud invention explosions. Language stays at G-rated taunts like \"booger breath,\" with a bit of coffee-drinking and an adult wearing what looks like a nicotine patch. Positive: Lewis keeps trying despite repeated rejection and refuses to hold a grudge against his rival, and the film's core message — that failure is just part of the path to success — is reinforced by its warm, oddball vision of family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/meet-the-robinsons","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q221679","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":298,"t":"Bolt","y":"2008","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Super-dog adventure is fun, age-appropriate for kids.\" A TV-star dog who thinks his stunt powers are real sets off cross-country to save his person, running into peril mostly framed as scenes from his own show — explosions, a hostage situation, \"evil\" cats — plus a genuinely tense fire during the climax. Language is limited to mild insults like \"stupid,\" with some incidental Las Vegas product placement. Positive: Penny and the cynical cat Mittens both show real capability and courage, and Bolt's arc lands on the film's clear message that being loved matters more than having superpowers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bolt","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q212792","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":299,"t":"The Princess and the Frog","y":"2009","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"First African American Disney princess is a good role model.\" A menacing villain commands creepy shadow minions and casts voodoo spells, and a supporting character's death lands as genuinely intense for a kid-aimed movie, alongside cartoonish fights and some background champagne at parties. Language isn't a concern. Positive: hardworking waitress Tiana is Disney's first Black princess and a standout role model — resourceful and loyal, she saves herself rather than waiting to be rescued — though a few supporting characters carry some dated, underdeveloped stereotyping.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-princess-and-the-frog","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q171300","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":300,"t":"Tangled","y":"2010","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Fantastic princess adventure is fun, with great messages.\" Cartoonish chases, frying-pan bonks, and sword threats fill this Rapunzel retelling, and one character's death (plus a near-fatal knife wound for the hero) push past pure slapstick; language is mild (\"stupid,\" \"dumb\"), and a tavern scene plays a character's drunkenness for laughs kids likely won't clock. Heavy merchandising is also worth knowing about. Positive: Rapunzel is curious, brave, and self-rescuing rather than passive, and the film consistently rewards honesty, gratitude, and looking past appearances.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tangled","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q188439","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":301,"t":"Winnie the Pooh","y":"2011","la":"3+","ca":"3+","full":"\"Adorable big-screen Pooh adaptation is short and sweet.\" About as gentle as animated movies get: the only real wrinkle is the imagined \"Backson\" monster, whose description might unsettle the most sensitive tiny viewers, plus some harmless pratfalls and a fall into a pit. There's nothing to flag on language, romance, or substances. Positive: Pooh and friends model real teamwork and kindness, with Pooh learning to put others first, Piglet working through his fears, and Rabbit showing off his industrious side — a great pick for a child's very first movie.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/winnie-the-pooh","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":64,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q922193","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":302,"t":"Big Hero 6","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Awesome origin story is action-packed, deals with grief.\" A fire kills Hiro's beloved older brother Tadashi early on, and the film doesn't shy from the aftermath, pairing that loss with robot-combat action against a genuinely scary masked villain and one moment of possible self-sacrifice that plays as \"really upsetting.\" Language stays mild (\"nerd\" used affectionately), with some non-mean-spirited jokes about Baymax's rotund shape. Positive: the film treats grief honestly, showing that healing comes through leaning on the people who love you, while huggable healer-robot Baymax and Hiro's diverse, capable friend group model empathy, teamwork, and courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/big-hero-6","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q13091172","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":303,"t":"Moana","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Memorable musical with a Pacific Islander lead, some scares.\" Several genuinely dark, scary sequences punctuate this musical adventure — a lava monster's attack, a violent storm at sea, an enormous glowing crab, and coconut-shell pirates wielding weapons — alongside mild insults like \"sharkhead\" and a mostly-shirtless Maui. Positive: Moana is an outstanding role model, driven by curiosity, courage, and devotion to her people rather than any romance, and her influence pushes the once-selfish demigod Maui toward real personal growth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/moana","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18647981","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":304,"t":"Ralph Breaks the Internet","y":"2018","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Colorful, clever sequel tackles complexity of online world.\" A Grand Theft Auto-style racing game brings weapons and crashes, and an \"insecurity virus\" grows into a genuinely menacing monster amid looming deletion threats; language stays at affectionate name-calling and mild potty humor (\"stench breath,\" \"doody\"), with heavy real-brand product placement throughout. Positive: Ralph and Vanellope's friendship is put to a real test as their goals diverge, and the film thoughtfully weighs internet fame against what actually matters, modeling empathy, loyalty, and self-control along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ralph-breaks-the-internet","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q25167044","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":305,"t":"Frozen II","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Slightly darker sequel charms with catchy songs, messages.\" Battle flashbacks bring weapons and nongraphic references to past deaths, elemental spirits attack the group, and a stretch where Elsa appears frozen solid while Olaf melts away could genuinely upset younger kids (both are resolved happily). Language is essentially clean, romance stays at hugs and cheek kisses, and there's heavy merchandising to be aware of. Positive: the film leans into themes of sisterhood, courage, and accepting people from different backgrounds, with both Anna and Elsa modeling bravery and using their strengths to protect the people they love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/frozen-2","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Frozen 2","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":306,"t":"Strange World","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Sci-fi adventure/tender family drama has scares, peril.\" The Clade family's expedition into a hostile, unmapped world brings several life-or-death close calls (aircraft crash, ATV chase, on-foot danger), flamethrowers and weapons used against creature threats, and a presumed character death that isn't lingered on; there's also brief parental drinking and a sad stretch where a father walks away from his son mid-mission. Positive: the story centers on honest communication and repairing strained family bonds across generations, with supportive parents who accept their son as he is and a grandfather who owns his mistakes, alongside real environmental and diplomacy-over-conflict themes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/strange-world","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q107473453","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":307,"t":"Wish","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Celebration of Disney animation is fun—but only just fine.\" The villain King Magnifico turns genuinely intimidating and uses his magic to hurt people in scenes that verge on torture-like, a heavy object gets pushed onto someone (no injury shown), and Asha's father's earlier death is discussed as an ongoing source of grief. Language is minimal. Positive: the film's central message is that your dreams are part of who you are and shouldn't be taken from you, with Asha modeling compassion, courage, and integrity while rallying her community toward teamwork and doing what's right.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wish","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q113883193","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":308,"t":"Moana 2","y":"2024","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Teamwork, courage overcome danger in engaging sequel.\" Moana and her crew face several genuinely touch-and-go moments — a god-summoned storm with towering waves, a giant killer clam, poison darts from the Kakamora, and other close brushes with mortal danger — with only mild language (\"hate,\" \"crazy,\" \"butt\") and a single flirtatious wink as the extent of romantic content. Positive: Moana continues to model strong, devoted leadership as both sister and daughter, and the film's throughline about following your calling and persevering through setbacks comes through in genuine teamwork among the crew.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/moana-2","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q124457266","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":309,"t":"Beauty and the Beast","y":"2017","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Fantastic but scarier remake of the 'tale as old as time.'\" This live-action version turns up the intensity: a pack of snarling wolves attacks and leaves the Beast bloodied, Gaston shoots the Beast and whips the village into mob violence with torches and pitchforks, a character dies falling as the castle crumbles, and flashbacks show mothers dying of illness and children being separated from them. Language stays at mild insults (\"idiot,\" \"fool\"), with some kissing, cleavage in period dresses, and tavern drinking among villagers. Positive: Belle remains a smart, independent, book-loving heroine, and the story's core lesson — looking past appearances and class to see who someone really is — comes through clearly, alongside the Beast's arc toward humility and generosity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/beauty-and-the-beast-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19946102","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":310,"t":"Monsters, Inc.","y":"2001","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Cute, kid-friendly monster movie; may scare sensitive kids.\" Monsters who scare children for a living get an unlikely house guest in this comic-but-occasionally-tense film; its scariest stretch has the villain strapping a toddler into a machine built to harvest her screams, and a factory-wide panic breaks out over a child's sock. There's nothing to flag on language or other content. Positive: the film's clear message is that facing your fears pays off, with Sulley and Mike learning that making kids laugh beats scaring them, and the story rewards courage, compassion, and integrity while a corrupt authority figure faces real consequences for his choices.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/monsters-inc","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q187726","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":311,"t":"The Lion King 1½","y":"2004","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Clever and mostly charming.\" Timon and Pumbaa narrate the events of the original from their own sidelines, so the hyenas' menace and predator danger return, along with slapstick violence like falls and near-misses on cliff edges. There's a heavy dose of gas, belching, and nose-picking jokes typical of the duo. Underneath the comedy, it explores friendship and what's lost when you abandon family to chase a carefree life alone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lion-king-1-12","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q223217","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":312,"t":"Peter Pan: Return to Never Land","y":"2002","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Pleasant but forgettable sequel to Disney classic.\" Set during the WWII Blitz, it opens with real historical weight: bombs falling on London and children separated from their families. In Never Land, Jane faces mild peril and some scary moments from Captain Hook, though most of it plays for comedy rather than real threat. There's no profanity or objectionable content, and the film's clearest message is that girls can be just as brave and capable as boys, with Jane growing into a leader among the Lost Boys.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/return-to-never-land","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Return to Never Land","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":313,"t":"Cinderella II: Dreams Come True","y":"2002","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Sweet sequel has plenty of laughs for kids and parents.\" Told as three linked stories narrated by the Fairy Godmother and the mice, it's a gentle, low-conflict watch skewed toward girls, with a heavy layer of Disney Princess marketing around it. Cinderella models treating everyone as an equal regardless of rank, and staying true to herself rather than putting on airs now that she's royalty. Jaq the mouse gets his own spotlight adventure as a human for a stretch, which younger fans tend to love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cinderella-ii-dreams-come-true","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q852391","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":314,"t":"Cinderella III: A Twist in Time","y":"2007","la":"5+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Cinderella uses brains, not magic, to win prince.\" The stepmother steals the Fairy Godmother's wand to rewrite history so her own daughter marries the Prince, and she's genuinely menacing in a few scenes, including a frightening carriage ride that puts Cinderella in real danger near a ravine. There's mild slapstick violence too, like a food fight and a cat that gets set on fire, transformed, and shrunk. On the positive side, Cinderella wins the day through her own courage and cleverness rather than magic, and the story also builds a warm, respectful father-son relationship on the side.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cinderella-iii-a-twist-in-time","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1092313","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":315,"t":"The Little Mermaid II: Return to the Sea","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"An uninspired rehash of the first movie.\" This one flips the original's setup: Ariel's daughter Melody is forbidden from the ocean after the sea witch Morgana tries to kidnap her as a baby, and years later defies her parents to swim anyway. Morgana closely echoes Ursula's menace and dangles baby Melody over a shark's open mouth in flashback, sharks later stalk Melody herself, and she nearly drowns in an undersea cave. The review flags real downsides in the messaging too, since Melody runs away after a fight with her mother and her parents deal with it by lying to her about her own heritage rather than being honest.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-little-mermaid-ii-return-to-the-sea","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q467678","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":316,"t":"The Little Mermaid: Ariel's Beginning","y":"2008","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Through grief and peril, Ariel discovers music's magic.\" King Triton has banned music from the kingdom after Queen Athena is lost to pirates (it's left vague whether she's dead or captured, and the family mourns her), so this prequel leans on real grief and a temperamental, yelling father before Ariel finds an underground club that reawakens her love of song. There are chase scenes and peril along the way, plus some mermaid chatter about boys and kissing. Ariel comes across as adventurous, rebellious, and brave, and the story ultimately celebrates the joy that music can bring back to a grieving family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-little-mermaid-ariels-beginning","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q659725","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":317,"t":"The Return of Jafar","y":"1994","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A genie that should have stayed in the bottle.\" This made-for-video sequel brings Jafar back for revenge after a bumbling thief accidentally frees him from his lamp, and the ongoing threat he poses may frighten younger kids. It's noticeably rougher around the edges than the original, and Robin Williams' absence as the Genie is a letdown longtime fans will notice. On the positive side, Aladdin is falsely accused during the story and has to stand firm on his principles, showing real courage and tenacity under pressure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-return-of-jafar","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":66,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q817261","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":318,"t":"Aladdin and the King of Thieves","y":"1996","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A reunion Aladdin fans will love.\" Robin Williams returns as the Genie for this one, and a band of sword-wielding bandits called the Forty Thieves crash Aladdin and Jasmine's wedding while hunting a treasure that turns everything to gold, leading to clashing swords, a rampaging elephant, and a fight to the death on a cliff's edge. The story also digs into heavier emotional territory as Aladdin confronts the father who abandoned him as a child. It's a lighter, less frightening villain than Jafar, but the mix of wedding chaos and abandonment themes plays a bit older than the original.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/aladdin-and-the-king-of-thieves","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q817003","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":319,"t":"Pocahontas II: Journey to a New World","y":"1998","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"More romance than history, but kids will enjoy.\" Believing John Smith has died, Pocahontas travels to London to plead with the King on her people's behalf and falls for another Englishman along the way, with her animal friends providing comic mayhem throughout the journey. The film takes major liberties with real history, and there's a scene where characters (including a dog) get comically drunk. It's generally inoffensive family entertainment, though Common Sense Media notes it doesn't offer much in the way of clear positive messages or role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pocahontas-ii-journey-to-a-new-world","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1349588","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":320,"t":"Mulan II","y":"2004","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Mediocre sequel has lightweight story; some peril, violence.\" Mulan and Shang are engaged when the emperor sends them, alongside three princesses being sent off for arranged marriages, on a mission that includes sword and trident fighting and a tense scene hanging from a rickety bridge. A jealous dragon character stirs up conflict, and there's a silly song about underwear. The film leans hard into its central message that love should be a personal choice made with the heart rather than a duty owed to family or country, though reviewers note the characters feel a bit more selfish and flighty than in the original.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mulan-ii","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q837847","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":321,"t":"Tarzan II","y":"2005","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Sequel offers an enjoyable jungle jaunt with young Tarzan.\" This prequel-style story looks back at Tarzan's boyhood among the gorillas, when he fears his human differences put his family at risk after a near-fatal accident and runs off on his own. Most of the roughhousing is slapstick, but one young gorilla shows a genuinely aggressive streak, breaking rocks against his own head and threatening to throw Tarzan off a cliff. It touches on real feelings of not belonging and fear of losing family, and the runaway Zugor, who starts out using trickery, eventually grows into someone willing to take responsibility for others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tarzan-ii","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q258815","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":322,"t":"Lady and the Tramp II: Scamp's Adventure","y":"2001","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Not as good as the original, but cute and fun.\" Lady and Tramp's rebellious son Scamp runs off to join a junkyard dog gang led by the genuinely menacing Reggie, which may unsettle younger viewers, and there's a tense dogfight and one mild use of \"butt\" as a punchline. Scamp gets disciplined by his father after breaking the rules, prompting real family conversations about why kids test boundaries and whether running away actually solves anything. The gang's charismatic leader ultimately gets exposed as a poor role model who loses friends over his bad attitude, reinforcing the story's message about appreciating home and being yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lady-and-the-tramp-ii-scamps-adventure","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":69,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q244434","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":323,"t":"Bambi II","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Bambi grows up in this sequel; some emotional intensity.\" Picking up right after his mother's death, Bambi is raised by his previously distant father, and the grief and loss from the original resurface, including a scene where a friend's mother is caught in a hunter's trap and frightening chases by hunting dogs. A rival fawn bullies Bambi over his name, and the Great Prince fights off dogs with his antlers in one intense scene. At its heart, though, it's about a father learning to open up emotionally and be present for his son, and about Bambi growing into patience and awareness of the woods' real dangers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bambi-ii","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q200889","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":324,"t":"The Fox and the Hound 2","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Milder than the original and full of country music charm.\" A much gentler watch than its predecessor, this one has young Tod and Copper sneaking off to a county fair, with slapstick mishaps like a runaway Ferris wheel, a cow stampede, and a couple of accidental gunshots along the way, plus a close call involving a puppy and a truck. Bluegrass and country music fans will appreciate the genuinely strong soundtrack. The story emphasizes that friends can come from very different backgrounds, and models characters apologizing and making amends after they hurt each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-fox-and-the-hound-2","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":67,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q188899","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":325,"t":"101 Dalmatians II: Patch's London Adventure","y":"2003","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Entertaining animated sequel has some peril and violence.\" Patch teams up with a TV star dog to foil Cruella De Vil, who's now scheming to turn dogs into abstract art with the help of a beatnik painter, and there's real cartoon violence as she hits characters with objects and throws knives, plus dialogue about ways puppies could be killed. Cruella smokes constantly and there's alcohol at a gallery party scene. Underneath the slapstick, the story's message is that you don't need to look or sound impressive to be a hero, and that being true to yourself matters more than fitting in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/101-dalmatians-ii-patchs-london-adventure","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q477365","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":326,"t":"Atlantis: Milo's Return","y":"2003","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Long on action, short on storyline.\" Actually three linked adventures stitched into one movie, Milo and his crew travel the globe investigating mythological threats drawn from Norse gods to the biblical Leviathan, and some of the imagery gets intense for younger kids: hypnosis, spirits being summoned, apocalyptic \"end of days\" talk, and some pushing and head-butting between characters. The historical and mythological references are loosely sourced and not meant to be accurate. Kids will mostly be swept up in the chase scenes and action, and the throughline about light overcoming darkness gives it a straightforward moral center.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/atlantis-milos-return","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q629833","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":327,"t":"Piglet's Big Movie","y":"2003","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Not very interesting, imaginative, or exciting.\" Piglet feels forgotten by his friends and sets out to prove his worth, leading to mild cartoon peril: tumbles, falls, a scary waterfall, and a chase by angry bees, with Piglet himself getting stuck in a boot and dangling from a tree branch. There are a few brief sad moments that resolve quickly, and no real villain beyond the bees. The heart of the movie is that size doesn't determine importance, and that being helpful and appreciated matters, with all the Hundred Acre Wood characters staying loyal, honest, and kind throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/piglets-big-movie","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1406374","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":328,"t":"Pooh's Heffalump Movie","y":"2005","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Gentle story of friendship is fine for wee ones.\" When a mysterious bellowing noise convinces the Hundred Acre Wood gang that a scary \"Heffalump\" is nearby, young Roo is told he's too little to join the search, so he sneaks off on his own and gets separated and frightened along the way. There are mild falls and characters getting stuck, but nobody is hurt, and the \"monster\" turns out to be a friendly mother looking for her lost son. It's a soft, reassuring lesson about facing fears, not judging by appearances, and being kind to those who seem different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/poohs-heffalump-movie","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":68,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1361113","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":329,"t":"Tinker Bell","y":"2008","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Sweet, simple story is best for young Tink fans.\" This origin story follows Tinker Bell discovering she's a tinker fairy and struggling to accept a talent that feels less glamorous than the nature fairies' gifts, with one scene of a hawk swooping menacingly at the fairies that could startle little ones. Expect heavy merchandising tie-ins throughout. Tinker Bell's arc as an inventor who'd rather build and fix things than follow traditional fairy expectations pushes back against girl stereotypes, and the story rewards curiosity, gratitude, and teamwork while a mean-spirited fairy faces real consequences for her behavior.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tinker-bell","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q550571","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":330,"t":"Tinker Bell and the Lost Treasure","y":"2009","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Gorgeously animated fairy fantasy teaches friendship lesson.\" Tinker Bell accidentally breaks the moonstone needed for fairy dust and, in a moment she isn't proud of, blames her friend Terence, setting off a journey through a dark, rat-infested shipwreck and past two initially scary (but ultimately silly) trolls. The friendship rift may be a little confusing for the youngest viewers before it resolves. The clear takeaway is about owning up to your mistakes and forgiving each other, with Tinker Bell showing real courage, creativity, and perseverance along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tinker-bell-and-the-lost-treasure","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q873598","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":331,"t":"Tinker Bell and the Great Fairy Rescue","y":"2010","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"A few tense scenes add drama to family and friendship tale.\" Tinker Bell gets captured by a fairy-believing young girl during a storm, and there are several tense stretches where she seems to be in real danger, including a threatening cat and a dramatic thunderstorm flight home, plus a scene where the girl's father wrongly accuses her of lying. It's balanced with plenty of humor so the tension never lingers. The story leans on \"faith, trust, and pixie dust,\" with Tinker Bell's curiosity and resourcefulness ultimately winning out and an emphasis on teamwork and imagination throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tinker-bell-and-the-great-fairy-rescue","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1507306","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":332,"t":"Secret of the Wings","y":"2012","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"\"Centers on sisterhood and family, with a wee bit of peril.\" Tinker Bell discovers she has a long-lost fairy sister, Periwinkle, living across the border in the frosty Winter Woods, but fairy law forbids the two lands from mixing. There are a few tense scenes where it looks like one sister's wings have been damaged, plus a sequence where the fairy lands start freezing over and threaten Pixie Hollow itself, which may worry the youngest viewers. The film centers on family, teamwork, and sisterhood, with both fairies choosing to defy the rules to stay connected to each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tinker-bell-and-the-secret-of-the-wings","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1702819","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":333,"t":"The Pirate Fairy","y":"2014","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Amusing pirate-themed Tinker Bell adventure; some violence.\" Tink's fairy friend Zarina grows frustrated collecting pixie dust without understanding it, so she steals some and joins a crew of pirates at Skull Rock, leading to more swordplay and hostage-taking than earlier Tinker Bell films, plus a baby crocodile that bites a character. No one is seriously hurt despite the increased action. As with the rest of the franchise, it circles back to friendship and teamwork, and gives Zarina a real arc toward redemption and forgiveness after her rule-breaking choices.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-pirate-fairy","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15396069","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":334,"t":"Tinker Bell and the Legend of the NeverBeast","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Exciting fairy adventure has loss, some scariness.\" This one centers on animal fairy Fawn, who befriends Gruff, a giant, lovable-but-genuinely-scary beast, while a militarized band of Scout Fairies hunts him down in intense chase and battle sequences. There are fierce storms and lightning, characters shown injured and unconscious, and real emotional weight around a bittersweet, separation-tinged ending, so it plays a bit heavier than other Tinker Bell entries. Its themes of curiosity, loyalty, and not judging by appearances come through clearly, with Fawn modeling compassion for a creature everyone else fears.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tinker-bell-and-the-legend-of-the-neverbeast","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18581780","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":335,"t":"Planes","y":"2013","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Airborne adventure is OK for a few laughs; some stereotypes.\" Crop-duster Dusty Crophopper dreams of racing despite his fear of heights, and the film has some genuine peril around plane crashes and storms that could startle sensitive viewers, plus bullying insults like \"farm boy\" and \"loser\" aimed at Dusty. Common Sense Media also flags national stereotypes among the international racer characters and a mildly suggestive kiss-mark gag. On the plus side, Dusty's story is a straightforward one about not being limited by where you come from, backed by discipline, hard work, and loyal friends who stick by him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/planes","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1657080","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":336,"t":"Planes: Fire & Rescue","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Much-improved 3D sequel has some intense fire scenes.\" Dusty joins a team of firefighting aircraft and vehicles battling a raging wildfire, and the rescue sequences get genuinely tense, with characters trapped by fire, floodwater, and in a mine, plus a reference to past character deaths. There's some mild crude humor and a few gender stereotypes in how female characters are portrayed. At its core, the film is a tribute to the real sacrifices firefighters make, with strong messages about teamwork, putting others' safety first, and adapting when things don't go as planned.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/planes-fire-rescue","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15631322","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":337,"t":"Treasure Island","y":"1950","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"Disney's first all-live-action feature is more intense than modern PG fare suggests: pirates get shot and stabbed (one shooting shown in a painful close-up), young Jim Hawkins is wounded by a thrown knife and ultimately kills an attacker in self-defense, and drinking runs rampant among the sailors, with one drunk pirate falling overboard. Long John Silver is a genuinely dangerous antihero, a cutthroat who shows real affection for Jim, which muddies the story's line between virtue and greed. Positive: Jim's courage and integrity anchor the adventure, though sensitive kids may find the violence startling for a Disney classic.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/treasure-island-1950","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q383854","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":338,"t":"Old Yeller","y":"1957","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"One of the best early Disney dramas,\" per Common Sense Media, and it earns that reputation with real stakes: the family dog fights off a rabid wolf and a wild hog (leaving Travis's father bloodied), and Travis ultimately has to shoot Yeller himself after the dog contracts rabies, a scene not softened for kids. Guns and hunting are a constant part of frontier life on screen. Positive: Travis grows into real responsibility running the ranch while his father is away, and the film treats grief honestly, showing that loving something worth losing is still worth it.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/old-yeller","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1851869","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":339,"t":"The Shaggy Dog","y":"1959","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A lovable mutt of a classic comedy,\" per Common Sense Media -- the mild fantasy premise (a boy periodically transforms into an Old English sheepdog) plays for laughs, with violence limited to a shotgun fired to scare the dog off and no one hurt. The bigger sticking point today is dated gender roles: women are mostly background decoration, and there are broad stereotypes about Eastern Europeans. Positive: gentle, largely inoffensive family comedy for school-age kids, though the pacing can drag for modern viewers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-shaggy-dog-1959","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1608728","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":340,"t":"Pollyanna","y":"1960","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Wonderful family film with excellent messages,\" says Common Sense Media -- Pollyanna's relentless optimism wins over a whole cynical town, modeling empathy and gratitude in the face of real hardship. The one genuine scare is a fall from a tree that seriously injures Pollyanna, a moment that lands hard for young viewers even though it resolves hopefully. Positive: the film's whole point is the value of looking for the good in people and circumstances, with Pollyanna herself an unusually generous, other-focused role model.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pollyanna","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2477507","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":341,"t":"Swiss Family Robinson","y":"1960","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"A shipwrecked family builds an elaborate treehouse home and eventually fights off pirates in a wild, gadget-filled climax -- Common Sense Media notes the battle (sword fights, cannons, homemade booby traps) is bloodless but still looks and sounds real, with pirates killed by tiger, explosion, and trap. There's also a moment where the family's youngest son, about 10, is allowed a sip of his father's drink, plus some teen-boy jokes about women and dated Asian stereotypes in how the pirates are portrayed. Positive: the family's cooperation, gratitude, and resourcefulness under pressure are the throughline, even if some of the survival tips are more fun than realistic.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/swiss-family-robinson","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":128,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1367163","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":342,"t":"The Absent-Minded Professor","y":"1961","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"'60s classic is sweet, clever, and funny,\" per Common Sense Media -- the comedy leans on cartoonish pratfalls (head bonks, knockouts), a couple of head-on car crashes played for laughs with no injuries shown, and a chase scene involving gunfire. Positive: Professor Brainard refuses to bump a failing student's grade despite pressure from the football team, modeling integrity, and the film's larger message is that thinking differently -- \"marching to a different drummer\" -- is something to celebrate, not fix.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-absent-minded-professor","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Absent-Minded Professor","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":343,"t":"In Search of the Castaways","y":"1962","la":"8+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Not on Common Sense Media; this draws on Wikipedia and viewer parents' guides instead. Hayley Mills and Maurice Chevalier lead a globe-trotting search for a shipwrecked sea captain that piles on perils -- an earthquake, a flood that strands the group in a tree, a jaguar, a giant condor that carries off the youngest boy, and capture by hostile tribesmen -- all played as boisterous, old-fashioned adventure rather than real menace, though the sheer number of close calls can feel intense for younger kids. Positive: courage, loyalty, and problem-solving carry the group through every setback.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Search_of_the_Castaways_(film)","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3129651","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":344,"t":"Son of Flubber","y":"1963","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fun, harmless sequel to the Disney classic,\" says Common Sense Media -- the plot leans on a gun-happy neighbor, hints of marital friction and jealousy, and dangerous pranks, including flubber gas misused to fix a football game and a jealous character's stunts that put people at risk. CSM lists no specific positive messages here, but the inventive, do-it-yourself spirit of Professor Brainard's tinkering can spark kids' own curiosity about science and invention.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/son-of-flubber","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1196177","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":345,"t":"The Three Lives of Thomasina","y":"1964","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Cat-centric family classic touches on deep topics,\" per Common Sense Media -- a grieving veterinarian's daughter believes her beloved cat, Thomasina, has died, and the film doesn't shy from real grief and estrangement between father and daughter. Kids who've lost a pet or family member may find the cat's death-and-return storyline upsetting rather than comforting. Positive: the story is ultimately about honest emotional communication within a family and the healing power of love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-three-lives-of-thomasina","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q663034","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":346,"t":"That Darn Cat!","y":"1965","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Amusing but long romp for both adults and kids,\" per Common Sense Media -- a Siamese cat leads an FBI agent to kidnappers holding a bank teller hostage, and though it's played for comedy, the kidnapping plot and the appearance of guns (no one is hurt) can unsettle younger or sensitive kids, and the runtime tests attention spans. Positive: Patti and Ingrid come across as independent, strong-willed young women, and the film credits following your instincts as genuinely useful.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/that-darn-cat-1965","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1102396","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":347,"t":"The Ugly Dachshund","y":"1966","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Slow-moving story is for dog lovers only,\" per Common Sense Media -- an overgrown Great Dane raised alongside a litter of dachshund puppies causes constant household chaos, while two Asian handyman characters are played for racist stereotype-based laughs by today's standards. There's champagne at a party and a husband snaps \"shut up\" at his wife mid-argument (he apologizes). Positive: the mutual devotion between dog and owner is sweetly depicted, even if little else in the film holds up.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-ugly-dachshund","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2406141","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":348,"t":"The Happiest Millionaire","y":"1967","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Some drinking in long, corny Disney musical,\" per Common Sense Media -- an extended tavern scene has two leads chugging mug after mug of beer and ends in a bar fight, plus champagne, wine, and constant cigar smoking elsewhere, all set against a lengthy 141-minute runtime and dated attitudes about gender and class. CSM flags no real positive role models here; the film's guiding idea is simply to seize the day, for better or worse.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-happiest-millionaire","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":164,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q206437","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":349,"t":"Blackbeard's Ghost","y":"1968","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A yo-ho-wholesome retread of Disney favorites,\" per Common Sense Media -- the ghost of the pirate Blackbeard haunts a mild-mannered track coach, drinking rum and getting into comical scuffles with an invisible foe rather than anything genuinely scary. More of a concern: the coach cheats and compromises his principles for a competitive edge, and there's careless gun handling, gambling, and reckless driving played for laughs. Positive: not much beyond harmless, old-fashioned slapstick fun.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/blackbeards-ghost","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1495195","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":350,"t":"The Love Bug","y":"1968","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"'60s comedy has dated stereotypes, drinking,\" per Common Sense Media -- Herbie the sentient VW Beetle helps a down-on-his-luck driver win race after race, but the film leans on broken-English Asian American stereotypes played for comedy, along with drinking, cigarette smoking, hippie drug jokes, and a scene where the car dangles from the Golden Gate Bridge in an apparent suicide gag. CSM flags no real positive role models; it's dated entertainment rather than a model of good behavior.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-love-bug","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1305705","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":351,"t":"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes","y":"1969","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"1960s Disney comedy has lesson on fame's price,\" per Common Sense Media -- after a lightning strike gives college student Dexter Riley a computer-like brain, mobsters with guns chase his friends in cartoonish, slapstick fashion (car chases, attempted abductions) rather than anything realistically scary. Positive: when overnight fame and luxury go to Dexter's head, he learns that everyone is out for himself in that world and chooses his real friends over status.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-computer-wore-tennis-shoes","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q127055","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":352,"t":"$1,000,000 Duck","y":"1971","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"'70s comedy about duck that lays golden eggs,\" per Common Sense Media (reviewed under its alternate title, The Million Dollar Duck) -- the main scare is a boy stuck on a breaking ladder several stories above the street, and the film leans on outdated gender stereotypes, showing women as financially incompetent and confined to domestic roles. The father becomes so fixated on the duck's cash value that he neglects his family, especially his hurt young son -- a cautionary example rather than a role model. Positive: the story's underlying point is that family matters more than money.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-million-dollar-duck","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Million Dollar Duck","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":353,"t":"Bedknobs and Broomsticks","y":"1971","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Delightful Disney charmer may be too long for youngest,\" per Common Sense Media -- three children evacuated during WWII end up with an apprentice witch, and the backdrop includes Nazi invasion and London bombings, plus a lively animated/live-action battle finale with mild violence (a cartoon fish even smokes a cigar). There are some sexist remarks and outdated gender attitudes typical of the era, and thick British accents plus the 140-minute runtime can challenge younger kids. Positive: Miss Price is strong, confident, and kind to the children, and the film celebrates cooperation and standing up for causes bigger than yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bedknobs-and-broomsticks","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":119,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q945138","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":354,"t":"Now You See Him, Now You Don't","y":"1972","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Not on Common Sense Media; this draws on Wikipedia and other sources instead. In this Dexter Riley sequel to The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes, a college student invents an invisibility formula that gets stolen by a paroled con man scheming to turn the school into a casino, and the ensuing bank-robbery caper and chase play out as broad, cartoonish slapstick rather than real menace. Positive: Dexter and his friends' teamwork and ingenuity save their college, echoing the earlier film's message that cleverness and integrity beat greed.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Now_You_See_Him,_Now_You_Don%27t","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1366508","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":355,"t":"Charley and the Angel","y":"1973","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Wholesome, life-affirming family tale has some violence,\" per Common Sense Media -- a distracted 1930s father is told by a guardian angel that he'll die that night, and along the way there's a Chicago bootlegging subplot with gun-toting gangsters who threaten adults and even force boys into driving bootleg deliveries at gunpoint, plus a couple of near-fatal accidents. Positive: Charley transforms from a distant, grumpy father into one who truly appreciates his family, the film affirms that crime doesn't pay, and the daughter asserts her own choice in romance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/charley-and-the-angel","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3284825","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":356,"t":"Herbie Rides Again","y":"1974","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Slapstick, friendly, heroic car returns in Love Bug sequel,\" per Common Sense Media -- a greedy developer tries to force a widow from her home, and along the way there's a drunk character slurring and stumbling, cartoonish slapstick violence (car chases, punching, building demolitions), a nightmare sequence where animated cars menace a man who falls from a skyscraper, and an insensitive Native American stereotype played as a gag. Positive: courageous Mrs. Steinmetz stands up to bullying and greed, and the film credits friendship, loyalty, and persistence with winning out.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/herbie-rides-again","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1609444","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":357,"t":"The Apple Dumpling Gang","y":"1975","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Rollicking Old West ride lassos some stereotypes,\" per Common Sense Media -- a slick gambler is saddled with three orphaned kids who strike gold, and the comic Western trades in stereotypical Asian and Latino characters, along with slapstick falls and chases, drinking, and smoking. Positive: the film argues that abandoning kids is wrong and caring for them is admirable, though the ending's message that the female lead finds happiness only by giving up her career for homemaking reflects dated gender expectations.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-apple-dumpling-gang","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Western"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2081291","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":358,"t":"Escape to Witch Mountain","y":"1975","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"They don't make them like this anymore,\" says Common Sense Media -- orphaned telepathic twins Tony and Tia are pursued by men who want to exploit their powers, with mildly scary chase and tension scenes (antagonists carry guns that are never fired) that could unsettle sensitive kids, but nothing graphic. Positive: the twins use their extraordinary abilities for good, and teamwork and perseverance ultimately get them home safely.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/escape-to-witch-mountain","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1212511","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":359,"t":"Freaky Friday","y":"1976","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Endearing '76 original may feel outdated to kids,\" per Common Sense Media -- a mother and teenage daughter swap bodies for a day, with comic driving mishaps and crashes played for laughs (no real injuries) and one secondary character's alcoholism referenced, though not shown on screen. Positive: living a day in each other's shoes builds real empathy between Annabel and her mother, and the film's whole engine is learning to appreciate what someone else deals with.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/freaky-friday-1976","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1305497","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":360,"t":"The Shaggy D.A.","y":"1976","la":"7+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Dad turns into a dog in this vintage Disney movie,\" per Common Sense Media -- grown-up Wilby Daniels runs for district attorney while still cursed to turn into a sheepdog, and the sequel leans more adult than the original, with 1970s-style bar scenes (smoking, beer), corrupt criminals, theft, and mild peril, and only one real child character in the cast. Positive: the Daniels family pulls together to support Wilby's campaign, and the crooked gangsters ultimately face consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-shaggy-da","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q226944","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":361,"t":"Pete's Dragon","y":"1977","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Offbeat live-action/animation mix with lots of drinking,\" per Common Sense Media -- the seaside town's resident drunk, Lampie, is a running gag throughout, plus a villainous song joking about harming Pete, a teacher who hits a student, comic roughhousing, and some stereotyped supporting characters. Positive: Pete stays honest and kind and never turns to violence even when threatened, and his invisible dragon Elliott ultimately looks out for the whole town, with the film's throughline being hope and holding onto childlike innocence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/petes-dragon","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1332299","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":362,"t":"Herbie Goes to Monte Carlo","y":"1977","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Silly but fun French adventures of Herbie in love,\" per Common Sense Media -- Herbie falls for a Lancia during a Paris-to-Monte-Carlo road race, and the only real concern flagged is one mostly slapstick fight scene, with nothing notable on drinking, language, or romance content. Positive: CSM calls out a female mechanic character as an unusual example of a strong woman doing a traditionally male job, and the film is otherwise pure, harmless silliness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/herbie-goes-to-monte-carlo","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1199687","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":363,"t":"The Cat from Outer Space","y":"1978","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Talking alien cat outsmarts lesser humans in '70s comedy,\" per Common Sense Media -- an extraterrestrial cat with telepathic and mind-control powers gets pursued by the U.S. military and a greedy schemer, with soldiers pointing guns at the scientist who befriends him and references to Cold War-era Soviet threats; the special effects and pacing feel dated to modern kids. Positive: the story's takeaway is that looks can be deceiving, with the unassuming cat proving smarter than the humans around him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-cat-from-outer-space","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1213779","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":364,"t":"Return from Witch Mountain","y":"1978","la":"8+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Creepy classic about mind control still provides thrills,\" per Common Sense Media -- in this Escape to Witch Mountain sequel, an evil scientist implants a mind-control device in young Tony, stripping away his ability to refuse commands, and injects him with sedatives more than once, which can be genuinely unsettling for kids. Positive: Tony and Tia's sibling bond stays strong throughout, and a group of streetwise kids help the siblings escape, modeling teamwork and looking out for one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/return-from-witch-mountain","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1925695","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":365,"t":"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again","y":"1979","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Not on Common Sense Media; this draws on Wikipedia and other sources instead. Reformed outlaws Amos and Theodore try to go straight but keep stumbling into trouble -- an accidental bank robbery, an army supply-theft scheme -- in a broad comic Western full of pratfalls, punch-bowl brawls, and a flaming-fort finale, none of it played as real menace. Positive: the two bumbling leads are essentially good-hearted, and the film's slapstick chaos stays light and consequence-free throughout.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Apple_Dumpling_Gang_Rides_Again","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Western"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3821386","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":366,"t":"Unidentified Flying Oddball","y":"1979","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Disney time-travel fantasy adventure has mild peril,\" per Common Sense Media -- a NASA scientist and his android double land in King Arthur's Camelot, where a character is threatened with burning at the stake, there are sword fights with falls from heights, the robot loses limbs in battle, and a bikini-magazine image appears as a running gag. Positive: Tom uses his scientific know-how creatively and with integrity, and the film shows friendship forming across a huge gap in backgrounds and eras, with characters growing past their initial prejudices.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/unidentified-flying-oddball","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1795954","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":367,"t":"Herbie Goes Bananas","y":"1980","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"More adventures of the lovable Volkswagen Bug,\" per Common Sense Media -- Herbie tangles with a young Mexican pickpocket and Inca-treasure thieves aboard a cruise ship, and there's one genuinely upsetting scene where Herbie is thrown overboard, plus stereotyped depictions of Hispanic characters. Positive: the film centers on the growing friendship between Herbie and the pickpocket boy, and CSM calls it overall silly, harmless fun for young viewers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/herbie-goes-bananas","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q732518","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":368,"t":"The Watcher in the Woods","y":"1980","la":"10+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Dated Disney horror tale has occult themes, mild scares.\" An American family moves into an old English manor plagued by unexplained events tied to a decades-old disappearance; concerns include a girl thrown from a horse causing a car crash, a child nearly drowning, unsettling occult rituals, and a church fire. CSM notes the film offers little in the way of positive messages or fleshed-out characters -- it's mostly mood and mystery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-watcher-in-the-woods","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Horror","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1845888","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":369,"t":"Amy","y":"1981","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Disney TV movie about a compassionate teacher for deaf and blind children in the early 1900s. Amy leaves a controlling, unhappy marriage to teach speech to deaf students who face bullying from classmates and skepticism from adults who doubt they can learn to talk; the story also includes a child struck and killed by a train and another child's death from illness. Positive: perseverance and the message that disabilities don't limit what someone can achieve.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/amy-1981","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4749055","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":370,"t":"Condorman","y":"1981","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No Common Sense Media review exists for this Disney spy-comedy about a mild-mannered comic-book artist who builds real gadgets and gets pulled into an actual Cold War spy mission. Per Wikipedia/IMDb parents' guides: mostly lighthearted, comic-style action with car chases and stunts, no real gun violence, blood, or strong language -- closer to a live-action cartoon than a thriller. Positive: ingenuity, courage, and an ordinary guy living out a hero fantasy. Substitute assessment -- no CSM page exists for this title.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condorman","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1124617","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":371,"t":"Night Crossing","y":"1982","la":"10+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No Common Sense Media review exists for this Disney dramatization of two East German families' real 1979 escape to the West by homemade hot-air balloon. Per Wikipedia/IMDb: the film opens with a startlingly intense sequence for a Disney movie -- a teen tries to breach the border and is shot by an automatic gun, shown with visible blood -- and sustains Cold War tension (Stasi surveillance, arrests, fear of betrayal) throughout. Positive: courage, family loyalty, and the risks people take for freedom. Substitute assessment -- no CSM page exists for this title.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Crossing","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q490076","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":372,"t":"Tex","y":"1982","la":"12+","ca":"13+","full":"\"A very frank and gritty story about two brothers.\" Mason and Tex fend largely for themselves while their rodeo-circuit father is away for long stretches; concerns include teen drinking and smoking, a friend's father dealing drugs, a police shooting, and candid talk about sex and pregnancy, including a girlfriend clearly stating her limits. Positive: responsibility, resilience, and learning to think beyond yourself despite a hard family situation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tex","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":4,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3519310","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":373,"t":"Trenchcoat","y":"1983","la":"9+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No Common Sense Media review exists for this Disney mystery-comedy in which an aspiring novelist vacationing in Malta stumbles into a real conspiracy and murder plot. Per Wikipedia/IMDb: PG-level comic mystery/action with a mugging and a body count implied more than shown, plus mild romantic tension, but no explicit violence, language, or sexual content. Positive: curiosity, resourcefulness, and trusting your instincts. Substitute assessment -- no CSM page exists for this title.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trenchcoat_(film)","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q7838244","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":374,"t":"Something Wicked This Way Comes","y":"1983","la":"10+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Book-based '80s movie about an evil carnival is scary.\" A sinister traveling carnival arrives in a small Midwestern town at night, offering to grant dark wishes while preying on residents; concerns include a decapitated head falling from the sky, kids fleeing through a graveyard in terror, a man tortured into a skeletal husk by electrocution, and a swarm of tarantulas attacking two boys, plus use of \"hell\" and \"damnation.\" Positive: that happiness can overcome evil, loyalty between friends, and forgiveness for a father who feels he's let his son down.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/something-wicked-this-way-comes","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Horror"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2624855","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":375,"t":"Never Cry Wolf","y":"1983","la":"11+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Suspenseful, poignant wilderness film; a few gross scenes.\" A government biologist sent to the Arctic to study wolves faces real physical peril, including falling through ice and close encounters with the pack, and eats live mice in a gross-out experiment paralleling a wolf's diet; also includes brief non-sexual nudity and some pipe smoking and beer drinking. Positive: overcoming fear, questioning assumptions, and a strong environmental message about respecting wildlife.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/never-cry-wolf","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Never Cry Wolf (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":376,"t":"Splash","y":"1984","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"'80s fishy fairy tale has sex, some cursing.\" Tom Hanks falls for a mysterious mermaid (Daryl Hannah) who appears in his life out of nowhere; concerns include brief nudity, sexual innuendo throughout, a character shown extremely drunk, a lecherous coworker who brings pornography to the office, and language like \"bitch\" and \"goddamn.\" CSM notes the central romance leans more on physical attraction than genuine connection, and finds little in the way of real positive role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/splash","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1127184","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":377,"t":"The Journey of Natty Gann","y":"1985","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Compelling adventure too violent for some kids.\" Left behind during the Depression when her father heads west for work, Natty sets off alone to find him, riding the rails alongside other drifters; concerns include a man who picks her up hitchhiking and attempts to sexually assault her, a bloody dog fight, a train derailment, and vigilantes burning a shantytown, plus some smoking, drinking, and mild profanity. Positive: though Natty resorts to theft and other survival tactics, she finds real care and protection from unlikely companions, including a wolf and a young drifter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-journey-of-natty-gann","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1210807","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":378,"t":"Return to Oz","y":"1985","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"1985 follow-up to classic musical is tin-eared and creepy.\" Far darker than the original Wizard of Oz, this sequel has Dorothy institutionalized and threatened with electroshock therapy before she's swept back to a crumbling Oz menaced by a headless princess and a vengeful stone king; also includes a near-drowning and menacing creature chases. CSM warns kids 8 and under will likely find it disturbing. Positive: courage in the face of real fear, and loyalty in going to great lengths for friends, even when the adults around Dorothy dismiss her.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/return-to-oz","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Return to Oz","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":379,"t":"Flight of the Navigator","y":"1986","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"'80s time-travel adventure has some cursing.\" A 12-year-old is abducted by an alien ship and returns eight years later, having aged only a few hours, then escapes NASA custody in the spacecraft; concerns include surprisingly strong language for a Disney film (\"s--t,\" \"hell,\" \"bastard\"), a slur used about a dog, a stereotyped gag about tourists, a fat joke, and mild violence involving soldiers with machine guns. CSM notes the film is light on positive messages and role models overall.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-flight-of-the-navigator","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1193503","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":380,"t":"Benji the Hunted","y":"1987","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Benji shines in another simple but engrossing dog tale.\" Swept overboard in a storm, Benji washes ashore in the wilderness, where he witnesses a cougar shot by a hunter and takes on the job of feeding, protecting, and sheltering her orphaned cubs against threats from the hunter, a wolf, an eagle, and a bear. Nearly wordless and animal-driven, with minimal human presence that younger kids may need help following. Positive: selfless heroism, responsibility, and compassion -- Benji even spares a frightened rabbit despite being hungry.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/benji-the-hunted","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q817786","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":381,"t":"Ernest Saves Christmas","y":"1988","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Goofy holiday movie is OK fun for families, knowwhatImean?\" Jim Varney's Ernest P. Worrell picks up Santa Claus at the airport and ends up helping him find and convince a reluctant replacement, alongside a runaway teen; the plot's premise about swapping out Santa may confuse younger kids' sense of the legend, and there's heavy, brand-name product placement throughout. Positive: redemption and forgiveness, especially in the runaway teen's reconciliation with her family, and Ernest's well-meaning persistence in doing the right thing.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ernest-saves-christmas","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q554843","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":382,"t":"Honey, I Shrunk the Kids","y":"1989","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Silly but occasionally scary movie has lots of peril.\" An inventor accidentally shrinks his kids and two neighbor kids to ant size, and they must cross the backyard -- now a hostile jungle of monstrous insects -- to be found; concerns include a near-drowning that requires resuscitation, a harrowing run from a lawnmower, the death of a friendly ant, a father who speaks harshly to his son about sports, teens making out, and some parents smoking and drinking wine. Positive: bravery and teamwork among the kids, a father owning his mistakes and working to fix them, and a capable, resourceful girl who helps steer the group to safety.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/honey-i-shrunk-the-kids","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1426248","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":383,"t":"DuckTales the Movie: Treasure of the Lost Lamp","y":"1990","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Ducks race a wizard for riches; mild thrills and spills.\" Scrooge McDuck and his nephews chase an ancient treasure and a genie's lamp beneath a desert pyramid while a shape-shifting evil wizard, Merlock, races to beat them to it; expect comic-book action -- tumbling buildings, a raging river, a burning bridge, and lots of narrow escapes -- that CSM says only the youngest or most sensitive kids will find scary. Positive: the family learns that a fortune isn't worth risking your life for, and shows real protectiveness and courage looking out for one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ducktales-the-movie-treasure-of-the-lost-lamp","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1263501","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":384,"t":"The Rocketeer","y":"1991","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"More style than substance -- but fun, if gun-heavy, action.\" A stunt pilot who discovers a jet-pack becomes an unlikely hero when Nazi agents try to reclaim it, leading to car chases, aviation disasters, gunfights, and explosions, plus a mobster's menacing threat with a grill and a scene implying a kidnapped, drugged heroine in a compromising situation; mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\"). Positive: the hero moves from chasing personal gain to real heroism, and supporting characters turn patriotic once they learn their employer is working with Nazis.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-rocketeer","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1740704","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":385,"t":"Newsies","y":"1992","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Kids go on strike in gritty, historical musical.\" Newsboys led by Jack Kelly organize a strike against a greedy publisher, facing adults who threaten to beat children with clubs and chains and real fistfights; kids and teens smoke cigarettes, a child drinks beer, and there's some language (\"damn,\" \"dumbasses\"). Positive: strong pro-union, pro-worker themes about collective action against corporate greed, perseverance, self-belief, and Jack's growth into a trustworthy leader.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/newsies","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":121,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1056698","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":386,"t":"Honey, I Blew Up the Kid","y":"1992","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Silly scientific mayhem.\" A sequel in which the inventor dad's experiment goes wrong again, this time growing his toddler son to giant size and sending him rampaging through Las Vegas; the film avoids realistic violence, sex, or profanity, but shows a genuinely out-of-control child, parents unable to control him, and reckless driving as adults scramble to catch up. Positive: mostly reassuring -- although one scientist cares more about his career than the endangered child, the other adults work together to keep the boy safe.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/honey-i-blew-up-the-kid","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1517554","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":387,"t":"Cool Runnings","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Delightful underdog story of Jamaican Olympic bobsledders.\" Concerns include infrequent profanity (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"a--hole\"), several bobsled crashes, one cartoonish bar brawl with breaking bottles, and heavy product placement (Coca-Cola, Adidas, Red Stripe beer) alongside casual beer drinking. Positive: that outlandish dreams can come true through hard work, that integrity matters more than winning, and teamwork and perseverance overcoming prejudice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cool-runnings","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q282748","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":388,"t":"The Three Musketeers","y":"1993","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Frothy '90s Disney remake offers light amusement.\" Concerns: sword-fighting deaths and one suicide by jumping, frequent sexual innuendo, cleavage and revealing costumes, kissing, a partial nude scene, drinking, and occasional mild language (\"damn\"). Positive: teamwork, honor, duty, and loyalty run through the story, though the swashbuckling heroes also lie and womanize even as they stay loyal to each other and their country.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-three-musketeers-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q508931","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":389,"t":"Homeward Bound: The Incredible Journey","y":"1993","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Adventurous animal tale will have kids riveted.\" An uplifting, heartwarming trek with a few tense, scary moments as the three pets face bears and rushing rivers in peril; kids under 5 may not follow the plot, while older tweens might find the humor juvenile. Positive: family, teamwork, loyalty, courage, and perseverance, as the animals stay resourceful and devoted to one another the whole way home.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/homeward-bound-the-incredible-journey","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q230558","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":390,"t":"The Santa Clause","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Heartwarming holiday tale has potty humor, arguments.\" Concerns: the original Santa's fatal accidental fall, police drawing guns during an arrest, ongoing divorce-related conflict between Scott and his ex-wife, a slightly suggestive \"naughty or nice\" joke, \"hell,\" flatulence humor, and a vague reference to 1960s drug use. Positive: giving is framed as the true spirit of Christmas, and Scott's arc shows a selfish person growing into compassion, with Charlie's steady belief rewarded.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-santa-clause","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q497850","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":391,"t":"Angels in the Outfield","y":"1994","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Heartwarming movie about hope and baseball.\" Concerns: characters frequently smoke and one pours alcohol into coffee, comic slapstick violence including a bat hitting a character's face, occasional insults like \"idiot,\" and heavier themes of foster care and a friend's cancer diagnosis. Positive: teamwork and compassion bring about positive change, and unwavering optimism inspires even cynical people, as Roger's persistence and George's growth into a caring mentor show families and communities pulling together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/angels-in-the-outfield","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q659037","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":392,"t":"The Jungle Book","y":"1994","la":"9+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No dedicated Common Sense Media review exists for this live-action version, so this draws on Wikipedia and contemporary reviews. Shere Khan the tiger kills soldiers and Mowgli's father in the backstory, and later scenes involve deaths by quicksand, falls, and animal attacks that critics (including Roger Ebert) called unexpectedly intense for a PG family film; there's also a chaste adult romantic subplot between Mowgli and Kitty. Positive: courage, loyalty to one's chosen family, and standing up against greedy treasure hunters. Substitute assessment — treat the recommended age here as approximate.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Jungle_Book_(1994_film)","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Jungle Book (1994 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":393,"t":"A Kid in King Arthur's Court","y":"1995","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No dedicated Common Sense Media review exists for this title, so this draws on Wikipedia and general parents-guide sources. Content is mild: jousting and sword-combat sequences with no graphic violence, an opening earthquake that could startle younger viewers, and a chaste, age-appropriate crush between the two young leads. Positive: resourcefulness, courage, and using knowledge (and modern gadgets) to help others and stand up to a scheming villain. Substitute assessment — treat the recommended age here as approximate.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Kid_in_King_Arthur%27s_Court","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q947262","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":394,"t":"Homeward Bound II: Lost in San Francisco","y":"1996","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Definitely not as good as the first.\" No real violence, but enough mild peril to unsettle sensitive kids: the pets are nearly struck by a plane, one dog is feared killed by a truck, and aggressive dogfights and cigar-smoking dognapping villains (selling dogs to a lab) run through the plot. CSM notes no clear positive messages or role models in this sequel, unlike the original.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/homeward-bound-ii-lost-in-san-francisco","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q889691","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":395,"t":"101 Dalmatians","y":"1996","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Engaging live-action canine caper has some peril, pratfalls.\" Glenn Close's Cruella De Vil is rarely without a cigarette and repeatedly demands the puppies be \"dog-napped and skinned\" for a fur coat; slapstick violence includes two thieves electrocuted on a fence, characters dragged into water by dogs, a purse-swinging assault, and a pitchfork menacing a hiding puppy. CSM notes the cartoonish characters offer no clear-cut positive messages or role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/101-dalmatians-live-action","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q8594","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":396,"t":"James and the Giant Peach","y":"1996","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Fabulous adaptation of Roald Dahl's classic book.\" James loses his parents to a charging rhino in the opening and is forced to live as a servant to his abusive, threatening aunts; later a many-toothed shark attacks during the ocean crossing. Positive: friendship, facing your fears, and finding people who love you as you are, with James modeling courage, curiosity, and teamwork alongside his insect friends.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/james-and-the-giant-peach","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1131380","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":397,"t":"Flubber","y":"1997","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM calls this a silly comedy many kids will enjoy, recommended for about age 9+. Concerns: a brief mild-nudity gag (Professor Brainard stumbles into a life-drawing class), nearly inaudible profanity, a sad scene where a beloved robot \"dies,\" and Flubber-coated balls used to bash the villains in a slapstick fight. CSM also flags the absent-minded-professor stereotype and a cast with little diversity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flubber","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1325217","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":398,"t":"George of the Jungle","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Live-action take on popular tale is family fun.\" Concerns: a mild George-and-Ursula romance with some sexual innuendo (jokes about \"Coffee, Tea, or Me\" and ape mating rituals), plus potty humor like flatulence and wedgie jokes. Positive: kindness and open-mindedness, with George, Ursula, and the jungle's native characters shown as more decent and intelligent than the condescending, exploitative \"civilized\" villains.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/george-of-the-jungle","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q225260","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":399,"t":"Air Bud","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline notes this \"sweet dog tale has some peril and mature themes,\" recommended for about age 5+. Josh is grieving his father's death, and the film depicts both animal abuse and a coach's physical abuse of a boy; mild language (\"sucks,\" \"hell\") and one adult drinking beer appear. Positive: teamwork over a win-at-all-costs mindset, responsible pet care, and Josh gaining confidence through caring for Buddy and joining the basketball team, with a resilient single mom and a mentor coach as role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/air-bud","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q406916","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":400,"t":"Meet the Deedles","y":"1998","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Teen slacker comedy has some peril, potty humor.\" Broad, Wayne's-World-style humor includes crude terms (\"heinie,\" \"screw,\" \"fart\"), escaped-animal chaos, vehicle accidents and explosions played for laughs, and a couple kissing on screen. Positive: that easygoing, seemingly unmotivated people can still rise to responsibility, with one twin's science and computer skills coming in handy when it counts.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/meet-the-deedles","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2043529","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":401,"t":"My Favorite Martian","y":"1999","la":"9+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's blunt tagline: \"A terrible movie -- beware,\" recommended for about age 8+. Concerns: crude, vulgar references (mostly euphemisms), potty humor, cartoonish violence, and a scene of non-alcoholic \"intoxication.\" CSM notes the film has no meaningful positive messages or role models, making it more filler than family classic.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-favorite-martian","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q682191","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":402,"t":"Inspector Gadget","y":"1999","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Not nearly as good as the TV show.\" CSM's 10+ reflects relentless cartoon violence and a villain (RoboGadget) who threatens a child with knives and other weapons and burns down the town while shouting aggressively; heavy commercial tie-ins and one offensive Asian stereotype are also flagged. On the positive side, Gadget's niece Penny is called out as a strong, capable role model for girls.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/inspector-gadget","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1535654","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":403,"t":"The Straight Story","y":"1999","la":"10+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Great, but young kids may be bored and restless,\" recommended for about age 13+ due to its slow, contemplative pace rather than any objectionable content — there's no strong language or nudity. Concerns: most characters smoke, and there are references to past alcohol abuse and an unwed pregnancy. Positive: the essential decency of ordinary people, close family bonds, and a thoughtful meditation on reconciling with an estranged sibling.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-straight-story","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Biography"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1139454","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":404,"t":"102 Dalmatians","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Sequel better than first live-action Dalmatians movie.\" Almost nonstop cartoon-style peril has puppies and dogs falling from high places, jumping onto a moving train, and threatened with knives, plus assorted human pratfalls; Cruella smokes in several scenes and there's a champagne toast, alongside mild insults and one \"hell.\" Positive: that actions speak louder than words — genuine change requires follow-through, not just declarations — with upstanding, honest, and brave heroes and a pointed critique of the fur trade.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/102-dalmatians","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q165847","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":405,"t":"The Kid","y":"2000","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Very funny and genuinely insightful family movie.\" CSM flags some rude, PG-level language, a schoolyard scuffle, a sad off-screen death, and a parent-child confrontation that may upset sensitive kids. The film digs into why insecure, hurting people can be unkind, giving families a real window into bullying dynamics. Positive: it favors honest self-reflection over a polished image, and shows a man reconnecting with his authentic, younger self.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-kid-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Disney's The Kid","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":406,"t":"Remember the Titans","y":"2000","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Inspiring football drama brings history to life.\" CSM flags real 1971 integration-era racism: angry crowds, slurs, segregated settings, fistfights, a brick thrown through a Black family's window, and a car accident that leaves a character paralyzed; football violence includes hard tackles and a broken wrist. Positive: empathy, integrity, and teamwork, as Coach Boone and Coach Yoast lead players across racial lines and team captains Julius and Gerry overcome prejudice to lead together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/remember-the-titans","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q117696","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":407,"t":"Recess: School's Out","y":"2001","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Simply a TV episode blown up for the big screen.\" CSM notes the G rating undersells some vulgar humor, including T.J.'s crude bathroom jokes broadcast over the school PA and a gag referencing adult hygiene products, plus T.J. reading his sister's diary aloud without permission. Positive: a racially diverse cast with capable female characters, and the kids model loyalty, cooperation, and teamwork as they save summer vacation together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/recess-schools-out","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q969270","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":408,"t":"Snow Dogs","y":"2002","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Comic action, appealing hero, splendid dogs; some scares.\" CSM flags extensive slapstick and cartoon-style pratfalls, a genuinely tense near-fatal cliff fall, an angry bear and a threatening dog, heavy product placement, and the emotional jolt of a man learning he was adopted. Positive: the hero models professionalism, honesty, and family devotion, and the film encourages openness to new people, places, and cultures.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/snow-dogs","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q968587","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":409,"t":"The Country Bears","y":"2002","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A dumb story about a bear adopted by humans.\" CSM flags a runaway-from-home plot where the bear hero doesn't tell his worried adoptive parents where he's going, an early deception about his adoption, a jealous sibling who cruelly reveals it, and a gag where a character plays music with his armpit that kids may imitate. Positive: the film explores how everyone feels different sometimes and encourages building connections with people (or bears) unlike yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-country-bears","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Country Bears","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":410,"t":"The Rookie","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Sweet, engaging true story more appealing to tweens and up.\" CSM flags a cold, unsympathetic father figure, family financial strain, references to divorce and remarriage, mild language (\"hell,\" \"damn\"), and adults casually drinking beer or wine after games without becoming intoxicated. Positive: perseverance and faith in a dream at any age, as Jim Morris models being an engaged teacher, attentive father, and loving husband who never gives up on his goals.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-rookie","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1212198","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":411,"t":"Tuck Everlasting","y":"2002","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Lovely version of the favorite middle-school book.\" CSM's 10+ reflects a kidnapping/abduction plot thread, characters shot at with rifles (they get up unharmed, being immortal) and a blow to the head, some drinking in a bar setting, and heavy themes of mortality. Positive: Angus Tuck's wisdom that you should fear an unlived life rather than death, plus Winnie's growing independence and the Tucks' hard-won kindness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tuck-everlasting","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q749624","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":412,"t":"Freaky Friday","y":"2003","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Mother-daughter switch is fun comedic chaos.\" CSM flags occasional strong language (\"screwed,\" \"harlot\"), ableist insults like \"psycho\" and \"freak,\" romantic awkwardness once mother and daughter swap bodies, mild slapstick violence (an earthquake, a football tackle), and some dated stereotyping in a Chinese restaurant scene. Positive: empathy and communication, as both Tess and Anna learn self-control and gratitude by literally walking in each other's shoes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/freaky-friday","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q118713","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":413,"t":"Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl","y":"2003","la":"10+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Rip-roaring fun for kids who don't mind skeletons.\" CSM's 12+ reflects sustained action violence and character deaths, a genuinely creepy undead pirate crew revealed in moonlight, alcohol throughout, mild profanity (\"bastard,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"), and revealing costumes with mild sexual references. Positive: female characters who resist damsel-in-distress tropes and captain their own fate, though the roguish hero and other authority figures are morally murky and frequently deceive one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pirates-of-the-caribbean-the-curse-of-the-black-pearl","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":137,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q46717","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":414,"t":"Miracle","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A moving retelling of the 1980 US Olympic hockey team's gold-medal run. CSM flags frequent hockey violence (hard checks, on-ice fights, a bloody nosebleed), occasional profanity (\"candy-ass,\" \"bastard\"), beer at social gatherings, and players making sexual innuendos about women in the stands. Positive: perseverance and dedication, as Coach Herb Brooks's demanding training pushes his players toward an extraordinary, team-first victory.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/miracle","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1312200","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":415,"t":"The Princess Diaries 2: Royal Engagement","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"A fun romp for girls of all ages.\" CSM flags several romantic kisses, a spooky-music passageway scene, mild action sequences, and one champagne toast (no smoking or drugs). Positive: Mia navigates a law forcing her to marry before becoming queen with bravery, intelligence, and kindness, learning to balance following the rules with following her heart, laughing at her own mistakes along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-princess-diaries-2-royal-engagement","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q696096","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":416,"t":"Around the World in 80 Days","y":"2004","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Book-based Jackie Chan adventure has cursing, innuendo.\" CSM's 10+ reflects nonstop slapstick and martial-arts action with many crotch-injury gags, mild profanity (\"bloody hell\"), crude bathroom humor, comedic drunkenness, a cross-dressing joke, and sexual innuendo. Positive: friendship, teamwork, and honesty, with women shown as just as brave, strong, and skilled as men in the film's fight sequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/around-the-world-in-80-days","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q156519","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":417,"t":"Sky High","y":"2005","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Cartoony high school superhero drama; OK for tweens.\" CSM flags knock-down, cartoonish superpowered violence (kids slammed through walls and windows), bullying including a literal dunking, a character who smokes, and high schoolers drinking at a party, plus mild language (\"butt,\" \"sucks\"). Positive: loyalty over popularity, as the hero learns his real worth has nothing to do with his social status or superpowers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sky-high","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q858508","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":418,"t":"The Pacifier","y":"2005","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"A crass, crude, and overly-familiar comedy.\" CSM flags cartoonish action violence including an exploding helicopter and a glimpsed dead body, heavy potty humor (diaper jokes, a character drenched in sewage), crude language throughout, and racist and sexist stereotyping among the antagonists. CSM notes the film is thin on positive messages, leaning on stereotypes and clichés rather than real role models, though a Navy SEAL does grow to genuinely care for the grieving kids he's protecting.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-pacifier","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1192363","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":419,"t":"Herbie: Fully Loaded","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Kids may enjoy it; most parents will snooze.\" CSM flags potentially disturbing demolition-derby and monster-truck imagery, mild sexual innuendo about Herbie's crush on a female VW, and heavy brand-name product placement. CSM notes the film is light on positive role modeling — the heroine lies to her father about racing, the villain cheats, and Herbie himself resorts to questionable tricks against rivals — though family loyalty and following your passion still come through.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/herbie-fully-loaded","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q641492","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":420,"t":"The Greatest Game Ever Played","y":"2005","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Predictable but inspiring family sports movie.\" CSM flags family conflict (a father who opposes his son's golf ambitions), period-typical smoking (cigars, pipes, cigarettes), rowdy pub drinking scenes, mild teasing of a short caddy, a budding romantic interest, and one disturbing childhood flashback. Positive: perseverance and passion, as Francis Ouimet pursues golf against class prejudice with his mother's steady encouragement even as his father resists.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-greatest-game-ever-played","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1171320","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":421,"t":"Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man's Chest","y":"2006","la":"11+","ca":"12+","full":"Darker and scarier than the first film: Davy Jones is a genuinely nightmarish villain with a tentacled head and crab-claw hand, a severed beating heart sits in a box, and characters are stabbed, flogged, shot at, and nearly roasted alive over a fire. A giant sea-monster sequence plucks sailors off the deck, and there's talk of cannibals considering eating people (and a dog). Language is mild (\"damn,\" \"bloody\"), but innuendo is rampant throughout. Positive notes: Will and Elizabeth show real courage and loyalty, and even the selfish Jack Sparrow reveals a core of honor when it counts.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pirates-of-the-caribbean-dead-mans-chest","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":145,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q161087","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":422,"t":"Eight Below","y":"2006","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Inspiring story about brave sled dogs; injuries, dog deaths\" is how Common Sense Media sums it up, and the peril is real: stranded huskies are attacked by a leopard seal and some die from cold and starvation, while their human companions suffer frostbite with visibly blackened fingers. There's a single use of \"s--t\" and one \"hell.\" It's genuinely distressing in places and may upset kids under nine, but the film's heart is loyalty, compassion, and refusing to give up on a friend, with Jerry's dogged (literally) perseverance the emotional center.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/eight-below","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q571164","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":423,"t":"The Shaggy Dog","y":"2006","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"A silly, harmless remake that CSM says \"will entertain grade schoolers.\" Expect a lot of dog-related slapstick and butt-sniffing jokes, plus a cattle prod and a large needle used to threaten Tim Allen's character (who spends much of the movie turning into a dog himself); he also winds up accidentally unclothed outside a courthouse in a played-for-laughs moment. Language is mild (\"butt,\" \"pee\"), and there's noticeable product placement for Kellogg's and Coca-Cola. Underneath the chaos, a workaholic dad learns to reconnect with his family, and bad behavior gets real consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-shaggy-dog-2006","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q137109","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":424,"t":"Invincible","y":"2006","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A fact-based underdog sports story CSM calls \"an inspiring movie about working hard and not giving up.\" The gritty 1970s South Philly setting brings considerable drinking and smoking, some profanity, hard-hitting football violence, and references to a character's death, reflecting a working-class world of scarce jobs and desperate times. Vince Papale's real-life journey from bartender to NFL walk-on shows how determination and self-belief can overcome long odds, even when others doubt him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/invincible","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1070160","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":425,"t":"Bridge to Terabithia","y":"2007","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM calls it a \"beautiful lesson in friendship for young and old,\" but it's genuinely sad: a main character dies suddenly in an accident, and the grief that follows is handled honestly rather than softened. A teen bully shoves and menaces younger kids, and one boy punches another in the face; the story also touches on loneliness and family and class tensions. Leslie is held up as a strong, imaginative, independent role model, and Jess's growth through their shared fantasy world of Terabithia is the emotional core -- a story about opening your heart to find magic in everyday life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bridge-to-terabithia","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q279274","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":426,"t":"Enchanted","y":"2007","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM's \"adorable fairy tale\" and \"fabulous family flick\" is gentle overall, though a wicked witch tries to poison Giselle, Edward duels a troll with his sword, and a dragon battle at the climax could startle sensitive younger kids. There's a modest shower/towel scene played for comedy, a character getting tipsy at a bar, and a few kisses including a \"true love's kiss.\" Amy Adams's relentlessly sunny Giselle wins parents over despite the naivete, and the film's real message -- that love doesn't have to look like a storybook prince to be real -- lands as a warm, gentle spoof of Disney's own princess formula.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/enchanted","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q490464","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":427,"t":"Underdog","y":"2007","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's verdict -- \"not too many new tricks left for the old Underdog\" -- sums up this live-action update: cartoonish violence has characters dragged and hit with objects, a dog and a girl get tied up near a bomb, and a building is threatened with destruction, but nothing is graphic. Language stays mild (\"imbecile,\" \"idiot\"), with a little dog flirting and a human couple's kiss thrown in. Underdog's core message is using your powers to help others, and the story doubles as a bonding tale between a lonely boy and his widowed dad.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/underdog","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1583966","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":428,"t":"National Treasure: Book of Secrets","y":"2007","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM flags this treasure-hunt sequel for frequent action violence: screeching car chases, shootouts, a flashback of a boy witnessing his father's death, and a staged reenactment of Lincoln's assassination, plus cave sequences with near-falls and rushing water that nearly drowns trapped characters. The review is notably blunt that the film offers few real positive role models, since Ben Gates and company repeatedly break laws -- including a plot to kidnap the president -- without much consequence. It's a fast-paced popcorn adventure more than a values lesson.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/national-treasure-2-book-of-secrets","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q388360","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":429,"t":"College Road Trip","y":"2008","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A gentle, G-rated father-daughter comedy CSM says \"even young kids will like.\" Content stays mild: some \"stupid\" and \"dumb\" name-calling, brief hugging and kissing between the parents, teasing flirtation between teens, and broad slapstick (a police chief nearly falls out a window, a runaway pig wrecks a wedding, a taser gets used for laughs). The daughter lies to sneak off on her trip and the overprotective dad poses as a college student to follow her, both played for comedy rather than consequence. At heart it's a relatable, if exaggerated, story about a parent struggling to let a kid grow up.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/college-road-trip","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1109085","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":430,"t":"Bedtime Stories","y":"2008","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM notes Adam Sandler \"tames his jokes for family-friendly fantasy flick\" here, aiming squarely at kids rather than his usual crude comedy crowd. Expect only mild language (\"butt kiss\" is about as strong as it gets), some cartoonish gunplay in a Western-themed dream sequence, a brief clothed hot-tub scene with light flirting, and a passing reference to a character's party-guy reputation. The story's real engine is family: an uncle bonds with his niece and nephew while helping his sister, and the group teams up to save their school, modeling teamwork and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bedtime-stories","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q726464","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":431,"t":"Race to Witch Mountain","y":"2009","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM calls this sci-fi reboot \"action packed and intense for a PG film,\" and warns it's \"more violent than most PG-rated Disney flicks\": explosions, gunfire, hand-to-hand fights, and car crashes make for loud, frightening confrontations, though there's no blood or visible death. Language stays mild, but characters do throw around lines like \"you're dead\" and \"deadly force authorized.\" On the positive side, Jack learns to trust the two mysterious kids he's protecting, a side character selflessly helps troubled kids, and the UFO-believing conspiracy theorists who get mocked early on turn out to be right all along.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/race-to-witch-mountain","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q922006","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":432,"t":"Old Dogs","y":"2009","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's blunt verdict is \"clueless-dad comedy is forgettable family fluff.\" Two grown men get drunk on cocktails, prescription pills cause exaggerated comedic side effects, and there's plenty of slapstick falling and an Ultimate Frisbee mishap played for laughs; mild profanity and scatological humor round out the language, alongside flirting, kissing, an implied conception of twins, and a brief partial-nudity gag. Underneath the goofiness, Dan chooses time with his newly discovered kids over a big business deal, and the review highlights Dan and Charlie's decades-long friendship as a genuine model of loyalty, even as it flags the shakier message that the mom hid the twins from Dan for seven years.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/old-dogs","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1229857","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":433,"t":"The Sorcerer's Apprentice","y":"2010","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Kid-friendly thriller is fun, if lacking in real magic.\" The action is larger-than-life rather than realistic, with sword duels, electric blasts, and a few impalement-style scares that can rattle kids under 8. Language is very mild (a couple of \"hell\"/\"God\" exclamations), and there's little sex or substance content to worry about. Positive messages center on self-belief, with Balthazar as a principled mentor pushing hesitant Dave toward doing the right thing.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sorcerers-apprentice","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q477865","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":434,"t":"Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time","y":"2010","la":"10+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Tepid video-game fantasy flick tame enough for young teens.\" Expect frequent chase-and-sword combat with on-screen deaths, plus a genuinely creepy hooded assassin squad; violence isn't gory but is near-constant. Language stays mild, and romance is limited to flirting and a couple of chaste kisses. The film's core message is that family loyalty should outweigh greed and envy, with the king modeling righteous leadership and Tamina holding her own alongside Dastan rather than just needing rescue.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/prince-of-persia-the-sands-of-time","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q245172","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":435,"t":"Secretariat","y":"2010","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Inspiring true story about an amazing woman and her horse.\" Content is mild: a handful of \"hell,\" \"crap,\" and \"damn,\" some sexist pushback Penny Chenery faces as a housewife entering the male-dominated horse-racing world, and mentions of her parents' deaths that could sting sensitive kids. Slower stretches may test younger viewers' patience. The real draw is Penny herself, a determined role model who balances family life while proving she belongs in a world that doubts her.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/secretariat","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q470665","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":436,"t":"Tron: Legacy","y":"2010","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Visually dazzling techie reboot has peril, fighting.\" Expect disc-weapon duels and motorcycle chases with near-death peril, mild profanity (\"hell,\" \"dammit\"), some flirting/kissing between characters in skintight bodysuits, and programs sipping bright cocktails from martini glasses. CSM flags the plot as confusing with thin characters, but the positive threads are there: Sam grows by taking responsibility for his father's company, Kevin owns his past mistakes, and Quorra models curiosity and self-sacrifice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tron-legacy","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18954","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":437,"t":"Mars Needs Moms","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Surprisingly touching adventure has sad moments amid comedy.\" The motion-capture animation makes tense scenes (chases, a near-execution, moments where Mom seems dead) feel more realistic than typical CG, which can hit younger or sensitive kids harder than expected. Insults like \"stupid\" and \"idiot\" pop up, plus mild flirting, but nothing worse. The heart of the film is genuinely sweet: it's about a kid learning to appreciate everything his fair, loving, selfless mom does for him, chores and discipline included.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mars-needs-moms","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1320985","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":438,"t":"Prom","y":"2011","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Unrealistic prom flick is bland for teens, fine for tweens.\" Compared to most teen movies, this one stays tame: dating and kissing but no sex talk or nudity, one character's admitted infidelity, a brief scuffle with a bloody chin, and mild language like \"oh my God.\" Two students also get chased by police after sneaking into a rival school. Positive threads include looking past reputations and stereotypes, choosing not to stay with someone unfaithful, and Nova's hardworking, compassionate example.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/prom","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1369031","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":439,"t":"The Muppets","y":"2011","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Muppet comedy offers memorable laughs, musical numbers.\" A brawl breaks out during Animal's anger-management class, there's plenty of slapstick, mild words like \"idiot\" and \"oh God,\" some romantic subplot, and a stream of celebrity cameos and product placement. Underneath the gags, the film leans hard into teamwork and encouragement: Walter's fan enthusiasm helps him believe in himself, Kermit leads with optimism, and Gary learns to put others' needs ahead of his own.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-muppets","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q550558","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":440,"t":"Chimpanzee","y":"2012","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Chimp 'adoption' documentary has some scary moments.\" Young chimp Oscar's mother dies after a territorial clash with a rival group, and there's a tense leopard encounter during a thunderstorm plus a (non-graphic) monkey hunt that could upset sensitive kids. The heart of the film is Oscar's unlikely adoption by the group's alpha male, showing that love and care, not just biology, are what orphaned young ones need, alongside real cooperation within the chimp community.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chimpanzee","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2963686","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":441,"t":"John Carter","y":"2012","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Mars-based action epic has strong fantasy violence.\" Battles get genuinely gory in places (decapitations, body piercing), a shape-shifting villain threatens planetary destruction, and a flashback reveals a character's wife and child's charred remains; there's also on-screen torture and death sentences. Language stays mild (\"hell,\" \"damn\") with brief drinking. On the positive side, John Carter grows from self-interest into selflessness, Dejah Thoris is a capable heroine who can defend herself, and the story champions alliance-building across different peoples.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/john-carter","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":132,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q235347","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":442,"t":"Frankenweenie","y":"2012","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Burton's creepy young Frankenstein is perfect for tweens.\" True to Tim Burton's style, the black-and-white stop-motion film is dark and macabre: a beloved dog dies, reanimated pets and creatures terrorize the town, and scary imagery with suspenseful music runs throughout, which can be too much for sensitive kids under 9. On the positive side, Victor is shown as brave and loving toward his dog, Sparky, science and independent thinking are celebrated, and eccentric teacher Mr. Rzykruski encourages pursuing your own path.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/frankenweenie","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1051023","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":443,"t":"Oz the Great and Powerful","y":"2013","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Colorful prequel is scarier, less magical than the original.\" This one skews darker than the 1939 classic: flying baboons that can be downright terrifying in 3-D, Glinda tortured by magical lightning, China Girl left with broken legs amid a destroyed China Town, and an intense twister with sharp flying debris. Oz himself starts out as a selfish womanizer who kisses four different women, though mild language is the only real language concern. The film's heart is believing in yourself and others, with Glinda's self-sacrifice and Oz's growth into a genuine protector.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/oz-the-great-and-powerful","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q590216","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":444,"t":"The Lone Ranger","y":"2013","la":"12+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Occasionally entertaining but overlong and overly violent.\" There's more violence here than the PG-13 rating might suggest, including a graphic cannibalism/heart-removal scene, references to violence against women, scalping, explosions, and a high body count shot fairly close-up. Despite the comedic tone, dark content runs throughout. On the positive side, the Reid brothers stand for justice, Tonto is driven to right wrongs done to his tribe, and Rebecca is written with real courage rather than as a damsel in distress.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lone-ranger","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Western","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":149,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q548919","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":445,"t":"Million Dollar Arm","y":"2014","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Feel-good sports dramedy is a fine pick for tweens.\" There's talk about J.B.'s sex life with some kissing and a morning-after scene, infrequent mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"stupid\"), young characters getting sick drunk at a party, and heavy product placement. The film champions hard work, perseverance, and playing sports for love of the game rather than money, with J.B. growing from a self-interested agent into someone who genuinely cares for the athletes he represents, and Rinku and Dinesh showing real bravery chasing their dream.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/million-dollar-arm","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15043347","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":446,"t":"Bears","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Some tense moments in Disney's nature documentary.\" Several sequences are genuinely nerve-wracking, including a hungry wolf and rival predator males stalking the cubs, plus a scene where a cub briefly vanishes and viewers may fear the worst (all the bears survive). The film centers on mother bear Sky's determined care for her cubs Scout and Amber, modeling themes of sticking together, protecting one another, and family devotion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bears","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q12101942","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":447,"t":"Into the Woods","y":"2014","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Sondheim's fairy tale musical is dark, complex, sublime.\" Central characters die and leave children parentless, a wolf preys on and eats a young girl (off-screen but implied), a witch may frighten younger kids, rampaging giants cause destruction, and there's depicted infidelity between married characters — none of it wraps up in a tidy happy ending. The payoff is a nuanced look at flawed but well-meaning people: choices have real consequences, family can take unexpected shapes, and bravery matters even when balanced against caring for others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/into-the-woods","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q14847067","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":448,"t":"McFarland, USA","y":"2015","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Poignant story about Latino runners a winner for families.\" There's a knife fight that sends someone to the hospital, a possible suicide attempt, and a couple of instances of domestic aggression (a thrown beer bottle, a punched wall), plus themes around class and economic privilege. The story lands on strongly positive messages about teamwork and looking past stereotypes: Coach White, despite his flaws, helps his runners see their own potential, and the boys' hardworking, loving families are shown as the real source of strength.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mcfarland-usa","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16253025","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":449,"t":"Tomorrowland","y":"2015","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Visually exciting sci-fi adventure has unexpected violence.\" Robotic villains shoot and instantly disintegrate people in several scenes, and there are frequent explosions, chases, crashes, and some hand-to-hand combat, along with mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\") and heavy product placement. The film's throughline is unapologetically hopeful: Casey's relentless optimism inspires others, Athena believes in her recruits, and Frank finds redemption by trading cynicism for purpose, all pushing the idea that dreamers and inventors can change the world if they keep going.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tomorrowland","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":130,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q7820305","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":450,"t":"Cinderella","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Visually impressive fairy tale promotes kindness.\" Being live action makes it more intense than the animated original: Ella's mother and then her father die in drawn-out, emotional scenes, her stepmother and stepsisters are cruelly abusive (insults, neglect, locking her in the attic), and there are threats of poisoning and violence. Mild words like \"stupid\" and \"hussy\" appear. The film's guiding message, \"have courage and be kind,\" plays out through Ella's compassion and respect for others, though some reviewers note she's more often rescued than proactive.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cinderella-2015","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Cinderella (2015 American film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":451,"t":"The Finest Hours","y":"2016","la":"10+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Death-defying rescue comes alive in intense drama.\" Based on the Coast Guard's most famous small-boat rescue, this true story has frequent peril and frighteningly realistic natural violence, with boats breaking apart and being tossed by huge waves, and one crewman dies attempting to transfer between vessels. Language is mild (\"jackass,\" \"screw,\" \"hell\"). Positive messages center on Bernie Webber's honesty and willingness to risk his life for strangers, and Ray Sybert's calm, creative problem-solving under pressure that saves his crew.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-finest-hours","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18031184","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":452,"t":"Alice Through the Looking Glass","y":"2016","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Uneven, less-violent sequel has girl-empowerment theme.\" Calmer than the first film but still unsettling in places: Alice is briefly institutionalized and plunges a needle into a doctor's neck to escape, a storm-tossed ship endangers the crew, and there's a comically depicted death, plus insults like \"imbecile\" and \"bloody.\" Positive messages emphasize that a girl can do whatever she sets her mind to, with Alice shown as a courageous, determined sea captain who bucks convention, and the film underscores that family and friends who love you unconditionally are worth risking safety for.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alice-through-the-looking-glass","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q17485699","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":453,"t":"Pete's Dragon","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Wonderful remake of Disney classic has peril, sad moments.\" This gentle remake opens with a car accident that kills Pete's parents, and later includes a wolf encounter, a gun pointed at the dragon, a tranquilizer shooting, and a fiery chase, all wrapped in frequent peril and a few sad, scary beats. Language is minimal, with only mildly crude jokes. Positive messages celebrate believing in magic, loyalty, and honesty, with Pete showing bravery and resourcefulness, and the story defining family as more than just biology while valuing forest and wildlife preservation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/petes-dragon-2016","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18786473","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":454,"t":"The BFG","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Sweet Dahl book adaptation has big heart, big scares.\" Roald Dahl's dark tone survives the adaptation: Sophie is kidnapped by the BFG and hunted by other, much larger giants who eat children, a nightmare is planted in her mind, and drunk men are shown for comic effect alongside plenty of \"whizzpopping\" fart humor. Strong themes of courage, perseverance, and empathy run through the story, with Sophie and the BFG modeling genuine friendship, mutual protection, and the importance of not judging others by their appearance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-bfg","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19689203","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":455,"t":"Born in China","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Nature docu has gorgeous vistas, moments of peril.\" This Disneynature documentary follows snow leopard, golden monkey, and giant panda families through breathtaking Chinese landscapes, but nature is unsentimental here: animals fight for dominance sometimes fatally, a hawk snatches a baby monkey, and a mother animal's death is shown, which can be upsetting for younger or sensitive viewers. Positive messages highlight courage and sacrifice through the snow leopard mother's fierce dedication to her cubs, family bonds, and perseverance in a harsh environment, with the panda mother patiently teaching her cub survival skills.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/born-in-china","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Born in China","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":456,"t":"Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No Tales","y":"2017","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Talented cast can't save tired, action-heavy franchise.\" This installment keeps the body count high, with sword fights, drownings, a throat slitting, and creepy supernatural ghost villains, plus Jack Sparrow frequently drunk onscreen and mild profanity like \"damn\" and \"hell.\" Positive messages come through Carina, who embodies intelligence, logic, and curiosity as she pursues knowledge despite being dismissed for being a woman, and Henry, who shows selflessness and bravery trying to save his father, with the story valuing unconditional family love and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pirates-of-the-caribbean-dead-men-tell-no-tales","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No Tales","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":457,"t":"A Wrinkle in Time","y":"2018","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Inclusive but imperfect take on classic story of hope, love.\" The kids face genuinely perilous situations, including a twister and a frightening sequence where a possessed boy uses telekinesis to hurt his sister, along with some bullying and cruel comments, though profanity is minimal. Positive messages run deep: Meg, a brilliant young woman of color, leads as a scientifically gifted hero, and the guiding Mrs. Whatsit, Mrs. Who, and Mrs. Which model optimism, kindness, and courage, with the story centering on embracing your uniqueness, staying in the light, and the power of love and family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-wrinkle-in-time","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24301388","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":458,"t":"Christopher Robin","y":"2018","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Sweet but slow tale about the power of family, imagination.\" Early scenes show Christopher Robin mourning his father's offscreen death and fighting in WWII, with guns and an explosion briefly seen, and a tense dream sequence along with anxious, monster-fearing animals (heffalumps and woozles) that younger kids might find unsettling. Positive messages emphasize the value of play, imagination, and work-life balance, as Christopher learns to prioritize his family over professional stress, and Pooh and friends model loyalty, compassion, and teamwork despite years apart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/christopher-robin","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24301991","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":459,"t":"The Nutcracker and the Four Realms","y":"2018","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"Disney's visually lush but somewhat dark reimagining of the classic ballet leans into a creepy Mouse King made of swarming mice, sword combat, unsettling clowns, and peril-filled battle scenes, with a mother's death and ongoing family grief central to the plot, plus a single use of \"damned.\" Positive messages emphasize believing in yourself, using your talents, and persevering through mistakes, with Clara showing courage, cleverness, and selflessness as a girl passionate about science and invention, guided by a father and godfather who model handling grief and communicating through pain.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-nutcracker-and-the-four-realms","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24290097","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":460,"t":"Dumbo","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"Tim Burton's live-action remake is sweet but noticeably darker than the original, with a character crushed by a collapsing tent, threatening scenes, characters in peril from heights and fire, a spooky \"Nightmare Island\" attraction, and the sad separation of Dumbo from his mother, plus minimal language like \"hell\" and \"heck.\" Positive messages focus on treating animals right and not ridiculing others for how they look, with Mrs. Jumbo's fierce, protective maternal love and the human children's kindness and patience toward Dumbo reinforcing themes of empathy, compassion, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dumbo-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24284798","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":461,"t":"Aladdin","y":"2019","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Live-action remake has charming stars, intense moments.\" This version leans into a scary Cave of Wonders sequence with lava and pursuit, a confirmed death (a man pushed down a well), a drowning scene, armed guards, and a frightening full display of Jafar's sorcery, alongside very mild insults like \"street rat\" and \"riffraff.\" Positive messages emphasize looking beyond social class to see people's true character, with Aladdin growing from a thief into someone who stays true to himself, and an expanded, more empowered Jasmine shown as intelligent, empathetic, and capable of leadership.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/aladdin-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":128,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Aladdin (2019 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":462,"t":"The Lion King","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Visually stunning remake is darker, more violent.\" The photorealistic CGI intensifies everything from the original: lifelike scenes of animals hunting and fighting, a traumatic stampede that kills Mufasa, and genuinely creepy hyena antagonists, with mild language like \"stupid\" and \"pathetic.\" Positive messages center on family, responsibility, and sacrifice, with Mufasa modeling wise, compassionate leadership and Simba learning courage, accountability, and that a true king's power lies in compassion rather than force.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lion-king","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27044293","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":463,"t":"Noelle","y":"2019","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Christmas comedy has predictable storylines, positive messages.\" This gentle holiday film keeps things light, with only some out-of-control sleigh rides and chimney tumbles for peril, no profanity, and a passing reference that could raise questions about Santa's reality. Positive messages emphasize that Christmas is about giving rather than getting, encouraging kindness, self-belief, and following your own path, with characters extending forgiveness for mistakes and working to bring joy to others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/noelle","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q39765162","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":464,"t":"Lady and the Tramp","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Remake has humor and heart; some peril, emotional intensity.\" The realistic CGI makes this version's threats land harder than the animated original: dogs face danger from cars, rats, cats, and a menacing dog catcher, with Lady imprisoned in the pound, Tramp appearing unconscious after being thrown from a moving cart, and a rat pouncing on the baby's crib, alongside mild language like \"dang it\" and \"mangy mutt.\" Positive messages emphasize family loyalty and belonging, courage and teamwork in protecting loved ones, and not judging others by their appearance or background.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lady-and-the-tramp-2019","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q56596746","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":465,"t":"Togo","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"10+","full":"\"True Alaska tale mixes action and drama; some peril.\" Based on the true 1925 serum run, the film puts its sled dog team through life-threatening blizzards, near-cliff falls, and cracking ice, including a dog jumping through broken glass, with minor profanity (\"damn,\" \"Satan\") and some bar-scene drinking, plus the real backdrop of a diphtheria epidemic endangering children. Positive messages celebrate determination, courage, and selflessness, with musher Leonhard Seppala risking his life to save others and Togo himself embodying loyalty and persistence, while the Seppalas' marriage shows mutual kindness and support.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/togo","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q58814567","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":466,"t":"Timmy Failure: Mistakes Were Made","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A quirky, book-based misfit tale about a fifth grader who runs his own (imaginary) detective agency and refuses to see himself as anything but a genius. Content is mild: a fantasy car-crash-through-a-window daydream, a brief comic fistfight, and light insults like \"loser\" and \"dumb.\" A teacher and student face a tense moment on a bridge, and some adults treat Timmy unkindly, but a caring school counselor and his overworked single mom model patience and unconditional love. Positive messages about celebrating individuality, accepting help from caring adults, and learning self-awareness run throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/timmy-failure-mistakes-were-made","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q55762028","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":467,"t":"Artemis Fowl","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A dense fantasy adaptation about a 12-year-old criminal-mastermind-in-training whose father goes missing. Expect frequent peril: a hostage situation with Artemis's father held in genuinely frightening captivity, a giant troll rampage that nearly kills several characters, fairy military battles, and fire-wielding goblins; one character appears to die before being revived by magic. Language stays mild (insults like \"traitor\" and \"thief\"), but the missing-parent plot and intense action may unsettle younger kids. Positive messages emphasize that people are complicated and shouldn't be judged solely by their parents' choices, with Artemis's cleverness, Holly's bravery, and the Butlers' loyalty offered as models, even as the Fowls' own illegal schemes complicate the picture.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/artemis-fowl","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q12302227","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":468,"t":"Safety","y":"2020","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Emotional, intense, inspiring true tale of family, teamwork,\" as Common Sense Media puts it, based on the real story of Clemson football player Ray McElrathbey secretly raising his younger brother on campus. Heavier than typical Disney fare: their mother struggles with drug dependency and cycles through prison and rehab, there are scenes of family separation and Ray's angry outbursts, college students drink at parties, and mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\") appears. Positive messages about sacrifice, asking for help, and how teammates and coaches can become family carry the film, with Ray's determination to keep his brother safe while chasing his own future as the clear takeaway.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/safety","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":122,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Safety (2020 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":469,"t":"Godmothered","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"A modern, comic riff on Cinderella following Eleanor, a bumbling fairy-godmother-in-training determined to prove happy endings still matter. Silly fairy-tale-style profanity substitutes (\"mother of fudge,\" \"son of a butterscotch\") and mild insults like \"weirdo\" fill the dialogue, along with a bar scene where adults drink, a couple of innuendo-laden jokes likely to sail over kids' heads, and a reference to a father's death in a car accident. The film's real message pushes back against fairy-tale convention: true love comes in many forms, and a full life doesn't require a storybook romance, with Eleanor's earnest kindness and the grieving family's mutual support as the emotional center.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/godmothered","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q83726410","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":470,"t":"Elephant","y":"2020","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This Disneynature documentary follows elephant matriarch Gaia leading her herd, including young Jomo, across the Kalahari in search of water. Common Sense Media calls out real peril along the way: a baby elephant gets stuck in thick mud, a river crossing turns frightening, and predators like crocodiles, lions, and hyenas threaten the herd; near the end, an elderly matriarch dies of natural causes in a tender but sad scene, with the possibility her body may be scavenged afterward. The film's heart is family loyalty, showing elephants as emotionally intelligent animals whose herd \"never leaves a member behind,\" alongside a strong conservation message about protecting the ecosystems they depend on.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elephant-0","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q89411396","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":471,"t":"Dolphin Reef","y":"2020","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Narrated by Natalie Portman, this Disneynature documentary follows a young dolphin named Echo exploring his coral reef home. Two sequences bring real tension: a dolphin calf gets separated from his mother and pod overnight, and a mother-and-calf humpback whale pair is chased by hunting orcas before other whales intervene to protect them; the film also shows the ocean food chain plainly, including creatures being caught and eaten. Otherwise gentle and soothing, it emphasizes family bonds, teamwork, and how adult dolphins and whales teach and protect their young, framing every creature, however small, as essential to the reef's balance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dolphin-reef","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Dolphin Reef (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":472,"t":"Cruella","y":"2021","la":"11+","ca":"12+","full":"\"De Vilishly delightful, daring, and dark,\" as Common Sense Media describes this villain origin story. Estella's mother is killed on screen, attack dogs menace characters, and the film includes childhood bullying and cruel, abusive behavior woven through its revenge plot; \"hell\" appears on signage, mild words like \"stupid\" and \"psycho\" pop up, and one scene implies drunkenness at a party. Positive messages about friendship, teamwork, and resilience come through Estella's fearless determination and her loyal friends Jasper and Horace, and the film updates the classic with more racial diversity and LGBTQ+ representation than the 1961 original, though parents may want to discuss its more morally ambiguous heroine.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cruella","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24284363","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":473,"t":"Jungle Cruise","y":"2021","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"A ride-inspired adventure that's \"fun, if predictable,\" with frequent peril: undead conquistadores made of bees and snakes, dangerous encounters with piranhas and a jaguar, and guns, swords, and knives in near-constant use. Adults drink throughout (flasks, taverns), the leads flirt and share a few kisses, and an early stereotypical depiction of Amazonian tribespeople as cannibals is later subverted. Language stays mild. The film promotes courage, perseverance, and teamwork, with Dr. Lily Houghton standing out as a pioneering, unapologetically bold female scientist who refuses to shrink herself to fit expectations.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jungle-cruise","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24285605","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":474,"t":"Pinocchio","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This live-action/CGI retelling leans darker and more intense than the animated original, with frequent peril: Pinocchio is kidnapped, imprisoned, nearly turned into a donkey, and swallowed by a giant sea monster, while a beloved character appears to die and others are threatened, set on fire, or enslaved along the way. Mild insults like \"jackass,\" \"stupid,\" and \"loser\" appear, and some sequences may frighten or confuse younger viewers. The story's core message is about developing a conscience and telling right from wrong, with Geppetto's unconditional love and Jiminy Cricket's ethical guidance helping Pinocchio earn honesty, bravery, and self-control.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pinocchio-2022","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q105482844","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":475,"t":"Hocus Pocus 2","y":"2022","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Campy but entertaining,\" with the Sanderson sisters back to threaten teenagers, cast spells involving blood and bones, and set fires, plus a played-for-laughs decapitated zombie. The witches openly discuss eating children to stay young, teens drink unsupervised at a party, and mild language (\"damn,\" \"idiot,\" \"nitwit\") rounds out the concerns. On the positive side, the film champions female friendship and empowerment, warning against choosing power over relationships, and its teen characters show real courage confronting danger to protect the people they love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hocus-pocus-2","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Hocus Pocus 2","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":476,"t":"Chip 'n Dale: Rescue Rangers","y":"2022","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"A live-action/CGI buddy reboot with a lot of cartoon-style violence: characters are tied up, slammed, shot, electrocuted, and frozen, and main characters appear to die and are mourned before it's revealed no one actually died. Menacing giant creatures threaten kids, mild language like \"hell\" and \"butthead\" pops up, and some jokes aim more at watching parents than kids. Positive messages celebrate loyal friendship over ambition, with Dale learning to value his old partnership and Chip letting go of a long-held grudge as both risk themselves to help each other and stop a black-market crime ring.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chip-n-dale-rescue-rangers","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106075513","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":477,"t":"Disenchanted","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This Enchanted sequel brings back Giselle for a lighter fairy-tale romp with mild scares: dragons, giants, a sleeping-potion curse, fires, and a wish gone wrong that briefly turns Giselle cruel and manipulative before she comes to her senses. Adults sip wine, teenagers flirt, a married couple kisses, and the villain Malvina is willing to put children in danger to hold onto power. The film's warmer message is that blended step-families are real families, nobody is perfect, and the real world can hold its own magic, with Giselle's underlying kindness and her daughter Morgan's courage anchoring the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/disenchanted","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27121159","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":478,"t":"Polar Bear","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Majestic footage, positive lessons, natural perils,\" as this Disneynature documentary follows a mother polar bear teaching her cubs to survive a changing Arctic. Nature is shown plainly: bears stalk and feed on prey including baby penguins and walruses, with graphic discussion of blood and blubber, a cub dies during a harsh winter, and male bears are shown preying on cubs. The film frames polar bears as resilient survivors passing hard-won knowledge across generations, with the devoted mother bear's teaching and protection of her cubs as the emotional throughline, alongside a clear message about climate change reshaping their world.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/polar-bear","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Documentary","Live-Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q111720319","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":479,"t":"Haunted Mansion","y":"2023","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"A spirited ride with peril, some scares,\" including jump scares, headless ghosts and skeletons, an ax-wielding ghost bride, a suggested suicide, an alligator chase, and a character struck by a car. Adult characters drink, sometimes to cope with depression, though language stays minimal (just one \"pissed off\"). Grief and loss run through the film honestly rather than exploitatively, landing on the message that grief can become \"a doorway to joy\" when faced together, with a diverse cast of characters modeling compassion, bravery, and teamwork as they support each other through loss.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/haunted-mansion","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Haunted Mansion (2023 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":480,"t":"Peter Pan & Wendy","y":"2023","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Captivating, moody adaptation has peril, some scares,\" as this darker, more atmospheric retelling leans into the weightier themes of Barrie's original: the psychological roots of Hook's rage, Peter's refusal to grow up, and Wendy's reluctance to leave childhood behind. Expect sword fights with Hook's crew, genuine peril for the Darling children, and a moodier visual tone than past Disney versions of the story. The film still lands on classic, hopeful messages about the value of imagination, courage, and family, while giving Wendy in particular more agency and depth than earlier adaptations.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/peter-pan-wendy","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28973277","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":481,"t":"Mufasa: The Lion King","y":"2024","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Well-acted but predictable\" origin story with real peril and violence: young Mufasa nearly drowns in a flood, the villain Kiros and his gang commit off-screen killings, and the climactic battle involves injuries and deaths that, while bloodless, land harder thanks to photorealistic animation. Kiros himself is drawn as genuinely scary and bloodthirsty, and a rift between brothers creates real emotional distress alongside a mild romantic subplot. The film's heart is found family, teamwork, and earning respect through action rather than birthright, with Mufasa's courage and compassion and Sarabi's boldness modeling how strength and empathy work together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mufasa-the-lion-king","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q114242678","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":482,"t":"Descendants: The Rise of Red","y":"2024","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This franchise entry sends Red, the Queen of Hearts' rebellious daughter, and Chloe back in time to try to fix their villain mothers' pasts. Content includes threats of \"beheadings and banishments,\" sword fights and chases, magical pranks that transform people into creatures, and psychologically abusive parenting; language stays mild (\"witch,\" \"tyrant,\" \"heck\"), and time-travel elements may confuse or unsettle younger viewers. Positive messages encourage treating others kindly (even adversaries), believing people deserve second chances, and letting kids grow into their own identities rather than their parents', with both leads learning to move past black-and-white thinking about who's good or bad.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/descendants-the-rise-of-red","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Descendants: The Rise of Red","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":483,"t":"Snow White","y":"2025","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Uneven, occasionally dark\" live-action musical remake in which the Evil Queen orders men to kill Snow White, menacing trees and creatures fill a frightening forest sequence, a character is shot with a crossbow, and Snow White's parents both die (one off-screen, one presumed). Mild language (\"shut it,\" \"fool\") and a budding romance with a few kisses round out the concerns, including one kiss whose consent Common Sense Media flags as ambiguous. The film firmly champions inner character over vanity, with Snow White's generosity, fearlessness, and empathy contrasted against the Evil Queen's greed and envy, and the diverse cast, including a wide range of ages and abilities, broadens who gets to be a hero.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/snow-white-2025","source":"DISNEY","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Snow White (2025 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_PIXAR = [{"num":484,"t":"Finding Dory","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Delightful sequel promotes teamwork; sadness, scares.\" Dory's search for the family she lost brings emotionally heavy separation flashbacks, a threatening giant squid, and tense escape sequences involving water deprivation and a runaway vehicle — the emotional weight can run heavier than the original for sensitive kids, though language stays at fish-safe substitutes like \"carp.\" Positive: the film's message that parents never give up on their children lands hard, and Dory's memory loss is treated as a difference to work around rather than something that defines her, with the whole cast modeling teamwork and unconditional love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/finding-dory","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q9321426","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":485,"t":"Ratatouille","y":"2007","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Cute rat tale has some peril and potentially scary moments.\" A gifted rat chef named Remy gets hunted by a gun-wielding grandmother and knife-throwing chefs, and a tense sewer chase may spook sensitive kids; language stays mild (\"stupid,\" \"loser,\" one \"hell\"), and plenty of the humor about French cuisine and culture is really aimed over kids' heads at adults. Positive: both Remy and his human partner Linguini learn from their mistakes and keep pursuing their unconventional dreams, and the film's throughline about giving credit where it's due and valuing family comes through clearly by the end.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ratatouille","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q170035","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":486,"t":"Cars","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Pixar comedy is full of four-wheeled fun.\" A hotshot racer named Lightning McQueen gets stranded in a small town and slowly learns humility. Content is mild for the genre: a rip-roaring chase tears up a town's roads, a gang of rusty cars briefly menaces Lightning, there's some flirtation between characters, and one use of \"hell.\" Positive messages about valuing differences and choosing integrity over ego anchor the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cars","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q182153","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":487,"t":"Cars 2","y":"2011","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Cars sequel revs up action and mixes in spy thrills.\" This installment trades small-town charm for a globe-trotting spy plot, and it's noticeably more intense than the original: gunplay, explosive chases, crashes, and a few character deaths, plus mild insults like \"stupid fool\" and \"idiot.\" Positive messages still come through, mainly via Mater, whose loyalty and self-acceptance carry a \"being yourself, dents and all\" theme, and a reminder that real friends accept each other's flaws.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cars-2","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q192212","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":488,"t":"Cars 3","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Some intense scenes in story of empowerment, mentorship.\" Lightning McQueen faces a serious crash early on with flips, sparks, and heavy damage, and a demolition-derby sequence includes cars armed with chains and saws; language stays mild (\"dang,\" \"loser,\" \"shut up\"), with a brief moonshine reference at a saloon. The film's core messages land well for families: mentorship and passing on wisdom, perseverance through setbacks, and the idea that \"you don't need to win to be a hero,\" with Cruz Ramirez modeling determination and resilience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cars-3","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q21079862","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":489,"t":"The Incredibles","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Story of superhero family has violence, positive messages.\" This one runs hotter than typical Pixar fare: many scenes of intense, sustained action violence (weapons, explosions, deaths, though not bloody), plus a glancing reference to an affair and a body-shaming joke or two, and adults are shown drinking and smoking. What balances it out is a strong family-first throughline, with the Parr family learning to combine their individual strengths, communicate honestly, and stick together under pressure, prizing courage and perseverance along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-incredibles","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Incredibles","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":490,"t":"Incredibles 2","y":"2018","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Terrific, action-packed superhero sequel was worth the wait.\" Expect sustained action violence and peril across several set pieces, a flashback that implies a shooting (not shown directly), and a scene with intense flashing lights flagged as a possible seizure risk for photosensitive viewers; language stays mild (\"crap,\" \"hell,\" \"damned\") and adults are shown with cocktails and a cigarette. The film's heart is in its family-first, role-reversal setup, with Bob taking over as primary caregiver while Helen leads missions, reinforcing messages about teamwork, communication, and valuing everyone's different strengths.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/incredibles-2","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24832112","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":491,"t":"Brave","y":"2012","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Mother-daughter princess tale has some very scary scenes.\" Merida's mother is transformed into a bear, and the film leans into genuinely frightening territory: intense bear-attack sequences, clansmen brawling with weapons, a witch's eerie hut, and will o' the wisps drifting through dark woods, plus brief animated nudity on adult men and boys. At its core the story is about mending a strained mother-daughter bond, with Merida modeled as strong-willed and independent and both women learning communication, courage, and self-control from their ordeal.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/brave","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q126796","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":492,"t":"Monsters University","y":"2013","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Monsters Inc. prequel is a fun college comedy for all ages.\" Monsters practice scaring kids (real and simulated), a flying Dean character can be startling, and there's mild fraternity-style bullying and pranks along with a few red-cup college-party scenes and a single kiss. Positive messages about friendship, perseverance, and teamwork run throughout, with Mike's hard work and Sulley's growth from slacker to disciplined worker showing that looking past surface differences reveals what people have in common.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/monsters-university","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q641362","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":493,"t":"Toy Story 2","y":"1999","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Witty sequel continues Toy Story magic; peril, sad scenes.\" The toys cross a busy street and get caught up in crashes and chaotic near-misses, there's mild name-calling (\"stupid,\" \"moron,\" \"idiot\"), some toy flirtation and kissing, and heavy toy-store brand placement. Woody learns not to fear good things ending, and the film celebrates loyalty, friendship, courage, and teamwork, with Jessie introduced as a brave, athletic addition to the crew.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/toy-story-2","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q187266","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":494,"t":"Toy Story 3","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Smart, funny 'threequel' is scarier than the first two.\" This entry leans darker: a creepy Big Baby doll and cymbal-clapping Monkey serve as unsettling antagonists, toys are restrained and bullied at Sunnyside, and an intense incinerator sequence has the whole gang facing what looks like certain doom. The payoff is a story about friendship, loyalty, and sacrifice, with Woody's steadfast devotion to Andy anchoring themes of teamwork, bravery, and being there for one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/toy-story-3","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q187278","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":495,"t":"Toy Story 4","y":"2019","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Big-hearted, touching entry in Pixar's legendary franchise.\" Expect peril during several rescue-and-escape sequences, a couple of creepy ventriloquist-dummy characters, a cat that swallows a toy, and mild language (\"crazy,\" \"idiot,\" \"stupid\"). The film's emotional core is about friendship, loyalty, and caring for kids, with Woody's devotion to his friends and Bo Peep's growth into a brave, resourceful adventurer modeling teamwork, empathy, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/toy-story-4","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18517638","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":496,"t":"Lightyear","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Buzz origin story is exceptionally animated and inclusive.\" Space rangers are attacked by sentient vines and battle a robot army and the film's villain, with chases and combat throughout; language stays mild (\"shoot,\" some bathroom humor), and one character's engagement and brief kiss with her wife are shown matter-of-factly. Positive messages about teamwork, empathy, and perseverance run through the story, with Buzz and Commander Alisha Hawthorne modeling courage, care, and the value of asking for help.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lightyear","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q104409060","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":497,"t":"Turning Red","y":"2022","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Pixar coming-of-age tale explores puberty and parent issues.\" Thirteen-year-old Mei's transformation into a giant red panda causes real chaos, including a scene where she rampages through a concert crowd; mild insults (\"dork,\" \"jerkwad,\" \"crap\") appear throughout, and puberty and periods are frequent, frank topics, alongside boy-band crushes and romantic daydreaming. The film pushes for open, honest communication between parents and teens, with Mei learning that lying to her overprotective mother backfires even as both of them ultimately grow through curiosity, compassion, and self-control.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/turning-red","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Turning Red","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":498,"t":"Inside Out 2","y":"2024","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Growing up is emotional in thoughtful sequel; some peril.\" Joy and the other emotions get caught in storms, avalanches, and chases, and are at one point locked in a dark room, while new emotion Anxiety triggers a portrayal of a panic attack; language is minimal, limited to mild words and silly substitute curses. The film's message is that every emotion, including the uncomfortable ones, is essential to a healthy sense of self, and that loving someone unconditionally means accepting their imperfections too, with the characters modeling teamwork, empathy, and resilience through Riley's hardest moments.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/inside-out-2","source":"PIXAR","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Pixar","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q113877606","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_DREAMWORKS = [{"num":499,"t":"Antz","y":"1998","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Great effects and characters, but surprisingly violent for a cartoon. There's extensive fighting with many on-screen deaths, a somber deathbed scene, and a plot to drown an entire ant colony; language includes mild swearing like \"hell\" and \"damn.\" A couple of romances include flirting, falling in love, and kissing with light innuendo. Positive messages about individualism (\"be your own ant\"), teamwork, and a strong work ethic run throughout, with Z growing from self-involved to genuinely brave and loyal.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/antz","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q610502","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":500,"t":"The Prince of Egypt","y":"1998","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This animated retelling of Moses's story carries real weight for a cartoon. Enslaved people are whipped and abused, babies are thrown into crocodile-infested water, and Moses kills an overseer in anger -- all handled seriously rather than for shock. Miriam and Tzipporah are strong, independent women, and Moses himself is a kind, responsible protagonist wrestling with duty and freedom. A solid, thoughtful introduction to the Book of Exodus for kids ready for its intensity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-prince-of-egypt","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Drama","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q245227","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":501,"t":"Joseph: King of Dreams","y":"2000","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"An animated Bible story that's too scary for very young viewers. Joseph's jealous brothers sell him into slavery, his prophetic dreams include unsettling imagery of wolves, destruction, and beheadings, and he's later falsely accused of assault and imprisoned. Despite the dark turns, the story lands on forgiveness: once Joseph rises to power in Egypt, he chooses reconciliation with his brothers over revenge, a strong model of moral growth after real hardship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/joseph-king-of-dreams","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Drama","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1465155","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":502,"t":"Shrek","y":"2001","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Gross-out laughs meet a marvelous fairy tale mix. There's a scary dragon and a torch-wielding mob, but the violence stays cartoonish, and mild profanity (\"damn,\" \"ass,\" \"crap\") plus plenty of crude humor may go over younger kids' heads. Princess Fiona breaks the passive-princess mold with real fighting skills, Shrek turns out to be loyal and brave beneath his gruff exterior, and Donkey is the ultimate devoted friend. Strong themes about looking past appearances and staying true to yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shrek","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q483815","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":503,"t":"Spirit: Stallion of the Cimarron","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Intense animated mustang tale has lots of peril and violence. A wild horse is captured by the U.S. Cavalry and subjected to harsh training attempts -- whips, spurs, branding, and days without food or water -- plus separation from his family, a near-drowning in rapids, a fire, and a runaway train with rifle fire. Native Americans are portrayed as brave and honorable, but there aren't many positive role models otherwise, since the Cavalry is shown pursuing conquest through cruelty and theft.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spirit-stallion-of-the-cimarron","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Spirit: Stallion of the Cimarron","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":504,"t":"Sinbad: Legend of the Seven Seas","y":"2003","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Fun, if standard, animated adventure with battles and innuendo. Expect sword-and-dagger combat, execution threats, mild flirting and sexual innuendo, a glimpse of a partially animated bare bottom, and wine and martinis in a few scenes. The film leans on themes of love, friendship, loyalty, and peace among people -- Sinbad grows from a mercenary into someone who values loyalty, his first mate Proteus embodies duty, and the women in the cast are smart and capable even as the chaos goddess Eris makes an effective villain.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sinbad-legend-of-the-seven-seas","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1043425","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":505,"t":"Shrek 2","y":"2004","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"As much fairy tale fun as the first, with some added potty humor. Expect crude jokes, mild profanity (\"ass,\" \"bloody\"), bar scenes with implied drinking, a couple of drug-related jokes, and some innuendo including moments played for cheap laughs at gender expression. On the positive side, the story is really about integrity and accepting people as they are: Shrek shows real love and tenderness toward Fiona, and Fiona learns to follow her own path instead of everyone else's expectations.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shrek-2","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q485983","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":506,"t":"Shark Tale","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Fast, fresh, funny action comedy set undersea, with a mob-movie spin. Sharks act like mafia bosses who chase and eat fish, there's a staged pro-wrestling-style brawl, a mafia-funeral parody, and occasional crude humor. Lenny the shark learns to accept being a vegetarian despite peer pressure, and Oscar realizes chasing fame and glamor matters less than genuine friendship -- solid messages under the fin-flapping jokes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shark-tale","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Shark Tale","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":507,"t":"Madagascar","y":"2005","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"Cute animal story with some crude humor and innuendo that will sail past younger viewers -- including a hippo miming modesty with starfish and crabs and a tranquilizer-induced hallucination. There's real peril once the zoo animals wash up in the wild, and Alex the lion has an unsettling personality shift that threatens his friends. Still, the movie lands on friendship, teamwork, and putting the group's needs above your own, with Marty's adventurousness and Alex's eventual compassion as the takeaways.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/madagascar","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q174555","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":508,"t":"Wallace & Gromit: The Curse of the Were-Rabbit","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A funny and charming stop-motion movie for the whole family. The were-rabbit's transformation is mildly scary with its werewolf-like features, and there's cartoon chasing and shooting as villagers pursue the creature with guns and garden tools, plus minor adult drinking at a party. At its heart, though, it's a story about the loyal, trusting friendship between Wallace and Gromit, and the greedy villain gets a well-earned comeuppance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wallace-gromit-the-curse-of-the-were-rabbit","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q318428","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":509,"t":"Over the Hedge","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Cute animated tale with some mild scares and plenty of cartoon violence -- characters get crushed, blown up, flattened, and bounced, a bear threatens to kill a raccoon, and an exterminator shows up armed with traps. The animals steal food from humans and each other along the way, but the story ultimately values found family and teamwork over solo scheming, even as it shows characters lying and stealing before learning better.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/over-the-hedge","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q245366","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":510,"t":"Flushed Away","y":"2006","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"Crude but imaginative adventure is flush with fun. Expect abundant potty humor about a pampered rat flushed into the sewers, a belching and farting sidekick named Sid, cartoon violence with characters shot at, chased, and electrocuted, and mild innuendo like an accidental kiss. Rita is a capable, independent female lead, and the film's real message is about stepping outside your comfort zone to actually live your life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flushed-away","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q752301","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":511,"t":"Shrek the Third","y":"2007","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"Cute but not as fun as past entries, with more cartoon violence and adult-aimed jokes. Expect references to alcohol and drugs, mild name-calling (\"dork,\" \"loser,\" \"stupid\"), innuendo about procreation, bullying (including wedgie talk), and frequent slapstick destruction. Still, the princesses stop waiting to be rescued and defend themselves, a fairy tale villain chooses redemption, and young Arthur learns to step into leadership -- all while Shrek stays devoted to family and staying true to himself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shrek-the-third","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q486588","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":512,"t":"Bee Movie","y":"2007","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"Seinfeld comedy is cute fun for the whole family, though some jokes are clearly aimed at adults. There's a harrowing Manhattan flight sequence, an imagined plane crash and explosion, insect-killing attempts, and even a passing mention of a \"suicide pact,\" plus references to bees as \"honey slaves\" that may confuse kids. Barry learns to value his role within the hive, and Vanessa shows real compassion by protecting him -- the film ultimately lands on environmental stewardship and respect for all living things.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bee-movie","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q275167","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":513,"t":"Kung Fu Panda","y":"2008","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Action-packed start of a franchise, with scary scenes and some fat-shaming jokes aimed at Po. Expect martial-arts punches, kicks, weapons, and explosions, plus an intense villain prison-escape sequence that can startle younger kids. The film's heart is a strong message that \"there's no secret ingredient to greatness -- you just have to be yourself,\" with Po's perseverance and Master Oogway's wisdom reinforcing integrity and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kung-fu-panda","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q129193","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":514,"t":"Madagascar: Escape 2 Africa","y":"2008","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Fun sequel has some romance, peril, and adult-aimed humor. A plane crash strands the crew in Africa, hunters show up with guns, and there's an upsetting moment where young Alex is forcibly separated from his father in a flashback; a flirty hippo comments on another's figure. The heart of the film is loyalty -- the four friends learn to accept their own flaws and, through the journey, become better friends to each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/madagascar-escape-2-africa","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q188474","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":515,"t":"Monsters vs. Aliens","y":"2009","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Homage to '50s alien flicks that's too intense for the youngest kids. Expect gunfire, explosions, widespread destruction, panicking crowds, and some deaths, plus a scene where a good character is briefly presumed dead. Language stays mild (\"jerk,\" \"stupid\"), and romance is limited to flirting and one interrupted kiss. The film's real message is that teamwork and determination save the day, as the monsters overcome humans' initial fear and prejudice to work together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/monsters-vs-aliens","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q681918","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":516,"t":"Shrek Forever After","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Fiona's fierce and Shrek's lovable in this still-funny fourth movie. Expect cartoonish medieval combat between ogres and witches, mild innuendo, some jokes at characters' expense over their looks, and a scene of Shrek downing several cocktails. Fiona is the standout here, rallying fellow ogres and leading a resistance against a tyrant, while the story overall emphasizes appreciating what you have and standing up for the disenfranchised.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shrek-forever-after","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q208131","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":517,"t":"Megamind","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Clever animated superhero story is fun, not too scary. It flips the formula by centering on the supervillain, and while one scene shows a skeleton and an apparent death, it's played cartoonishly rather than realistically scary. There's mild language, some hand-holding, flirting, and a kiss, and a line stating the Tooth Fairy and Easter Bunny aren't real. The film's real point is that our choices, not our past, define who we are, and Roxanne is a brave, kind role model who sees Megamind's potential for good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/megamind","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Superhero"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q81205","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":518,"t":"Kung Fu Panda 2","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Panda hero saves the day in thoughtful family film.\" Concerns: plenty of hand-to-hand combat and explosive cannon fire, though injuries stay mostly bloodless; the emotional core involves Po's parents being taken from him as a baby and an implied past massacre, which can distress sensitive kids. No language/substance issues. Positive: family isn't only about blood, letting go of grudges for inner peace, integrity, perseverance, and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kung-fu-panda-2","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q487447","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":519,"t":"Puss in Boots","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Swashbuckling adventure features irresistible warrior cat.\" Concerns: frequent sword duels, a cannon/gun fight, a monster chase, and one character's death (another willingly plummets to it), all played with cartoon flair; mild innuendo around Puss as a \"lover\" and some flirting/romance. Orphan themes may resonate differently for adopted kids. Positive: redemption, unconditional friendship, the bond between mother and child, and that your choices define you more than your past.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/puss-in-boots","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q324262","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":520,"t":"Madagascar 3: Europe's Most Wanted","y":"2012","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Entertaining 'threequel' has some mild violence, innuendo.\" Concerns: mostly slapstick action with a relentless dart-gun-wielding animal-control officer chasing the zoo crew, one near-curse-word gag (\"BULLshevik\"), and a bit of romantic innuendo. No real scares or substance content. Positive: loyalty, friendship, the value of freedom, and not letting past mistakes stop you from trying again.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/madagascar-3-europes-most-wanted","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q244247","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":521,"t":"Rise of the Guardians","y":"2012","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Holiday icons defend childhood in gorgeous adventure.\" Concerns: intense fantasy action as Pitch Black (the Boogeyman) destroys a Guardian and unleashes nightmare stallions that can frighten younger kids; the Australian Easter Bunny frequently says \"bloody,\" and a flashback shows a character drowning (though he transforms rather than dies). No substance issues. Positive: the wonder and importance of childhood belief, bravery in protecting children, and Jack Frost's journey to find where he belongs.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rise-of-the-guardians","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q136625","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":522,"t":"The Croods","y":"2013","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Gorgeously animated adventure has intense themes.\" CSM's 8+ reflects frequent talk of death and the constant risk of dying in a wild, unstable prehistoric world, plus natural disasters and perilous survival situations that can unsettle younger viewers. Mild name-calling (\"fat,\" \"dummy,\" \"sucky\"). Positive: that hiding gets you nowhere, courage and self-expression, and a father learning to trust his daughter's growth, though female characters sometimes still need rescuing.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-croods","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q495850","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":523,"t":"Turbo","y":"2013","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Speedy snail dreams big; expect peril, stereotypes.\" Concerns: a snail hero repeatedly risks death crossing freeways, dodging lawnmowers, and fleeing crows that prey on his kind, plus mild language (\"son of a gun,\" a character named \"Skid Mark\") and heavy product placement. Positive: \"no dream is too big, no dreamer too small\" — perseverance, self-belief, and supportive friendship, though some side characters lean on ethnic stereotypes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/turbo","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1523217","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":524,"t":"Mr. Peabody & Sherman","y":"2014","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Punny time-travel adventure with lots of comic peril.\" Concerns: the time-traveling duo face imprisonment in ancient Egypt and a near-execution during the French Revolution (all survive), plus mild insults (\"stupid,\" \"dumb,\" \"loser\") and two scenes of Mr. Peabody mixing cocktails. Positive: family doesn't need to look conventional to be loving, unconditional parental devotion, kindness, and loyalty across unlikely friendships.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mr-peabody-sherman","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q6929072","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":525,"t":"How to Train Your Dragon 2","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Epic, thrilling 3D adventure sequel is outstanding.\" Concerns: a significant character dies at the hands of a mind-controlled dragon, and large-scale dragon-army battles may frighten younger viewers; mild insults and some age-appropriate romance (kisses, a joke about physique) now that Hiccup and Astrid are 20. Positive: cooperation and diplomacy over war, tough independent female characters (Valka, Astrid, Ruffnut) who need no rescuing, and courage over brute strength.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-to-train-your-dragon-2","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q10298666","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":526,"t":"Penguins of Madagascar","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Entertaining Madagascar spin-off mixes peril and humor.\" Concerns: nonstop action with explosions and chases, a scene where the team believes a member has been killed, kidnapping and caging, and characters transformed into monsters; a crude \"butt hand\" joke and brief hints of alcohol. Positive: not judging others by appearance, loyalty, bravery under pressure, and teamwork, though the reviewer flags a notable lack of female representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/penguins-of-madagascar","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15616479","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":527,"t":"Home","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Animated alien comedy is sweet, cute, if not super original.\" Concerns: an alien invasion of Earth, a character who appears to die but survives, some toilet humor, and the emotional thread of a girl separated from her mother. No language or substance issues. Positive: tolerance, cross-cultural friendship, and being who you really are, as the misfit alien Oh learns that genuine connection matters more than fitting in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/home","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4499813","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":528,"t":"Kung Fu Panda 3","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Upbeat but intense threequel looks at identity, family ties.\" Concerns: extensive martial-arts combat, a scary supernatural villain (Kai) and unsettling jade-warrior imagery, flashbacks of parent-child separation, and mild language (\"stupid,\" \"loser\") plus bathroom humor. Positive: integrity, perseverance, teamwork, and self-discovery — \"if you only do what you can do, you'll never be more than you are now\" — with a warm portrayal of a blended biological-and-adoptive family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kung-fu-panda-3","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15055043","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":529,"t":"Trolls","y":"2016","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fun, colorful adventure has some peril, lots of great music.\" Concerns: the menacing Bergens brandish knives and cooking implements while hunting the trolls, tense chases with a vicious dog-like creature, mild insults, some flirting/innuendo, and a wistful moment when Branch recalls losing someone he loved. Positive: never giving up, self-acceptance (don't change yourself to make someone like you), and Poppy's bravery, loyalty, and growth as a strong female lead.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/trolls","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Trolls (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":530,"t":"The Boss Baby","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Animated comedy about sibling rivalry has peril, body humor.\" Concerns: chases and peril, including a spooky imagination sequence with attacking animals; frequent potty language and body humor (bare infant bottoms), plus a scene with champagne and a reference to Tim trying an adult drink. Puppies are treated more as products than living creatures, which some parents flag. Positive: a family's love isn't a fixed quantity that runs out, and the brothers learn cooperation, teamwork, and mutual appreciation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-boss-baby","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Boss Baby","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":531,"t":"Captain Underpants: The First Epic Movie","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Book-based adventure is fun ... if you like potty humor.\" Concerns: it's true to the source material's constant potty language (\"poop,\" \"poopypants,\" \"diarrhea,\" \"butt\") and slapstick action/peril, softened by cartoonish tone; some mild insults (\"weirdo,\" \"stupid\") and light stereotyping. Positive: friendship, teamwork, creativity, and empathy — the boys ultimately learn that laughing at someone's expense is wrong and everyone deserves understanding.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-underpants-the-first-epic-movie","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q20979182","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":532,"t":"How to Train Your Dragon: The Hidden World","y":"2019","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Family-friendly threequel has peril, bloodless battles.\" Concerns: extensive dragon-vs-human and dragon-vs-dragon battles with suspense and peril, including a presumed fatal fall, though violence stays bloodless; mild insults, a wedding kiss, and Vikings drinking unspecified ale without intoxication. Positive: inclusion, rising above self-doubt, courage, teamwork, and family support, as Hiccup and Toothless both grow into the responsibilities of adulthood.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-to-train-your-dragon-the-hidden-world","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22970530","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":533,"t":"Trolls World Tour","y":"2020","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Amusing, upbeat musical sequel promotes joys of diversity.\" Concerns: aggressive Hard Rock Trolls terrorize and kidnap other troll leaders, a character nearly drowns and briefly glimpses \"heaven\" (played for laughs), mild insults (\"you suck,\" \"we're screwed\"), some romantic tension, and brief glittery bare-bottom gags. Heavy merchandising. Positive: listening to others instead of pushing your own agenda, teamwork, empathy, and celebrating differences across musical genres and backgrounds as a source of strength.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/trolls-world-tour","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q29825830","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":534,"t":"The Croods: A New Age","y":"2020","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Prehistoric cartoon sequel has slapstick, rude humor.\" Concerns: frequent slapstick punching (especially between monkeys and humans), monster battles and sacrifice scenarios, glowing-eyed creatures that may scare younger kids, a character acting drunk after a bee sting, teen/young-adult romance with kissing, and the implied death of a boy's family in a flashback. Positive: people are stronger together than alone, women shown as equally capable as men in rescues, courage, teamwork, and looking past assumptions about those who are different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-croods-a-new-age","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24832743","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":535,"t":"Spirit Untamed","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"So-so story, strong girls in upbeat horse adventure; peril,\" per Common Sense Media. Lucky's mother died in a rodeo accident before the story begins (handled off-screen, but it's an early emotional gut-punch), and later Lucky and her friends face real danger from a band of horse thieves, including a tense rescue. The girls are brave and resourceful but also impetuous, sneaking off without permission more than once. Positive messages about courage, teamwork, and open communication with parents run throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spirit-untamed","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q97289392","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":536,"t":"The Boss Baby: Family Business","y":"2021","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Sibling-themed sequel will entertain young fans; mild peril,\" says Common Sense Media. Expect cartoonish chases and fights, including armed Baby Ninjas and a villain who uses hypnosis/mind control on kids, plus some potty humor and a character who overdoes it on candy. Mild language like \"stupid\" and \"sucks\" pops up occasionally. The film's heart is about brothers Tim and Ted rebuilding their bond, valuing family teamwork, and recognizing that pushing young kids too hard to achieve isn't healthy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-boss-baby-family-business","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Boss Baby: Family Business","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":537,"t":"Puss in Boots: The Last Wish","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Danger, peril ratchet up a notch for charismatic cat,\" per Common Sense Media, and that's no exaggeration: Puss is killed in the opening scene, wakes up on his last of nine lives, and spends the movie pursued by a genuinely creepy, whistling wolf bounty hunter wielding twin blades. There are sword fights, explosions, falls, and a flashback where Puss is shown comically drunk, along with mild language like \"hell\" and \"crap.\" Underneath the scares, the film lands a real message about facing mortality, letting go of selfish glory-seeking, and choosing found family over going it alone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/puss-in-boots-the-last-wish","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Puss in Boots: The Last Wish","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":538,"t":"Ruby Gillman, Teenage Kraken","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fun animated coming-of-age fantasy has thoughtful messages,\" according to Common Sense Media. A climactic battle whips up a tidal wave that puts the town in real peril, and one teen is shown sinking underwater unconscious before being saved; there's also some slapstick creature violence and a couple of innocent kisses tied to a prom-date subplot. Mild insults like \"stupid\" and \"shut up\" crop up. The film's core theme, that \"what makes you different is what makes you powerful,\" plays out through Ruby's self-acceptance journey, with strong, capable female role models and a nuanced look at how well-meaning parental overprotection can hold kids back.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ruby-gillman-teenage-kraken","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q117188308","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":539,"t":"Trolls Band Together","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Cheery threequel is silly, sweet fun; some innuendo, peril,\" per Common Sense Media. Villains kidnap a character in a magical cage, and there's a startling clown-face jump-scare and a trippy psychedelic sequence, plus bathroom humor like \"barf\" and \"pee.\" Married couple Poppy and Branch share kisses and there's a honeymoon joke that will sail over kids' heads. The story leans hard into family loyalty and honest communication, with Poppy's leadership and Branch's devotion to his long-lost brothers driving home that \"family is always worth it.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/trolls-band-together","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q117323743","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":540,"t":"Chicken Run: Dawn of the Nugget","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Stop-motion sequel has cartoon violence, mild threat,\" says Common Sense Media. This time Ginger's daughter Molly gets trapped inside a nugget factory, and the chickens face electrocution, an ax-wielding threat, explosions, and the constant looming danger of an \"untimely end\" on the processing line, though nothing graphic is shown. There's mild name-calling like \"toe rag,\" and the film carries a clear anti-factory-farming message. At its core it's an underdog story about courage and teamwork, with Ginger learning to balance protecting Molly against letting her grow independent.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chicken-run-dawn-of-the-nugget","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q60836051","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":541,"t":"Kung Fu Panda 4","y":"2024","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Peril, some potty humor in Dragon Warrior buddy comedy,\" per Common Sense Media. Po faces off against the shape-shifting villain Chameleon, who can summon the stolen powers of dead kung fu masters, leading to a village's destruction, a blazing quarry, and characters being captured and imprisoned; the martial-arts fights are frequent but quick, with few serious injuries shown. Language stays mild (\"stupid,\" \"screw up\"), with the usual bathroom-humor asides. The film's real message is about redemption and not letting past mistakes define you, with Po's optimism and new friend Zhen's growth from selfishness to loyalty carrying the theme home.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kung-fu-panda-4","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q114707487","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":542,"t":"The Wild Robot","y":"2024","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Beautiful, heartwarming adaptation with moments of peril,\" says Common Sense Media. Several animals die, mostly off-camera to predators, including the accidental death of a goose that leads Roz to adopt her gosling Brightbill; there's also a character's self-sacrifice, a dangerous wildfire, an intense storm, and armed robots firing on the island's creatures, plus young possums who joke morbidly about death. Brightbill is bullied for being different, and mild stand-in language like \"bovine excrement\" appears. The film's real strength is its portrait of found family and devoted parenting, as Roz grows from a task-focused machine into someone genuinely kind and empathetic, alongside themes of tolerance, teamwork, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wild-robot","source":"DREAMWORKS","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q124378349","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_NICK = [{"num":543,"t":"Harriet the Spy","y":"1996","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"Harriet spies on neighbors and classmates for her notebook, and when it's stolen and read aloud, she's ostracized with real bite: name-calling, shunning, a bra hung from the flagpole in revenge, and blue paint dumped on her clothes. There's a hard slap across a classmate's face, the word \"retarded\" used as an insult, and offhand references to a \"psycho killing spree\" and suicide; parents are shown drinking martinis most nights. Positive: the film is honestly about learning that good writing (and friendship) takes empathy, not just harsh judgment, and that words have consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harriet-the-spy","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q934004","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":544,"t":"Good Burger","y":"1997","la":"8+","ca":"10+","full":"Two goofy teens (Kenan Thompson and Kel Mitchell) save their fast-food job from a corporate rival in a movie built on cartoonish slapstick, sight gags, and reckless-driving humor. There's mild language (\"hell,\" \"ass\"), some sexual innuendo and brief played-for-laughs partial nudity, and jokes at the expense of mental illness and developmental disabilities that read as dated today. Positive: underneath the silliness, Ed and Dexter show loyalty and a real work ethic, and the film quietly values compassion and unconventional smarts over conformity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/good-burger","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2355815","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":545,"t":"The Rugrats Movie","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"Tommy and the gang wander into the woods after a new baby brother shakes up the family, leading to genuine cartoon peril: a plane crash, close calls with wolves and monkeys, and a scary tumble off a cliff. Humor leans heavily on potty jokes and gross-out bathroom gags. Positive: at its heart it's a sympathetic look at sibling jealousy and adjusting to a new baby, though the grown-ups and villains are played too broadly to work as real role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-rugrats-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q857211","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":546,"t":"Snow Day","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"A group of kids scheme to keep their snow day going by sabotaging the town's snowplow driver, while a teen tries to win over his high school crush. Concerns are mild: comic peril like pelting the principal with snowballs and confronting the plow driver, some playground language and potty humor, and a few teen kisses. No drinking, drugs, or smoking. Positive: a lighthearted, low-stakes family comedy about friendship and first crushes.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_Day_(2000_film)","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1296385","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":547,"t":"Rugrats in Paris: The Movie","y":"2000","la":"5+","ca":"4+","full":"Chuckie's dad travels to Paris for work and Chuckie sets out to find him a new wife, running afoul of the theme-park villain Coco LaBouche, who at one point has henchman Jean-Claude lock the babies in a warehouse. There's a giant mechanical-Reptar-versus-snail battle, gross-out gags (Phil and Lil eating bugs and boogers), and a brief underwear-visible moment when a dress rips. Positive: a genuinely heartfelt story about parents and children, with Chuckie growing braver and the franchise's first major Asian characters, Kira and Kimi, adding welcome representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rugrats-in-paris","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q663990","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":548,"t":"Jimmy Neutron: Boy Genius","y":"2001","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"Jimmy's inventions accidentally get every parent on Earth kidnapped by an alien fleet that threatens to feed them to a giant three-eyed monster, leading to plenty of cartoon explosions, crashes, and an air battle that's played for laughs rather than real menace. There's a steady stream of potty humor (\"sugar booger,\" \"holy cow pie\") and Jimmy and his friends get mocked for being short, chubby, or nerdy before winning their classmates over. Positive: intelligence and being different are treated as real strengths, and the film gently reassures kids that parents' rules come from love, not control.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jimmy-neutron-boy-genius","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1743785","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":549,"t":"Hey Arnold! The Movie","y":"2002","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Arnold and his friends race to stop a greedy developer from bulldozing their neighborhood, with cartoonish scuffles, a bear trap, and a dynamite explosion that leaves everyone unhurt, plus a brief bar scene with adults holding drinks and mild name-calling like \"Football head.\" Common Sense Media calls it a fairly thin, \"nothing new\" entry that doesn't add much to the TV show. Positive: Arnold's loyalty to his friends and community, and the film's earnest message about protecting historic neighborhoods and small businesses from being paved over.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hey-arnold-the-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Hey Arnold!: The Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":550,"t":"Clockstoppers","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A teen discovers a watch that lets him speed up his own molecules to seem to freeze time, and uses it to dodge corporate agents chasing the technology; the \"guns\" in the chases only fire ice bullets to knock people out of hyper-time, and nobody is seriously hurt. There's some romance, including a couple of kisses, and Francesca wears some revealing outfits. Positive: Common Sense Media highlights a multi-ethnic cast of heroes and villains and praises Francesca as strong, smart, and brave rather than a passive love interest.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/clockstoppers","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q533849","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":551,"t":"The Wild Thornberrys Movie","y":"2002","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Eliza's quest to save a cheetah cub from poachers takes the Thornberry family through genuinely suspenseful action, hanging from a helicopter ladder, swept down a rushing river, and cornered by menacing villains and wild animals, though nothing has lasting consequences. Positive: the Thornberry parents are held up as real role models, encouraging independence, respecting their kids' quirks, and staying honest and resourceful, and the film reinforces both why parents' rules exist and why protecting animals and the environment matters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wild-thornberrys-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1210797","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":552,"t":"Rugrats Go Wild","y":"2003","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Shipwrecked on a deserted island, the Rugrats crew meets the Wild Thornberrys in a crossover heavy on gross-out gags: birds pooping on heads, burping and flatulence jokes, a dog's mucus, and babies trying to eat bugs. There's a tiger scratch and a storm that sinks the family's boat, played for cartoon thrills rather than real danger. Positive: a message about cooperation and family, including one boy realizing his own dad is more heroic than his celebrity idol, though the grown-ups are broad parodies rather than models to imitate.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rugrats-go-wild","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3180765","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":553,"t":"The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie","y":"2004","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"SpongeBob and Patrick trek to Shell City to clear Mr. Krabs's name after King Neptune's crown goes missing, in a film that keeps the TV show's edgier streak: a barroom brawl involving a knife-wielding, visibly drunk pirate biker gang, plus crude humor, name-calling, and heavy junk-food tie-in marketing. Positive: Mindy shows real intelligence and compassion, and even though SpongeBob and Patrick are deliberately written as reckless and obnoxious, the film's underlying message is about loyalty, compassion, and being yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-spongebob-squarepants-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q579928","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":554,"t":"Barnyard","y":"2006","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Common Sense Media reviewed this film under its later re-release title, \"Barnyard: The Original Party Animals,\" calling it a rehash of tired clichés. The barnyard animals gamble, steal, joy-ride, and drink milk played as if it were alcohol, tossing around words like \"Oh, milk me!\" as stand-in profanity, and Otis's father is killed by coyotes after Otis sneaks off to a party against his warning. Common Sense Media's review lists no positive messages or role models here: the animals evade authority and act without accountability, and the human characters don't set a better example.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/barnyard-the-original-party-animals","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1129308","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":555,"t":"Firehouse Dog","y":"2007","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"A pampered Hollywood stunt dog gets lost and lands with a struggling fire crew and a grieving, troubled boy whose firefighter dad he doesn't get along with, leading into real emotional weight: fear of a parent dying, grief over a relative's death, intense fire scenes, and a boy trapped with an arsonist. Language stays mild (\"suck,\" \"crap,\" \"jerk\"). Positive: the story values helping others over fame, works through father-son communication problems honestly, and gives the crew's female firefighter real respect as a strong, capable role model.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/firehouse-dog","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2194964","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":556,"t":"The Last Airbender","y":"2010","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM calls this live-action adaptation \"boring -- but age-appropriate for young fans of the TV show.\" Fight scenes involving elemental bending aren't graphic, there's a gentle self-sacrificial death, and a brief kiss between two characters, with only mild insults instead of real profanity. Positive messages about teamwork and using power without causing harm run throughout, and supporting characters selflessly help the young Avatar accept his destiny.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-last-airbender","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q11593","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":557,"t":"Rango","y":"2011","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM flags this Western-styled animated film for guns and cultural clichés, recommending it for age 10+. There are Old West-style gunfights, a near-hanging, a menacing hawk, and a sadistic rattlesnake, plus insults like \"dumb Indian\" and mild swearing (\"damn,\" \"hell\"), along with some smoking and drinking among background characters. Positive messages balance the edge: Rango transforms from a fake tough guy into a genuine protector of his town, and Beans bravely stands up to a corrupt mayor to save her family's farm.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rango","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Western"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q275432","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":558,"t":"A Fairly Odd Movie: Grow Up!","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's tagline calls this series-inspired TV movie \"great fun for families,\" recommended for 7+. Cartoonish mishaps (falling out of trees, motorcycle wrecks) never cause real injury, there's a budding romance with flirting and one kiss, and a steady stream of potty humor (farting, burping, diarrhea jokes). Positive messages come through as adult Timmy learns that taking on responsibility has real rewards, and Tootie consistently models putting others first.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-fairly-odd-movie-grow-up-timmy-turner","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":61,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:A Fairly Odd Movie: Grow Up, Timmy Turner!","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":559,"t":"A Fairly Odd Christmas","y":"2012","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM describes this holiday sequel as \"worry-free holiday fun for kids,\" recommended for 7+. Expect mild peril like tumbles down snowy ravines, some potty-flavored jokes about bad breath, a single kiss, and language no stronger than \"butt.\" The positive takeaway is that good intentions still carry real consequences, and Timmy works to undo the mess he's made while characters talk through their feelings rather than fight.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-fairly-odd-christmas","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":63,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2157682","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":560,"t":"Fun Size","y":"2012","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM's tagline warns this is a \"predictable party flick... too edgy for star's [Victoria Justice's] younger fans,\" recommending age 13+. Underage teens drink and smoke at a house party, language includes \"s--t\" and \"bitch,\" there are passionate makeout scenes and implied hookups, and an amateur MMA fighter threatens people and kidnaps a little boy. On the positive side, the film values family bonds and looking past superficial qualities in others, with Roosevelt's two moms modeling honest communication.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fun-size","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q886187","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":561,"t":"A Fairly Odd Summer","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"This third live-action Fairly OddParents TV movie has no Common Sense Media review, so this is drawn from Wikipedia and fan-wiki plot summaries instead. Timmy and his friends head to Hawaii while Timmy is left guarding the Abra-Cadabrium, the universe's magic source, which the villains Foop and Crocker scheme to steal; expect the same brand of cartoonish slapstick, mild peril, and light romance between Timmy and Tootie as the earlier films in the series. The takeaway is a familiar one for the franchise: taking responsibility for what's been entrusted to you and working together with friends to fix a crisis.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Fairly_Odd_Summer","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","runtimeMinutes":66,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18342116","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":562,"t":"The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM's tagline calls it \"fun, goofy SpongeBob movie... as trippy as the show,\" recommending age 6+. There's exaggerated cartoon combat with guns and cannons, a moment where SpongeBob appears to sacrifice himself, some post-apocalyptic imagery, and mild insults like \"jerk\" and \"stupid.\" Positive messages celebrate teamwork and trust, with SpongeBob's relentless optimism, loyalty to his friends, and pride in his Krabby Patty craft carrying the film's heart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-spongebob-movie-sponge-out-of-water","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q7765993","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":563,"t":"Monster Trucks","y":"2016","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM sums this up as \"lots of action, thin story in boy-meets-creature adventure,\" recommended for age 7+. A private security team shoots at teens Tripp and Meredith during high-stakes chases, captive creatures appear starving, and there's destruction and a character who seems to fall to their death, alongside mild insults like \"loser.\" On the positive side, the film pushes environmental protection and the idea that \"there are things more important than profit and status,\" with Tripp and Meredith showing bravery, kindness, and smarts in protecting their creature friend.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/monster-trucks","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16939122","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":564,"t":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: Out of the Shadows","y":"2016","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM calls this sequel \"funnier than the first but still only OK,\" recommending age 11+. Expect plenty of long-range action violence (explosions, martial arts battles), one use of real profanity plus words like \"damn\" and \"jackass,\" and sexual innuendo including an outfit joke involving April. Positive messages emphasize that different perspectives and talents make a team stronger, with the Turtles acting bravely and selflessly to defend the city and Master Splinter serving as a steady father figure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-out-of-the-shadows","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: Out of the Shadows","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":565,"t":"Hey Arnold!: The Jungle Movie","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's tagline notes this \"long-awaited sequel sends Arnold on quest to find parents,\" recommending age 7+, and cautions that it's more mature than the animated style suggests. Arnold and his friends face river pirates, near-falls off cliffs, and jungle booby traps, with machetes in use and a villain responsible for minor characters' deaths, plus name-calling like \"jerk face\" from Helga. Positive messages highlight perseverance and community, as Arnold's friends stay loyal through danger and a whole town pulls together to help one of their own.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hey-arnold-the-jungle-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27052277","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":566,"t":"Wonder Park","y":"2019","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline warns this is an \"imaginative but intense adventure [that] deals with worry and fear,\" recommending age 8+. Hordes of weapon-wielding \"chimpanzombies\" attack in explosive battle scenes, June's mother has a serious unnamed illness that leaves her weak, and there's an ominous purple storm cloud along with intense roller-coaster sequences. Positive messages center on imagination and curiosity as essential parts of life, with June learning not to let fear stop her growth, alongside themes of love, loyalty, and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder-park","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28869533","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":567,"t":"Dora and the Lost City of Gold","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM calls this a \"quirky, aged-up adventure [with] positive messages,\" recommending age 8+. Dora and her friends are gassed, taken hostage at gunpoint, and face perils like quicksand and arrow attacks, plus one teen kiss and mild language (\"stupid,\" \"shut up\"). Positive messages run strong: Dora models determination, intelligence, kindness, teamwork, and perseverance, while the film portrays her supportive parents and Latino and Indigenous characters and cultures with respect.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dora-and-the-lost-city-of-gold","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q56064745","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":568,"t":"Invader Zim: Enter the Florpus","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline sums it up as \"alien, tween rivals match wits again over Earth's fate,\" recommending age 8+, and notes this is better suited to tweens than younger kids. Expect cartoon-style violence like laser blasts and explosions, name-calling (\"moron,\" \"loser\"), and gross-out humor involving bodily fluids, plus a villain in Zim who manipulates others while seeming sympathetic. On the positive side, Dib stays determined to save Earth even without support at first, and his father eventually steps up to fight alongside him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/invader-zim-enter-the-florpus","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Invader Zim: Enter the Florpus","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":569,"t":"The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM describes this as a \"silly quest [with] scary villains, message about courage,\" recommending age 7+. There's a gambling/casino sequence in an Atlantic-City-style setting, mild profanity (\"crappy,\" \"stupid\"), a menacing live-action villain wielding a flaming knife, and a brief moment of SpongeBob undressed. The positive core is that \"we all have courage inside of us,\" with friends reflecting on how SpongeBob's kindness and thoughtfulness have shaped their lives.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-spongebob-movie-sponge-on-the-run","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q61450772","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":570,"t":"Paw Patrol: The Movie","y":"2021","la":"5+","ca":"4+","full":"CSM's tagline calls this \"brave, talented pups save the day in pre-K adventure,\" recommending age 4+. Perilous moments include vehicles about to crash, buildings about to collapse, a scary weather event, a fire from fireworks, and dogs being abducted and locked up, though it's only slightly more intense than the TV series. Positive messages emphasize perseverance, teamwork, and learning from mistakes, with Ryder leading bravely, Chase overcoming self-doubt, and newcomer Liberty proving herself brave and capable.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paw-patrol-the-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Paw Patrol: The Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":571,"t":"Rumble","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM calls this \"charming WWE-produced wrestling comedy... a champ,\" recommending age 7+. Expect slapstick monster-wrestling action, including a folding chair comically thrown into the stands, over-the-top trash talk between competitors, and a background theme of loss from legendary figures who died years earlier, though it's handled lightly. Positive messages celebrate hard work and perseverance, with Winnie a confident teen aiming to coach in a male-dominated field, plus a diverse cast and a character whose love of dancing pushes back on wrestler stereotypes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rumble","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Rumble (2021 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":572,"t":"Rise of the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: The Movie","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline is direct: \"action-packed animated tale has lots of peril, violence,\" recommending age 8+. There's cartoon blood alongside guns, explosions, and stabbing, alien creatures that possess people, and character deaths across parallel timelines, plus mild exclamations like \"badass\" and \"oh God.\" Positive messages focus on hope, teamwork, and not giving up, with Leonardo growing as a leader from his mistakes and Raph pushing his brothers to collaborate to save their world.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rise-of-the-teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-the-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q111958728","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":573,"t":"Under the Boardwalk","y":"2023","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"CSM describes this as a \"cute musical Jersey crab adventure [with] mild peril, romance,\" recommending age 6+. A storm sweeps characters out to sea and destroys property, and there's flirting with a few brief kisses and hand-holding between young crab couples. Positive messages encourage looking past background and class to see someone's true self, with shy Armen finding courage to rescue his friends and Ramona proving braver than her sheltered upbringing suggested.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/under-the-boardwalk","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Mystery"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Under the Boardwalk (2023 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":574,"t":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: Mutant Mayhem","y":"2023","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM calls this \"clever, tween-friendly animated reboot [with] action violence,\" recommending age 8+. Expect infrequent profanity (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"heck\"), extensive car chases, hand-to-hand combat, and explosions, with occasional character deaths. Positive messages of teamwork, brotherhood, courage, and curiosity anchor the film, and the four turtles model empathy and bravery even when their impulsiveness gets them into trouble, while April is written as a strong, enterprising young woman.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-mutant-mayhem","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q110271518","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":575,"t":"Good Burger 2","y":"2023","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM's tagline warns of a \"silly sequel [with] crude language, cartoonish violence,\" recommending age 10+. There's crude humor and language (\"hell,\" \"jackass,\" \"punk-ass\"), bodily-function jokes, and frequent slapstick violence like car strikes, lightning hits, and near-miss machinery accidents played for laughs. Positive messages come through in themes that \"friends watch out for friends\" and \"greed doesn't pay,\" with Ed's steady kindness and the story's emphasis on forgiveness and genuine friendship over money.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/good-burger-2","source":"NICK","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Good Burger 2","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":576,"t":"Paw Patrol: The Mighty Movie","y":"2023","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline describes \"superpowered pups use teamwork, courage vs. evil scientist,\" recommending age 5+. A meteor crashes and destroys buildings including PAW Patrol Tower, a thief sets a scrapyard fire that traps characters, and one pup appears to nearly drown before being saved. Positive messages emphasize teamwork, courage, and learning from mistakes, with Ryder leading loyally and Skye discovering inner strength despite her small size, while Liberty finds purpose mentoring the newer pups.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paw-patrol-the-mighty-movie","source":"NICK","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Paw Patrol: The Mighty Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_EXTRA = [{"num":577,"t":"Free Willy 2: The Adventure Home","y":"1995","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Predictable sequel will thrill Willy fans; some peril.\" Concerns: kids are trapped on a sinking boat surrounded by flaming, oil-covered water during the climax, one boy falls from a rescue harness, and there's an awkward father-son talk after the dad hears rumors his tween has been kissing a girl he just met, plus one use of \"sucks.\" Positive: Jesse's devotion to Willy's welfare and marine conservation, his half-brother Elvis learning to drop his dishonesty and appreciate wildlife, and the blended family working through friction together with patience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/free-willy-2-the-adventure-home","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q584057","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":578,"t":"Free Willy","y":"1993","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A wayward boy befriends a moody killer whale.\" Jesse, a street-tough delinquent, breaks into an aquarium and bonds with Willy the orca; the plot hinges on insurance fraud that may go over younger heads, and there's one brief fistfight plus a single use of \"screw.\" The climax involves trespassing and vandalism as Jesse's crew races to free Willy from captivity. Positive: shows how friendship and empathy can turn around a troubled kid's life, with strong messages about animal welfare.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/free-willy","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q473628","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":579,"t":"Free Willy 3: The Rescue","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"For devoted -- and young -- Willy fans only.\" Jesse joins a whale-research expedition and discovers a fishing crew secretly hunting orcas, leading to threatened harpoonings and one barroom brawl, plus adult drunkenness in a few scenes. CSM notes the whalers aren't painted as cartoon villains but as men carrying on a hard-scrabble trade, even as the film pushes its conservation message hard. Positive: strong environmental and animal-welfare themes, though the slow, bedtime-story pacing best suits younger, dedicated fans.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/free-willy-3-the-rescue","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1032889","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":580,"t":"Free Willy: Escape from Pirate's Cove","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Mild orca-tainment with adorable Bindi Irwin.\" Set in South Africa, the story centers on a captive orca threatened with poisoning; there are minor scuffles, a father hospitalized after a fall, a reference to a deceased mother, and adult beer drinking, though the language stays as mild as \"sack of scum.\" Positive: young heroine Kirra shows determination and moral conviction rallying her community to free the whale, carrying on the franchise's anti-captivity message.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/free-willy-escape-from-pirates-cove","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2767704","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":581,"t":"Air Bud: Golden Receiver","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Cute but more intense than other Air Bud movies.\" Villains kidnap Buddy the golden retriever to force him into a circus act and keep other animals caged, football scenes get rough with no serious injuries, and mild slang like \"kick butt\" and \"fanny\" turns up alongside a widowed parent's new romance and a couple of kisses. Positive: models resilience and courage in coping with grief, and even shows the film's villains learning from their mistakes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/air-bud-golden-receiver","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q732071","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":582,"t":"Air Bud: World Pup","y":"2000","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Wholesome, endearing dog movie will delight grade schoolers.\" Buddy and Josh join the school soccer team, where a dog-napping subplot creates brief suspense (all puppies are safely returned), and the story folds in Josh's first crush plus a budding romance between Buddy and a new dog named Molly. Positive: CSM praises its unpreachy emphasis on teamwork, resisting peer pressure, and putting the team ahead of personal glory.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/air-bud-world-pup","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1988727","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":583,"t":"Air Bud: Seventh Inning Fetch","y":"2002","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Terrific dogs but painfully slow, pointless sequel.\" A girl is struck by a fastball while catching, a car chase ends with a crash into a pigsty, and a scheming scientist wants to kidnap the dogs, though CSM flags the weak writing and thin plot more than anything genuinely troubling. Positive: heroine Andrea models practice-makes-perfect resilience and good sportsmanship as she works hard to improve at baseball.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/air-bud-seventh-inning-fetch","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1988751","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":584,"t":"Air Bud: Spikes Back","y":"2003","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Cute dogs but dull plot; one of weaker Air Bud titles.\" Buddy is falsely accused of a museum jewel theft while escaped dogs cause chaos at a street fair, two bumbling thieves get thrown off a merry-go-round, and there's one notably gross vomit scene. Positive: Andrea earns her own money rather than asking her parents for it, modeling the value of saving and teamwork on the volleyball court.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/air-bud-spikes-back","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1988785","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":585,"t":"Spider-Man","y":"2002","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Fun superhero movie may be too intense for younger kids.\" Comic-book action gets intense: punching, strangling, and characters thrown through walls, plus a couple of graphic villain deaths. Mild profanity (one muffled harsher word, plus \"ass\" and \"damn\") and a couple of passionate kisses, including the famous upside-down rain kiss. Positive: Uncle Ben's \"with great power comes great responsibility\" anchors the whole film, and Peter Parker models empathy, self-control, and courage even when revenge tempts him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":121,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q484442","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":586,"t":"Spider-Man 2","y":"2004","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"A popcorn pleasure with heart, soul, and insight.\" Doc Ock's rampage brings cars hurled into buildings and people thrown from skyscrapers, including a genuinely upsetting scene where flying glass kills his wife. Language stays mild (just \"hell\"), and a heartbroken Harry is shown drinking whiskey alone. Positive: Peter's struggle to balance ordinary life with heroic duty models integrity and perseverance, and the film argues that people with real gifts shouldn't hide them just to fit in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-2","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":122,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q190145","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":587,"t":"Spider-Man 3","y":"2007","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Kids will be dazzled, but the story falls short of No. 2.\" Extended battles bring visible blood, disfigurement, and character deaths, and the symbiote suit turns Peter aggressive enough that he strikes people he loves. Harry drinks heavily more than once, and there's mild language (\"damn,\" \"ass\"). Positive: the film centers on redemption, showing that people can walk back self-destructive choices, and even Sandman is drawn with sympathy as a father trying to help his sick daughter rather than a pure villain.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-3","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":139,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Spider-Man 3","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":588,"t":"The Amazing Spider-Man","y":"2012","la":"11+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Action-packed series reboot has lots to offer Spidey fans.\" Comic-book violence runs heavy, with cars thrown off bridges, a bloody mugging victim, and a villain impaling a police officer with lizard claws. Language is occasional (\"ass,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\") and romance stays to flirting and a few kisses. Positive: \"with great power comes great responsibility\" drives the story again, and Gwen Stacy is written as smart and independent rather than a damsel, while Uncle Ben and Aunt May model steady, unconditional love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-amazing-spider-man","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Amazing Spider-Man (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":589,"t":"The Amazing Spider-Man 2","y":"2014","la":"11+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Uneven Spider-Man sequel mixes action, romance.\" Large-scale destruction dominates the climax, with cop cars piling up, gunfire, and Manhattan landmarks toppling, plus a major character death that hits hard for a franchise film. Language stays mild (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"oh my God\"), and romance is limited to kisses and declarations of love between Peter and Gwen. Positive: the film's throughline is holding onto hope and passing it to others, with Peter shown as a devoted nephew, boyfriend, and friend valued for his generous spirit rather than his powers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-amazing-spider-man-2","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":142,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4254026","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":590,"t":"Spider-Man: Homecoming","y":"2017","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Diverse, entertaining reboot has some language, violence.\" Peter takes real hits, including getting buried in rubble and a genuinely tense ferry-splitting-in-half sequence, alongside regular but not constant profanity (\"s--t,\" \"bastard,\" \"damn\"). A house party has teens holding red cups and there's a brief drug reference and one crude joke. Positive: \"with great power comes great responsibility\" remains the core lesson, and Peter's eager, if impulsive, drive to help his diverse Queens community models courage, perseverance, and friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-homecoming","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":133,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23010088","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":591,"t":"Spider-Man: Far From Home","y":"2019","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Fun, fast-paced sequel has some dark, dizzying violence.\" The Elemental battles bring mass destruction and dizzying, near-fall moments, plus mid-level language (\"bulls--t,\" a near-miss \"bitch,\" one partial harsher word). Peter appears shirtless a couple of times, and there's flirting and brief kissing with MJ. Positive: still grounded in \"with great power comes great responsibility,\" the film has Peter working through grief over Tony Stark's death while learning to balance personal wants against doing right by his community, with Ned's loyal friendship as a steady anchor.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-far-from-home","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27985819","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":592,"t":"Spider-Man: No Way Home","y":"2021","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Fun, funny, touching Spidey sequel has comic book violence.\" Multiverse battles bring characters slammed through walls and off high places, explosions, brief gunplay, and a major character's death that lands emotionally. Language includes an interrupted stronger word plus several uses of \"s--t\" and \"ass,\" and Aunt May catches a shirtless Peter with MJ. Positive: the film argues everyone deserves a second chance and that revenge doesn't actually fix anything, with Aunt May's compassion and Ned's loyalty reinforcing that great power still means great responsibility.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-no-way-home","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":148,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q68934496","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":593,"t":"Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse","y":"2023","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Spidey sequel is an action-packed delight; peril, violence.\" Large-scale multiverse battles bring explosions, close-quarters fights, and characters held captive, with mild language like \"crap,\" \"ass,\" and \"hell.\" Miles and Gwen share clear romantic tension without any physical follow-through, and adults are shown drinking wine at a party. Positive: the film leans hard on courage, empathy, and mentorship, using Miles's fight against a rigid multiversal bureaucracy to explore imposter syndrome and gatekeeping, while Peter B. Parker models growth as a patient, present father figure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":140,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q76448600","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":594,"t":"Hocus Pocus","y":"1993","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Rollicking Halloween fun has scares, gross-out moments,\" per CSM, which recommends this campy witch comedy for age 10+. The humor is broad, but there's a child's life-force drained early on, reanimated corpses, gallows imagery, gross-out bits like eating spiders, mild profanity (\"hell,\" \"damn\"), and innuendo built around virginity jokes; a couple of teens mention \"hash\" and cigarettes. Positive: Max, Dani, and Allison lean on teamwork and courage to outwit the witches, and the story shows bullying has real consequences.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hocus-pocus","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q431140","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":595,"t":"Now and Then","y":"1995","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM calls this \"'90s coming-of-age movie has some sex, profanity,\" recommending it for age 12+ as four 12-year-old friends spend a formative summer together. Concerns include girls watching boys skinny-dip, frank talk about puberty and bodies, kids trying cigarettes, adult smoking, and mild language (\"s--t,\" \"bitch,\" \"hell\"); a storm-drain near-drowning and news accounts of a murder and fatal crash add real weight. Positive: the film argues that facing life's curveballs beats hiding from them, and the four leads model loyalty and empathy that carries their friendship into adulthood.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/now-and-then","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"New Line Cinema","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q614966","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":596,"t":"The Mighty Ducks","y":"1992","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Classic kids' hockey movie has iffy humor, language,\" says CSM, which sets the age bar at 10+. Coach Gordon Bombay starts the film freshly arrested for drinking and driving, and the ragtag team deals with body-checking, a player knocked unconscious against a goalpost, swearing (\"bastards,\" \"hell\"), and boys ogling a swimsuit magazine. Positive: Bombay learns that playing fair and having fun matter more than winning at all costs, while Charlie models maturity and devotion to his single mom.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-mighty-ducks","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1536259","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":597,"t":"Beethoven","y":"1992","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's take: \"Lovable dog tale has violence, innuendo, slapstick,\" recommended for age 8+. Beyond the pratfalls, a veterinarian secretly runs a dog-fighting and animal-testing ring, there's a scary near-drowning, mild swearing (\"hell,\" \"damn\"), and a bedroom scene built around a husband-mistakes-the-dog-for-his-wife joke. Positive: the St. Bernard Beethoven is a steady, loyal presence who looks out for each of the kids, even as the human adults skew toward dimwits or villains.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/beethoven","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q754892","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":598,"t":"3 Ninjas","y":"1992","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"1990s martial arts comedy; slapstick violence, potty humor,\" per CSM, age 9+. Kid heroes Rocky, Colt, and Tum Tum fight off adult kidnappers with nunchaku, swords, and plenty of groin-kick gags, plus toilet humor and mild insults. Positive: their grandfather's training stresses that martial arts are for defense, never for attacking the weak, and the brothers show real teamwork and courage under pressure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/3-ninjas","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2363062","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":599,"t":"Jumanji","y":"1995","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM describes it as \"Effects-driven kids' adventure is charming but a bit grim,\" recommending age 10+. Once the cursed board game is opened, kids face stampeding animals, biting and stinging creatures, a hunter shooting at moving vehicles, and a boy getting beaten by bullies -- tense stuff even though language is limited to the occasional \"damn.\" Positive: Alan's arc is about breaking his own painful childhood by becoming the steady, encouraging adult he never had, and the film rewards facing fears instead of running from them.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jumanji","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q222939","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":600,"t":"Mrs. Doubtfire","y":"1993","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Heartfelt divorce movie has language, outdated gender roles,\" says CSM, landing the recommended age at 13+. Robin Williams's Daniel disguises himself as a British nanny after a bitter divorce, and the film carries real profanity (including one f-word, plus \"s--t,\" \"bastard,\" \"hell\"), dinner-table innuendo about a parent's sex life, and moderate drinking and smoking. Positive: the kids end up being, in CSM's words, \"the anchor that pulls the best out of the people around them,\" and the story argues families can hold together in unconventional shapes even after separation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mrs-doubtfire","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q483852","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":601,"t":"The Addams Family","y":"1991","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM sums it up as a \"dark comedy has sexual innuendo, bloody images.\" Knives, swords, and other medieval weapons are visible throughout as the family jousts with real blades, ties each other to a torture rack, and lets the kids play with bows and an electric chair; two intruders get hurled from a window into open coffins. Gomez and Morticia's marriage is played as intensely flirtatious, with frequent kissing, sexual innuendo, and jokes about using torture devices for pleasure, plus mild language like \"damn\" and \"hell.\" Positive: Gomez and Morticia model a devoted, unshakeable partnership, and the family's real message is unconditional acceptance of anyone who doesn't fit in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-addams-family-1991","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1210947","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":602,"t":"Hook","y":"1991","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"CSM calls it a \"clumsy mishmash of a comedy has violence, profanity.\" Captain Hook kidnaps Peter Banning's kids and threatens to kill them, sword fights leave pirates dead on screen, and Hook fatally stabs a Lost Boy and slashes Peter's arm into a bloody gash; language includes \"ass,\" \"bitch,\" and \"fornicate,\" and pirates pass a brothel where Hook flirts with a sex worker. Adults drink whiskey and wine, and Peter himself gulps whiskey and stumbles. Positive: Peter's arc is genuinely redemptive, as an absent, workaholic father rediscovers play and puts his kids first, and the Lost Boys show what teamwork looks like even when it's chaotic.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hook","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q646389","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":603,"t":"Heavyweights","y":"1995","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Early Judd Apatow film makes fat camp mischievous and fun.\" A cruel new camp owner locks a struggling camper inside an electric-fenced cage as punishment and a father throws a punch, there's mild language like \"damn\" and \"kick his ass,\" and a bit of teen kissing at a dance. Positive: CSM flags real mixed messages here, some scenes push self-acceptance while others lean on cruelty and fat jokes toward the campers, so it's worth talking through with kids rather than taking at face value.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/heavyweights","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q239413","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":604,"t":"Mouse Hunt","y":"1997","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Clever slapstick with cartoonish violence, profanity,\" per CSM. Two brothers wage all-out war on a single mouse using a shotgun, a nail gun, and eventually a house-leveling gas explosion, all played for over-the-top comedy; there's scatological gags, including the mouse defecating on an exterminator, lingerie-related innuendo, and language like \"bastard\" and \"son of a bitch.\" Positive: under all the cartoon mayhem, the story turns on the two feuding brothers reconciling and choosing family loyalty over their inheritance squabble.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mouse-hunt","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Mouse Hunt","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":605,"t":"The Little Rascals","y":"1994","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Madcap, mischievous Our Gang remake has potty humor.\" The He-Man Woman Haters Club leans hard on \"girls are gross\" jokes and some anti-gay-coded humor, a bully threatens the gang, a Doberman knocks Alfalfa flat, and the clubhouse catches fire; there's potty humor and a few double entendres kids might pick up, like \"bite me.\" Positive: CSM notes the film offers little in the way of role models, though the racially integrated cast and the gang's loyalty to one another soften some of the dated attitudes carried over from the original.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-little-rascals-1994","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q644634","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":606,"t":"The Parent Trap","y":"1998","la":"6+","ca":"7+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Delightful, family-friendly remake has smoking, drinking.\" One twin gets her ears pierced by her sister in a wincing DIY scene, a woman screams and tumbles into a lake over a small lizard, and there's real substance use: an anxious character smokes and drinks heavily, a vineyard-owning parent pours wine, and an 11-year-old is given a taste of wine at dinner. Positive: both divorced parents are shown as caring and devoted despite their split, and the twins are clever and resourceful, though CSM cautions that their scheming to reunite Mom and Dad plays more charming on screen than it would be if kids tried it themselves.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-parent-trap","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q729782","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":838,"t":"The Sheep Detectives","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Cozy family mystery with a murder at its center, so it is warmer than a crime premise sounds but still not for the youngest viewers. A beloved shepherd is found dead, characters grieve, a body is partly shown, and there are tense animal fights, aggressive dogs, talk of poison, a scary building, a crash aftermath, and adults shown with wine or whiskey. Language is infrequent but includes words like damn, crap, idiot, stupid, and shut up. Positive: Lily and the flock model courage, teamwork, perseverance, inclusion, and the idea that remembering loved ones keeps them close.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-sheep-detectives","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Amazon MGM Studios","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q126405648","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":839,"t":"Moana","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This live-action remake sticks close to the 2016 original's story, though the peril hits harder without animation's softening touch: a fiery lava monster, a violent storm at sea, coconut-shell pirates with weapons, and a glowing crab all return, plus a grandparent's death and return as a guiding spirit. Mild language includes \"son of a beach,\" \"sucks,\" \"dumb,\" and \"butt.\" Positive: Moana remains a strong, capable leader driven by her calling rather than romance, and Maui grows from selfishness into real mentorship; the film leans into courage, teamwork, communication, and perseverance, with authentic Pacific Islander casting throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/moana-2026","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q118996994","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":840,"t":"Star Wars Episode V: The Empire Strikes Back","y":"1980","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"This first sequel darkens the saga's tone with laser battles, a Force-choking villain, a severed limb, and an off-screen torture scene, though profanity stays minimal. It still champions loyalty, courage, and sacrifice for others, and gives kids a tough, capable heroine in Leia.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-v-the-empire-strikes-back","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Empire Strikes Back","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":841,"t":"Star Wars Episode VI: Return of the Jedi","y":"1983","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"The original trilogy's finale mixes lightsaber duels and a monster-pit sequence with a slow strangulation scene and a scantily-clad Leia in Jabba's palace. Themes of friendship and resisting a corrupt empire carry through, and Luke's self-control alongside Leia's boldness give kids strong examples to root for.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-vi-the-return-of-the-jedi","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":132,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Return of the Jedi","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":842,"t":"Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace","y":"1999","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"The first prequel keeps its violence mostly bloodless but includes a major character sliced apart by lightsaber, a tense podrace, and a heavy scene where a young boy is separated from his mother. It also explores how power can corrupt and how calm judgment matters, with Queen Amidala revealed as sharp and courageous underneath a passive exterior.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-i-the-phantom-menace","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: Episode I – The Phantom Menace","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":843,"t":"Star Wars Episode II: Attack of the Clones","y":"2002","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"This chapter ramps up battle violence with amputations, a poison-dart death, and a large arena fight, plus a bar scene where a dangerous offer of 'death sticks' is turned down. It keeps a clear line between right and wrong while showing a beloved hero start sliding toward darkness, alongside a gentle, mostly chaste romance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-ii-attack-of-the-clones","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":142,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: Episode II – Attack of the Clones","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":844,"t":"Star Wars Episode III: Revenge of the Sith","y":"2005","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"The darkest prequel includes an off-screen massacre of children, a beheading, and a fiery amputation, making it the most intense entry for younger viewers. At its core it's a cautionary tale about anger and jealousy curdling into evil, with secondary characters modeling loyalty and integrity even as the hero falls.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-iii-revenge-of-the-sith","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":140,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: Episode III – Revenge of the Sith","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":845,"t":"Star Wars Episode VII: The Force Awakens","y":"2015","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"This sequel-trilogy opener brings space battles, a torture scene, and an unsettling masked villain, plus a brief cantina moment implying drinking, though language stays mild. It leans into found-family themes and standing up for your values, introducing Rey and Finn as courageous, empathetic leads in a notably diverse cast.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-vii-the-force-awakens","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":138,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: The Force Awakens","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":846,"t":"Star Wars Episode VIII: The Last Jedi","y":"2017","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Expect large-scale space combat, a bloodless in-half lightsaber moment, mild swearing like 'hell' and 'ass,' and a casino scene with drinks. The film keeps pushing courage, teamwork, and doing right even when it's hard, with several women holding key leadership roles across a diverse Resistance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-viii-the-last-jedi","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":152,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: The Last Jedi","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":847,"t":"Star Wars Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker","y":"2019","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"The saga's closer brings its heaviest action yet, including a beheading, an execution, and unsettling creature encounters, plus mild language and a drug-adjacent nickname for one character. It closes on messages of hope and redemption and the idea that people aren't fixed as purely good or bad, with Rey, Finn, and Poe modeling loyalty and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-episode-ix-the-rise-of-skywalker","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":141,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":848,"t":"Rogue One: A Star Wars Story","y":"2016","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This standalone war story is grimmer than most Star Wars films, with a high body count, civilians and a child in danger, and a mind-invasion torture sequence. It's built around sacrifice for a cause and doing right at great cost, headlined by Jyn Erso as a tough, capable lead in the franchise's most diverse cast yet.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","War"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":133,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19590955","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":849,"t":"Solo: A Star Wars Story","y":"2018","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A younger Han Solo's origin story brings large battles, executions, a creature-confinement scare, pub drinking, and a bit more kissing than usual for this franchise, though language stays mild. It highlights teamwork and choosing to do right, while raising themes of equal treatment for droids and other beings in a cast with plenty of representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/solo-a-star-wars-story","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":135,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27038847","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":850,"t":"Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu","y":"2026","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This film brings blaster fights, scary monster encounters, and a poisonous bite, plus a cantina scene with light drinking and very mild language. Din Djarin's devotion to protecting Grogu underscores loyalty, responsibility, and found family, with heavy toy and merchandise tie-ins as the main non-content caveat.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-the-mandalorian-and-grogu","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":132,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Mandalorian and Grogu","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":851,"t":"D2: The Mighty Ducks","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This hockey sequel has some rough, dirty on-ice hits that leave players hurt, plus very mild flirting and a couple of chaste kisses, with no swearing or substance use. Coach Bombay's arc about getting distracted by fame before refocusing on his players shows real growth, and the team wins through teamwork and knowing their own strengths.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/d2-the-mighty-ducks","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q598549","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":852,"t":"D3: The Mighty Ducks","y":"1996","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"The trilogy closer has some rink roughhousing, a bit of comedic bullying, mild words like 'hell' and 'stupid,' and light teen romance. It pushes solid lessons about hard work, humility, and loyalty, including a storyline where kids push back on a demeaning team name, alongside a boys-and-girls-together roster.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/d3-the-mighty-ducks","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q610421","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":853,"t":"Yellow Submarine","y":"1968","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This psychedelic Beatles feature keeps peril cartoonish and harmless, such as arrows that don't actually hurt anyone, though a group of villains smoke cigars and some songs carry rumored, never-depicted drug references. Otherwise it's a joyful, nonviolent celebration of creativity and wit, built entirely around a message of love overcoming division.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/yellow-submarine","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1131791","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":854,"t":"Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets","y":"2002","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Harry's second year at Hogwarts brings genuinely scary content -- giant spiders, a deadly basilisk, and a house-elf who hurts himself as punishment -- plus one use of a wizarding slur. It's balanced by strong themes of friendship, courage, and teamwork, with Hermione's cleverness driving the plot.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-chamber-of-secrets","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":161,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":855,"t":"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban","y":"2004","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Alfonso Cuaron's moodier take introduces the soul-sucking Dementors along with a werewolf chase and an injured hippogriff, plus mild slang like \"bloody\" and \"damn.\" Kids visit a pub and drink butterbeer. Positive throughlines include facing fear, loyalty, and compassion for misunderstood characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-prisoner-of-azkaban","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":141,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":856,"t":"Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire","y":"2005","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"The Triwizard Tournament brings dragon attacks, an underwater rescue, and a genuinely upsetting on-screen death of a classmate, alongside first stirrings of teen romance and mild cursing. The series still centers on doing right under pressure, with Harry staying humble despite his sudden fame.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-goblet-of-fire","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":151,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q102225","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":857,"t":"Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix","y":"2007","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"Dolores Umbridge's cruel discipline, visions of Voldemort and the Death Eaters, and a major character's death make this a heavier entry, though the violence mostly stays bloodless. Students forming a secret defense club highlight courage and teamwork, and the story frames personal choices, not fate, as what defines someone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-order-of-the-phoenix","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":133,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q102235","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":858,"t":"Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince","y":"2009","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"A beloved character is killed by a curse, and other scenes include poisoning, a life-threatening seizure, and Death Eaters setting fires, while teens drink butterbeer, mead, and wine at parties. Romantic subplots multiply alongside continued themes of loyalty and self-sacrifice, with Dumbledore held up as a selfless mentor.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-half-blood-prince","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":147,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q161687","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":859,"t":"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1","y":"2010","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"The franchise's darkest chapter yet has its highest body count, including a disturbing snake-from-corpse moment and a torture scene, alongside mild profanity. It stresses that heroism takes teamwork and that ancestry shouldn't determine worth, with ordinary people shown capable of real courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-deathly-hallows-part-1","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":146,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":860,"t":"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 2","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"The trilogy's climactic battle at Hogwarts brings extensive fighting, several major character deaths, and one gory creature-attack moment, plus a single strong swear word. It closes the series on themes of selflessness, loyal friendship, and unexpected bravery from side characters like Neville.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-potter-and-the-deathly-hallows-part-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":130,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q232009","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":861,"t":"Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them","y":"2016","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"Set in 1920s New York, this more adult-leaning entry includes magical creature attacks, a belt-whipping that leaves visible marks, mild language, and a speakeasy scene implying alcohol. Newt Scamander models curiosity and compassion toward creatures others fear, and the film promotes understanding differences instead of assuming danger.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-beasts-and-where-to-find-them","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":133,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18199330","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":862,"t":"Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald","y":"2018","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This sequel turns darker still, with magical battles, drownings, and a villain using deadly curses in an execution-style manner, alongside minimal profanity. It warns viewers to be wary of charismatic figures with hidden motives, while Newt and his allies model loyalty, hard work, and courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-beasts-the-crimes-of-grindelwald","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18199331","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":863,"t":"A Charlie Brown Christmas","y":"1965","la":"3+","ca":"3+","full":"This gentle holiday classic includes some name-calling of Charlie Brown by his friends and leans heavily into the Christian nativity story via Linus's reading. Ultimately the Peanuts gang rallies around Charlie Brown, delivering a message about Christmas mattering more for love and generosity than presents or commercialism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-charlie-brown-christmas","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"CBS","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":25,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1393337","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":864,"t":"How the Grinch Stole Christmas","y":"1966","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"Boris Karloff narrates this brief, largely gentle special whose roughest moment is the Grinch's dog being mistreated while pulling the overloaded sleigh. The story's core lesson -- that people can change and that the holiday is about love rather than gifts -- makes it a low-concern pick even for very young kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dr-seuss-how-the-grinch-stole-christmas","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":24,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:How the Grinch Stole Christmas! (TV special)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":865,"t":"The Great Muppet Caper","y":"1981","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"This Muppet caper-comedy mixes slapstick tumbles, a bit of adult-aimed innuendo, and a passing curse word in a song lyric, plus a champagne toast. Kermit, Fozzie, and Gonzo solve the mystery through teamwork, and the film is notably body-positive toward Miss Piggy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-great-muppet-caper","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1218526","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":866,"t":"A Christmas Story","y":"1983","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Beneath its nostalgic tone, this comedy includes real bullying with a bloody-nosed fight, a frightening department-store Santa, several outdated and racially insensitive jokes, and language strong enough that a boy gets his mouth washed out with soap. It still lands on themes of self-control and family sticking together through a chaotic, imperfect holiday.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-christmas-story","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q556933","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":867,"t":"Nanny McPhee","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Before order is restored, the unruly Brown children pull cartoonish pranks on a string of nannies, and the film includes potty humor, a mortuary scene with visible corpses, and one instance of British profanity. Nanny McPhee ultimately teaches the kids respect, cooperation, and care for one another through natural consequences rather than punishment.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/nanny-mcphee","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q523249","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":868,"t":"Stuart Little 2","y":"2002","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This sequel has mild cartoon action -- chases, falls, and a menacing falcon -- plus a villain who meets a rough end, but nothing graphic; language is limited to light potty humor. The story rewards honesty and resilience, and Stuart's parents model warmth and trust throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/stuart-little-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1070554","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":869,"t":"Space Jam","y":"1996","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This basketball comedy blends live action and Looney Tunes animation with nonstop slapstick violence (gunfire, explosions, falls), a few mild swears, a cigar-smoking villain, and heavy product placement, plus a joke that pokes fun at an overweight character. A flashback to a young Michael Jordan highlights hard work and dedication, and the team wins through cooperation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/space-jam","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q207659","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":870,"t":"The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe","y":"2005","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This fantasy adaptation carries battle sequences and a genuinely frightening White Witch that could unsettle younger or sensitive kids. The story carries overt religious allegory about good triumphing over evil, which families may want to discuss together. There's no language, drug use, or sexual content to worry about.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-chronicles-of-narnia-the-lion-the-witch-the-wardrobe","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":143,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q485803","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":872,"t":"Willow","y":"1988","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"This Lucasfilm-produced fantasy adventure has sword fights, scary villains, a two-headed monster, and a tavern brawl with drunken behavior, plus some crude innuendo and mild slurs. Despite the peril, the film champions courage, loyalty, and sacrifice, and gives its short-statured hero a fully realized, non-tokenized starring role.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/willow","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q515931","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":874,"t":"The Lego Ninjago Movie","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This entry has cartoonish martial-arts action (including a limb loss played for laughs) and virtually no bad language. It leans on messages of self-acceptance, forgiveness, and reconciling with an estranged parent, alongside a diverse voice cast, though it's even more overtly a marketing vehicle for the toy line.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lego-ninjago-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22131901","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":875,"t":"The Lego Movie 2: The Second Part","y":"2019","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This sequel has Mad-Max-style action, a monstrous Unikitty transformation, and mild words like 'jerk,' plus a wink to an adult movie franchise. Its throughline is about accepting friends as they are and staying loyal under pressure, modeled by an unfailingly upbeat Emmet.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lego-movie-2-the-second-part","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23796643","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":876,"t":"Who Framed Roger Rabbit","y":"1988","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This noir hybrid's cartoon-violence gags get dark (an acid-like substance that erases characters), the detective hero is a heavy daytime drinker, Jessica Rabbit is drawn very provocatively, and the human characters swear more than expected for a PG movie. Its core message -- not to prejudge people, or toons, by appearances -- lands well for older kids who can handle the tone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/who-framed-roger-rabbit","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q379873","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":878,"t":"The Secret of NIMH","y":"1982","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This Don Bluth-directed animated film swings dark for a G-era rating -- a rat dies in a sword duel, animals are shown being experimented on and injected, and a giant spider appears before being crushed. It ultimately celebrates a mother's courage and teamwork in protecting her family, but younger kids may find the imagery genuinely creepy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-secret-of-nimh","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q174374","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":879,"t":"The Transformers: The Movie","y":"1986","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This animated sci-fi actioner has near-constant robot destruction, some incidental swearing, and the death of several likable characters -- unusually dark for what's essentially an extended toy commercial. It still promotes courage, loyalty, and self-belief among the Autobots, though the story leans on the idea that war is unavoidable.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-transformers-the-movie-1986","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Action","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"De Laurentiis Entertainment Group","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q250378","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":881,"t":"Jurassic Park","y":"1993","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Spielberg's original pits terrifyingly lifelike dinosaurs against a small group of park visitors, with several people mauled or eaten and one gruesome severed-limb moment. There's occasional strong language, background smoking and drinking, and sustained danger for two child characters. On the upside, it rewards teamwork, quick thinking, and courage, and its female leads come across as sharp, capable problem-solvers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-park","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Jurassic Park (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":882,"t":"The Lost World: Jurassic Park","y":"1997","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This sequel turns up the gore, including one especially brutal death, as dinosaurs defending their young go on the attack, first on a remote island and then loose in Los Angeles. Expect scattered strong language and light drinking, plus a subplot involving cruelty to a baby dinosaur. It leans into a message about the fallout of human meddling with nature, and its female scientist proves just as resourceful as the men around her.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lost-world-jurassic-park","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q200873","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":883,"t":"Jurassic Park III","y":"2001","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"A shorter, faster-paced entry that keeps its characters in near-constant danger from a new, more aggressive dinosaur, with a few side characters killed off along the way. Content is fairly mild otherwise: a little language, adults drinking at a bar, and a brief glimpse of a woman in her underwear. A child character shows real grit under pressure, and the story quietly warns against pushing too far into nature's territory.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-park-iii","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1102220","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":884,"t":"Jurassic World","y":"2015","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"The franchise reboot amps up the scale and body count, as a genetically engineered super-predator escapes a fully operational theme park and kills numerous people over the course of the film. There's moderate swearing, heavy tension, and kids placed in real danger, plus a lot of visible brand tie-ins. It still lands on themes of courage, compassion, and teamwork, and reminds viewers that nature can't simply be engineered into submission.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-world","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3512046","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":885,"t":"Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom","y":"2018","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"Set on an erupting volcanic island, this sequel delivers relentless peril and a genuinely frightening stretch where an engineered dinosaur specifically hunts a young girl; deaths include burning, trampling, and worse. Language stays fairly light and substance use is minimal, though product placement is everywhere. It keeps the series' running theme that science shouldn't outrun ethics, with its leads showing real bravery and compassion for the animals in their care.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-world-fallen-kingdom","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":128,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q21877685","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":886,"t":"Jurassic World Dominion","y":"2022","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"The trilogy-closer mixes dinosaur attacks with human-on-human fights and a swarm of oversized, kid-terrorizing locusts, and it lands a handful of mild profanities along the way. Children are put in danger more than once, though the returning original trio (Sattler, Grant, Malcolm) anchor the film's push for integrity over corporate profit. Overall it favors teamwork and doing the right thing, even as the action stays intense.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-world-dominion","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":146,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q55178974","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":887,"t":"Jurassic World Rebirth","y":"2025","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"A mercenary crew hunting dinosaur DNA runs into near-constant attacks, with some fairly graphic imagery (a severed arm, skeletal remains) and a couple of gut-punch fake-out scares involving kids. There's infrequent strong language, some drinking, and one throwaway joke about marijuana made to a tween. Its emotional core is redemption -- self-interested characters learn to act selflessly -- alongside themes of teamwork and putting people ahead of profit.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jurassic-world-rebirth","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Jurassic World Rebirth","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":888,"t":"The Hobbit","y":"1977","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This Rankin/Bass animated TV special condenses Tolkien's story into a family-friendly adventure with sword fights, a fire-breathing dragon, giant spiders, and menacing trolls; a few dead bodies are shown at a distance after the climactic battle. Pipe-smoking is a running visual gag, and the wood-elves get tipsy on wine at one point, but there's no language or romance to worry about. It's ultimately a gentle lesson in how an unassuming, comfort-loving hero can grow into someone genuinely brave, and how greed and warfare accomplish little.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-hobbit-1977","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Rankin/Bass Productions","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q74229","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":889,"t":"The End of Oak Street","y":"2026","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"A 1980s suburban cul-de-sac gets yanked into dinosaur-infested territory in this sci-fi thriller, and it earns its higher age rating with bloody corpses, severed body parts, and creatures that snatch and devour people on camera. There's a bit of strong language and an adult secretly drinking to cope with the crisis. Still, the story centers a struggling couple who ultimately put their kids' safety first, framing courage as something that can look like calm, positive thinking rather than physical heroics.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-end-of-oak-street","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Horror"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q124804916","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":891,"t":"The Railway Children","y":"1970","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Three siblings relocate to the countryside after their father mysteriously vanishes, and they end up risking their own safety to stop a train wreck. It's a gentle period piece with only mild trouble spots -- a slap, a bloody broken leg, a doctor's hip flask, and a railway worker having a beer. The children come across as responsible, kind, and resourceful, and the story rewards good manners and looking out for others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-railway-children","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"EMI Films","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q211525","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":892,"t":"The Water Horse: Legend of the Deep","y":"2007","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A lonely Scottish boy hatches a mysterious egg into a fast-growing lake creature and has to keep it hidden from soldiers who eventually shoot at and bombard it with artillery; a family dog is also killed off-screen. There's some social drinking and smoking at a wartime banquet and pub, plus mild language, but nothing stronger. The soldiers are cast as bullies against the children's compassion for their misunderstood pet, and the film leans on themes of loyalty and quiet cooperation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-water-horse-legend-of-the-deep","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Water Horse: Legend of the Deep","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":894,"t":"Nacho Libre","y":"2006","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"A monastery cook moonlights as a masked wrestler to earn money for the orphans in his care, with plenty of slapstick ring violence, food gags, and heavy bathroom humor along the way. Mild profanity and a broadly played accent are present, but the story is ultimately driven by generosity and helping people in need.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/nacho-libre","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q909767","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":895,"t":"Tron","y":"1982","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A programmer gets pulled inside a computer world where he must battle a corrupt system in stylized, video-game-style action, including one unsettling scene with a glowing skeleton. Mild language and vague references to past relationships appear, but the story functions as a light allegory about standing up to corruption, with a scientist heroine among the leads.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tron","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Action"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Tron","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":896,"t":"Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade","y":"1989","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Indy and his estranged father race Nazis across Europe to find the Holy Grail, with frequent hand-to-hand fighting, gunplay, and a couple of gruesome side-character deaths. There's mild language and some suggestive banter, but the film centers on courage, cleverness, and repairing a strained father-son bond, despite some dated ethnic stereotyping in its depiction of the region.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/indiana-jones-and-the-last-crusade","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":122,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q185658","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":897,"t":"Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom","y":"1984","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Indy, a nightclub singer, and a young sidekick square off against a murderous cult, including a notoriously intense ritual sacrifice scene and other nightmare-inducing imagery. There's whipping, hand-to-hand combat, and gross-out food moments, alongside mild profanity, but the film also rewards courage, loyalty, and teamwork between its unlikely trio, despite some dated depictions of Indian and Asian characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/indiana-jones-and-the-temple-of-doom","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":117,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":898,"t":"Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull","y":"2008","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Now facing Soviet agents in the 1950s, Indy chases a mysterious crystal skull through jungle traps, a killer-ant attack, and an atomic-test sequence that could unsettle younger viewers. Fights involve guns, swords, and some blood, with mild language throughout, but the film keeps its focus on ingenuity, loyalty, and protecting history from those who'd exploit it.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/indiana-jones-and-the-kingdom-of-the-crystal-skull","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q182373","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":899,"t":"Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny","y":"2023","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"In his final outing, an aging Indy chases a time-bending artifact while enemies shoot bystanders abruptly and sometimes execution-style, making this entry noticeably darker than earlier films. Frequent drinking and smoking appear alongside mild language, but the story leans heavily on themes of found family and people who show up for one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/indiana-jones-and-the-dial-of-destiny","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":154,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24278982","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":901,"t":"Labyrinth","y":"1986","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A teenage girl must navigate a goblin king's magical maze to rescue her baby brother, encountering puppet creatures, sword fights, and a villain whose fixation on her has an uncomfortable undertone for adult viewers to notice. There's no real gore and only mild exclamations for language, and the story rewards Sarah's cleverness, courage, and willingness to work with unlikely allies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/labyrinth","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Labyrinth (1986 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":902,"t":"Ghostbusters","y":"1984","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"A trio of scientists-turned-paranormal-exterminators battle decomposing ghosts and a possessed woman while blasting energy weapons around New York. Swearing is fairly frequent and one lead's persistent pursuit of a woman who keeps turning him down plays as comedy in a way that hasn't aged well, though the film's central idea of scientists saving the day through teamwork and curiosity still lands.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ghostbusters","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q108745","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":903,"t":"Ghostbusters II","y":"1989","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The team reunites to stop a river of slime and demonic imagery, including a startling shot of severed heads and some real peril involving a baby near traffic and a high ledge. Language stays infrequent and mild, and while the characters are too cartoonish to be true role models, the story's message about kindness overcoming negativity comes through as goofy family entertainment.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ghostbusters-ii","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q492214","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":904,"t":"The Karate Kid Part II","y":"1986","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Daniel and Mr. Miyagi travel to Okinawa, where old rivalries reignite into severe karate beatings and threatening confrontations, plus some gambling on a fight's outcome. The film preaches mercy and forgiveness even as its climax resolves through combat, but the cross-cultural mentorship between Daniel and Miyagi still offers genuinely touching moments.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-karate-kid-part-ii","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1418251","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":905,"t":"The Karate Kid Part III","y":"1989","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"A revenge-driven new villain manipulates Daniel's training in this weaker sequel, which includes a bloody-knuckled fight scene, a tense cliffside confrontation, and a racial slur aimed at an Asian character. The antagonist smokes and drinks, and mild profanity recurs throughout, but Mr. Miyagi still models integrity, teaching that self-belief and hard work outlast brute strength and grudges.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-karate-kid-part-iii","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Action"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1586077","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":906,"t":"Gremlins","y":"1984","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This horror-comedy gets surprisingly graphic for a PG-era movie, with a blender death, a shooting, an explosion, and a character thrown from a window, plus scattered swearing and references to suicide. Gremlins and humans alike are shown smoking and drinking, and some transformation and jump-scare sequences are genuinely unsettling for younger kids. The teen leads show real courage and resourcefulness fighting back against the chaos, and the story doubles as a cautionary tale about greed and messing with things you don't understand.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/gremlins","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Horror"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Gremlins","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":907,"t":"Gremlins 2: The New Batch","y":"1990","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"The sequel leans hard into slapstick, with gremlins meeting cartoonish but graphic ends (including one shredded on-screen) and plenty of drinking and smoking played for laughs. Language stays mild, limited mostly to \"hell,\" and the tone is more goofy satire of corporate greed and pop culture than genuine horror. There's little real substance or role-modeling here beyond Gizmo's small moments of heroism, so it's best treated as chaotic fun rather than a movie with a lesson.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/gremlins-2-the-new-batch","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Horror"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Gremlins 2: The New Batch","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":908,"t":"The Santa Clause 2","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A gentle family comedy with a bit of slapstick and some bathroom humor, including a robot Santa double whose rear end gets an unnecessary close-up and who acts tipsy after drinking cocoa. There's noticeable brand placement for fast food and candy, and the elf world leans on old-fashioned gender roles. It does touch on the real meaning of Christmas, though the film ultimately cares more about presents than heart, even with some capable female characters in the mix.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-santa-clause-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1469426","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":909,"t":"The Santa Clause 3: The Escape Clause","y":"2006","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This lighter, sillier entry keeps things G-rated, with only mild slapstick like a shovel to the face or a pratfall off a roof for danger. There's no bad language or scary content to speak of. The story sets up a clear contrast between Scott's genuine holiday spirit and Jack Frost's selfish scheme to steal Christmas for himself, giving families an easy opening to talk about generosity versus greed.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-santa-clause-3-the-escape-clause","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1325828","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":910,"t":"Turner & Hooch","y":"1989","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This buddy-cop comedy opens with a stabbing and includes a dog being shot and dying on screen, along with mild cursing and a drug-smuggling subplot, so it's heavier than its goofy dog-movie premise suggests. Hooch himself drinks beer for laughs in a couple of scenes. Underneath the mess and noise, the film rewards Turner's persistence and integrity, offering a message about loyalty and following through even when a case, or a partnership, seems hopeless.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/turner-hooch","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1537568","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":911,"t":"Flash Gordon","y":"1980","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This campy space opera stages its violence in an unrealistic, comic-book way, ray-gun blasts, impalements, and bodies dissolving, but a few images (like an eye being gouged from a cyborg) are still fairly gruesome for a PG movie. Swearing is minor, an alien drink and a passing pill reference cover substance use, and skimpy costumes plus some ogling account for the mild sexual content. Underneath the spectacle, the story champions the idea that ordinary courage can unite the oppressed against a tyrant, even if the characters themselves stay pretty broad and archetypal.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flash-gordon-1980","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1427252","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":912,"t":"The Muppets Take Manhattan","y":"1984","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A mostly gentle backstage comedy where the roughest moments are Kermit getting hit by a car (leading to amnesia) and Miss Piggy fending off a mugger and some construction-worker leering, plus a bit of cigarette smoking in the background. The jokes work on two levels, broad slapstick for kids and knowing references for adults, so younger viewers won't catch everything but won't be bothered by it either. The heart of the film is Kermit and company's determination to make it on Broadway despite repeated rejection, modeling persistence and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-muppets-take-manhattan","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1214915","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":913,"t":"Harry and the Hendersons","y":"1987","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The biggest surprise for parents here is the language, several instances of stronger swearing than you'd expect from a family Bigfoot comedy, while the action itself stays cartoonish with no blood despite guns and hunting scenes. Some of the hunter sequences may be intense for younger or more sensitive kids. The film's real strength is its message of empathy: the Henderson father starts out as a hunter and, with his family's help, comes to protect Harry instead of harming him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/harry-and-the-hendersons","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Harry and the Hendersons","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":914,"t":"Popeye","y":"1980","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Robert Altman's odd, musical take on the comic strip keeps its fights with Bluto and other villains cartoonish and harmless, with only a few mild curse words scattered through the dialogue. There's nothing to flag around scares, substances, or sexual content. It's a quirky, love-it-or-hate-it film, but Popeye's willingness to take in an abandoned baby and look out for his community comes through as a quiet, caring throughline.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/popeye","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q941944","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":915,"t":"All Dogs Go to Heaven","y":"1989","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This Don Bluth musical is darker than its cute premise suggests: the dog characters are basically Prohibition-era gangsters who drink at a bar, smoke cigars (even blowing smoke at a child), gamble, steal, and try to kill one another, and there's a nightmarish, demon-tinged sequence plus a brief racial caricature. Despite all that, the throughline is redemption -- Charlie's arc is about learning that loyalty and friendship matter more than revenge or self-interest, and that people (and dogs) can change for the better.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/all-dogs-go-to-heaven","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1067080","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":916,"t":"The Jetsons Meet the Flintstones","y":"1987","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. This Hanna-Barbera TV crossover sends the Jetsons back to the Stone Age (and the Flintstones forward to the Space Age) through a time-machine mix-up, playing out as light workplace and family comedy rather than anything scary or edgy. No violence, language, or substance content is flagged, consistent with its made-for-syndication, all-ages design. The story mostly celebrates friendship and loyalty, as Fred and Barney's bond is tested and repaired, and both families end up helping each other out of job trouble.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Jetsons_Meet_the_Flintstones","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Hanna-Barbera Productions","runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2392121","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":917,"t":"Mickey's Christmas Carol","y":"1983","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"This short, Disney-fied Dickens adaptation softens the story for young viewers but still has a few mildly frightening beats, a menacing Ghost of Christmas Future and a burning coffin, plus background cigar and cigarette smoking. In one odd moment Mickey roughly grabs Pluto by the neck, which sits oddly against his usual kindly persona. Overall it delivers the classic lesson that greed isolates and harms people while generosity brings connection and joy, using Scrooge's turnaround as the emotional core.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/disney-animation-collection-7-mickeys-christmas-carol","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Holiday","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":25,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1539739","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":918,"t":"My Little Pony: The Movie","y":"1986","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"A toyline tie-in aimed squarely at young kids, with cartoon peril, a menacing purple ooze, a spider-like monster, and glowing-eyed trees, plus a trio of cruel witches who shove and strike each other, that could startle the youngest viewers even though nothing is graphic. Insults among the witches (like \"stupid\" and \"pea brain\") are as edgy as the language gets, and there's no substance use or sexual content at all. The ponies model bravery, teamwork, and facing problems head-on rather than running away.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-little-pony-the-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"De Laurentiis Entertainment Group","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2059996","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":919,"t":"The Wiz","y":"1978","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This musical reimagining of The Wizard of Oz features an all-Black cast including Diana Ross and Michael Jackson, with fantasy peril like flying monkeys, a fire-breathing giant head, and scenes where characters are threatened or harmed. Adults drink and smoke at a holiday dinner, there's some mild language, and one storyline touches on a suicide attempt that's stopped by friends. Positive themes of friendship, resilience, and finding inner strength run throughout as the characters support each other on their journey.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wiz","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q428158","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":920,"t":"Little Monsters","y":"1989","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. This fantasy comedy follows a sixth-grader who befriends a monster living under his bed and discovers a hidden underground world where monsters sneak into kids' rooms at night to cause mischief. Expect plenty of gross-out gags and slapstick along with a few genuinely spooky moments involving a menacing villain, though the tone stays playful and kid-friendly overall. At its core it's a story about an unlikely friendship and standing up for someone in trouble.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Monsters_(1989_film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3902620","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":921,"t":"Richie Rich","y":"1994","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Macaulay Culkin stars as the world's richest kid in this gadget-filled comedy that leans heavily on flashy toys and product placement. There's some cartoonish action-movie violence with guns and lasers used at close range plus a tense plane sequence, along with a bit of mild language and a brief suggestive workout scene. Underneath the consumerism, the film argues that money can't buy real friendship and that treating employees and friends with genuine kindness matters more than wealth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/richie-rich","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q506394","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":922,"t":"It Takes Two","y":"1995","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"The Olsen twins play lookalike strangers, an orphan and a wealthy heiress, who swap places to bring a caring social worker and a wealthy dad together. The plot leans on the girls sneaking around, lying to adults, and even taking a horse without permission, plus some mild name-calling and a jilted bride who threatens to strike the kids. It's a predictable but harmless comedy that wraps up happily, though it doesn't offer much in the way of explicit positive lessons.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/it-takes-two","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1308622","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":923,"t":"Babes in Toyland","y":"1986","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. In this NBC television musical, a young Drew Barrymore is whisked away to a magical Toyland on Christmas Eve, teaming up with a hero played by Keanu Reeves to stop a villain from taking over. The story includes a menacing antagonist and a monster that threatens the young heroes, presented within a family Christmas musical framework. Themes of courage, friendship, and Christmas spirit anchor the fantasy adventure.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babes_in_Toyland_(1986_film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Orion Television","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q319158","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":924,"t":"Babes in Toyland","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. This direct-to-video animated musical sends orphaned siblings Jack and Jill to live with their villainous Uncle Barnaby in the land of Toyland, where goblins led by a menacing Goblin King pursue and try to imprison the children. Expect some frightening imagery, including a character being knocked over a bridge and scenes of goblins invading and setting fires, though nothing especially graphic. The film sticks to themes of family loyalty and courage typical of the source operetta.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babes_in_Toyland_(1997_film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"MGM","runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q11118441","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":925,"t":"The Care Bears Movie","y":"1985","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"The original Care Bears film follows two grieving orphaned children and a lonely boy who falls under the influence of a shadowy Evil Spirit threatening to end all caring in the world. Preschoolers may find the misty villain and scenes of destruction a little intense, though there's no language or substance use to worry about. The film's heart is squarely on teamwork, compassion, and banding together against negativity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-care-bears-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"The Samuel Goldwyn Company","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2546045","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":926,"t":"Care Bears Movie II: A New Generation","y":"1986","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This origin story for the Care Bears finds baby bear cubs kidnapped and caged by the villain Dark Heart, with one tense scene where a girl is accidentally zapped into another dimension. There's no bad language or substance use, but the film is fairly thin on educational value and heavy on toy tie-ins. What positive material there is centers on teamwork, guardians protecting their young, and gently addressing bullying.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-care-bears-movie-ii-a-new-generation","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2298395","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":927,"t":"The Adventures of Elmo in Grouchland","y":"1999","la":"3+","ca":"3+","full":"Elmo chases his beloved blanket into Grouchland, a topsy-turvy world where being rude is the norm, and must get it back from a selfish villain who hoards everything he touches. A few perilous moments, like a rollerblading chase and a fall down a tunnel, might startle very sensitive toddlers, but there's essentially no scary language or violence. The film's heart is all about sharing, cooperation, and believing in yourself, wrapped in classic Sesame Street songs and humor.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-adventures-of-elmo-in-grouchland","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q735716","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":928,"t":"The Brave Little Toaster to the Rescue","y":"1997","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"In this sequel, the appliances head off to rescue their owner's college thesis from a computer virus and to save some animal friends from being sold to a testing lab. The peril stays mild and cartoonish, with only brief, non-graphic references to animals being mistreated and a little name-calling. The film's real focus is on friendship, loyalty, and not discarding things, or people, just because they're no longer new.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-brave-little-toaster-to-the-rescue","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Brave Little Toaster to the Rescue","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":929,"t":"Casper","y":"1995","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Christina Ricci plays a grieving teen who befriends a friendly ghost haunting the mansion her father is hired to exorcise, in a film built around groundbreaking CGI for its time. There's a fair amount of ghostly slapstick and three character deaths (all shown continuing on as ghosts), plus some mild swearing, drinking and smoking by adult and ghost characters, and a brief moment of animated cleavage. Underneath the effects, it's a sweet story about friendship, loss, and a father-daughter bond, with balanced roles for its female characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/casper","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1048166","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":930,"t":"Escape to Witch Mountain","y":"1995","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. This ABC television remake of the Disney classic follows two orphaned siblings with psychic powers who go on the run after a greedy millionaire tries to exploit their abilities. Described as mild family adventure fare with a hostage situation and a confrontation with the antagonist rather than graphic peril. It carries the same underlying themes as the original: family loyalty, kindness, and using one's gifts responsibly.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escape_to_Witch_Mountain_(1995_film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4366137","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":931,"t":"FernGully 2: The Magical Rescue","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"In this direct-to-video sequel, the fairies of FernGully venture into the human world to rescue baby animals captured by poachers who've also set the rainforest on fire. There's some real peril here, including caged and nearly-drowning animals and a villain who whips his dogs, though nothing especially graphic and no bad language. The film leans hard into pro-conservation, anti-animal-testing messaging, continuing the original's environmental themes for a younger audience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ferngully-2-the-magical-rescue","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3623997","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":932,"t":"Warriors of Virtue","y":"1997","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. A middle-schooler with a leg injury is pulled into a Taoist-inspired fantasy world where anthropomorphic kangaroo warriors battle a tyrannical sorcerer threatening to invade Earth next. Expect stylized martial-arts fighting and fantasy peril throughout, in line with its PG rating, though nothing graphic. The story leans into themes of courage and pushing past physical limits as the boy finds his footing among the warriors.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warriors_of_Virtue","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"MGM","runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3233113","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":933,"t":"Turbo: A Power Rangers Movie","y":"1997","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Frequent stylized fights fill this Power Rangers spinoff, with the team punching, kicking, and using crossbows against villains, plus a tense scene involving a giant snake and characters dangling near lava. Language stays mild and the villain's costume is a bit more revealing than typical kids' fare. On the plus side, the Rangers consistently look out for each other and model teamwork under pressure, even if critics found the story thin.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/turbo-a-power-rangers-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Saban Entertainment","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2048984","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":934,"t":"Pippi Longstocking","y":"1997","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"This musical take on Astrid Lindgren's story opens with Pippi's sea-captain father swept overboard in a storm, and comic thieves take some pratfall tumbles, but violence stays very mild. It touches on the loss of both parents in a way sensitive kids might need help processing, though the tone stays playful overall. The film celebrates Pippi's independence and generosity while also showing that reuniting with family feels good in the end.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pippi-longstocking","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Nelvana","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2971575","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":935,"t":"Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie","y":"1995","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Like the TV series, this spinoff is full of cartoonish martial-arts combat as the Rangers punch, kick, and spin their way through fights with a rampaging monster and the villain Ivan Ooze. Insults stay silly rather than harsh, though one warrior character's outfit is fairly revealing. The film underscores teamwork and persistence, showing the heroes keep working together even after losing their usual powers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mighty-morphin-power-rangers-the-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Saban Entertainment","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1473596","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":936,"t":"Balto","y":"1995","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Based on the real 1925 diphtheria serum run, this animated adventure follows a half-wolf sled dog who is shunned for being different but proves himself by saving sick children. There's real tension in the ice and blizzard sequences, including near-falls off cliffs and a tense grizzly bear encounter, plus a somber moment showing coffins being readied for children who might not survive. The film is fundamentally about accepting outsiders and how friends supporting each other can be as important as any single act of heroism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/balto","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q764116","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":937,"t":"Dennis the Menace","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This live-action take on the comic strip leans hard into slapstick, with Mr. Wilson repeatedly on the receiving end of Dennis's mishaps, including one gag that leaves his face bloodied and swollen. There's also a kidnapping subplot involving a menacing drifter, some crude jokes about bodies and grown-ups, and background references to beer and cigarettes. Positive messaging is thin, though the film does end with Dennis and his grumpy neighbor finding a way to get along.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dennis-the-menace","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q783486","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":938,"t":"Flipper","y":"1996","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A New York City kid staying with his uncle in Florida befriends a dolphin, though the story opens with another dolphin being shot, and a hammerhead shark attack ramps up tension later on. The uncle is frequently shown drinking beer and smoking cigars, and a bit of mild profanity turns up in the dialogue. The film's heart is really about protecting fragile ocean ecosystems, with the boy and his uncle modeling environmental responsibility together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flipper","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1428947","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":939,"t":"Jungle 2 Jungle","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A businessman brings his jungle-raised son to New York in this broad comedy, where Russian mob characters wave around guns and knives, though it's all played for laughs rather than real menace. The bigger issue is how heavily the humor leans on ethnic stereotyping. Underneath the slapstick, there's a father-son reconciliation arc, even if the film doesn't dwell on it much.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jungle-2-jungle","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q777632","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":940,"t":"Tom and Huck","y":"1995","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This Disney adaptation of Twain's novel keeps the book's darker edge, including a stabbing death the boys witness, a villain who threatens children with a knife and gun, and references to child abuse. Expect some mild cursing, adult drinking, and a boy shown smoking a pipe, along with an ethnic stereotype in its central villain that hasn't aged well. That said, the film does champion loyalty, courage, and doing right even when it's frightening, as Tom learns what real friendship means.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tom-and-huck","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1616185","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":941,"t":"We're Back! A Dinosaur's Story","y":"1993","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Four time-traveling dinosaurs land in 1990s New York in this Amblin production, and while it's mostly playful, a scheming circus ringmaster creates genuinely frightening scenes meant to prey on kids' fears, including fire-breathing effects and mind-altering treats. Language stays very mild. Underneath the scares, the film reassures kids that fear doesn't have to control them, and its dinosaur heroes model bravery, kindness, and resourcefulness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/were-back-a-dinosaurs-story","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1575362","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":942,"t":"Wild America","y":"1997","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. Based on the real Stouffer brothers, this film follows three siblings road-tripping across the American West in 1967 to film wildlife, running into alligators, wolves, bears, and rattlesnakes along the way. The encounters generate real suspense and a few close calls, though the violence stays at an adventure-peril level rather than anything graphic. It's ultimately a story about brotherhood, ambition, and respect for the natural world.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_America_(film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q221982","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":943,"t":"Cats Don't Dance","y":"1997","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"This animated musical follows a hopeful cat trying to break into 1930s Hollywood, who's sabotaged by a jealous child star with a nasty private side. There's little violence or language to worry about, just a mildly menacing villain and some slapstick chaos. Its heart is squarely about pursuing dreams despite setbacks and judging people by character rather than image.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cats-dont-dance","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q930134","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":944,"t":"The Land Before Time II: The Great Valley Adventure","y":"1994","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"The dinosaur friends from the original film return to protect a hatchling that turns out to be a baby Sharptooth, with the bigger dinosaurs growling and baring teeth and a rockslide creating some peril. Content stays mild otherwise, appropriate for young viewers. The film keeps its predecessor's message about teamwork and accepting those who are different, with Littlefoot again modeling responsibility and compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-land-before-time-ii-the-great-valley-adventure","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q389358","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":945,"t":"The Land Before Time III: The Time of the Great Giving","y":"1995","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"A meteorite strike dries up the Great Valley's water, sparking territorial squabbles and recurring bullying among three young dinosaurs while the whole herd faces a drought. Only mild peril (a mudslide, a threatening trio of tyrannosaurs) and occasional name-calling, with no language or substance-use concerns. The film models cooperation, admitting when you're wrong, and working through scarcity together, and the kids display a strong sense of fairness throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-land-before-time-iii-the-time-of-great-giving","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2548919","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":946,"t":"The Land Before Time IV: Journey Through the Mists","y":"1996","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. This direct-to-video sequel is aimed at a preschool-through-early-grade audience, with the young dinosaurs braving a foggy, dangerous marshland to find medicine for an ailing grandparent. The main thread is Littlefoot's friend Ali learning to accept a stranger who looks and acts differently rather than fear her, in keeping with the franchise's mild-peril, message-driven formula. No language or substance-use content is noted.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Land_Before_Time_IV:_Journey_Through_the_Mists","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q645879","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":947,"t":"Quest for Camelot","y":"1998","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A spirited teenage girl sets out to recover her late father's stolen sword and save Camelot, aided by a blind former squire and a bumbling two-headed dragon. A couple of tense scenes and the death of a sympathetic character could rattle sensitive kids, though there's no bad language or substance use. Positive themes include teamwork, loyalty, and recognizing the strengths of people with disabilities, embodied by the resourceful blind hero.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/quest-for-camelot","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1764174","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":948,"t":"Pokémon: The First Movie","y":"1998","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Scientists clone a hyper-powerful Pokémon named Mewtwo, whose fury at his creators erupts into near-constant battles, explosions, and a stretch where the hero appears to die. The fast, dark, storm-heavy action could overwhelm kids too young to separate real from pretend danger, though there's no bad language or substance use. The film argues that fighting solves nothing and that character matters more than origin, with the young hero modeling courage and compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pokemon-the-first-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q834799","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":949,"t":"The Land Before Time V: The Mysterious Island","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. A swarm of pests strips the Great Valley of food, forcing the herd to migrate and sparking arguments over what's left; the kids sneak off at night and end up stranded on an island after a wave destroys their path home. Expect the series' typical chase-and-peril sequences rather than graphic violence. The story centers on resourcefulness and sticking together when resources run short.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Land_Before_Time_V:_The_Mysterious_Island","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2552049","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":950,"t":"The Land Before Time VI: The Secret of Saurus Rock","y":"1998","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. Young dinosaurs fall from a rock formation and are chased by an Allosaurus and a Tyrannosaurus, plus a tornado strikes the valley -- peril typical of the franchise, including an implied predator death that could unsettle very young viewers. One of the weaker sequels, but it keeps the series' usual message about looking past hero-worship and relying on your community.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Land_Before_Time_VI:_The_Secret_of_Saurus_Rock","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2301435","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":951,"t":"An American Tail: Fievel Goes West","y":"1991","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"The Mousekewitz mouse family heads west chasing a promised cat-free frontier, only to find new predators and swindlers waiting. A fair amount of cartoon-style peril between cats, dogs, and mice, none of it graphic, though the film's dated, stereotyped portrayals of Eastern European Jewish immigrants and Native American characters are the bigger concern. Musical numbers and a friendship-and-looking-out-for-each-other message balance an occasionally grating comic-relief subplot.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/an-american-tail-fievel-goes-west","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Western"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1402152","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":952,"t":"Baby's Day Out","y":"1994","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A wealthy infant is kidnapped by three bumbling crooks, escapes, and toddles unsupervised through city traffic and a construction site while his pursuers suffer one slapstick injury after another. The head-bonk, groin-hit style physical comedy and the baby's string of dangerous near-misses without a scratch could send a confusing safety message. The film's point about valuing family over money lands weakly, and there's no strong adult role model in the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/babys-day-out","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q637884","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":953,"t":"Blank Check","y":"1994","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"An overlooked 11-year-old cashes a criminal's blank check for a million dollars and buys himself a mansion and toys, drawing the attention of both the mobster and an FBI agent posing as a love interest. Gun threats, a couple of scuffles, adult drinking at a party, and a jarring moment where a grown woman kisses the boy on the mouth, along with some innuendo. The story does land on family mattering more than money and windfalls revealing real friends, though the dad's early neglect and the boy's scheming are shakier role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/blank-check","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1632535","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":954,"t":"The Borrowers","y":"1997","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A four-inch-tall family living secretly inside a normal house must stop a scheming lawyer from evicting the humans upstairs, leading to inventive traps, chemical mishaps, and slapstick chases. The peril has real (if non-fatal) stakes -- burns, prong pokes -- plus very mild language and a cigar-smoking villain who ends up doused in cheese. The film is praised for its decisive, capable female Borrowers and its messages about teamwork and family loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-borrowers","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"PolyGram Films","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1304483","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":955,"t":"Doug's 1st Movie","y":"1999","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Doug and Skeeter try to protect a gentle lake monster from a scheming, publicity-hungry town boss, all while Doug tries to work up the nerve to ask his crush to the school dance. Mild action (sharpshooters targeting a mechanical monster at the dance) and some spooky noises at the lake, with no language or substance-use content. The film's message about doing the right thing and protecting the environment comes through clearly, even if the story feels more like a stretched TV episode.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dougs-1st-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2625713","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":956,"t":"Dunston Checks In","y":"1996","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"An orangutan smuggled into a posh hotel by a jewel thief instead befriends a neglected boy, leading to chandelier swinging, cigar smoking, and a tranquilizer-gun chase. Mild profanity, some drinking, and rough slapstick tussling (ear-biting, mock karate), plus mild peril that could worry kids sensitive about the animal's safety. Underneath the antics is a workaholic single dad learning to put his sons first.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dunston-checks-in","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q645480","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":957,"t":"First Kid","y":"1996","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A Secret Service agent is assigned to guard the rebellious teenage son of the president and ends up teaching him to stand up to bullies, ask out a girl, and just act like a normal kid. Comedic pratfalls, guns drawn during a climactic scene, a brief mooning gag, mild language, and Secret Service agents shown drinking beer, alongside an online-stalker subplot. At its core the film is about compassionate mentorship, with the boy growing from bratty to likeable as he's given room to be a regular teenager.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/first-kid","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1627076","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":958,"t":"The Flintstones","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This live-action take on the cartoon town of Bedrock includes some cartoonish but occasionally rough violence like clubbing and a hanging threat, plus beer, martinis, and cigarettes shown around town. A flirty secretary delivers a few sexually loaded lines to Fred, and the whole film leans hard on old-fashioned gender roles for its women. There's a mild theme about sacrificing for friends, but the movie doesn't offer much in the way of real role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-flintstones","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q602094","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":959,"t":"Jingle All the Way","y":"1996","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Arnold Schwarzenegger's frantic hunt for a sold-out toy leads to plenty of slapstick brawling, a tasering, and even a bomb scare with police drawing weapons, all played for laughs. Mild language, an outdated ethnic joke, some drinking and cigar smoking, and a subplot flirting with infidelity. The movie gestures toward a message about family mattering more than stuff, though the frantic toy chase mostly undercuts it, and the dad is a flawed model who lies his way through the day.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jingle-all-the-way","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1064530","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":960,"t":"Sister Act","y":"1992","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The story opens with an off-screen mob killing and includes gunplay and a kidnapping threat, plus some strong language and casual references to drinking and smoking around the casino scenes. Light kissing and a few mild sexual references. On the positive side, the convent's nuns are drawn as individuals rather than a stereotype, and the film centers on teamwork, community pride, and using your talents to lift others up.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sister-act","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q776302","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":961,"t":"Sister Act 2: Back in the Habit","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Much gentler than the original, this sequel drops the crime and violence entirely, leaving only occasional mild language and some reckless driving played for comedy. Deloris's nun impersonation is treated as good-hearted rather than deceptive. The movie leans fully into positive territory, celebrating school participation, follow-through, and a diverse, well-run inner-city high school where one person's effort makes a real difference.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sister-act-2-back-in-the-habit","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1140762","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":962,"t":"Miracle on 34th Street","y":"1994","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This remake has a store Santa knocking down a rival with his cane, some mild insults, and background drinking among department-store Santas and one drunk impostor. A grown-up romance with kissing, a hinted pregnancy, and a brief moment of nudity, alongside a cynical corporate-greed subplot. Its heart is still in the right place, championing kindness, imagination, and faith in things you can't prove.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/miracle-on-34th-street-1994","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q258204","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":963,"t":"North","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Not on CSM; substitute source used. In this widely panned satire, a neglected boy declares himself a free agent and auditions new parents around the world, encountering broad cultural caricatures along the way, including mockery of Amish life that drew criticism. Content-wise it's mild -- a handful of mild curses, no violence or sexual content -- but its ethnic stereotyping is its biggest problem. Underneath the satire, the story does land on a sincere message about appreciating the parents you already have.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_(1994_film)","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1072666","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":964,"t":"Night at the Museum","y":"2006","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Once the museum exhibits wake up, there's a lot of cartoonish fighting, chasing, and prop-weapon mayhem, plus a few scary beats like a looming dinosaur skeleton and an Attila the Hun chase that could rattle younger kids. Language stays mild, an adult has a glass of wine, and a couple of cultures get flattened into stereotypes. The story rewards Larry for pursuing his dreams, taking responsibility for his family, and learning through history, with Teddy Roosevelt as an encouraging mentor.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/night-at-the-museum","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q387601","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":965,"t":"Night at the Museum: Battle of the Smithsonian","y":"2009","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This sequel keeps up the chasing and prop-weapon threats, adds a genuinely creepy giant octopus and an eerie underworld sequence, and includes mild language plus some passionate kissing and light innuendo between adult characters. It stays true to its message about being yourself and doing what you love, with Amelia Earhart standing out as a spirited, independent role model who helps the hero grow from self-centered to community-minded.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/night-at-the-museum-battle-of-the-smithsonian","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q476726","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":966,"t":"The Polar Express","y":"2004","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"The train ride is full of genuine peril -- runaway cars, falls, cracking ice, and treacherous climbs -- and a dark detour with a puppet-controlling stranger surrounded by unsettling, human-like broken toys can spook sensitive kids. No language, substance use, or sexual content anywhere in the film. What it does deliver in spades is a message about believing in things you can't see, the value of friendship and courage, and the real meaning of the holiday living in your heart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-polar-express","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Holiday"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q862197","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":967,"t":"Curious George","y":"2006","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"This gentle, preschool-friendly adaptation has only slapstick monkey mischief for its rough edges, along with some light adult flirting that ends in a kiss and a moment where animal control takes George away that can feel emotionally intense for little ones. A bit of product placement and a small deception around a museum exhibit. Mostly, the film is a warm celebration of curiosity, loyalty, and the growing friendship between George and the Man in the Yellow Hat.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/curious-george-2006","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1753443","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":968,"t":"Happy Feet","y":"2006","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Mumble's world includes real danger from leopard seals, orcas, and a fishing trawler, plus an unsettling hallucination sequence once he's trapped in captivity. Courtship among the penguins comes with a lot of suggestive talk and movement, some mild insults and crude language, and a few flattened cultural stereotypes among the supporting characters. Still, the film champions individuality, honesty, friendship, and environmental awareness through Mumble's determination to be himself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/happy-feet","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q126800","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":969,"t":"Happy Feet Two","y":"2011","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"This sequel is milder than the original, with peril coming from an icy trap, threatening predators, and background scenes of smaller sea creatures being eaten, plus a bit of mild name-calling and light romantic innuendo between penguin couples. It leans heavily into positive territory, with strong themes about environmental awareness, chasing your own passions, and family and friends supporting each other through hard times.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/happy-feet-two","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q816857","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":970,"t":"Star Wars: The Clone Wars","y":"2008","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This animated Star Wars entry is packed with near-nonstop laser and lightsaber battles between clones, droids, and Separatist forces, with characters destroyed on screen though without blood. Young Anakin is shown eating live bugs, a gag that could tempt imitation. Good and evil are drawn in fairly stark terms except for Anakin's simmering inner conflict, and the Republic is shown as a proudly multicultural coalition of species working together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/star-wars-clone-wars","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Action","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Lucasfilm","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q382289","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":971,"t":"Corpse Bride","y":"2005","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Tim Burton's stop-motion fairy tale leans into playful-creepy imagery: talking skeletons, decaying corpses, and an eyeball that pops out to reveal a wisecracking maggot living inside the bride. It's more whimsical than frightening, with minimal language and only fantasy-context drinking among the dead. At its heart it's a gentle romance about love, selflessness, and choosing what truly matters over status.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tim-burtons-corpse-bride","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q164417","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":972,"t":"ParaNorman","y":"2012","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"This stop-motion horror-comedy gets genuinely eerie, with zombies, ghosts, and unsettling imagery plus a dark backstory involving the execution of a child centuries earlier. Schoolyard name-calling, an implied curse word, and teens who drink and flirt. The payoff is a heartfelt message about empathy, courage, and giving misunderstood kids the benefit of the doubt, delivered partly through a supporting gay character treated with easy, matter-of-fact humor.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paranorman","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Horror"],"studio":"Focus Features","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q198028","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":973,"t":"Isle of Dogs","y":"2018","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Wes Anderson's stop-motion tale is edgier than typical family animation, with dogfights, a disturbing image of a boy with debris lodged in his head, an unsettling sushi-prep scene, occasional coarse language, and adult drinking and pipe smoking. A suicide is referenced. Underneath the darker edges are messages about uncovering lies, redemption through sacrifice, loyalty, and one character using her voice against corruption and abuse of power.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/isle-of-dogs","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Fox Searchlight Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28065409","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":974,"t":"Diary of a Wimpy Kid","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This animated take on the book series keeps things light, with bike wipeouts, a broken arm, food fights, shoving, and a chaotic Halloween chase, plus mild insults like 'moron' and some bathroom humor. The boys occasionally fib to their parents, but the film centers on the idea that true friendship matters more than popularity, with Greg and Rowley having each other's backs through middle-school chaos.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/diary-of-a-wimpy-kid-0","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":58,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q108549760","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":976,"t":"The Bad Guys 2","y":"2025","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"The reformed crew is back for a heist-caper sequel loaded with chases, explosions, and slapstick, including characters getting drugged and tranquilized, plus mild swearing and a hinted romance between two animal characters. As with the first film, it champions teamwork, self-control, and the idea that people (and wolves) can genuinely change, with strong female leaders again at the center of the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-bad-guys-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q125363929","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":977,"t":"Minions: The Rise of Gru","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This Despicable Me prequel is wall-to-wall slapstick and martial-arts action, including a tied-up torture threat and a near-miss with crocodiles, all played for laughs and survived unharmed. A few brief rear-end gags and mild insults. Even with its villain-glorifying premise, it lands on messages about loyalty, teamwork, and mentorship, though its depiction of Chinese culture leans stereotypical and exoticized.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/minions-the-rise-of-gru","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Minions: The Rise of Gru","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":978,"t":"Sonic the Hedgehog","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The live-action debut of Sega's speedy hero features cartoonish weapon battles that leave no one really hurt, one crude gesture, a single use of 'hell,' and a female character shown in revealing clothing plus a played-for-laughs marriage-and-kids fantasy sequence. The story is fairly thin on real takeaways, with characters too one-dimensional to serve as strong role models and some dated gender stereotyping.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sonic-the-hedgehog-the-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q29906232","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":979,"t":"Sonic the Hedgehog 2","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"The sequel ramps up fantasy peril with near-drownings and characters getting struck by vehicles, though nothing feels graphically real, plus some mild swearing, fart jokes, and adults drinking on a stressful Hawaii trip. The film's throughline is that heroism finds you rather than the other way around, with strong messages about teamwork, family bonds, and Sonic winning over a former enemy through compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sonic-the-hedgehog-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":122,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Sonic the Hedgehog 2 (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":980,"t":"Sonic the Hedgehog 3","y":"2024","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"This installment hits noticeably harder than its predecessors, with a drone attack, a hospitalization, and two character deaths including a child, alongside mild swearing and emotionally heavy material around a captured character's mistreatment that may frighten younger viewers. The film's core message is that people are defined by the choices they make, reinforced through family, teamwork, and open communication among the leads.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sonic-the-hedgehog-3","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Adventure"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q115859490","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":981,"t":"The Super Mario Bros. Movie","y":"2023","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The video-game adaptation delivers fantasy action violence like missile fire and a finger-crushing piano gag, plus a genuinely startling zombie-skeleton sequence and a bit of schoolyard-style insult humor. Power-up mushrooms stand in for the game's classic mechanic. The story rewards perseverance, teamwork, and courage, with Peach portrayed as brave and proactive rather than a passive damsel alongside Mario.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-super-mario-bros-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q108671102","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":982,"t":"The Super Mario Galaxy Movie","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This sequel leans into frequent fantasy-action peril, with menacing creatures, a kidnapping plot, magical weapon attacks, and a skeleton-emerging-from-lava moment that could unsettle younger kids, plus mild insults and a casino scene with implied alcoholic drinks. Its heart is a story about teamwork and the importance of family and friends, and it gives Bowser a redemption arc about learning to change for the better.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-super-mario-galaxy-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q124806421","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":983,"t":"Transformers One","y":"2024","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"An animated origin story set on Cybertron following miner-bots Orion Pax and D-16 before they become Optimus Prime and Megatron. Frequent, explosive sci-fi battles with characters crushed or dismembered, plus some mild swearing and heavy Hasbro toy marketing throughout. On the plus side, the film champions teamwork, courage, and the idea that physical strength isn't what makes a true leader.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/transformers-one","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Action"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q116638627","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":984,"t":"IF","y":"2024","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A blend of live action and animated imaginary friends, following a girl coping with her mother's death and her father's heart surgery, both shown in flashback. A few jump scares and one use of a stronger swear word, but nothing graphic. The story leans into grief, curiosity, and using imagination as a healthy way to process hard emotions.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/if","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q111918059","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":985,"t":"KPop Demon Hunters","y":"2025","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"An animated adventure about a K-pop girl group who moonlight as demon fighters, battling soul-stealing creatures and a menacing demon king. Fights are stylized rather than graphic, though shadowy villains and tense confrontations can feel intense for younger kids, and there's some flirtatious byplay between two characters. The trio models perseverance, self-acceptance, and leaning on friends to face what scares you.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kpop-demon-hunters","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q130268157","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":986,"t":"Diary of a Wimpy Kid: The Last Straw","y":"2025","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Greg Heffley's dad threatens military school unless Greg can prove he's capable of real responsibility, leading to a wilderness-camp showdown. Cartoonish mishaps like a dog bite and a wasp's-nest tumble, plus mild insults and some brief comic nudity, all played for laughs. The film's heart is showing that shortcuts and lying backfire, while patient parenting and effort pay off.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/diary-of-a-wimpy-kid-the-last-straw","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Diary of a Wimpy Kid: The Last Straw (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":987,"t":"Smurfs","y":"2025","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This reboot mixes animation, live action, and musical numbers as the Smurfs face off against dark wizards who threaten to destroy them. The word 'Smurf' stands in for harsher language throughout, and there's some peril including a fall and menacing magical portals. Messages about self-belief, teamwork, and finding your own strengths run through the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/smurfs","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q124125148","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":988,"t":"The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants","y":"2025","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"SpongeBob sets out with Patrick to prove his courage after the ghostly Flying Dutchman tricks him into a series of deep-sea trials. Slapstick mishaps, toilet humor, and some genuinely spooky creatures (a three-headed bird, skeleton guards) round out the adventure. Underneath the gags, it reassures kids that being scared doesn't make you any less brave.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-spongebob-movie-search-for-squarepants","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q118847776","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":989,"t":"Gabby's Dollhouse: The Movie","y":"2025","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Gabby and her grandmother Gigi chase down Gabby's runaway dollhouse after it falls into the hands of an eccentric cat-loving stranger. Several intense chase and jump-scare moments, plus a brief gag where a character acts woozy after sniffing catnip. The film centers a loving, multigenerational family and shows its young heroine leading with bravery and compassion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/gabbys-dollhouse-the-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q126414863","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":990,"t":"Swapped","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A curious woodland creature and a small bird accidentally trade bodies and have to team up to survive predators and a wildfire while figuring out how to switch back. The peril feels real but isn't graphic, and mild insults are the extent of the rough language. It's ultimately about empathy, cooperation with nature, and understanding someone by walking in their world.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/swapped","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q126709560","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":991,"t":"GOAT","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"An underdog goat chases his dream of going pro in a rough, full-contact animal sport called roarball. Competitive shoving and taunting on the field plus a few mentions of a parent's death, but nothing graphic, and the humor stays mild. The story pushes back against being judged by your size and celebrates a devoted single dad and hard-won self-belief.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/goat-0","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Sports","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Goat (2026 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":992,"t":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles II: The Secret of the Ooze","y":"1991","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"The Turtles face off against two new mutant villains created by Shredder using the same ooze that made them who they are. Fight scenes are choreographed and bloodless, though the monster designs might startle very young viewers, and there's a brief scene of a minor character smoking. Splinter's mentorship and the Turtles' loyalty to each other anchor the film's message about teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-2-the-secret-of-the-ooze","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Comedy"],"studio":"New Line Cinema","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1326619","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":993,"t":"Beethoven's 2nd","y":"1993","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The lovable St. Bernard is back with a mate and puppies in this family comedy, but one subplot -- a teen party scene where a drunken boy nearly assaults a girl before the dog interrupts -- is a jarring, out-of-place inclusion for what's otherwise a kids' movie. Teen drinking at that party and a mild, awkwardly handled conversation about where puppies come from. On a lighter note, the film follows the family learning to take responsibility for the new litter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/beethovens-2nd","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1306317","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":994,"t":"Mr. Popper's Penguins","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A career-focused real estate developer's life is upended when he inherits a family of penguins, forcing him to slow down and reconnect with his kids. Mostly harmless slapstick, though there's a joke about erectile-dysfunction medication and champagne at a party that adults will catch and kids will miss. The throughline is a familiar but effective lesson about choosing family over ambition.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mr-poppers-penguins","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q682549","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":995,"t":"We Bought a Zoo","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This warm family dramedy follows a widowed dad and his kids restoring a rundown zoo, but the emotional core involves grief over the mother's death that can hit younger viewers hard, plus more profanity than typical for a PG movie, a disturbingly violent teen drawing, and some adult social drinking. On the plus side it models open family communication, teamwork, and resilience through loss.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/we-bought-a-zoo","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q956681","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":996,"t":"Earth to Echo","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Four kids team up to help a stranded alien get home in this E.T.-style adventure shot in a shaky found-footage style, with mild peril, a bar and party scene where alcohol appears in the background, some near-swearing and name-calling, and innocent flirting. The story rewards loyalty, courage, and friends looking out for each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/earth-to-echo","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Relativity Media","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16031637","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":997,"t":"The House with a Clock in Its Walls","y":"2018","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Directed by horror filmmaker Eli Roth as a gentler 'starter' spookfest, it's full of creepy imagery and jump scares, living dolls, a corpse, a graveyard scene, a bullying incident, and war-flashback references with blood, plus mild swearing. Underneath the frights, it champions individuality, perseverance, and found family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-house-with-a-clock-in-its-walls","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q42914959","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":998,"t":"Diary of a Wimpy Kid: Rodrick Rules","y":"2011","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Greg navigates seventh-grade sibling rivalry with older brother Rodrick, featuring schoolyard-style insults, mild physical scuffling, and a teen party scene where cup contents are never specified as alcoholic. It leans into gentle comedy about family embarrassment rather than anything harsh, and Greg ultimately learns to value being himself over chasing popularity.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/diary-of-a-wimpy-kid-rodrick-rules","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1156830","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":999,"t":"Mirror Mirror","y":"2012","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This lighter, comedic spin on Snow White includes bloodless sword fights, menacing puppet-like creatures, adult drinking at parties, and a few innuendos likely to fly over kids' heads. It reframes the princess as an active, capable heroine trained by the dwarfs in self-defense, warning against vanity and greed while celebrating kindness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mirror-mirror","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Relativity Media","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":106,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q628851","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1000,"t":"Barbie","y":"2023","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Greta Gerwig's satirical comedy tackles gender expectations and patriarchy with one bleeped strong swear word, milder profanity, cartoonish slapstick fights, party scenes with drinking, and some suggestive jokes and innuendo that skew older, plus heavy toy-brand promotion throughout. Its core message champions female empowerment, self-acceptance, and mutual support between women.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/barbie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q55436290","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1001,"t":"Roald Dahl's Matilda the Musical","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This musical adaptation includes a genuinely frightening tyrant headmistress who swings a child by the pigtails, locks kids in a spiked closet, and force-feeds one an entire cake, plus a scene where a circus performer falls and later dies in a hospital, alongside brief adult cocktail-drinking. It strongly promotes courage in facing bullies, love of reading, and standing up for others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/roald-dahls-matilda-the-musical","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Matilda the Musical (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1002,"t":"Wonka","y":"2023","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This musical origin story for the famous chocolatier includes a gunpoint threat with one shot fired, a near-drowning, an explosion, and a child locked in a birdcage-like coop, along with mild insults and one instance of a stronger word. A running joke about a character gaining extreme weight reads as fat-shaming, and one candy causes a simulated drunk effect, but themes of imagination, hope, perseverance, and generosity carry the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonka","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q108456719","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1003,"t":"Sing 2","y":"2021","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The animated musical sequel has cartoonish, non-graphic peril like near-falls and a shock gag, mild insults, mentions of a character's grief over a late spouse, and a brief married-couple kiss, plus some intimidating villain characters that could unsettle sensitive kids. It emphasizes teamwork, honesty, and persistence in chasing your dreams.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/sing-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Sing 2","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1004,"t":"The Garfield Movie","y":"2024","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This animated adventure includes cartoon slapstick, a bird getting swallowed, an electrocution gag, and chases with intimidating adversaries, plus mild insults and one stronger British-style curse word. A scene of young Garfield left alone and frightened in a dark alley may affect sensitive kids, and heavy brand product placement runs throughout, but the story highlights teamwork, forgiveness, and family bonds.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-garfield-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Garfield Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1005,"t":"The Angry Birds Movie","y":"2016","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Based on the mobile game, it centers on an outcast bird who must overcome his anger to protect his island from invading pigs, with cartoon violence like explosions and characters launched into buildings, crude jokes, party drinking, and a voyeuristic gag. Some scenes imply real danger, but it ultimately encourages not judging others too quickly and taking personal responsibility.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-angry-birds-movie","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18703062","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1006,"t":"The Angry Birds Movie 2","y":"2019","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The animated sequel pairs the birds and pigs against a new rival, with slapstick action, potty humor, and a handful of mildly suggestive jokes about mating season and nudity, though peril always resolves safely with no lasting harm. It builds on the original by emphasizing teamwork, diplomacy, accountability, and earning forgiveness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-angry-birds-movie-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18722273","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1007,"t":"Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle","y":"2017","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Teens get sucked into a video-game jungle where their avatars die and respawn repeatedly, including a jaguar mauling and a couple of jump scares, alongside scattered swearing and some body-swap humor about gender and anatomy. One sequence has teen avatars drinking cocktails and getting tipsy. On the plus side, the group has to lean on teamwork, honesty, and generosity to survive, and popularity turns out not to matter much once everyone is equally out of their depth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jumanji-welcome-to-the-jungle","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":119,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q20762680","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1008,"t":"Jumanji: The Next Level","y":"2019","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The gang is pulled back into the game, this time with two grandfathers along for the ride, and again dies and regenerates through animal attacks, falls, and explosions without any blood shown. There's frequent strong language and a backstory involving a villain who killed a character's parents. The film keeps leaning on teamwork, courage, and empathy, showing that having people you can count on matters most when things get hard.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jumanji-the-next-level","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":122,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q60501923","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1010,"t":"Ramona and Beezus","y":"2010","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This adaptation of Beverly Cleary's books follows spirited young Ramona as her family deals with her dad losing his job, all while she navigates squabbles with her older sister. Content is mild: a bit of slapstick, a kitchen mishap, a gently handled pet death, and a couple of light adult and teen kisses. The film centers family loyalty, staying true to yourself, and finding the bright side of hard times.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ramona-and-beezus","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1147079","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1011,"t":"Zathura: A Space Adventure","y":"2005","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Two feuding brothers get pulled into a wild game that lands their house in the middle of space, complete with armed ships, hostile aliens, and a malfunctioning robot. Some mild profanity, plenty of peril and explosions, and a bit of physical fighting between the siblings. Like its cousin Jumanji, the danger forces the brothers to stop competing and start looking out for each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/zathura-a-space-adventure","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q148326","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1012,"t":"My Girl","y":"1991","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Eleven-year-old Vada, who is still processing her mother's death, spends a formative summer with her best friend Thomas J. before a sudden, off-screen death shakes her world again. Some mild swearing and a passing reference to marijuana, but the emotional weight of grief is the real content note here. The film handles loss with care, showing kids that life continues and that talking through pain with family helps.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-girl","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":1,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q833299","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1013,"t":"My Girl 2","y":"1994","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Now a bit older, Vada travels to Los Angeles to learn more about the mother she never knew, while also dealing with the recent loss of her best friend and her dad's job as an undertaker. Mild language shows up, a hippie character is shown smoking pot, and two teens sneak out at night, but there's no violence. Every parental figure in the story is loving and engaged, and the film centers on self-discovery and taking pride in where you come from.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-girl-2","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1420668","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1014,"t":"The Secret Garden","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This is Agnieszka Holland's well-known adaptation, following orphaned Mary Lennox as she's sent to live with her withdrawn uncle and discovers a locked-away garden that helps heal both her and her sickly cousin. Content concerns are light: an earthquake causes the parents' deaths before the story begins, there's a slap and some unkind name-calling, and the pacing is slow and quiet rather than action-driven. The film's real strength is showing how nature, curiosity, and friendship can pull spoiled, grieving children out of their shells.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-secret-garden","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q525421","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1015,"t":"Life-Size","y":"2000","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A grieving girl accidentally magics her fashion doll into a living person, played by Tyra Banks, leading to a fish-out-of-water comedy about what actually makes someone whole. Mild peril, some flirty adult humor and a near-kiss, and the doll-world segments lean into dated ideas about shopping and appearance. Still, the film pushes back on those stereotypes some by having its young lead prefer football to fashion, and it lands on messages about trying your best and valuing connection over perfection.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/life-size","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q228992","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1016,"t":"Ella Enchanted","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"In this loose, comic take on the Cinderella story, Ella is cursed at birth to obey any command given to her and has to find a way to break the spell before it forces her to harm the prince she loves. The peril and villainy (an ogre, a menacing curse, a mother's illness) are played mostly for laughs rather than real scares, and a fairy character gets comically drunk at one point. The film's heart is about reclaiming your own agency and choosing kindness, with good characters rewarded and cruelty ultimately punished.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ella-enchanted","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Miramax Films","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q939325","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1017,"t":"How to Eat Fried Worms","y":"2006","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"A new kid at school gets dared into eating ten worms in a single day after a bully sets out to humiliate him, and the film leans hard into gross-out, potty-style humor along the way. Bullying and name-calling drive much of the plot, though it stays free of real violence. The takeaway is a fairly earnest one about facing down bullies with courage instead of running, backed by a supportive, understanding family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-to-eat-fried-worms","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"New Line Cinema","flags":{"violence":1,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3285972","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1018,"t":"Where the Wild Things Are","y":"2009","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Spike Jonze's adaptation follows a lonely, misbehaving boy named Max who sails off to an island of temperamental monsters who crown him their king. The Wild Things smash and burn things when they lose their tempers, there's a tense storm sequence, some mild swearing, and an overall melancholy, muted tone that stays with real feelings of loneliness and insecurity rather than resolving neatly. It's ultimately about the messy, complicated nature of childhood emotions and the pull of home and family, carried by a Wild Thing who models inclusion even when others reject her.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/where-the-wild-things-are","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q622742","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1019,"t":"Adventures in Babysitting","y":"1987","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"This is the 1987 original, not the 2016 Disney Channel remake: a babysitter's night watching three kids spirals into an unplanned trip through downtown Chicago full of car chases, run-ins with a street gang, and mistaken danger from criminals who aren't actually after them. Frequent strong language, guns and knives brandished for tension, a scary high-rise ledge scene, and some innuendo including a college guy taking an interest in a 17-year-old. The night's chaos mostly plays out with the babysitter prioritizing the kids' safety, though the film doesn't dwell much on consequences for the risky choices made along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/adventures-in-babysitting","addedAt":"2026-08-24","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":4,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1215038","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1020,"t":"To Kill a Mockingbird","y":"1962","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"A childhood memoir turned courtroom drama: young Scout Finch watches her lawyer father Atticus defend a Black man falsely accused of raping a white woman in Depression-era Alabama. This one runs genuinely heavy for a family list -- a racial slur is used repeatedly by the story's bigots, an angry mob confronts a jailed man, courtroom testimony touches on the assault (handled with period-era restraint), and a man is shot and killed near the end. Even so, it's held up as a landmark portrait of empathy and injustice: Atticus's insistence on understanding people before judging them, and Scout and Jem's own moral growth, make it best suited to older kids and teens ready for a serious conversation about racism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/to-kill-a-mockingbird","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q177922","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1021,"t":"A Series of Unfortunate Events","y":"2004","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Jim Carrey headlines this darkly comic adaptation of the Lemony Snicket books, following the three orphaned Baudelaire children as their conniving new guardian, Count Olaf, schemes to steal their fortune and get rid of them along the way. Expect near-constant peril and gothic, macabre humor rather than graphic violence -- parents die off-screen, kids are threatened and manipulated, and the mood stays gloomy throughout, which can unsettle more sensitive viewers even as older kids find it deliciously creepy. On the plus side, the Baudelaire siblings are resourceful, brave, and fiercely loyal to each other, and the underlying message is that persistence and cleverness can win out even when the adults around you won't listen.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/lemony-snickets-a-series-of-unfortunate-events","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate Events","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1022,"t":"Spy Kids 2: The Island of Lost Dreams","y":"2002","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Carmen and Juni Cortez return as full-fledged junior spies, racing a rival sibling duo to a mysterious island crawling with hybrid creatures while trying to rescue their parents. There's plenty of gadget-fueled peril, chases, and gross-out creature gags, but nobody gets seriously hurt and the scary-looking stuff reliably turns out friendly; language stays essentially clean. It's praised for putting smart, capable Latino and female characters front and center, with teamwork and courage as the throughline -- a fun, low-worry sequel for the original's fans.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spy-kids-2-the-island-of-lost-dreams","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Miramax Films","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q549908","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1023,"t":"Spy Kids 3-D: Game Over","y":"2003","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Juni goes it mostly alone this time, diving into a deadly virtual-reality game to rescue his sister Carmen and stop a villainous Toymaker from taking over the world. The action is stylized and cartoonish -- giant robots, lava, exploding toy soldiers -- and stays within family-adventure bounds, with no real bloodshed or profanity to speak of, though it leans more on level-to-level spectacle than the earlier films' stronger plotting. Family loyalty and teamwork remain the throughline, and the wheelchair-using grandfather gets a meaningful, capable role, even if the messages are stated more than shown this time around.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spy-kids-3-d-game-over","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Miramax Films","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q550196","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1024,"t":"Addams Family Values","y":"1993","la":"12+","ca":"13+","full":"This gleefully macabre sequel sends the Addams kids off to a chirpy summer camp while Uncle Fester falls for a gold-digging new bride with murder on her mind. The humor leans harder into innuendo and mock-violence than the original -- comedic near-electrocutions, a baby nearly tossed off a roof, and grown-up jokes that sail over young kids' heads but register with teens and parents. What keeps it from feeling mean-spirited is the Addams family's genuine, unconditional love for each other, framed as healthier than the smiling conformity of the outsiders mocking them -- a dark-humored but ultimately warm case for embracing being different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/addams-family-values","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q204725","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1025,"t":"High School Musical 3: Senior Year","y":"2008","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Troy, Gabriella, and the Wildcats face graduation, prom, and college decisions in this theatrical send-off to the Disney Channel trilogy, packed with big dance numbers. Content is very mild: a little flirting, a couple of kisses, and low-stakes teen drama over choosing between colleges and following your heart. Messages about supporting friends' dreams and staying true to yourself make it a safe, catchy pick for tweens.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/high-school-musical-3-senior-year","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q53115","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1026,"t":"The Chronicles of Narnia: Prince Caspian","y":"2008","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The Pevensie siblings are pulled back into Narnia to help young Prince Caspian reclaim his throne from a tyrannical uncle, and this sequel leans harder into war than the first film. Expect extended battle sequences and a brutal one-on-one duel, plus a light romantic thread that ends in a single kiss. The story rewards resisting revenge and pride, and owning up to mistakes, but the heavier combat makes it a better fit for kids past the youngest ages.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-chronicles-of-narnia-prince-caspian","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":140,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q222023","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1027,"t":"The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader","y":"2010","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Edmund, Lucy, and their whiny cousin Eustace join King Caspian's voyage to find seven lost lords, running into a giant sea serpent, an island where visitors go missing, and a genuinely unsettling green mist. There's sword fighting, hand-to-hand combat, and one on-screen death, alongside real scares for younger viewers in a nightmare sequence. The quest doubles as a lesson in facing down jealousy, greed, and self-doubt, which makes it worth a post-movie chat with older kids.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-chronicles-of-narnia-the-voyage-of-the-dawn-treader","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q474082","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1028,"t":"Scooby-Doo","y":"2002","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"The gang reunites to solve spooky goings-on at a resort island in this live-action take on the cartoon, blending genuinely creepy visuals with gross-out slapstick. Parents should know about a drug-adjacent sight gag, a scene implying Velma got drunk, a prolonged belching-and-farting contest, and general college-age partying and flirting. Underneath the crude jokes, the mystery still comes down to the gang working as a team and trusting each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/scooby-doo","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q936302","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1029,"t":"Scooby-Doo 2: Monsters Unleashed","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"The Mystery Inc. gang returns for a sillier, effects-heavy sequel built around a costume-exhibit heist and cartoonish monsters come to life. Expect frequent potty humor, mildly scary ghoulish creatures, a bar scene with beer, and a quick joke about Shaggy sniffing something that smells like marijuana. Underneath the slapstick, it still carries the original show's message about teamwork and looking past first impressions.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/scooby-doo-2-monsters-unleashed","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Mystery"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q581666","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1030,"t":"How the Grinch Stole Christmas","y":"2000","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"Ron Howard's live-action spin on the Dr. Seuss classic gives Jim Carrey's Grinch a manic, physically intense performance, with cartoonish fires, explosions, and falls, plus a few genuinely creepy moments and a threatening line aimed at kids. Mild crude language slips into the broad slapstick humor throughout. Despite the chaos, the story still lands its original message about kindness and community mattering more than presents.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/how-the-grinch-stole-christmas","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:How the Grinch Stole Christmas (2000 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1031,"t":"Charlie and the Chocolate Factory","y":"2005","la":"8+","ca":"9+","full":"Tim Burton's darker, more visually stylized take on Roald Dahl's story follows Charlie through Willy Wonka's factory alongside four misbehaving kids who each get a strange, fitting comeuppance -- one inflates like a giant blueberry, another is sucked up a pipe, another is dragged off by squirrels. The imagery leans more unsettling than the 1971 original, including an eerie flashback involving burned dolls. Charlie's own honesty and devotion to his struggling family anchor the film's message about character mattering more than greed.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/charlie-and-the-chocolate-factory-2005","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q218235","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1032,"t":"Cheaper by the Dozen","y":"2003","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Steve Martin and Bonnie Hunt play parents juggling a new coaching job, a book deal, and twelve kids, with the resulting chaos played for slapstick -- broken furniture, mild name-calling, and a running joke about a vasectomy. Adults are shown drinking champagne at a party, and mild language like \"damn\" pops up here and there. The family ultimately learns to put each other first over career ambition, a message about prioritizing family that anchors the comedy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cheaper-by-the-dozen","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q822930","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1033,"t":"Troop Beverly Hills","y":"1989","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This 1989 fish-out-of-water comedy is a silly parody of Beverly Hills excess, following socialite Phyllis Nefler as she reluctantly takes over her daughter's Wilderness Girls troop. Concerns include her near-constant smoking and daytime wine drinking, crude language, innuendo-laden jokes, and a steady parade of luxury-brand name-dropping that glamorizes materialism. On the positive side, Phyllis grows from a self-absorbed trophy wife into a genuinely attentive leader, and the girls are encouraged to embrace their own quirks rather than conform.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/troop-beverly-hills","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1217565","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1034,"t":"Alexander and the Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad Day","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"Loosely adapting Judith Viorst's classic book, this Disney comedy piles an entire family's disasters into one single day for 11-year-old Alexander. Concerns include his teen sister accidentally getting drunk on cough syrup, their dad's shirt catching fire, a car fender-bender during a driving test, and a cruel prank where a boy's photo is composited onto pinup images and circulated at school. Underneath the chaos, the story lands a sweet, book-based message about families sticking together and everyone having a bad day sometimes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alexander-and-the-terrible-horrible-no-good-very-bad-day","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15104217","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1035,"t":"Air Bud Returns","y":"2026","la":"6+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"This franchise relaunch follows grieving 12-year-old Jacob, who finds his late father's VHS tape of the original Air Bud and befriends a stray golden retriever, and the two chase a basketball dream together with a scrappy underdog team. Content concerns mirror the earlier films: a child processing the death of a parent is a persistent emotional undercurrent, alongside typical sports-movie competition and mild schoolyard conflict. Positive messages echo the series' hallmarks -- perseverance, teamwork, and healing through connection with an animal companion and a found community.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_Bud_Returns","addedAt":"2026-08-27","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Cineverse","runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Air Bud Returns","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1036,"t":"Scoob!","y":"2020","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Goofy Scooby reboot with hijinks and scenes of peril.\" There's cartoon chase-and-monster action (a giant three-headed dog, laser-shooting robots), name-calling insults, some gross-out humor, and a couple of mild innuendo lines. Positive: the gang leans on friendship, courage, and teamwork, and Shaggy discovers real bravery along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/scoob","addedAt":"2026-08-28","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23999279","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1037,"t":"The Greatest Showman","y":"2017","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A dazzling, loosely biographical musical about circus founder P.T. Barnum's rise, built around big anthems about chasing dreams and embracing people who don't fit in. Expect some kissing and light romance, a bar fight, mild language, and scenes of prejudice and public shaming directed at the show's performers, alongside genuinely positive messages about self-acceptance, found family, and standing up to bullies.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-greatest-showman","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27942936","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1038,"t":"Annie","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A modern-day update of the classic hard-knock-life musical, following foster kid Annie as she's temporarily taken in by a self-serving mayoral candidate. A boozy, hostile foster mother verbally torments the kids in her care, there are a couple of tense scenes where Annie is in danger, mild language, and heavy brand product placement -- but the film's core is about family, honesty, and hope winning out over greedy, scheming adults.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/annie-2014","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15039835","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1039,"t":"Wicked","y":"2024","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Part one of the big-screen Broadway adaptation, tracing how green-skinned Elphaba and blonde Glinda go from rival roommates to unlikely friends before Elphaba is branded the \"Wicked Witch.\" There are light jump-scares (flying monkeys, the Wizard's giant floating head), bullying and prejudice aimed at Elphaba for being different, mild name-calling, and brief suggestive material, balanced against strong messages about accepting difference, questioning propaganda, and loyalty between friends.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wicked","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":160,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q24797403","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1040,"t":"Wicked: For Good","y":"2025","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"The darker second half of the Wicked story, as Elphaba is hunted as a fugitive and Glinda rises to power under the Wizard's regime. Expect fantasy and more realistic violence -- flying-monkey attacks, mob aggression, fights, pistol threats, and a magically created storm that results in a character's death -- plus heavier emotional stakes and more romance than part one. The throughline stays positive: who we become is shaped by our own choices, not other people's judgment, and no one is entirely good or wicked.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wicked-for-good","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":4,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":137,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q114817050","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1041,"t":"Pokémon Detective Pikachu","y":"2019","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A live-action mystery-adventure where a wisecracking Pikachu (voiced by Ryan Reynolds) teams up with a teenager to solve his missing father's disappearance in a city where humans and Pokémon live side by side. There's a lab fire and a fatal car crash early on, Pokémon battles that cause injuries and property damage, a tense chase through a shifting dreamlike landscape, and a couple of mild innuendos, alongside solid messages about teamwork, courage, and friendship. Resolved from a generic \"Pokémon movies\" request -- Detective Pikachu is the best-known Pokémon film not yet in the catalog (the 20+ numbered anime films are out of scope for one batch; \"Pokémon: The First Movie\" is already at num 948).","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pokemon-detective-pikachu","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Mystery"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Detective Pikachu (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1042,"t":"Minions","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Illumination's origin story for Gru's yellow henchmen follows a trio of Minions on a globe-trotting 1960s quest to find a new evil boss, landing them with supervillain Scarlet Overkill. It's mostly slapstick and gag-based, but there are cartoonish battles, freeze-ray zaps, torture-device sight gags, a few glimpses of bare Minion behinds, and mild infrequent insults like \"idiot\" and \"loser.\" The story leans into the appeal of being bad, but it also rewards loyalty, teamwork, and sticking with friends through failure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/minions","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q13619743","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1043,"t":"Saving Bikini Bottom: The Sandy Cheeks Movie","y":"2024","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"In this SpongeBob spinoff, marine biologist Sandy Cheeks gets to be the hero: when a corporate villain scoops up all of Bikini Bottom to harvest for a pet-transformation scheme, Sandy has to out-science and out-fight her way to a rescue. Peril stays cartoonish -- characters are cloned, trapped in a containment globe, launched from cannons, and chased by rattlesnakes -- and language is limited to mild insults and a fake-swear (\"holy sugar cookies\"). Sandy herself is a brave, brainy, athletic role model who leads with curiosity and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/saving-bikini-bottom-the-sandy-cheeks-movie","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q118196554","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1044,"t":"Plankton: The Movie","y":"2025","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"This darker, musical SpongeBob spinoff centers on Plankton admitting his endless Krabby Patty schemes have wrecked his marriage to his AI wife Karen, who responds by turning into a world-conquering robot he has to stop with SpongeBob's help. A giant robot lays siege to Bikini Bottom with explosions and cannon fire, and Karen's monstrous robotic form may unsettle younger viewers, though the destruction stays cartoonish. Insults like \"moron\" and \"idiot\" show up but nothing stronger, and the film pushes a real message about owning your mistakes and choosing empathy over greed.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/plankton-the-movie","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Plankton: The Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1045,"t":"Extinct","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"This Netflix original follows donut-shaped siblings Ed and Op, the last of a species called flummels, who get flung from 1835 into present-day Shanghai and learn their whole kind died out while they were gone. It's a comic sci-fi adventure with cartoon slapstick violence and mild scares, though the siblings bicker and say hurtful things to each other along the way, and there's a running joke about the blue-footed booby. The heart of the film is Ed and Op learning to set aside their rivalry and work together, with a light nod to real ideas about extinction and conservation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/extinct","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q85760113","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1046,"t":"Pets United","y":"2019","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A stray dog named Roger, wrongly hunted by robot police in a city called Robo City, teams up with a friendly robot pet and a ragtag group of animals after the city's mayor exiles every non-robot resident. This leans hard into action for a family cartoon -- chases, fights, a dog shot with a net gun, flying knives, car and train crashes, and an animal seemingly crushed by a scrap-metal machine -- alongside mild insults and one mild swear. The underlying message is misfits banding together against an unjust system, aiming at loyalty and standing up for the vulnerable.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pets-united","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Action"],"studio":"Serious Productions","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q98931267","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1047,"t":"Latte and the Magic Waterstone","y":"2019","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"A gentle computer-animated adventure about a brave young hedgehog named Latte who sets out to recover a stolen magic waterstone so her drought-stricken forest can have water again. There are a handful of playground-style scuffles (shoving, slapping), some verbal bullying about being different, and a few chase sequences where Latte and her friends are pursued by predators or tumble down cliffs -- all mild and cartoonish. Latte models courage, determination, and persistence, and the story's message is that natural resources like water belong to everyone, not the powerful few.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/latte-and-the-magic-waterstone","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Dreamin' Dolphin Film","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q76025588","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1048,"t":"Arlo the Alligator Boy","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A sweet, goofy animated musical road-trip about a half-alligator, half-human boy who leaves the bayou to track down the father he's never known, picking up an oddball found family along the way. There's a shadowy, threatening \"beast\" that looms over much of the film, mild cartoon violence, a couple of adult-aimed jokes that will sail over kids' heads, and some old-fashioned Southern stereotypes among characters who want to exploit Arlo as a tourist attraction. Its heart is in the right place: messages of belonging, being your true self, and valuing friendship over wealth or fitting in.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/arlo-the-alligator-boy","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Netflix","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q102036294","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1049,"t":"Scrooge: A Christmas Carol","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Netflix's big, energetic musical retelling of Dickens' classic -- Ebenezer Scrooge gets visited by three ghosts on Christmas Eve and is pushed toward redemption, set to original songs. The ghost sequences run genuinely eerie for younger viewers, Scrooge is comically electrocuted at one point, and there's slapstick violence and insult-style name-calling, plus a brief kiss and a passing mention of wine at dinner. The throughline is strongly positive: real change and generosity are possible for anyone willing to open their heart, even someone as miserly as Scrooge.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/scrooge-a-christmas-carol","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Holiday"],"studio":"Timeless Films","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q115091011","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1050,"t":"Hilda and the Mountain King","y":"2021","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"In this darker, feature-length continuation of the Netflix series, adventurous Hilda is magically swapped bodies with a troll baby -- she's stuck living as a troll in the eerie caves under the mountain while the troll now walks around in her old life with her mom. It leans into genuinely dark, atmospheric visuals and sound design from the opening scene on, with real dangers like falls from cliffs alongside fantastical threats of being stomped on or eaten by giant trolls, plus a sustained separation-anxiety thread. Hilda stays resourceful, empathetic, and brave throughout, with real emotional depth about identity, belonging, and what makes a family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hilda-and-the-mountain-king","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Silvergate Media","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q110287209","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1051,"t":"Dog Gone Trouble","y":"2021","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A pampered dog named Trouble loses his cushy mansion life when his elderly owner dies and her greedy relatives dump him out of a moving van; lost in the woods, he has to team up with a ragtag pack of strays and a struggling street musician to find his way home. Expect dogs in peril throughout -- younger kids may find the premise sad -- plus animated skirmishes between the dogs and a gang of squirrels, close-call traffic scares, shouting matches, and scatological humor along with mild name-calling. The message lands well for elementary-age viewers: love, loyalty, and family matter more than money or material comfort.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dog-gone-trouble","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Vanguard Animation","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Trouble (2019 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1052,"t":"Orion and the Dark","y":"2024","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A Charlie Kaufman-written tale in which an anxiety-ridden 11-year-old boy is whisked away for a night with a talking personification of Dark itself, who wants to prove that nighttime isn't something to fear. It's funnier and more emotionally sophisticated than a typical kids' cartoon, but also more intense: Orion's fear-fueled imagination conjures menacing clowns, swarming bees, and a fall from a skyscraper, plus public humiliation and a school bully, with a handful of mild insults. The payoff is a genuinely useful message for anxious kids: facing fears head-on is more empowering than avoiding them.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/orion-and-the-dark","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q119455303","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1053,"t":"Octonauts & the Caves of Sac Actun","y":"2020","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"A feature-length outing for the preschool-friendly underwater rescue crew, in which Captain Barnacles and Peso escort a young octopus named Coba back to his Caribbean home, only to get diverted into a maze of flooded Mexican caves. The team faces cave-ins, dwindling air supply, and encounters with cave-dwelling predators -- played more seriously than a typical episode but never graphic. The Octonauts model calm teamwork, perseverance, and courage under pressure; note that the story stays tightly focused on their own crew rather than showing much curiosity about the people they encounter along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/octonauts-the-caves-of-sac-actun","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Silvergate Media","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"australian-classification:T20/2856","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1054,"t":"Octonauts & the Ring of Fire","y":"2021","la":"4+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"This Octonauts special sends the crew into the volcanically active Pacific \"Ring of Fire\" after a chain of undersea eruptions triggers tsunamis and strands ocean animals, including a beached whale the team races to save. It's TV-Y and stays true to the franchise's gentle preschool tone, but the disaster-movie premise -- erupting volcanoes, tidal waves, animals in real danger -- pushes the peril a notch higher than a typical episode. The throughline is classic Octonauts: quick thinking, ingenuity, and cooperative rescue work, with every creature saved by the end.","srcUrl":"https://octonauts.fandom.com/wiki/The_Octonauts_and_the_Ring_of_Fire","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Silvergate Media","runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"thetvdb:342734","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1055,"t":"Octonauts & the Great Barrier Reef","y":"2020","la":"4+","ca":"4+","full":"A musical Octonauts special built around a coral polyp named Corey who dreams of growing into a full coral, only to have his home reef threatened by a swarm of hungry, coral-eating starfish. It doubles as a gentle environmental-science lesson on real reef ecosystems, delivered through original songs. Sensitive younger viewers might feel a little worried watching the reef and its creatures put in danger, but the show never lingers on the threat and resolves it with a hopeful ending, modeling teamwork, kindness, and outreach to a scared new friend.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/octonauts-the-great-barrier-reef","addedAt":"2026-09-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Silvergate Media","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-08","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":47,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q102395499","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1056,"t":"Home Alone 2: Lost in New York","y":"1992","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Kevin gets separated from his family again on a holiday trip and ends up alone in New York City, outwitting the same two bumbling burglars from the first film using elaborate booby traps. The slapstick violence against the crooks is even more over-the-top than the original -- falls, electrocutions, and blunt-force gags played entirely for laughs, with no real injuries taken seriously. Being separated from his family is central to the plot and could be unsettling for a child prone to separation anxiety, though the tone stays comedic rather than frightening. Kevin's resourcefulness and problem-solving carry the film, alongside a reminder that spending time with family matters more than any comfort or getaway.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/home-alone-2-lost-in-new-york","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q221202","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1057,"t":"Home Alone 3","y":"1997","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A new lead character (no returning cast from the first two films) uses booby traps to fend off a group of international thieves after a stolen microchip hidden in his toy car. The trap sequences are more intense than earlier films -- exaggerated electric shocks, vehicle crashes, and explosive mishaps -- and the criminals are shown carrying real guns, which may be more unsettling for younger or sensitive kids than the cartoonish slapstick of the earlier movies. He's left alone while sick with chickenpox rather than through a travel mix-up, so the separation is framed differently than the original. Positive themes of resourcefulness and standing up to danger carry through, though the film is generally considered weaker than the first two.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/home-alone-3","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Action"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q382320","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1058,"t":"Descendants: Wicked Wonderland","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"The fifth film in Disney's fairy-tale-inspired musical franchise sends Red and Chloe into a magical dreamworld to rescue Red's mother, the Queen of Hearts. Expect fantasy peril rather than realistic violence -- falls, dodging falling objects, getting lost, being taken prisoner, and a tense scene riding a giant teacup through rough seas -- along with magical duels using spells and colorful bursts of energy. No sexual content, no real-world substance use (potions and enchanted treats are fantastical, not drinking), and only mild insults for language. Some villain scenes and the rough-seas sequence could be intense for younger or more sensitive kids. The story leans on the franchise's usual themes of loyalty and teamwork, built around Red and Chloe's friendship and a rescue mission.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/descendants-wicked-wonderland","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Descendants: Wicked Wonderland","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1059,"t":"Mac and Me","y":"1988","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"A young wheelchair-using boy befriends a stranded alien in this late-1980s family sci-fi adventure, widely regarded as a well-meaning but weaker imitation of a more famous alien-friendship film. The alien is connected to a few vehicle-collision scenes played as comic peril rather than real danger, and the film is notorious for unusually heavy, repeated on-screen branding for a fast-food chain. The alien's separation from its own family, and the human family's own cross-country move, both echo a loose \"finding home\" theme, but the tone stays light adventure rather than heavy drama. Positive messages center on kindness, acceptance, and friendship, and the wheelchair-using lead is portrayed as capable and resourceful rather than defined by his disability.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mac-and-me","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Orion Pictures","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1761515","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1060,"t":"Tom and Jerry: Forbidden Compass","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"No Common Sense Media review exists yet for this new theatrical release, so content details here come from other parents-guide sources rather than CSM directly. Tom and Jerry chase each other through a museum and stumble into a fantasy world inspired by Chinese mythology after finding a magic compass. Expect the franchise's usual frequent slapstick violence -- characters struck, shocked, and shot at with arrows -- plus a flooding/collapsing-structure peril sequence and a scene involving a character being intoxicated by a drink. Minor name-calling and one brief comment about a character's looks are noted, but nothing more serious. Themes of teamwork, cooperation, responsibility, and courage run through the adventure, consistent with the franchise's usual style.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_and_Jerry:_Forbidden_Compass","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Tom and Jerry: Forbidden Compass","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1061,"t":"Barbie in the Nutcracker","y":"2026","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"This all-new 45-minute animated special reimagines Barbie's original 2001 holiday film for its 25th anniversary, with Barbie \"Brooklyn\" as the Sugarplum Princess and Barbie \"Malibu\" as Clara on a musical journey through a magical dreamworld. No Common Sense Media review exists yet for this new special specifically, so this entry is written from general coverage rather than a full CSM breakdown; the original 2001 film (CSM age 5+) featured some mild peril from a menacing Mouse King, and a similarly gentle tone is a reasonable expectation here, though that's not confirmed for this new version. No sad or emotional content is indicated in available coverage. The special is built around courage and friendship as its central themes, framed as a lighthearted holiday adventure.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbie_in_the_Nutcracker_(2026_film)","addedAt":"2026-09-11","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Holiday"],"studio":"Netflix","runtimeMinutes":45,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Barbie in the Nutcracker (2026 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1062,"t":"Descendants: The Royal Wedding","y":"2021","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"An animated Disney Channel TV special and direct sequel to Descendants 3, following Mal and Ben as they prepare for their wedding in Auradon while friends help with decorations, hair, and party planning -- until Hades threatens to crash the celebration. Content is mild: some peril from falls, chases, and characters escaping fire, plus images of dragons breathing fire and a villain being deliberately mean, but nothing more intense than the mainline films. No sexual content beyond wedding-day romance, no real-world substance use, and only mild insults for language. Worth knowing: this special quietly honors the memory of actor Cameron Boyce, who died in 2019 -- his character Carlos isn't recast, and his absence is acknowledged rather than explained away, which could prompt a question from a kid who remembers him from the earlier films. Themes center on friendship, loyalty, and that true love (and a good wedding) is worth the effort.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/descendants-the-royal-wedding","addedAt":"2026-09-12","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":22,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q107484397","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1063,"t":"La La Land","y":"2016","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"A modern-day romantic musical set in Los Angeles, starring a struggling jazz pianist and an aspiring actress, told in old-Hollywood musical-number style and ending on a bittersweet note about the tradeoffs between love and ambition. Content parents should know: one use of the f-word plus scattered milder profanity, wine and bar/party drinking in a couple of scenes, some kissing and a scene of the couple waking up together in bed (nothing explicit), and a single aggressive gesture during a traffic-jam argument. Positive messages center on pursuing your dreams and staying true to yourself, with love and creative ambition treated seriously rather than played for laughs. One nuance worth knowing: a subplot has the male lead lecturing a Black musician friend about jazz, a dynamic some viewers find tone-deaf given the genre's roots in Black musical tradition.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/la-la-land","addedAt":"2026-09-17","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"Lionsgate","runtimeMinutes":128,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:La La Land","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1064,"t":"RocketMan","y":"1997","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A klutzy, awkward NASA engineer accidentally ends up launched on the first manned mission to Mars after a paperwork mix-up, then has to prove himself as an astronaut mid-flight. Leans on slapstick and some toilet humor rather than classic Disney charm -- expect pratfalls not to be imitated at home, plus a genuinely perilous space-accident sequence where the crew nearly dies, which could be intense for younger kids. No sexual content beyond mild flirtation, no substance use, and only mild language. CSM recommends it for kids 7 and up given the peril and cruder humor, closer in tone to a broad slapstick comedy than the studio's more polished family classics.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rocketman","addedAt":"2026-09-17","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q5550401","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1065,"t":"Camp Rock 3","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A reboot of Disney's Camp Rock franchise, introducing a new cast of camper misfits who start out competing against each other before learning they're stronger as a team, with cameos from the original stars (Demi Lovato, the Jonas Brothers as Connect 3) tying it back to Camp Rock (2008) and Camp Rock 2 (2010). Expect catchy musical numbers, blooming teen romance -- longing glances, an almost-kiss -- and some social-bullying dynamics like passive-aggression and hidden or damaged belongings, though softer than in the earlier films. No real violence, no substance use, and only mild language. Positive messages center on empowerment, perseverance, and accepting yourself and others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/camp-rock-3","addedAt":"2026-09-17","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Camp Rock 3","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1066,"t":"The Pagemaster","y":"1994","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"A timid, overprotected boy takes shelter in a library during a storm and is magically transformed into an animated character, journeying through classic books -- adventure, fantasy, and horror -- to find his way home. It's mostly cartoon peril rather than anything graphic: characters fall from great heights, get chased by a scary ghost-hound and a dragon, and face a genuinely creepy Dr. Jekyll/Mr. Hyde transformation sequence that CSM and parent reviewers flag as frightening for kids under 6, even though the official age rating is 5+. There's no language, romance, or drinking/drug content, and no grief or loss themes. At its heart it celebrates the joy of reading and imagination, with a timid boy finding real courage and confidence through his adventure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-pagemaster","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1196110","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1067,"t":"Rookie of the Year","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A 12-year-old boy breaks his arm, and it heals so tightly that he can suddenly throw a 100+ mph fastball -- landing him a spot pitching for the real-life struggling Chicago Cubs. There's some mild language (\"hell,\" a near-miss stronger word cut off before it's said), and brief background smoking and adult cocktail-drinking in a club scene. Worth knowing: Henry's father is established as deceased, a former minor-league player -- a loss that's part of his backstory but not a dwelt-on plot focus. The film's real strength is its underdog-achieves-dream story, with themes of perseverance, teamwork, and not letting money-driven adults exploit you, plus a warm mentorship arc with a veteran player.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/rookie-of-the-year","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3212960","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1068,"t":"Little Giants","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"When his football-star brother won't let his talented daughter play because she's a girl, a mild-mannered dad starts a rival Pee Wee football team made up of misfits and outcasts to take him on. Expect mild rude/crude humor typical of a '90s PG comedy and some football roughhousing/trash talk, but nothing graphic. There's a mild romantic subplot -- a girl on the team offers to teach a teammate to kiss \"for practice\" and is stung when he initially prefers a \"cheerleader type\" -- played innocently rather than sexualized. No grief or loss themes. Strong messages about gender inclusion, teamwork over raw talent, good sportsmanship, and standing up to a bullying authority figure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/little-giants","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1401572","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1069,"t":"The Big Green","y":"1995","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A British exchange teacher in a down-on-its-luck small Texas town starts a ragtag youth soccer team out of a class of kids everyone's written off, and their surprising success helps revive the whole community. Content is mostly mild -- some pushing/shoving among classmates and typical bored-kid mischief -- but worth flagging explicitly: one main child character's father is shown as a heavy drinker, passed out drunk at a bar, a real reference to alcoholism and parental neglect rather than just vague \"family issues.\" There's also a light, non-explicit romance thread between the two adult coaches. Positive messages center on believing in overlooked kids, self-worth over being written off, and community coming together, with the alcoholic-parent storyline handled through mentorship rather than left unaddressed.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-big-green","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q753676","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1070,"t":"Despicable Me 3","y":"2017","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Reformed supervillain Gru gets fired from the Anti-Villain League and, mid identity-crisis, discovers he has a long-lost identical twin brother, Dru, who wants his help pulling off one last heist against a washed-up '80s child star turned supervillain. Action leans heavier than the first two films (a destructive laser-armed robot, giant gumball weapons), and there's a played-for-laughs nudity gag where a weapon blows off characters' clothes, strategically covered by bubblegum. Language is mild (\"loser,\" \"screw up\"). No death or grief, but real themes of identity, belonging, and reconciling with a brother he never knew existed. Strong messages about family and sibling loyalty, with Lucy remaining a competent, positive role model.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/despicable-me-3","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22997984","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1071,"t":"Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs","y":"2009","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A failed small-town inventor builds a machine that turns water into food, raining cheeseburgers and spaghetti tornadoes on his town -- until it spirals out of control and starts producing giant, dangerous mutant food. Several disaster-movie-style sequences (food monsters destroying the town) could unsettle kids sensitive to storm/danger imagery, alongside mild language and a light mutual-crush romance. Worth knowing: Flint's mother is deceased, and much of the film's emotional core is his strained, awkward relationship with his widowed, unsupportive father -- a real undercurrent of loss and distance, not just background color. It resolves warmly, with messages against overconsumption and strong themes of creativity and persistence through failure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cloudy-with-a-chance-of-meatballs","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q637169","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1072,"t":"The Road to El Dorado","y":"2000","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Two small-time Spanish con artists win a map to the legendary lost city of gold, stow away to the New World, and end up worshipped as gods after they arrive in El Dorado. Expect mild swordfights and chases, some mild swearing, and a notable amount of adult-aimed sexual innuendo and flirtation that pushes above younger-kid appropriateness. Parents should also know the portrayal of the Indigenous civilization has been criticized as racially stereotyped, including a villainous \"maniacal\" priest and the two White leads being treated as literal gods -- a dated, uncomfortable element worth knowing about going in. No grief or death themes; the real conflict is greed and betrayal. Ultimately the leads choose friendship and loyalty over riches.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-road-to-el-dorado","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"DreamWorks","runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q866358","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1073,"t":"Osmosis Jones","y":"2001","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Inside the body of a slobby, unhealthy zookeeper named Frank, a rule-breaking white-blood-cell cop teams up with a by-the-book cold-pill capsule to stop a deadly virus within 48 hours, while outside the body Frank's own health crisis worries his young daughter. Heavy on gross-out humor (vomiting, pimple-popping, snot) plus a live-action character smoking a cigar throughout and an inside-the-body bar scene with alcohol-styled drinks. Important to know: Frank is a widower, and his depression and self-neglect after his wife's death is the reason his body is so vulnerable in the first place -- his daughter is shown emotionally withdrawn and worried as a result, a real grief undercurrent beneath the comedy. Underneath it all is a genuine biology lesson and a sincere father-daughter reconnection arc.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/osmosis-jones","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q966690","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1074,"t":"Looney Tunes: Back in Action","y":"2003","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Fired from the studio, Daffy Duck teams up with a studio exec's son to rescue the boy's secret-agent father from the villainous head of the ACME Corporation, in a globe-trotting live-action/animation romp. It's wall-to-wall cartoon violence and slapstick peril -- explosions, falls, chases -- but nobody is ever actually hurt, plus a little potty humor, a couple of mildly naughty words, and brief cross-dressing gags. No drinking/drugs or romance beyond light kissing bits, and no grief, death, or loss themes. A fast, funny introduction to classic Looney Tunes characters, with themes of loyalty and teamwork between Daffy and his young companion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/looney-tunes-back-in-action","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q834165","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1075,"t":"The Nutcracker Prince","y":"1990","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"On Christmas Eve, young Clara's nutcracker doll comes to life as a prince and whisks her into a magical battle against the sinister Mouse King to break a witch's curse. This version leans darker and scarier than the gentler ballet adaptations: the Mouse King is genuinely frightening, there's a sword duel with visible blood, the Mouse Queen's corpse is shown on screen, and the Mouse King later tries to kill Clara -- real nightmare-fuel potential for younger kids. The word \"hell\" is used once; no sexual content beyond a chaste fairy-tale romance, no drinking/drugs, and no death of a major sympathetic character. Clara shows real courage and cleverness, using self-sacrifice to save the Nutcracker Prince, with themes of bravery and breaking curses through kindness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-nutcracker-prince","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Holiday"],"studio":"Lacewood Productions","runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q45847","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1076,"t":"Rover Dangerfield","y":"1991","la":"8+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"A wisecracking Las Vegas lounge dog is dumped in a lake by his showgirl owner's gangster-connected boyfriend, survives, and finds a new life -- and love -- on a countryside farm. Despite its G rating, this has some surprisingly dark beats: an implied attempted-murder sequence (Rover is bagged and thrown into a reservoir), a turkey corpse used as a puppet for dark comedy, a farmer who appears to consider shooting a dog, and a wolf attack with a gunshot -- the film was originally written as an R-rated adult script and heavily re-cut, which explains the tonal edge. No sexual content beyond a sweet dog-crush storyline, and no on-screen death. Real themes of resilience, adapting after losing everything familiar, and choosing genuine community and love over empty glitz.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_Dangerfield","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3139910","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1077,"t":"Mr. Bean's Holiday","y":"2007","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"Mr. Bean wins a dream vacation to the French Riviera, and his string of accident-prone misadventures ends up separating a young boy, Stepan, from his father. Mostly gentle, cartoonish slapstick with no real injuries, but worth knowing: there's a genuine suicide-attempt scene played for dark comedy (a heartbroken man climbs onto a bridge; no violence is shown and it resolves comedically) and a drunk stranger who approaches Stepan at a train station. The father-son separation carries real, if brief, emotional stakes for young viewers even though it resolves happily. Ultimately a heartwarming story about accidental kindness, found friendship across a language barrier, and a genuinely happy reunion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/mr-beans-holiday","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q330332","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1078,"t":"Paulie","y":"1998","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"A talking parrot recounts, to a sympathetic janitor, his years-long cross-country quest to reunite with Marie, the little girl who raised him and was forced to give him up. Content is otherwise mild -- a few insults, one background beer-drinking scene -- but the emotional core is genuinely sad: young Marie is torn from Paulie against her will while crying and calling for him, and much of the story deals with years of loss, longing, and searching, which could hit hard for kids with separation anxiety or grief over a lost pet. Strong themes of loyalty, resilience, and the idea that being different doesn't make you unlovable, building to a heartfelt reunion.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paulie","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"DreamWorks","runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2533075","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1079,"t":"Hotel for Dogs","y":"2009","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"Two orphaned siblings cycling through the foster system secretly convert a derelict hotel into a gadget-filled refuge for the neighborhood's stray dogs. It's a lighthearted comedy built on slapstick sight gags, with only very mild language and a couple of innocent teen kisses. Worth flagging: the kids are grieving the loss of their parents and fear being separated from each other in foster care -- a real family-loss and separation thread underlying the comedy, though it resolves warmly. A solid pick for animal-loving kids, with strong messages about responsibility, resourcefulness, sibling loyalty, and choosing your own family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/hotel-for-dogs","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"DreamWorks","runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q662703","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1080,"t":"Racing Stripes","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A zebra foal, accidentally left behind by a traveling circus and raised on a Kentucky horse farm, dreams of racing the track's snobby thoroughbred champions. The humor leans heavily on bathroom jokes (poop, pee, gas) plus a surprising amount of adult-aimed innuendo, with words like \"s--t,\" \"bitch,\" and \"ass\" repeatedly implied or nearly spoken as a running gag that mostly goes over younger kids' heads. No drinking/drugs, real violence, or sad/emotional content. A fun underdog story about believing in yourself and it being okay to be different, with a found community among the farm animals.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/racing-stripes","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1165633","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1081,"t":"Kicking & Screaming","y":"2005","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"A mild-mannered dad takes over his son's hapless youth soccer team purely to finally beat his own hyper-competitive father. Runs a bit rough for kids' fare: it includes played-for-laughs but genuinely uncomfortable scenes of adults being physically aggressive with children (the dad kicks his own son; the grandfather shoves a kid into a pool, both framed as being in the wrong), plus bar drinking and a running gag about spiking coffee with vodka. No sexual content or grief/loss themes. Ultimately critiques win-at-all-costs coaching and toxic competitive parenting, modeling an adult learning to prioritize sportsmanship and kids' enjoyment over winning.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kicking-screaming","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q284086","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1082,"t":"Andre","y":"1994","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A shy young girl in a 1960s Maine fishing town befriends an orphaned harbor seal pup, and their bond changes how the whole town sees him. There's more edge here than the cute-seal premise suggests: teenagers are shown smoking, a character gets visibly drunk, there's a fistfight, and in one tense scene a local boy fires a shotgun at Andre, believing him a threat. Andre is not killed -- he survives every peril and the film ends with him alive, splitting time between an aquarium and the family. No sexual/romantic content, and no death or permanent loss. A warm story about tolerance for those who are different, loyalty, and standing up for a vulnerable creature.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/andre","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q501407","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1083,"t":"Prancer","y":"1989","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"An eight-year-old girl who still believes in Santa finds an injured reindeer in the woods, becomes convinced it's Prancer, and secretly nurses it back to health while trying to hold her grieving family together. Important to know: Jessica's mother has died before the story begins, and her father has grown cold and withdrawn as a result -- no on-screen death occurs during the film, but that earlier loss is the emotional engine of the whole story. A hunting rifle is fired and the reindeer is shown wounded (not killed), and there's some dated, casually negative talk about mental illness typical of an older film. Ultimately a tender story about faith, kindness to an injured creature, and a father and daughter finding their way back to each other after loss.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/prancer","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Holiday"],"studio":"Orion Pictures","runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1688276","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1084,"t":"The Secret of Roan Inish","y":"1994","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A young Irish girl sent to live with her grandparents on the coast becomes obsessed with the family legend that her baby brother, swept out to sea years earlier, is still alive and being raised by the seal-people of Roan Inish. The storm/cradle sequence and a scene of birds attacking two fishermen can be genuinely scary for younger or sensitive kids, and the emotional core is a family's long grief over a possibly-lost child -- importantly, no one actually dies on screen, and the story resolves with the baby found alive. No violence beyond the bird attack, no language or drinking/drug concerns, and only the faintest hint of pre-teen romance among village kids. A quiet, atmospheric film with strong messages about family devotion, courage, and honoring heritage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-secret-of-roan-inish","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Samuel Goldwyn Company","runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2255971","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1085,"t":"Dreamer","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"A down-on-his-luck horse trainer and his young daughter defy the odds to rehabilitate a racehorse injured in a bad fall and chase a Breeders' Cup dream, mending their family along the way. An early, intense scene shows the horse break her leg mid-race, and her owner initially wants to put her down -- frightening for sensitive viewers, though she is saved, recovers fully, and survives (and wins) by the end; no human or animal death occurs. Mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\"), brief wine drinking at an adult gathering, and real but non-scary family tension, including a father who loses his job and a rocky relationship with the grandfather that heals over the story. An uplifting underdog story about perseverance and father-daughter bonding.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dreamer-inspired-by-a-true-story","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Sports"],"studio":"DreamWorks","runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q625488","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1086,"t":"The Court Jester","y":"1955","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A cowardly former carnival entertainer poses as a jester to infiltrate a usurper king's castle and help restore the rightful infant heir to the throne. The swashbuckling is broad and cartoonish -- jousting, sword fights, a wild fencing match -- with no blood and nothing scarier than a chase scene. There's some mild romance (passionate kisses, low-cut period dresses) typical of 1950s Hollywood, but nothing explicit, no bad language, and no grief or loss themes. Underneath the slapstick and rapid-fire wordplay are solid messages about courage, wit beating brute force, and doing right even when scared.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-court-jester","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Court Jester","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1087,"t":"Mr. Hulot's Holiday","y":"1953","la":"5+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Jacques Tati's nearly wordless French comedy follows the awkward, well-meaning Monsieur Hulot as his presence at a seaside resort sets off one small disaster after another -- a folding canoe, a runaway tire mistaken for a funeral wreath, misfired fireworks. There's no violence, romance, bad language, or scary content of any kind; the only thing to note is background era-typical pipe smoking and wine at meals. Its real substance is in how one clumsy, sincere outsider's good intentions bring unexpected joy and connection to everyone around him -- essentially content-free, though its slow, dialogue-free pace may test action-hungry kids' patience rather than raise any real content flags.","srcUrl":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0046487/parentalguide/","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"Cady Films","runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Les Vacances de Monsieur Hulot","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1088,"t":"A Hard Day's Night","y":"1964","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A fictionalized, madcap day in the life of The Beatles as they dash between train rides, press conferences, and a live TV performance while trying to keep Paul's mischievous grandfather out of trouble. Content concerns are minimal: constant background cigarette smoking (standard for 1964), one mild swear (\"damn\"), a joking reference to an \"orgy\" that will sail over kids' heads, and brief drug-related humor most children won't catch. No violence and nothing sad or heavy. An infectious, funny introduction to the Beatles' music and personalities, modeling quick wit, friendship, and harmless irreverence toward authority.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-hard-days-night","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"MGM","runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:A Hard Day's Night (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1089,"t":"Shaun the Sheep: The Beast of Mossy Bottom","y":"2026","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"When Shaun's homemade growth potion accidentally turns Farmer into a hairy, Bigfoot-like beast, the Mossy Bottom flock scrambles through slapstick schemes to set things right before Halloween chaos takes over. True to its title, the film spoofs light horror-movie tropes -- a mysterious beast in dark woods, jump-scare setups, and winking nods to Psycho and \"Thriller\" -- but reviewers agree the scares are immediately punctured by jokes and cartoonish gags (rakes to the face, pratfalls) rather than anything genuinely frightening. There's no dialogue, language, romance, or drinking/drug content, consistent with the wordless Shaun the Sheep style. A couple of moments with the mysterious \"beast\" and dark nighttime chase scenes could be a bit intense for very young or easily-spooked kids. Carries the franchise's gentle, genuine messages about teamwork and looking out for each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shaun-the-sheep-the-beast-of-mossy-bottom","addedAt":"2026-09-22","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Aardman","runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q134694705","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1090,"t":"The Muppets' Wizard of Oz","y":"2005","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"This Muppet-cast retelling of The Wizard of Oz works on two levels: broad slapstick and songs for kids, plus plenty of knowing gags aimed squarely at the adults watching along (film-director Kermit gets \"notes\" from a cameoing Quentin Tarantino on how violent to make a scene, and there are winking nods to R-rated movies most kids won't recognize). The fantasy peril is played for laughs rather than real scares -- the Scarecrow and Tin Man get comically torn apart and reassembled, and the Wicked Witch (Miss Piggy) tussles with Dorothy -- and there's a passing grown-up conversation about what counts as \"sexy\" that will go over younger viewers' heads. The ending nudges Dorothy toward chasing music-industry stardom rather than being content at home, a slightly mixed message parents may want to talk through. Underneath the gags, it's still a Muppet story about friendship and finding the courage/heart/brains you already had.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-muppets-wizard-of-oz","addedAt":"2026-09-25","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1953440","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1091,"t":"Alexander and the Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad Road Trip","y":"2025","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A spiritual sequel to the 2014 film (not a direct continuation), this Disney+ comedy follows a loving Mexican American family on a mishap-filled road trip in the spirit of National Lampoon's Vacation. The humor comes from a string of escalating disasters -- several car, trailer, and truck crashes played broadly for comedy -- that result in one character getting a black eye and, at points, put the kids in momentary movie-style peril (a brief risk of drowning, a close call with an explosion) before everything resolves safely. Nothing lingers or turns genuinely frightening. Positive messages carry the film: the family's mishaps ultimately pull them closer together, modeling resilience, humor under pressure, and sticking together when a plan falls apart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alexander-and-the-terrible-horrible-no-good-very-bad-road-trip","addedAt":"2026-09-25","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Alexander and the Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad Road Trip","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1092,"t":"Cheaper by the Dozen 2","y":"2005","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"This sequel pits the large Baker family against a rival family (led by Eugene Levy) during a competitive lake-house vacation, leaning harder into slapstick roughhousing and obnoxious, childish one-upmanship between the two dads than the original did. Content concerns include some tight/cleavage-focused clothing shots, a stretch of homophobic-tinged joking, and mild profanity; parents in general are shown behaving less admirably here than in the first film, more caught up in the competition than in their kids. Underneath the crude-humor stretches, the family's rivalry ultimately resolves with both families rediscovering that connection and togetherness matter more than winning.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cheaper-by-the-dozen-2","addedAt":"2026-09-25","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q911128","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1093,"t":"Forgotten Island","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A fast-moving animated fantasy-adventure set partly in the 1990s Philippines, where a girl named Raissa and a friend fall through a portal into Nakali, a mystical island world built from Philippine mythology. The film turns genuinely intense in its back half: the antagonist is the Manananggal, a self-segmenting, shapeshifting vampire-demon (voiced by Lea Salonga) that multiple reviewers single out as a real, unnerving scare rather than comic-book peril -- the MPAA's PG rating specifically cites \"scary action\" and \"some violence,\" not just language and rude humor. Several reviewers describe the tonal shift as too intense for kids under 8 and recommend skipping it for that age, which lines up with the 8+ rating here. Underneath the scares, it's a heartfelt friendship story about two kids navigating a strange, dangerous world together, with a clear, loving portrayal of Filipino culture and mythology.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/forgotten-island","addedAt":"2026-09-25","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"DreamWorks","runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q138335503","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":1094,"t":"The Halloween Tree","y":"1993","la":"8+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"A 1993 Hanna-Barbera animated TV special written and narrated by Ray Bradbury, based on his own novel. Four trick-or-treaters learn the real history of Halloween, Ancient Egyptian, Greek, Roman, Celtic Samhain, and Mexican Day of the Dead traditions, while racing across time with the mysterious Mr. Moundshroud (voiced by Leonard Nimoy) to save a fifth friend whose soul has been stolen. The film is moody and atmospheric rather than violent or gory, but it is built directly around the possibility of a child dying, and that fear runs through the whole story, including a visit to a graveyard and imagery tied to mourning and the dead across cultures. Reviewers describe it as eerie and melancholy rather than genuinely scary. No CSM review exists for this title; content summarized from other sources. Positive: friendship, loyalty, and facing fear and death with curiosity instead of denial, alongside a real history lesson about where Halloween customs come from.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Halloween_Tree_(film)","addedAt":"2026-10-04","addedVia":"request","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Animation","Holiday","Fantasy"],"studio":"Hanna-Barbera","runtimeMinutes":69,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Halloween Tree (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-10-04"},{"num":1095,"t":"Before the Ice Melts","y":"2026","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"A low-key hockey drama following a teen girl waiting to hear whether she's been drafted into a women's professional league, while juggling her mother's expectations and constant comparisons to her older sister. Mostly talky and earnest, with the physical content limited to normal on-ice hockey contact -- shoving, shouting, and a single bloody lip from a hit during play, not real fighting. Language is infrequent and mild (a few uses of \"hell,\" plus \"screw off\" and similar). Positive: a story about building confidence and pushing back against assumptions that hockey is a boys' sport, told from a young female athlete's own perspective.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/before-the-ice-melts","addedAt":"2026-10-08","addedVia":"discovery","source":"EXTRA","genre":["Live-Action","Sports","Drama"],"studio":"Winter State Entertainment","runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"rottentomatoes:before_the_ice_melts","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-10-08"}];
const MOVIES_CSM = [{"num":607,"t":"Modern Times","y":"1936","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Families will cherish Chaplin's silent slapstick,\" says CSM, though beneath the sight gags is a pointed Depression-era story of class struggle: a man dies in a workers' riot, prompting his daughter's grief, and Chaplin's Tramp unknowingly ingests a mysterious white powder and later gets drunk. Otherwise it's mostly gentle physical comedy. Positive: the Tramp meets hardship with kindness, resourcefulness, and unfailing optimism, and the gamine he befriends shows real cleverness and independence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/modern-times","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Drama"],"studio":"MGM","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":99,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q45602","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":608,"t":"Bringing Up Baby","y":"1938","la":"6+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Classic screwball comedy with loads of tame laughs.\" The mayhem -- a wayward leopard named Baby, a family gardener who nips from a flask for laughs, and a string of pratfalls and mistaken identities -- never leads to real injury or real danger. Some flirtatious banter and a single quip about a character going \"gay\" reflect the era. Positive: Katharine Hepburn's Susan brings feisty, independent energy that puts her on equal footing with Cary Grant's uptight David, and the film's message is that spontaneity and joy are worth loosening up for.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/bringing-up-baby","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Romance"],"studio":"RKO Radio Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q179743","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":609,"t":"An American in Paris","y":"1951","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Spectacular musical falters in treatment of women.\" The plot leans hard into old-fashioned romance: characters kiss passionately, drink cocktails and champagne in nightclubs, and Jerry doggedly pursues Lise even as she keeps turning him away, a dynamic the film treats as swoon-worthy rather than a red flag. Some French dialogue goes without subtitles, and the story references WWII occupation and the Resistance. Positive: Gershwin's musical numbers and Gene Kelly's dancing celebrate art and beauty as healing forces, even if the central romance hasn't aged as well as the choreography.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/an-american-in-paris","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"MGM","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q747570","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":610,"t":"Born Free","y":"1966","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Compelling classic nature story with some animal violence.\" This true story of Joy Adamson raising lioness Elsa includes real predation (lions killing and eating other animals), an offscreen-then-shown lion attack that leaves blood in a river, and a scary elephant stampede; adults drink at meals. Positive: Joy Adamson's tireless devotion to preparing Elsa for life in the wild models real stewardship of, and respect for, the natural world.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/born-free","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Other","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Born Free","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":612,"t":"Chitty Chitty Bang Bang","y":"1968","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"A fantastical car story custom-made for kids,\" says CSM. The cartoonish action (no one is actually hurt) is safe, but the sinister Child Catcher, who lures kids with candy before a long chase/battle, unsettles many young viewers, and a party scene includes drinking, smoking, and a lingerie dance number. Positive: Caractacus Potts is an inventive, devoted single father, and the film's message that ordinary people (and things) hold real worth resonates through Truly Scrumptious's kindness and the children's loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/chitty-chitty-bang-bang","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":144,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1637791","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":613,"t":"Charlotte's Web","y":"1973","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Heartwarming tale of love and friendship.\" The animated musical doesn't shy from real themes of death and the cycle of life -- Wilbur faces the threat of slaughter, and Charlotte herself dies near the end, which can be unsettling for younger viewers. Positive: friendship and love sit at the center of the story, with the film modeling how to process loss and keep loved ones alive through memory.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/charlottes-web-1973","genre":["Animation","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q37785","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":615,"t":"Annie","y":"1982","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Classic orphan tale has great songs, some iffy content.\" Concerns: Annie dangles from a bridge while fleeing a kidnapper, a bomb is thrown into Daddy Warbucks' office, orphanage matron Miss Hannigan shoves the girls around and is frequently played-for-laughs drunk with a bottle in hand, and kids are called names like \"pig droppings.\" Positive: Annie's grit, determination, and optimism, and the theme that a loving family can be built on more than blood.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/annie-1982","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Other","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q566890","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":617,"t":"An American Tail","y":"1986","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Heartwarming tale of immigrant mouse has peril,\" says CSM. Fievel's family flees pogroms in Russia and gets separated crossing to America, and the film doesn't shy from real danger: a village burns, cats stalk mice through the streets, and adults drink at a wake while a cigar gets passed around. Positive: Fievel's persistence and hope carry him through, his parents never give up searching for him, and a sympathetic cat proves that kindness crosses species (and cultural) lines.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/an-american-tail","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:An American Tail","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":618,"t":"Anne of Green Gables","y":"1986","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Faithful, sensitive take on classic novel is great for kids,\" per CSM. Content is mild for the age: Anne accidentally gets her best friend Diana tipsy by mixing up a bottle at tea, a beloved character's death and an infant's illness carry real emotional weight, and one teacher's attention to a teen student raises an eyebrow. Positive: Anne is imaginative, hardworking, and quick to make amends for her impulsive mistakes, while Marilla and Matthew show that found family can be as loving as any other kind.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/anne-of-green-gables","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Sullivan Entertainment","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":199,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Anne of Green Gables (1985 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":619,"t":"The Adventures of Milo and Otis","y":"1986","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Lovable pet tale about friendship despite differences,\" per CSM, though parents should know this is more intense than typical G-rated fare: the kitten and puppy stars encounter real predatory bears and seagulls, Milo jumps off a cliff, and the film has long faced unconfirmed animal-rights allegations about how some scenes were shot. Positive: Milo and Otis show unconditional loyalty and courage across their differences, modeling the idea that if they can be devoted friends, so can people.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-adventures-of-milo-and-otis","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1932371","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":620,"t":"The Brave Little Toaster","y":"1987","la":"7+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Appliances make a suspenseful, incredible journey,\" per CSM, but this one runs darker than expected: parents flag genuinely frightening scenes, including appliances dropped into a waterfall, sucked into quicksand, and chased by a scrapyard's malicious supermagnet, plus a subplot that reads as an appliance's near-suicidal sacrifice. No language or substance concerns. Positive: the toaster and friends model loyalty and teamwork under pressure, and the story gently critiques a throwaway culture that discards still-useful things for something newer.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-brave-little-toaster","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Hyperion Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1199692","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":621,"t":"The Land Before Time","y":"1988","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Original baby-dinosaur buddy tale has scares, sadness,\" per CSM. Littlefoot's mother dies after a battle with a Sharptooth early on, and the young dinosaurs face earthquakes, volcanoes, and repeated chases from a hunting T. rex as they journey alone to the Great Valley. Positive: Littlefoot leads with courage and good judgment, timid Petrie overcomes his fears, and the group's growing tolerance across dinosaur \"kinds\" models teamwork and unselfishness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-land-before-time","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q192403","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":622,"t":"Babar: The Movie","y":"1989","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Animated elephant adventure has some peril.\" CSM warns of a brief but intense opening in which Babar's village is raided and burned, elephants are separated from their children and enslaved by the rhinos, and some are shown restrained and whipped. Positive: the film champions loyalty, standing by friends, and resolving conflict without violence, with Babar and his companions repaying kindness with good deeds throughout their journey to reclaim their home.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/babar-the-movie","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Nelvana","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q797589","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":623,"t":"FernGully: The Last Rainforest","y":"1992","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Family favorite features strong environmental message.\" Fairy Crysta shrinks logger Zak down to size so he can experience the rainforest he's helping destroy, and together they face Hexxus, a menacing living blob of toxic sludge. The villain's attacks and a knife pulled out for a comedic beat bring some tension, plus one kiss and a \"bodacious babe\" comment. Positive: Crysta and the forest animals model kindness and care for nature, and Zak's arc teaches viewers to value and protect the environment.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ferngully-the-last-rainforest","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q240852","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":624,"t":"The Muppet Christmas Carol","y":"1992","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A gentle, fuzzy version of the Dickens classic,\" per CSM. The Ghost of Christmas Future is genuinely eerie for sensitive kids, and one vision shows Tiny Tim's projected death, though there's no real violence beyond Gonzo and Rizzo's slapstick tumbles. Positive: Scrooge's transformation from miser to generous, compassionate man -- learning to value relationships over wealth -- gives the film real heart alongside its Muppet humor and songs.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-muppet-christmas-carol","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Musical","Fantasy","Holiday"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q714721","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":625,"t":"Heidi","y":"1993","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Family entertainment at its best,\" per CSM, though this nearly three-hour two-part TV movie earns its warning for emotional intensity: young Heidi is left with a grandfather who initially rejects her, and she later watches her ailing grandmother decline and die. No violence, language, or substance concerns. Positive: the film treats death honestly as a natural part of life rather than something to fear, and gruff Grandfather Alp's hidden warmth teaches that people aren't always what they seem on the surface.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/heidi-1993","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":193,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q680626","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":626,"t":"The Nightmare Before Christmas","y":"1993","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Tim Burton holiday magic, with a touch of scariness.\" Characters casually remove their own heads and limbs, skeletons and zombies populate Halloweentown, and the sinister Oogie Boogie menaces the cast; one gag involves a child unwrapping a decapitated head as a gift. Jack Skellington's scheme to kidnap Santa and take over Christmas drives real tension before he learns from his mistakes. Positive: Jack's arc rewards gratitude over restlessness, and Sally's willingness to speak up against his plan, even at personal risk, models quiet courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-nightmare-before-christmas","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":73,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q322328","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":627,"t":"The Thief and the Cobbler","y":"1993","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A must for family viewing,\" per CSM, which lists no real concerns around violence, language, or romance, aside from noting the smallest children might be frightened by the hulking, menacing bad guys serving sorcerer Zigzag. Visually the film is a dazzling showcase of optical illusions from a Who Framed Roger Rabbit animator, with Vincent Price voicing the villain and Jonathan Winters stealing scenes as the thief. Positive: shy cobbler Tack proves his worth through courage and perseverance, and a musical number underscores that education and cleverness matter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-thief-and-the-cobbler","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"MGM","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Thief and the Cobbler","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":628,"t":"Black Beauty","y":"1994","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"A harrowing and Beauty-ful version of the book,\" says CSM. Told from the horse's own point of view, the film doesn't soften the cruelty Black Beauty and his friend Ginger endure under bad owners; Ginger's fate, in particular, is only implied but lands hard on kids who've grown attached to her. No language, substance, or romantic content. Positive: the story invites real reflection on how animals deserve to be treated, and Black Beauty's endurance through both mistreatment and kindness models resilience.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/black-beauty","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q537256","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":630,"t":"The Swan Princess","y":"1994","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Classic story is less scary than most animated fairy tales,\" per CSM. An evil sorcerer turns the princess into a swan, and there's a brief fire-and-lightning sequence where a beast is captured plus an arrow piercing a puffin's wing, but CSM notes these moments are quick and don't show real injury. Positive: the film's message is that loyalty, kindness, honesty, and cleverness matter more than looks -- both the princess and prince prove courageous and steadfast, and the prince learns not to judge by appearance alone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-swan-princess","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Musical","Romance"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1216146","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":631,"t":"Thumbelina","y":"1994","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Magical, musical story is a classic fairy tale.\" CSM flags a sword fight, a kidnapping-and-forced-marriage plot line, and a Beetle who won't stop calling Thumbelina \"Toots\" despite her objections; grown-ups sip cocktails at the Beetle Ball. Positive: strong messages about believing in yourself and not compromising your happiness just to please others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thumbelina","genre":["Animation","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q965266","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":632,"t":"A Goofy Movie","y":"1995","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Even tweens will enjoy this road trip with Goofy.\" Concerns include a scary car-off-a-cliff-into-a-river sequence, Max punching a mascot, Pete drinking beer and spitting it at the TV, and mild language (\"butt,\" an interrupted \"hell\"); a few background gags show women in slinky outfits. Positive: Goofy is an earnest, loving father learning patience as his son goes through an awkward, distancing phase, and their bond proves stronger than the friction.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-goofy-movie","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q869993","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":633,"t":"All Dogs Go to Heaven 2","y":"1996","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"This dark coming-of-age story is a unique romp.\" CSM notes cartoonish, mostly implied mayhem, references to Hell and the devious devil-figure Red, and mild innuendo that may unsettle younger or Christian-leaning families. Positive: Charlie's arc from selfish schemer to someone who works for others' good delivers a real lesson about acceptance and teamwork over self-interest.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/all-dogs-go-to-heaven-2","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"MGM","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2413112","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":634,"t":"Fly Away Home","y":"1996","la":"7+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Thrilling, touching adventure for animal lovers.\" The film opens with a jarring car accident that kills Amy's mother, shown from inside the flipping vehicle, and later includes hunters shooting at geese and one use of \"s--t.\" Adults drink wine and beer, and there's a brief shower scene with implied but not shown nudity. Positive: Amy and her father Tom's shared project to save an orphaned flock of Canada geese models perseverance, teamwork, and how a strained parent-child relationship can heal through shared purpose.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fly-away-home","genre":["Live-Action","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q49018","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":635,"t":"Anastasia","y":"1997","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Beautiful, not factual depiction of missing Russian duchess.\" Concerns: Rasputin appears as a decaying, rotting corpse, and the film builds to a burning castle, a runaway train racing a collapsing bridge, and a character nearly swept overboard in a storm; a young couple kisses at the end. Positive: Anastasia is, per CSM, \"a thoroughly modern, courageous role model for girls\" whose honesty and perseverance carry her through danger she largely handles herself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/anastasia","genre":["Animation","Musical","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q486609","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":636,"t":"Cinderella","y":"1997","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Musical take on classic fairy tale is an inclusion landmark.\" There's comical slapstick, bullying and name-calling that could read as ableist (\"stupid,\" \"lazy\"), champagne bottles played for comedic drunkenness in a musical number, and only the mildest kissing-based romance. Positive: the story insists that money and status never determine worth -- courage, perseverance, humility, and kindness do -- and it's celebrated for its groundbreaking multiracial casting, with Brandy as Cinderella and Whitney Houston as her fairy godmother.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/cinderella-1997","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Fantasy"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1092278","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":637,"t":"Kirikou and the Sorceress","y":"1998","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Enchanting folk tale with toddler hero, for all ages.\" A snarling skunk chases the toddler hero, a warthog threatens him, and the evil sorceress Karaba holds the whole village hostage with magic and fear; there's mild name-calling (\"little toad\") and non-sexualized nudity throughout, including bare-chested women and brief, non-detailed views of the young protagonist. Positive: rather than seeking revenge, Kirikou tries to understand Karaba's motives and wins through loyalty, bravery, wisdom, and compassion, and the film offers a rich introduction to West African art, music, and culture.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/kirikou-and-the-sorceress","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Les Armateurs","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":71,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q605620","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":638,"t":"Annie","y":"1999","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Joyous '90s version of classic musical,\" per CSM, this made-for-TV take on the Broadway musical has Miss Hannigan's cruelty played mostly for laughs, though her brother's threat to Annie with a knife and orphans plotting to spike her drink land as more menacing than musical-comedy filler. Positive: Annie stays defiantly optimistic and stands up to bullies despite a rough orphanage, and Grace models genuine warmth and advocacy for a kid who has none.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/annie-1999","genre":["Live-Action","Musical","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Annie (1999 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":639,"t":"Babar: King of the Elephants","y":"1999","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Delightful story, with one scary moment for younger kids.\" CSM flags an early scene where Babar's mother is shot and killed by a poacher, plus talk of war between the elephants and rhinos. Positive: Madame's kindness in taking in and educating orphaned Babar, and Babar's own patient, respectful leadership once he becomes king, model cooperation and resolving conflict through dialogue rather than violence.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/babar-king-of-the-elephants","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Nelvana","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q569991","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":640,"t":"Muppets from Space","y":"1999","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Plenty of jokes and mayhem to keep kids and parents amused,\" says CSM. Gonzo is captured by a shady government agent who wants to study his brain, and there's frequent cartoon-style peril -- electrification, an explosion, a rescue mission -- all played for laughs rather than real scares; language stays mild (\"wacko,\" \"freak-boy\"). Positive: the story champions individuality and finding your place, with Kermit, Piggy, and the gang showing loyalty and teamwork to save their friend.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/muppets-from-space","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1458649","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":641,"t":"Stuart Little","y":"1999","la":"5+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Sweet book-based tale has some emotional intensity.\" Stuart faces real peril from the family cat and two conniving alley mice, including a scary moment stuck in a washing machine, alongside mild language like \"damn\" and \"hell\" and some cat-flatulence humor. The adoption storyline -- a human couple choosing a mouse as their son -- may land differently for adoptive or foster families. Positive: the Little family's patience and unconditional love model what makes a family, and the story champions kindness toward those who look different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/stuart-little","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Comedy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1048958","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":642,"t":"Alvin and the Chipmunks Meet the Wolfman","y":"2000","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A loveable horror story with life lessons.\" CSM flags scary nighttime encounters, an offscreen werewolf bite, sibling scuffles with visible scratches, and a chemistry mishap that causes an explosion. Positive: the brothers stick together despite their squabbles, a supportive principal helps a struggling student, and the story nudges viewers to understand a bully's motivations rather than just fear him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/alvin-and-the-chipmunks-meet-the-wolfman","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Horror"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2840611","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":643,"t":"An American Tail: The Mystery of the Night Monster","y":"2000","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"A mystery with spunk, courage, and heart.\" CSM warns of nightmare-style imagery, including a devil-bat with a mousetrap tongue, and a villain who steals Fievel's family and burns their home. Positive: Fievel pushes through his fears to help save the day, and the story frames fear as a natural protective instinct while showing that imagination can sometimes make danger seem bigger than it is.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/an-american-tail-the-mystery-of-the-night-monster","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Mystery"],"studio":"Universal Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2448075","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":644,"t":"Buzz Lightyear of Star Command: The Adventure Begins","y":"2000","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM describes it as \"a spirited romp through space.\" Cartoonish space battles bring explosions, a shattered robot, and Buzz's mechanical arm destroyed, and Buzz believes his partner has died and mourns him at a funeral, while villain Zurg uses a mind-control device called the Uni-Mind to brainwash a ranger. Positive: the film emphasizes teamwork, following the rules, and the value of having a trusted partner, even if some characters break their own rules along the way.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/buzz-lightyear-of-star-command-the-adventure-begins","genre":["Animation","Sci-Fi","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1703163","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":645,"t":"Ice Age","y":"2002","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Clever, funny, touching; like a great road movie.\" The film opens with a mother drowning while saving her infant, and saber-tooth tigers and rampaging rhinos attack in intense close-up sequences, with one character impaled on icicles. Despite the prehistoric setting, animals are often played as calculating villains rather than acting from instinct. Positive: Manny, Sid, and Diego's mismatched herd learns to sacrifice for one another across species lines, and even the story's antagonists get a chance to find respect and empathy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ice-age","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Blue Sky Studios","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q305250","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":646,"t":"Robots","y":"2005","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Endearing 'follow your dreams' story with plenty of laughs,\" per CSM. Robots face cartoon chases, falls, and captures, with the villain melting outdated robots down in a fiery \"chop shop\" oven; humor leans on a stretch of fart jokes and a party scene where robots sip \"oil\" from martini glasses. Positive: hero Rodney Copperbottom shows intelligence, loyalty, and perseverance, and the film's core message -- that you can shine no matter what you're made of -- champions acceptance over forced upgrades.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/robots","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q756238","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":647,"t":"Brother Bear 2","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM calls it \"Bear's warm-furry quest finds love and friends.\" Kenai reunites with his childhood sweetheart Nita while the moose brothers crack crude jokes about female body parts, an avalanche and a pack of menacing raccoons create real peril, and a beloved character appears fatally injured before the story resolves. Positive: the film centers on friendship, love, and courage, with the theme that once you love someone, \"they stay in your heart forever.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/brother-bear-2","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q641310","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":649,"t":"Leroy & Stitch","y":"2006","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"More lively fun with Lilo, Stitch, and friends,\" per CSM. Villain Leroy has a devilish look and is cloned into a full army of himself, which could unsettle younger viewers, and there's a mild cartoon battle finale, but nothing graphic. Positive: previously bad experiments turn good and use their powers to help, wrapped in the Hawaiian themes of aloha and ohana (family) that run through the whole Lilo & Stitch series.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/leroy-stitch","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1069050","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":650,"t":"Coraline","y":"2009","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Cool but creepy animated fantasy too scary for young kids.\" CSM warns of a genuinely dark, unsettling tone, including implied child deaths, a severed hand that attacks the heroine, a strangling scene, and mild insults like \"jerkwad.\" Positive: Coraline's bravery and resourcefulness in facing the Other Mother, and her parents' humility in learning from her, model self-control, gratitude, and appreciating imperfect real life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/coraline","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Horror"],"studio":"Focus Features","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q632668","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":651,"t":"Dr. Dolittle: Million Dollar Mutts","y":"2009","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Latest sequel is surprisingly fun; good role models, too.\" A Hollywood agent gets comically chased by a menagerie of animals seeking justice, a sick dog recovers, there's one kiss between college-aged characters, and some brand product placement appears during a shopping scene. Positive: Maya Dolittle learns that shortcuts and celebrity promises can't replace real effort, owns up to her mistakes, and models a healthy body image and self-respect.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dr-dolittle-million-dollar-mutts","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3033503","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":652,"t":"Despicable Me","y":"2010","la":"5+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Clever, funny, and sweet villain-with-a-heart-of-gold tale.\" Supervillain Gru's schemes involve high-tech weapons blasting things to smithereens and scenes implying injury, though nobody is seriously hurt, and the orphanage keeps unwanted kids in a \"box of shame.\" Mild language includes \"stupid\" and \"poop.\" Positive: the three girls Gru adopts turn out to be the story's real role models, sweet and generous even as Gru's own heart softens, and the film's message that everyone -- even someone who seems irredeemable -- deserves love lands without being preachy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/despicable-me","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4447","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":653,"t":"Arthur Christmas","y":"2011","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fast-paced, funny holiday movie about the Christmas spirit.\" Concerns: a homeowner fires a gun at the sleigh, missile launches and other perilous chases, a tipsy Grandsanta and passing references to whiskey and pills, and some name-calling (\"bag of fleas,\" \"moron\") alongside outdated sexist and stereotyped jokes played for laughs. Positive: \"one person can really make a difference\" -- Arthur's compassion and perseverance save Christmas, and Mrs. Claus proves more capable than the men around her give her credit for.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/arthur-christmas","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Sony Pictures Animation","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q711918","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":654,"t":"Dolphin Tale","y":"2011","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Heartwarming tale is sweet, inspiring for kids and tweens,\" per CSM, but the true story of rescue dolphin Winter opens with her rope-tangled, bloody tail found on a beach, and a wounded veteran returns home in a wheelchair before a hurricane later threatens the aquarium. Language stays mild (\"crappy,\" \"stupid\"). Positive: Sawyer's loyalty and Hazel's compassion drive an ensemble that shows teamwork saving a life, and Winter's prosthetic-tail journey models resilience and living with disability.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dolphin-tale","genre":["Live-Action","Drama","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":113,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1064885","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":655,"t":"Ernest & Celestine","y":"2012","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Touching animated story celebrates unlikely friendships.\" A gruff bear and a small orphaned mouse form a forbidden bond that defies their two prejudiced, segregated societies, leading to traps, a police chase, and a fire that puts both in real danger. Mild insults like \"moron\" and \"stupid\" turn up, along with scenes of stealing and breaking rules. Positive: Ernest and Celestine protect each other and prove their communities' fears about \"the other\" wrong, modeling loyalty and courage in defending a friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ernest-celestine","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"StudioCanal","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3057240","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":656,"t":"Despicable Me 2","y":"2013","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"More minions and romance make for a sweet, silly sequel.\" Concerns: cartoonish weapons (tasers, flame guns, razors) and minions who briefly transform into monstrous creatures, mild insults (\"nut job\"), a bit of toilet humor, and a blossoming romance between Gru and Lucy that includes a date and kisses. Positive: the strong father-daughter bond between Gru and his girls, plus teamwork and compassion as Gru trades villainy for protecting his family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/despicable-me-2","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q637212","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":657,"t":"Song of the Sea","y":"2014","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Beautiful Irish tale explores myths, sibling relationship.\" CSM notes the film implies the mother's death in childbirth and features the menacing owl-witch Macha pursuing the children, alongside a few intense, heartbreaking moments. Positive: the story champions sibling love and cooperation, courage, and honestly embracing your feelings, with young Ben's growing bravery and the loyal dog Cu's heroics standing out as role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/song-of-the-sea","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"GKIDS","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q17125101","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":658,"t":"An American Girl: Grace Stirs Up Success","y":"2015","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Tale of young baker jam-packed with positive messages.\" CSM finds essentially no violence, language, romance, or substance concerns in this live-action American Girl story about a determined young baker navigating a trip to Paris and a newly blended family. Positive: discipline, follow-through, teamwork, and taking criticism constructively, with parents and grandparents offering strong mentoring throughout.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/an-american-girl-grace-stirs-up-success","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Other","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":1,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":101,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:An American Girl: Grace Stirs Up Success","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":660,"t":"Albert","y":"2016","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Spunky tree's adventures are filled with festive messages.\" CSM flags a few dicey scenes, including a near-miss at a paper mill, plus mild bathroom-style language like \"butt\" and \"jerkweed.\" Positive: Albert's determination to be chosen as the city's Christmas tree despite others' doubts models self-confidence and optimism, while his friendship with Maisy reinforces loyalty and the idea that sharing joy brings it back.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/albert","genre":["Animation","Holiday","Comedy"],"studio":"Nickelodeon","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":43,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Albert (2016 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":661,"t":"Elena and the Secret of Avalor","y":"2016","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Princess crossover features two strong female role models.\" A sorceress traps Elena's family inside inanimate objects, there are a few tense standoffs, and the villain takes a fall from a height whose outcome is briefly left uncertain. Positive: the story shows freedom and peace winning out over intimidation and fear, with Sofia coming across as clever, strong-minded, and brave, and Elena as resourceful and devoted to her family and kingdom, while the Avalor setting introduces kids to Latino dress, music, dance, and architecture.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elena-and-the-secret-of-avalor","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":63,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q27890317","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":662,"t":"Ferdinand","y":"2017","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Sweet story about compassion, nonviolence has a few scares.\" Ferdinand is slashed with a spear during a tense bullfighting climax, there's a genuinely scary sequence in a meat-processing facility full of dangerous machinery, and bullies taunt him with names like \"flower boy\" and \"loser.\" Positive: Ferdinand's quiet refusal to fight, even when the whole world expects otherwise, models gentle strength and staying true to yourself, and the film never asks other characters to become like him -- just to accept him as he is.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ferdinand","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Blue Sky Studios","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":108,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18740903","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":663,"t":"Dr. Seuss' The Grinch","y":"2018","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Pratfall-heavy take on holiday tale is fun, mostly gentle.\" Benedict Cumberbatch voices the Grinch, who schemes to steal Christmas from the too-cheerful residents of Whoville, leading to lots of physical comedy, sledding chaos, and a tense scene with the Grinch in peril on a mountain. Mild language (\"dumb,\" \"stupid,\" \"oh, sugar plum\") and a brief glimpse of the Grinch in his underwear round out the concerns. Positive: Cindy-Lou Who's generosity toward her hardworking mom and the Grinch's own transformation show how one act of kindness can change a hardened heart.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dr-seuss-the-grinch","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Holiday"],"studio":"Illumination","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The Grinch (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":664,"t":"Early Man","y":"2018","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"A charming stop-motion underdog sports comedy from Aardman, where Stone Age hero Dug rallies his tribe to save their home from invading Bronze Age conquerors. Expect slapstick violence (falls, hits, a village torn down), mild language like \"crap\" and \"stupid,\" some near-nakedness played for laughs, and potty humor. Positive: the film celebrates teamwork and perseverance, with strong female athletes standing up to bullies alongside Dug.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/early-man","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sports"],"studio":"Aardman","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":89,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q25136586","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":665,"t":"A Shaun the Sheep Movie: Farmageddon","y":"2019","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Delightful family-friendly sequel has positive themes.\" CSM notes slapstick mayhem, mild peril as a villain hunts the alien Lu-La with a robotic rig, and a character hyped up on soda, all played for laughs with no lasting harm. Positive: the film's core theme of friendship across differences shines through Shaun and Lu-La's bond, with the whole flock demonstrating teamwork, empathy, and inclusiveness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/a-shaun-the-sheep-movie-farmageddon","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Aardman","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q56277622","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":667,"t":"Ella Bella Bingo","y":"2020","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Animated tale has engaging story and music, some peril.\" This Norwegian import follows spirited Ella Bella Bingo as jealousy over her best friend Henry's new pal threatens their bond. Cartoon peril includes a bull chase, a wild roller-coaster ride, and a spooky haunted-house scene with ghosts and skeletons, plus lots of dog-fart humor. Positive: the film models kindness, loyalty, and welcoming others, with Ella growing past possessiveness and the adults around her showing generosity and dependability.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ella-bella-bingo","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Musical"],"studio":"Studio 100","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106959150","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":668,"t":"Phineas and Ferb the Movie: Candace Against the Universe","y":"2020","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Cosmic adventure offers more franchise fun for families,\" per CSM. When Candace is whisked to an alien planet and hailed as \"The Chosen One,\" the action includes mind-controlling spores, kids getting tossed around during a crash-landing, and an alien abduction, alongside mild language like \"freak\" -- typical energetic Phineas and Ferb chaos rather than real menace. Positive: the film leans on teamwork and courage, with Candace working through guilt toward her brothers and even the villain learning a lesson about jealousy and self-worth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/phineas-and-ferb-the-movie-candace-against-the-universe","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Disney","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q66725868","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":669,"t":"My Little Pony: A New Generation","y":"2021","la":"6+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Sweet tale of acceptance has some mildly scary scenes,\" per CSM. Earth ponies, unicorns, and pegasi distrust one another, and the peril -- ponies nearly falling from cliffs and buildings, a menacing military-style robot chasing defenseless characters -- can startle very young kids even though language stays at the level of \"stupid\" and \"brute.\" Positive: Sunny's courage in rejecting stereotypes and building bridges between the pony tribes carries a strong message about choosing friendship over fear.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-little-pony-a-new-generation","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Musical"],"studio":"Netflix","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q105747750","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":670,"t":"Epic Tails","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Mythology adventure has smart, brave characters; icky jokes.\" Set in ancient Greece, young mouse Pattie assembles a ragtag crew to recover a legendary treasure after a jealous Poseidon steals the golden fleece protecting her city. There's mild menace from a kraken and hungry cyclopes, name-calling like \"nerd\" and \"pipsqueak,\" and gross-out humor including vomiting and an exposed cyclops backside. Positive: Pattie leads with courage and resourcefulness, and the story champions teamwork and looking past assumptions about who can be a hero.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/epic-tails","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"TAT Productions","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Pattie and the Wrath of Poseidon","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":671,"t":"Luck","y":"2022","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Colorful, charming animated tale has positive messages.\" Sam, an unlucky orphan aging out of foster care, faces real disappointment as she's repeatedly passed over for adoption, and the Land of Bad Luck is populated by scary-looking monsters (though no one actually gets hurt). Mild language includes \"poop\" and \"screw it up.\" Positive: the film's core message that \"family is who you make it\" comes through Sam's resilience and gratitude, and both the Captain and the Dragon offer confident female leadership rare in animated fantasy.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/luck","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Skydance Animation","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q97359775","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":672,"t":"Marcel the Shell with Shoes On","y":"2022","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Sweet, poignant mockumentary goes small to make big points.\" CSM flags everyday perils like falls and a cracked-shell injury to Nana Connie, a few mild swears such as \"idiot\" and \"oh my God,\" and some crude humor. Positive: Marcel's bravery, loyalty, and perseverance while searching for his lost family, plus Nana Connie's independent, risk-taking spirit, offer real lessons about community and doing the hard thing anyway.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/marcel-the-shell-with-shoes-on","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"A24","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q109447163","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":673,"t":"Flow","y":"2024","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Superb animated 'cat-astrophe' has animals in peril.\" This dialogue-free Oscar winner follows a solitary cat and a growing crew of other animals surviving a catastrophic flood that submerges their world. Expect sustained life-or-death tension, a stampede, animal fights, near-drowning, and one moment that may suggest a character's death, all without any words to soften the mood. Positive: the animals learn to set aside their differences and cooperate, with a secretary bird sacrificing its own safety to protect the cat, modeling loyalty and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/flow","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Drama"],"studio":"Dream Well Studio","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q125622088","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":674,"t":"David","y":"2025","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Moving animated Biblical musical has battle violence, peril.\" This faith-based animated musical follows David from shepherd boy to king, with non-graphic but thematic battle violence -- including the fight with Goliath, swords and spears in play -- that may frighten younger viewers, plus very mild language (\"heck,\" \"wretched\"). Positive: courage in faith, humility, and perseverance, with David portrayed as a great but flawed hero who leads with kindness and loyalty.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/david","genre":["Animation","Musical","Drama"],"studio":"Other","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:David (2025 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":675,"t":"The Last Whale Singer","y":"2025","la":"7+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Fact-filled animated whale tale deals with loss; some peril,\" per CSM. Orphaned humpback Vincent watches his parents killed by a ship in a frightening early scene, later discovering the euphemistic \"star pool\" is actually a bone-filled graveyard, and a tentacled sea monster hunts him with poison and a jump-scare shark encounter along the way. Positive: Vincent's courage in forging his own path rather than his family's legacy, nanny Walter's steady care, and deaf orca Darya's heightened senses (framed as a strength, not a limitation) carry real messages about perseverance and difference.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-last-whale-singer","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Telescope Animation","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q137247498","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":676,"t":"Coyote vs. Acme","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Great messages in chaotic, hilarious, touching 'toon mashup,\" says CSM of this live-action/animation hybrid, where Wile E. Coyote sues ACME with the help of a struggling lawyer. Slapstick violence is constant (characters flattened, slimed, hit by trucks) alongside a knife threat, explosions, and a train crash played for cartoon laughs, plus scattered mild profanity and a joke about a bottle labeled \"XXX.\" Positive: the story champions perseverance over giving up, and Wile E. and Kevin's unlikely friendship models loyalty and standing up to a callous corporation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/coyote-vs-acme","genre":["Live-Action","Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106392679","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":677,"t":"Minions & Monsters","y":"2026","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Homage to Hollywood mixes massive monsters, 'toon violence,\" per CSM, this Hollywood-set adventure has giant monsters smashing property, a shark attacking the crew's boat, villains dispatched (including one beheaded by an ax), and a single \"handsome bastard\" line amid otherwise mild language; adults toast champagne and cocktails at studio parties. Positive: the Minions and their friends pursue creative dreams and stick together through loyalty and teamwork, though their habit of admiring villains and causing chaos means they're better comic relief than role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/minions-monsters","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Adventure"],"studio":"Illumination","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q127605787","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":678,"t":"PAW Patrol: The Dino Movie","y":"2026","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Canine heroes meet dinos in engaging but perilous adventure,\" per CSM, the pups' third big-screen outing turns up the intensity with river rapids, a dinosaur stampede, an erupting volcano throwing lava and fireballs, and a nighttime search for a missing friend that plays genuinely scary. Language is limited to words like \"stinky\" and \"nasty.\" Positive: Marshall learns to stop beating himself up over clumsiness, Ryder leads with encouragement, and new pup Rex shows that physical differences don't limit resourcefulness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/paw-patrol-the-dino-movie","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Paramount Pictures","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Paw Patrol: The Dino Movie","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":679,"t":"Toy Story 5","y":"2026","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"\"Some peril in thoughtful kids-and-tech animated adventure.\" As Bonnie grows attached to a tablet named Lilypad, the toys attempt rescues and daring missions with real tension; mild language (\"shut up,\" \"darned\") and a low-battery gag where tech toys slur their speech like they're intoxicated round out the concerns. Positive: Jessie models courage, leadership, and teamwork, and the film opens up conversation about balancing screen time with imaginative play.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/toy-story-5","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Comedy"],"studio":"Pixar","source":"CSM","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q113641997","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_MCUDC = [{"num":680,"t":"Batman","y":"1966","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Campy, goofy '60s movie may not appeal to today's kids,\" per Common Sense Media. Fistfights are punctuated with onscreen \"POW!\" graphics, a comically fake shark bites at Batman's leg while he dangles from a helicopter, and viewers are briefly led to think Batman has been blown up before he's shown to be fine; the Penguin smokes with a cigarette holder, and Batman goes on a date that includes a kiss. Positive: CSM notes the film draws a cartoonish but clear line between heroes and villains, though it flags weak overall role-modeling and a dated gag mocking overweight women.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-1966","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q810857","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":681,"t":"Superman","y":"1978","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Consent issues in sweeping, nostalgic superhero adventure.\" Concerns: extensive peril without graphic blood (an exploding planet, an earthquake, a plane crash), plus real consent problems played as humor -- Superman kisses an unconscious Lois and uses X-ray vision on her without permission, and a soldier jokes about giving \"mouth-to-mouth\" to an unconscious woman. Mild profanity (\"bulls--t,\" \"damn,\" \"ass\") and social smoking/drinking appear throughout. Positive: good against evil and personal integrity are central themes, with Superman modeling humility and honesty even as the film's women are frequently rescued or objectified.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-the-movie","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":143,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q213053","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":682,"t":"Superman II","y":"1980","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Witty, action-packed superadventure with big themes.\" Concerns: Lois is nearly crushed to death and Superman battles three escaped Kryptonian villains amid heavy destruction; a powerless Clark Kent is beaten by a bully and left with a bloody nose, which can startle younger viewers; scattered profanity (\"hell,\" \"damn,\" \"s--t,\" \"son of a bitch\"); and a discreetly depicted scene implying Lois and Clark's relationship is consummated. Positive: Superman is held up as \"the ultimate superhero role model,\" sacrificing his powers for love and then reclaiming his duty for the greater good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-ii","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Superman II","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":683,"t":"Superman III","y":"1983","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Outdated superhero movie may interest older kids,\" per Common Sense Media. Richard Pryor's comic-relief hacker Gus Gorman gets comically drunk to break into a restricted computer room, and a red-kryptonite-corrupted Superman turns cruel, vandalizes a bar, and spends a night with a seductive villainess; fights between super-beings involve missiles and lightning bolts but no blood. Positive: Superman's good nature ultimately wins out over his corrupted alter ego, and his integrity is restored by the story's end.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-iii","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Superman III","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":684,"t":"Supergirl","y":"1984","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Female superhero can't save this '80s clunker,\" says Common Sense Media. The villainous sorceress Selena and her minions drink and smoke, occasional \"s--t\" and \"Jesus\" appear as exclamations, a mentor character dies in a non-graphic scene, and Supergirl shares some kisses with a love interest; comic-book battles involve knives and a runaway amusement-park ride but no blood or gore. Positive: Supergirl is a conscientious, duty-driven role model, offering a rare female-led superhero story where good triumphs over evil.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/supergirl-1984","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Fantasy"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q283134","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":685,"t":"Superman IV: The Quest for Peace","y":"1987","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Terrible '80s sequel has violence, nuclear weapons,\" per Common Sense Media. Superman battles the powerful Nuclear Man across space and an erupting volcano in growling, brawling clashes that can startle younger kids, and the film repeatedly references the destruction of Krypton and the loss of Superman's parents; a character named Lacy tries to seduce Clark Kent, and adults smoke cigars. Positive: the story stresses that even a well-intentioned goal like world peace is too big for one person to achieve alone, and champions environmental and journalistic integrity alongside Superman's heroism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-iv-the-quest-for-peace","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":90,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Superman IV: The Quest for Peace","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":686,"t":"Batman","y":"1989","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Stylish, violent, and dark superhero adventure,\" per Common Sense Media. The film features numerous shoot-outs and killings, including a quill pen jabbed into a man's throat and another character electrocuted to death, plus flashbacks to young Bruce Wayne watching his parents murdered; street prostitutes appear in a crime-ridden city scene, the Joker makes crude advances on Vicki Vale, sex between Bruce and Vicki is implied, and there's cigar/cigarette smoking and profanity including \"s--t.\" Positive: CSM notes the film blurs hero and villain, with Batman's vigilante justice as much a factor in his actions as genuine heroism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-1989","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q116852","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":687,"t":"Batman Returns","y":"1992","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"A darkly violent take on the comic-book hero,\" per Common Sense Media. The sequel is notably darker than the original, with lots of gunfire and carnage, a man shoved from a window, a close-range shooting, an enemy set on fire, and the Penguin biting at a man's nose; the Penguin's crude double entendres about Catwoman and a Batman-Catwoman fight staged like foreplay add sexual undertones, alongside heavier themes of child abandonment and corporate corruption. Positive: Batman is shown as brave and trying to do the right thing, though CSM flags that he crosses a line by killing rather than just capturing his opponents.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-returns","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q189054","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":688,"t":"Batman: Mask of the Phantasm","y":"1993","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Tamer than live-action, but still moody, violent.\" This noir-tinged Batman feature includes real death (including a parent's), gunfights, explosions, blood, and unsettling scenes of corpses and a menacing Joker, plus some social drinking. Positive: Batman is shown as a hero who refuses to kill even when consumed by loss, and Andrea is a genuinely capable, strong female lead, though the film's revenge plot complicates its moral message.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-mask-of-the-phantasm","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q810858","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":689,"t":"Batman Forever","y":"1995","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Flashy live-action superhero tale has violence, vengeance,\" per Common Sense Media. Numerous fight scenes mix gunfire, fisticuffs, and explosions, and flashbacks show Bruce Wayne's father shot dead on the street and Dick Grayson watching his family killed at the circus; there's suggestive banter between Bruce and Chase, Two-Face's assistants wear revealing lingerie, and the Riddler brags about a device that taps into people's fantasies. Positive: CSM finds little here, noting the characters are \"too cartoonish\" to be real role models, and that Batman kills opponents rather than bringing them to justice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-forever","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":117,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q221345","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":690,"t":"Batman & Robin","y":"1997","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Weak superhero movie has lots of innuendo, some violence,\" per Common Sense Media. Hand-to-hand combat, gunshots, and a hockey-stick fight fill the action, plus a motorcycle race that nearly turns fatal; practically everything Poison Ivy says is sexual innuendo or double entendre, the camera lingers on Batgirl's costumed body, and there's champagne at a gala, cigar smoking, and homeless characters sharing alcohol. Positive: CSM rates both positive messages and role models as very low for this campy, merchandise-heavy entry.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-robin","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q276523","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":691,"t":"Steel","y":"1997","la":"12+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Not reviewed by Common Sense Media, so this draws on IMDb's parents' guide and Kids-In-Mind instead. Shaquille O'Neal's weapons-engineer hero opens with a Gulf War flashback where soldiers are shot and blown up, and Steel himself takes a bullet to the chest; later he brawls with gang members using laser weapons and regular guns amid explosions, falling debris, and near-misses with trains and vehicles, with some blood shown. Positive: Steel refuses to let his invented weapons fall into criminal hands and uses his engineering genius to protect his community rather than profit from it.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel_(1997_film)","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1790253","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":692,"t":"Batman & Mr. Freeze: SubZero","y":"1998","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Animated '90s Batman tale has cartoon violence, peril.\" Mr. Freeze's quest to save his cryogenically frozen wife brings gunfights, knife fights, a car crash, a polar bear attack, and a fiery oil-rig climax where Batgirl is held captive, plus a black-tie scene with cocktails. Positive: despite cartoonish exaggeration, the film gives each character real stakes and shows Batman and Robin working together under pressure to save an innocent life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-mr-freeze-subzero","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q498757","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":693,"t":"Batman Beyond: Return of the Joker","y":"2000","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Joker's back in dark animated tale with cartoon violence.\" One of the franchise's darkest entries: characters are shot and killed, gas bombs and laser guns fly, and a flashback shows a young Robin kidnapped, tied down, and tortured by the Joker and Harley Quinn until he's driven to madness, alongside champagne drinking and the Joker's pipe-smoking. Positive: the story is really about flawed heroes trying to atone for old mistakes, though the film offers little else in the way of uplifting messaging.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-beyond-return-of-the-joker","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1573706","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":694,"t":"X-Men","y":"2000","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Comic-book adaptation has brains, brawn, and style.\" Mostly bloodless but visceral fights between mutants (fisticuffs, stabbing, a character liquefied) anchor this origin story, with infrequent strong language, some kissing, a mostly-unclothed blue mutant, and adults smoking cigars and drinking. Positive: the film's throughline is that peaceful coexistence and tolerance beat prejudice and conflict, with Professor X and his students modeling integrity even as Magneto raises real philosophical questions about acceptance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:X-Men (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":695,"t":"X2","y":"2003","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Fun but violent sequel has peril, cursing.\" Colonel Stryker's forces raid Xavier's school as Wolverine claws soldiers and a mutant pins the president with a knife; there's a scene implying forced sexual coercion, plus profanity (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"d--k\") and teens smoking. Positive: Xavier's steady care for his students and the X-Men's loyalty and bravery model that embracing what makes you different can drive real progress.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x2-x-men-united","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q219776","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":696,"t":"Catwoman","y":"2004","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM's blunt verdict: \"this movie is kitty litter.\" Beyond the critical drubbing, parents should know it features comic-book action violence, peril, robbery, and murder, plus a pervasive sensuality with implied sex and references to adultery; a character drinks, and a beauty product is depicted as literally addictive. CSM doesn't flag strong positive messages or role models here -- it's a rare miss for the superhero genre.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/catwoman","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":4,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q115760","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":697,"t":"Batman Begins","y":"2005","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Smart and entertaining, but also very violent,\" per Common Sense Media. Hard, fast violence from martial arts and shootings is shot in dark, sometimes scary imagery, and the film revisits the murder of Bruce Wayne's parents; mild profanity (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"ass\") appears alongside drinking, smoking, and a hallucinogenic-drug plot device, with only minimal romance (one kiss). Positive: Batman is framed as fighting for justice and fairness even though his methods sometimes mirror the criminals he opposes, ultimately affirming that \"there are heroes... willing to sacrifice themselves for the greater good.\"","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-begins","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":140,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q166262","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":698,"t":"Elektra","y":"2005","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM's tagline sums it up as a \"violent comic book movie with lingerie costumes,\" recommending age 14+. The martial-arts violence is graphic for a PG-13, with numerous fights and character deaths, though language and sexual content stay comparatively restrained (just a couple of kisses). Positive: Elektra ultimately chooses to protect an innocent father and daughter over completing her assassin contract, a redemption arc the review says the film doesn't fully earn dramatically.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/elektra","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":96,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q610159","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":699,"t":"Fantastic Four","y":"2005","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Standard superhero fare; sexual innuendo, fantasy violence.\" Comic-book-style action has the team body-slamming, punching, and zapping each other, plus a bridge car pileup and a man catching fire while snowboarding; mild profanity (\"ass,\" \"goddamn,\" \"hell\"), suggestive dialogue, and partial nudity (a woman in only a jacket, Sue in undergarments) round out the concerns. Positive: Sue is the team's voice of reason and Reed models maturity, with the film urging viewers to work together and value each other's differences -- even if the story doesn't always live up to it.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-four","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":102,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q224130","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":700,"t":"Superman Returns","y":"2006","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Thrilling but violent, tense return for the Man of Steel,\" per Common Sense Media. The film opens with a fiery vehicle crash and includes explosions, earthquakes, a giant wave, a bank robbery, and a sequence where a henchman stabs and beats Superman; mild language (\"damn,\" one s-word) appears, and in a bar scene Jimmy drinks beer while Lois starts to light a cigarette, which Superman discourages. Positive: Superman shows selfless heroism, confronting his own fear and vulnerability while still generously serving others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-returns","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":148,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q328695","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":701,"t":"X-Men: The Last Stand","y":"2006","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM recommends this violent trilogy-closer for age 13+. Characters are repeatedly stabbed, shot, and smashed with bloody gashes, a boy attempts self-harm, Mystique appears largely nude (with key areas covered), and mild profanity (\"bitch,\" \"hell,\" \"ass\") runs throughout. Positive: the X-Men model friendship and group unity, standing up for those persecuted simply for being different.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men-the-last-stand","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q221168","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":702,"t":"Fantastic Four: Rise of the Silver Surfer","y":"2007","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"\"Much better than the first; OK for tweens and up.\" Expect lots of explosions and crowds in jeopardy, including two character deaths (little blood shown), plus mild profanity (\"ass,\" \"crap,\" \"damn\"), a towel-clad shower scene, flirtatious \"fireproof lingerie\" dialogue, and background beer-drinking at a club. Positive: the team grows into real loyalty and teamwork, with one member learning to put the group's needs over his own ego.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-four-rise-of-the-silver-surfer","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q390063","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":703,"t":"Ghost Rider","y":"2007","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Devilish Nic Cage action flick isn't on fire,\" per Common Sense Media, which recommends it for age 13+. Constant comic-book violence includes motorcycle chases and chain-weapon fights, with villains turned \"gray and veiny\" as Johnny Blaze transforms into a flaming skull-headed Ghost Rider; language stays mild (\"s--t,\" \"hell,\" \"son of a bitch\") and drinking/smoking appear in several scenes. Positive: Johnny's original motive - trying to save his dying father - comes from a good place, even if his path afterward is more vigilante than role model.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ghost-rider","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":110,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q41754","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":704,"t":"Superman: Doomsday","y":"2007","la":"12+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM calls it a \"violent cartoon spinoff with classic superhero,\" recommending it for kids 11 and up (parents lean toward 12+). Fights are intense enough that Superman visibly bleeds, characters die (including off-screen deaths of children and animals), and there are snapped-spine and gunshot deaths, plus scattered profanity like \"hell\" and \"ass.\" Positive: Superman risks everything to protect Earth, and the film digs into what really defines a hero beyond raw physical power.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-doomsday","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2407828","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":705,"t":"Batman: Gotham Knight","y":"2008","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM describes this anthology as a \"dark, animated flock of Bat-stories has bloody violence.\" Expect graphic fights with blood gushing from wounds in a gory hospital sequence, a decapitation, gunfire, and explosions, though language stays minimal (just one \"ass\"). Positive: Batman consistently shows a strong moral compass and avoids killing even his enemies, while Alfred remains a loyal, wise guide who grounds him.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-gotham-knight","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2287397","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":706,"t":"Iron Man","y":"2008","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"First MCU adventure has violence, Islamophobia,\" says CSM. Tony Stark's origin story brings extensive sci-fi war violence -- explosions, gunfire, a torture-and-escape sequence, and a child held at gunpoint -- plus scattered profanity (\"son of a bitch,\" \"damn\"), a smoked cigar, and a scene of Tony pressuring an assistant to dance with him despite her reluctance. Positive: Tony transforms from a careless arms-dealing playboy into someone who questions the morality of his own weapons, guided partly by his fellow hostage Yinsen's self-sacrifice, though CSM notes women are frequently objectified onscreen.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/iron-man","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Iron Man (2008 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":707,"t":"Justice League: The New Frontier","y":"2008","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"superheroes face Cold War paranoia in violent animated tale.\" Blood flows from injuries and dead bodies appear on screen, a boy is threatened with cult sacrifice by a knife-wielding fanatic, and there are two close-up fatal shootings along with mild profanity like \"son of a bitch.\" Positive: the League sets aside ego for teamwork and mutual respect even as the public and government turn against them, and the film closes on JFK's \"New Frontier\" speech linking pioneering spirit to confronting racism and prejudice.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-the-new-frontier","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2779056","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":708,"t":"The Dark Knight","y":"2008","la":"15+","ca":"15+","full":"\"Excellent sequel much darker, more violent than the first,\" per Common Sense Media. The film contains extensive, intense violence including shootings, stabbings, fistfights, and explosions, and the Joker's disturbing look and behavior can frighten viewers of any age; mild profanity (\"ass,\" \"hell,\" \"damn\") appears, along with background drinking at parties and bars and a scene implying intimacy between clothed characters. Positive: the film probes \"the rule of law versus the rule of force,\" contrasting Batman's morally gray vigilantism with the Joker's pure chaos and disregard for innocent life.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-dark-knight","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":153,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q163872","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":709,"t":"The Incredible Hulk","y":"2008","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Bloodier action than other comic book adventures,\" per CSM. Bruce Banner's fights as the Hulk are graphically destructive, with characters smashed and hurled through buildings, plus profanity including \"bitch,\" \"hell,\" and \"goddamn,\" some kissing in semi-clothed circumstances, and light cigar smoking. Positive: CSM calls the positive messaging thin -- the military hunts Banner hoping to weaponize him -- though Banner's own struggle to control his anger before it turns destructive offers a real lesson in self-restraint.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-incredible-hulk","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q466611","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":710,"t":"Green Lantern: First Flight","y":"2009","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"dark animated superhero yarn will entertain older viewers.\" Villain Sinestro uses intimidation, torture, and murder with what CSM calls \"casual brutality\" unusually dark for the genre, plus mild swearing (\"ass,\" \"bastard,\" \"hell\"), an intergalactic bar scene, and a character drugged for interrogation. Positive: the film shows that teamwork, courage, and loyalty prevail over evil, and Hal Jordan's resistance to Sinestro's authoritarian ideology models standing up to tyranny.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/green-lantern-first-flight","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2539818","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":711,"t":"Superman/Batman: Public Enemies","y":"2009","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM sums it up as \"framed superheroes fight back -- and fight some more.\" Superman is framed for murder and hunted by nearly every hero and villain in the DC universe, leading to extensive, prolonged hand-to-hand combat and energy-blast battles (no blood or visible injuries, but bleeped profanity opens the film). Positive: both heroes model nobility and self-sacrifice -- Batman is willing to give his life to save the planet -- and the story explores the moral complexity of following orders versus doing what's right.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-batman-public-enemies","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":67,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2121056","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":712,"t":"Wonder Woman","y":"2009","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM calls it an \"engaging animated superheroine tale\" that also \"has graphic violence.\" Fighting escalates to beatings, stabbings, and decapitations, with blood shown during an occult human sacrifice and a gruesome zombie onslaught; there are also cleavage-baring outfits, brief hair-covered topless bathing scenes, and references to prostitution and pick-up lines. Positive: the film champions strong, independent womanhood with Wonder Woman as a genuinely heroic role model, and her male love interest grows out of womanizing behavior over the course of the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder-woman-2009","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":70,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q609436","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":713,"t":"X-Men Origins: Wolverine","y":"2009","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"CSM recommends this darker franchise entry for age 13+, flagging frequent, brutal comic-book violence -- shootings, stabbings, claw-slashing, and grim medical-experimentation scenes -- plus occasional strong language (\"s--t\"), a couple making out, brief male nudity, and characters drinking beer and hard liquor. Positive: Logan grows into a leader, and the story argues mercy beats vengeance even if that message gets crowded out by nonstop action.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men-origins-wolverine","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":107,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q217552","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":714,"t":"Batman: Under the Red Hood","y":"2010","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Drug dealers and brutal beatings in animated Batman movie.\" Concerns: brutal, bloody violence including the Joker beating Robin with a crowbar, gunfire, explosions, and character deaths, plus scattered language (\"hell,\" \"damn,\" \"scumbags\") and drug dealers in the plot. Positive: Batman holds to his no-killing code even as the film wrestles with morally murky ideas about justice and revenge.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-under-the-red-hood","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2384094","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":715,"t":"Iron Man 2","y":"2010","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Downey whips out the big guns, sexy banter in fun sequel,\" says CSM. The sequel piles on explosions and two hanging deaths (CSM flags this as the film's worst moment), along with mild profanity (\"damn,\" \"bitches\"), a drunk Tony at his own birthday party, Ivan's frequent vodka drinking, and abundant sexual innuendo alongside skimpy costumes. Positive: the film argues that caring only about yourself isn't enough even facing death, with Pepper Potts' honesty and Rhodey's willingness to challenge Tony for the greater good standing out as the story's real role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/iron-man-2","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":125,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q205028","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":716,"t":"Jonah Hex","y":"2010","la":"15+","ca":"15+","full":"CSM's tagline says it all: \"dumb, violent action Western totally misfires.\" Violence is intense and constant -- characters are shot, stabbed, chopped, and burned with a high body count -- alongside supernatural scares, mild sexual innuendo, and a female character depicted as a prostitute in skimpy lingerie. CSM notes positive messages and role models are very limited here: Hex is driven by revenge and kills without remorse, though the female lead does show some self-defense capability.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/jonah-hex","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Western"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q596085","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":717,"t":"Justice League: Crisis on Two Earths","y":"2010","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM describes it as a movie that \"mixes cartoon violence, positive messages.\" Expect extensive fighting with punches, arrows, and laser blasts, some blood, minor character deaths, and mild language like \"ass\" and \"crap.\" Positive: the film argues that giving in to bullies only empowers them, with Batman growing from refusing to help into embracing his responsibility, and Wonder Woman and Superman both modeling the courage it takes to stand up for what's right.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-crisis-on-two-earths","genre":["Animation","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q2620599","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":718,"t":"Superman/Batman: Apocalypse","y":"2010","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Supergirl comes of age in so-so animated adventure.\" Concerns: superhero battles with heavy destruction and some blood (weapons, stabbing, a teen witnessing a parent's death), brief nude silhouettes, skimpy costumes, and mild language (\"ass,\" \"hell\"). Positive: Kara starts out dazzled by an over-the-top shopping montage but ultimately learns to stand up for herself and choose a life of responsibility over letting others control her fate.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/supermanbatman-apocalypse","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3129837","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":719,"t":"All-Star Superman","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Violence and minor sensuality in reflective Superman tale.\" Facing his own impending death, Superman deals with several scary/intense superhero battles, a steamy shower scene, and mild language (\"hell,\" one \"son of a bitch\"). Positive: Superman responds to mortality with love, forgiveness, and kindness, modeling a gentler, more compassionate hero focused on helping others.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/all-star-superman","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4728320","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":720,"t":"Batman: Year One","y":"2011","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Animated superhero drama is too intense for young fans.\" Concerns: a kidnapped infant in mortal danger, bloody shootouts and a burning victim, red-light-district scenes with suggested prostitution, an extramarital affair, and language (\"hell,\" \"bitch,\" \"bastard,\" \"goddamn\"). Positive: Jim Gordon risks his career and safety to fight a corrupt police department, standing up for justice even as the film shows him making messy personal mistakes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-year-one","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":4,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":64,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q129161","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":721,"t":"Captain America: The First Avenger","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Comic book adventure mixes patriotism, explosive action,\" says CSM. Gun battles, fireballs, and fistfights run throughout, including a point-blank shooting and a character pulled through an airplane propeller, plus a villain with an exposed skull-like face that can startle younger viewers, occasional \"hell\" and \"damn,\" pub drinking, and a couple of romantic kisses. Positive: CSM praises Steve Rogers as an old-fashioned, nearly flawless role model -- brave, compassionate, and self-sacrificing -- whose story champions courage and standing up for others over physical strength alone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-america-the-first-avenger","genre":["Live-Action","War","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q275120","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":722,"t":"Green Lantern","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM describes it as an \"entertaining but superficial superhero thriller.\" The villain Parallax is genuinely frightening for younger kids, and there's a disturbing syringe-to-eye moment along with loud explosions and battle scenes; language includes occasional \"s--t,\" \"a--hole,\" and \"goddammit.\" Positive: the film's core message is that admitting fear is the first step to overcoming it, and cocky test pilot Hal Jordan proves to have a genuinely caring heart beneath the swagger, using his new powers for good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/green-lantern","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q903885","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":723,"t":"Green Lantern: Emerald Knights","y":"2011","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Violent, animated superhero movie with thoughtful messages.\" Concerns: near-constant fighting via power rings and hand-to-hand combat, some blue alien blood, and mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\"). Positive: the anthology structure explores destiny versus free will, and new Green Lantern recruits show real courage and camaraderie despite veterans' occasional dismissiveness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/green-lantern-emerald-knights","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1093399","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":724,"t":"Thor","y":"2011","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Surprisingly complex superhero action-adventure,\" per CSM. Thor's battles bring stabbing, hitting, and explosions that stay intense without turning gory, plus mead-hall ale drinking at Asgardian celebrations, a little mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell\"), and a few kisses and comments about characters' looks. Positive: CSM highlights the film's message that revenge only spreads harm, embodied by Odin's effort to raise a son who tempers strength with wisdom, alongside a female scientist who won't compromise her research for anyone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thor","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Thor (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":725,"t":"X-Men: First Class","y":"2011","la":"13+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Superhero film has action, thrills, tough moral questions.\" Set against the Cold War, the film includes major explosions, a boy watching his mother killed, and a coin turned lethal weapon, plus one use of \"f--k,\" 1960s-style social drinking and smoking, and Bond-style outfits implying nudity. Positive: Xavier's clear moral compass and Erik's more conflicted, revenge-driven arc give kids real material for discussing self-acceptance and fear of the unknown.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men-first-class","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":131,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q223596","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":726,"t":"Batman: The Dark Knight Returns Part 1","y":"2012","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Extremely violent animated addition to the Batman story.\" Concerns: graphic fight scenes with stabbing and eye-gouging, a knife gang terrorizing citizens, a bloody flashback of the Waynes' murder, whiskey drinking, and mild language (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"son of a bitch\"). Positive: the film is less about clean heroism than about wrestling with good and evil in every person, as an aging Bruce Wayne returns to the cowl out of obligation rather than glory.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-the-dark-knight-returns-part-1","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Batman: The Dark Knight Returns (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":727,"t":"Ghost Rider: Spirit of Vengeance","y":"2012","la":"15+","ca":"15+","full":"Common Sense Media calls this sequel a \"crazy, violent, dumb action sequel [that] quickly burns out,\" rating it 15+. Characters burn and decay on-screen, a mother and young boy are slapped around, and the fights add gunfire and explosions to the skull-faced hero's usual mayhem; language includes one F-word plus \"d--k\" and \"goddamn,\" and a supporting character is referenced as an alcoholic. Positive: the film gestures at \"with great power comes great responsibility,\" though Johnny's devil's-bargain backstory undercuts it as real role-model material.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ghost-rider-spirit-of-vengeance","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q41854","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":728,"t":"Justice League: Doom","y":"2012","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Great teamwork in otherwise violent superhero adventure.\" Concerns: heavy fist fighting and fantasy-weapon violence, characters set on fire, buried alive, and shot with visible blood, plus mild language (\"crap,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"). Positive: seven heroes each contribute their own strengths to overcome the villains' plot, a strong lesson in teamwork even though Batman's short temper is on display.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-doom","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3137760","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":729,"t":"Superman vs. The Elite","y":"2012","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Strong violence countered by positive messages, good story.\" Concerns: heavy comic-book violence (punching, battering, wartime destruction, and torture flashbacks), British-slang profanity plus \"ass,\" \"damn,\" and stronger words, frequent sexual innuendo from one character pursuing Superman, and a supporting character's drinking problem. Positive: Superman refuses to abandon his commitment to fairness and non-lethal justice even under public pressure to get tougher, and Lois Lane is shown as brave and sharp.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-vs-the-elite","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q3977964","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":730,"t":"The Avengers","y":"2012","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Heroes work together in explosive comic-book adventure,\" per CSM. Massive battle sequences level city blocks with implied heavy casualties, alien combat, and weapons fire throughout, plus profanity like \"son of a bitch,\" \"bastard,\" and \"hell,\" minimal drinking, and only flirty banter for romance. Positive: CSM emphasizes teamwork as the throughline -- each hero works through a personal flaw, from Iron Man's selfishness to Black Widow and Hawkeye's troubled pasts -- to unite around a shared mission.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-avengers","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":142,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q182218","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":731,"t":"The Dark Knight Rises","y":"2012","la":"15+","ca":"15+","full":"\"Bale's final Batman is as gritty and dark as the first two,\" per Common Sense Media. The trilogy closer delivers frequent, cringe-inducingly realistic violence, including neck-breakings, stabbings, and mass explosions with a high body count; language stays fairly sparse (\"bitch,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"), cocktails appear at formal events, and Bruce Wayne shares passionate kisses with two women, one leading to an off-camera night together shown afterward in bare shoulders and embraces. Positive: the film explores identity, responsibility, sacrifice, and justice, with Batman modeling courage and selflessness while supporting characters John Blake and Selina Kyle show loyalty and growth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-dark-knight-rises","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":164,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q189330","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":732,"t":"Batman: The Dark Knight Returns Part 2","y":"2013","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Extremely violent, ambiguous end to animated Batman saga.\" Concerns: near-constant fighting with guns, stabbing, and visible blood, an escort-service subplot, partial nudity under Nazi-style imagery, and characters drinking to cope. Positive: Batman rallies a scattered group toward a greater good, though the film leaves viewers to wrestle with whether vigilante justice is really justice at all.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-the-dark-knight-returns-part-2","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Batman: The Dark Knight Returns (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":733,"t":"Iron Man 3","y":"2013","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Fewer playboy antics, but still plenty of violence,\" says CSM. Public bombings and assassinations bring a more grounded, human-scaled violence than earlier films, with language including \"s--t,\" \"hell,\" and \"goddamn,\" party and bar drinking (with one character admitting past substance problems), and women shown in bikinis and lingerie. Positive: CSM points to Tony Stark's real growth here -- toward commitment, selflessness, and mentoring a young boy -- as a caution that unchecked power breeds hubris.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/iron-man-3","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":130,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q209538","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":734,"t":"Justice League: The Flashpoint Paradox","y":"2013","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Violent animation about tragic pasts has frenzied action.\" Concerns: intense violence including Wonder Woman holding a severed head and causing a death by hanging, a bloodied face after a beating, a child discovering his murdered mother, a flask-drinking parent, and scattered profanity (\"hell,\" \"crap,\" \"a--hole\"). Positive: the story turns on themes of accepting what can't be changed (echoing the Serenity Prayer) as Flash reckons with grief over his mother's death.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-flashpoint-paradox","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":81,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q12125315","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":735,"t":"Man of Steel","y":"2013","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM calls it a \"brooding, action-packed reboot\" for Superman, recommending age 12+. Destruction is constant - buildings collapse, cars flatten, aircraft go down - and the climactic fight includes Superman breaking a villain's neck, a first for the character; language stays occasional (\"s--t,\" one use of \"f-ing\"). Positive: both of Clark's fathers model responsibility and selfless guidance, and Superman himself consistently uses his power to protect others rather than himself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/man-of-steel","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":143,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q622769","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":736,"t":"Superman: Unbound","y":"2013","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Superman fights, learns life lessons in animated thriller.\" Concerns: heavy super-powered fighting, terrorist threats with guns, bombs, and missiles, mild language (\"hell,\" \"God\"), and a grown-up romance between Superman and Lois Lane with kissing. Positive: Superman remains a steady role model for kids who feel like outsiders, and both he and Supergirl learn that overprotecting the people you love keeps everyone from truly living.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-unbound","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q7643809","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":737,"t":"The Wolverine","y":"2013","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Thrilling, action-packed adventure treads dark waters.\" Wolverine's claws maim and kill across bloody, bone-crunching fights, guns and swords are everywhere, and language includes \"bitch,\" \"s--t,\" and one \"f--k\"; there's implied intercourse and a scene of three underwear-clad characters kissing, plus some bar drinking. Positive: Logan's fierce sense of justice, and Yukio and Mariko's proactive strength -- they rescue him as often as he rescues them.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wolverine","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":138,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q197491","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":738,"t":"Thor: The Dark World","y":"2013","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Teen-friendly comic-book sequel is brutal but not gory,\" per CSM. Knife fights, gunfights, and explosions drive the action, with a single use of \"s--t\" among milder language, some social drinking, kissing and flirting, and one brief non-sexual scene of blurred male nudity. Positive: CSM highlights the film's takeaway that it's better to be a good man than a king, with Thor's steadfast convictions and the story's openness to redemption for even compromised characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thor-the-dark-world","genre":["Live-Action","Fantasy","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1201853","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":739,"t":"Batman: Assault on Arkham","y":"2014","la":"14+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Cynical and violent superhero tale has some cursing,\" says Common Sense Media. Amanda Waller sends the Suicide Squad -- Harley Quinn, Deadshot, Killer Frost -- into Arkham Asylum, and the film delivers exploding and frozen-then-shattered heads, hangings, and regular profanity (\"s--t,\" \"a--hole\"). Harley Quinn is shown undressing and two characters are implied to have sex, plus the Joker jokes about abusing her. Positive messages are essentially absent; CSM notes the story centers Batman's villains rather than any real role models, making it best suited for older teen superfans.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-assault-on-arkham","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q16155099","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":740,"t":"Captain America: The Winter Soldier","y":"2014","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Heavy fantasy violence, but no sex in superhero sequel,\" says CSM. Frequent hand-to-hand combat, shooting, and falls bring some blood and explosions, with \"s--t\" occasionally audible under the battle noise, minimal champagne drinking, and only a strategic kiss between Cap and Black Widow used to dodge pursuers. Positive: CSM praises the film's stand that \"fear does not equal freedom,\" with Cap modeling courage, integrity, and loyalty while the story questions weapons stockpiling and preemptive strikes.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-america-the-winter-soldier","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1765358","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":741,"t":"Guardians of the Galaxy","y":"2014","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Marvel sci-fi adventure has laughs and action violence,\" per CSM. Fistfights, shootouts, and explosions run through the film alongside a handful of character deaths, strong language including \"s--t\" and \"bulls--t,\" sexual tension and references to Peter Quill's past conquests, and unnamed alcohol leading to onscreen drunkenness. Positive: CSM says the flawed Guardians ultimately choose teamwork and selflessness over self-interest, protecting each other even at personal cost.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/guardians-of-the-galaxy","genre":["Live-Action","Sci-Fi","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":121,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q5887360","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":742,"t":"Justice League: War","y":"2014","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Dark animated tale has constant violence, some profanity.\" Concerns: unrelenting comic-book violence with sword fights and characters thrown through buildings, bullying and taunting between heroes, and language including \"s--t,\" \"son of a bitch,\" and \"ass.\" Positive: despite early infighting and disrespect toward Wonder Woman, the team ultimately learns the value of teamwork and perseverance against a shared threat.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-war","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15710938","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":743,"t":"Son of Batman","y":"2014","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Violent and noir-ish Batman is engaging but cynical,\" per Common Sense Media. Bruce Wayne discovers he has a hot-tempered son, Damian, and the pair face frequent sword-and-gun combat, including eye stabbings and a child pinned to a wall by blades. There's mild profanity (\"bastard,\" \"screw you\") and passing sex references, like a villain keeping prostitutes at his apartment. Positive: the film explores a complicated father-son bond, though CSM notes there isn't much traditional heroism -- the characters are deeply flawed rather than role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dcu-son-of-batman","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15635431","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":744,"t":"X-Men: Days of Future Past","y":"2014","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Time-traveling superhero sequel has lots of action violence.\" Bone-crunching super-powered battles include stabbing, shooting, and visible corpses; language includes \"s--t\" and \"a--hole\"; young Xavier injects a mobility-restoring serum styled like drug use and drinks heavily early on; a mutant's blue form appears unclothed. Positive: the film argues killing never solves anything -- friendship, unity, and hope do -- with Xavier modeling generosity and ethical leadership.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men-days-of-future-past","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Sci-Fi","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":131,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q4985891","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":745,"t":"Ant-Man","y":"2015","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Clever, funny, cool Marvel movie has lots of sci-fi action,\" per CSM. Fistfights and shootouts include villains dissolving into \"gelatinous goo,\" scattered strong language (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"damn\"), a couple of suggestive jokes and one kissing scene, and social champagne, beer, and wine drinking without excess. Positive: CSM highlights forgiveness and redemption as the film's core themes, with Scott Lang and Hank Pym both working to protect their daughters and Hope van Dyne portrayed as a strong, capable partner rather than a sidekick.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ant-man","genre":["Live-Action","Comedy","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":117,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q5901134","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":746,"t":"Avengers: Age of Ultron","y":"2015","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Superheroes reteam for entertaining, action-packed sequel,\" says CSM. The nonstop battling stays cartoonish rather than graphic but implies heavy civilian casualties throughout, with profanity like \"son-of-a-bitch\" and \"bastard,\" some celebratory drinking, and kissing and flirting in form-fitting costumes. Positive: CSM frames the team's motto -- \"united you stand, divided you fall\" -- as the film's real lesson, though it also notes both female heroes need rescuing at points, a wrinkle worth discussing.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/avengers-age-of-ultron","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":141,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q14171368","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":747,"t":"Batman vs. Robin","y":"2015","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Excellent tale with disturbing imagery, frequent violence,\" says Common Sense Media. Ten-year-old Damian/Robin rebels against his father's \"justice, not vengeance\" code, and the story includes a child abuser called the Dollmaker who sews doll masks onto children's faces, flashbacks to young Bruce watching his parents' murder, and a scene of Batman hallucinating after ingesting a drug. There's mild profanity, gun violence, and an implied-sex scene between Bruce and his girlfriend. Positive: CSM praises the film's honest look at Batman and Damian as \"cold, damaged, and temperamental\" people striving toward the film's core lesson about justice over vengeance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-vs-robin","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":4,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18844637","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":748,"t":"Fantastic Four","y":"2015","la":"13+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Disappointing adventure wastes talented cast, gets bloody.\" This darker reboot has the villain killing dozens of people, sometimes graphically (blood, an exploding head), and The Thing racking up a body count as a military weapon, plus profanity (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"d--k,\" \"damn\") and young characters drinking and making poor choices as a result. Positive: despite the grim tone, the four leads pull together as a team and the film argues young people deserve to be trusted with real responsibility.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/fantastic-four-2015","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Sci-Fi","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":100,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Fantastic Four (2015 film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":749,"t":"Justice League: Gods and Monsters","y":"2015","la":"14+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Engaging noir tale is dark and violent; some cursing, nudity,\" per Common Sense Media. This alternate-universe Justice League story includes a sword-to-the-chest killing, gunfire, explosions, and demonic imagery, plus profanity (\"s--t,\" \"goddammit\") and nudity -- a female android appears fully nude, and Wonder Woman wears revealing clothing. A college flashback references marijuana use. Positive: the film wrestles seriously with justice, power, and whether the ends justify the means, per CSM, even as its heroes remain morally complicated rather than idealized.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-gods-and-monsters","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":76,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19879419","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":750,"t":"Justice League: Throne of Atlantis","y":"2015","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Animated Aquaman origin story has violence, cursing,\" per Common Sense Media. Arthur Curry, grieving his father, gets severely drunk in a Maine dive bar and brawls with a group of longshoremen before later facing stabbings, a shark-attack death, and demonic imagery from an Atlantean uprising. Language includes \"s--t,\" \"crap,\" and \"bastard.\" Positive: the film is honest about grief and imperfection -- Superman and Wonder Woman struggle with their own powers -- though CSM found few clear positive messages in this darker take on the team's formation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-throne-of-atlantis","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18151272","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":751,"t":"Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice","y":"2016","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"Common Sense Media describes it as a \"promising but overlong superhero mash-up [that] is dark, violent,\" with an age recommendation of 13+. The body count is high from assassinations, building collapses, and an extended Batman-Superman brawl; a bathtub scene between Clark and Lois shows her bare shoulders and legs, and there's some partial nudity elsewhere. Positive: despite their early rivalry, Batman and Superman ultimately choose teamwork over conflict, and Wonder Woman's introduction offers an independent, agency-driven female hero.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-v-superman-dawn-of-justice","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":151,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":752,"t":"Batman: Bad Blood","y":"2016","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Superviolent superhero mayhem with a complex story,\" per Common Sense Media. With Batman missing, Nightwing, Robin, Batwing, and the newly introduced Batwoman fight a consortium of villains through buildings exploding and collapsing, gunfights, swordplay, and characters who appear dead before reviving. Mild profanity (\"crap,\" \"damn,\" \"bitch\") runs throughout, and a brief fantasy sequence shows Batman partially nude. Positive: CSM highlights an ethnically diverse team modeling intelligence, bravery, and loyalty, with the message that \"good triumphs over evil\" through teamwork -- including Batwoman's canon debut as a lesbian character.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-bad-blood","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":72,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q21095079","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":753,"t":"Captain America: Civil War","y":"2016","la":"12+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Intense, entertaining adventure is a great threequel.\" The Avengers split into warring factions, with tons of explosions, collateral damage, and even a graphically depicted flashback to a past violent act. Language includes scattered \"s--t\" and \"son of a bitch,\" plus a quick kiss between Cap and a love interest. Positive: the film wrestles with loyalty, personal will versus collective responsibility, and honesty, with most Avengers showing genuine remorse over civilian casualties.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-america-civil-war","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":147,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18407657","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":754,"t":"Doctor Strange","y":"2016","la":"11+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Mysticism, humor, and action surround unique Marvel hero.\" Expect large-scale magical destruction, a brutal car crash, a beheading (no gore shown), and unsettling operating-room scenes with blood. Language is fairly mild, and there's brief reference to a past relationship. Positive: arrogant surgeon Stephen Strange learns that \"it's not about you,\" embracing humility, perseverance, and eventual self-sacrifice for the greater good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/doctor-strange","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Fantasy"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18406872","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":755,"t":"Justice League vs. Teen Titans","y":"2016","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Animated violence, demonic imagery in solid DC installment,\" says Common Sense Media. Batman sends his son Damian to train with the Teen Titans just as the demon Trigon possesses the Justice League, leading to sword decapitation, electrocution, and explosions, plus mild language (\"hell,\" \"damn\") and Starfire shown in a skimpy, revealing robe on a video call. Positive: CSM notes Damian starts out arrogant and self-centered but grows through the story, ultimately learning to value teamwork and family alongside his new teammates.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-vs-teen-titans","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22251976","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":756,"t":"Suicide Squad","y":"2016","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM's tagline calls it a \"muddled, violent mess\" where \"DC's antiheroes disappoint,\" rating it 14+. Assassinations and shootouts run throughout, language includes \"s--t,\" \"p---y,\" and sexist dialogue about controlling women, and one scene shows a man striking a woman. Positive: the \"honor among thieves\" arc gives hardened criminals like Deadshot and Diablo real moments of parental love and redemption, per CSM's review.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/suicide-squad","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":123,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q18604504","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":757,"t":"X-Men: Apocalypse","y":"2016","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Superhero-size violence, fab effects in '80s-set threequel.\" Expect big explosions, hand-to-hand fighting, a bloody Wolverine rampage, and a tragic child death, plus one strong swear and milder language (\"damn,\" \"hell,\" \"ass\"); a few characters wear skimpy, armor-like outfits. Positive: \"united you stand, divided you crumble\" -- Professor X's faith in people and Mystique's loyalty anchor a message about teamwork beating fear.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/x-men-apocalypse","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Sci-Fi","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":131,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q17042878","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":758,"t":"Batman and Harley Quinn","y":"2017","la":"14+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Noir superhero story has sex, cursing, and violence,\" says Common Sense Media, warning that this entry skews more adult than typical Batman DTV films. Batman and Nightwing reluctantly team with a paroled Harley Quinn against ecoterrorist villains Poison Ivy and Jason Woodrue, in scenes featuring monster-stabbing deaths, martial arts combat, occasional profanity, and more sexual content than usual -- including implied sex and crude humor around Harley. Positive: CSM notes the film's underlying message that doing wrong to fight wrongdoing is still wrong, even as its cynical, cursing heroes fall short of being traditional role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-harley-quinn","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":74,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q30080476","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":759,"t":"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2","y":"2017","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Lots of laughs, thrills, tunes in slightly lesser sequel.\" Frequent weapon battles and space combat include people being \"spaced\" out of airlocks, high body counts, and a major character's death. Language is stronger than the original (\"s--t,\" \"bulls--t,\" \"d--k\"), and Ravagers drink to the point of drunkenness at a pub. Positive: the flawed, roguish Guardians make selfless choices for one another, driving home themes of teamwork, redemption, and found family.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/guardians-of-the-galaxy-vol-2","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":136,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q20001199","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":760,"t":"Justice League","y":"2017","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"All-star superhero adventure is uneven but entertaining.\" Concerns: large-scale battle violence with explosions, destruction, and hand-to-hand combat; scattered profanity (\"s--t,\" \"a--hole,\" \"son of a bitch\"); kissing between reunited lovers; and Aquaman downing a bottle of liquor before tossing it into the sea. Positive: the film centers on teamwork and working with others for the greater good, with Batman in particular learning the value of collaboration over solo heroics.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q20501835","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":761,"t":"Teen Titans: The Judas Contract","y":"2017","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Superteens resist betrayal and brutality; violence, cursing,\" per Common Sense Media. Cult leader Brother Blood hires the mercenary Deathstroke to hunt the Titans one by one, using an inside traitor, in a story full of point-blank shootings, torture, lasers, and hand-to-hand combat, plus occasional profanity (\"s--t,\" \"piss off\") and some kissing and revealing costumes. Positive: CSM praises the film's message that \"good defeats evil\" and its redefinition of family as loyal, unselfish people who work together -- including a betrayer's arc toward making amends.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teen-titans-the-judas-contract","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28465798","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":762,"t":"The Lego Batman Movie","y":"2017","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Clever, creative, action-packed adventure/toy ad.\" Darker and more explosive than the first Lego Movie, with constant battles, bombs, and destruction (all bloodless, since everyone's plastic), plus potty-adjacent insults like \"stupid\" and \"sucks,\" a joke about Robin going pantsless, and Alfred sipping wine. Positive: Batman's arc from egotistical loner to team player anchors the film, and Barbara Gordon is written as sharp and capable, with the story's real lesson being that working as a team with people you care about beats doing everything yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-lego-batman-movie","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23013169","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":763,"t":"Thor: Ragnarok","y":"2017","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Funniest Thor movie has tons of style, plenty of violence.\" Sword-and-sorcery battles include a bloody stabbing of a main character and a melting death, plus frequent explosions; numerous characters die. Language includes \"s--t\" and \"hell\" alongside adolescent humor, and one character has long used alcohol to cope with trauma. Positive: Thor grows from arrogant prince into a worthy, humble leader, while Valkyrie models courage in the face of past trauma, with teamwork as a throughline.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thor-ragnarok","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":130,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22665878","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":764,"t":"Wonder Woman","y":"2017","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Engaging, entertaining, empowering superhero adventure,\" per Common Sense Media, which recommends age 12+. Frequent WWI battle violence brings a real body count, a naked man briefly covers himself in one scene, and adults drink at pubs and receptions with one character shown intoxicated. Positive: Diana models courage, selflessness, and compassion as a genuine equal to her male co-stars, and CSM praises the film's message that women can be just as capable warriors and leaders as men.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder-woman","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":141,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q20502242","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":765,"t":"Ant-Man and the Wasp","y":"2018","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Funny, action-packed sequel is lighter Marvel fare.\" Frequent sci-fi chases and hand-to-hand combat put major characters in peril, including flashbacks of children in distress, though no major characters die; one character is drugged without consent. Language includes infrequent \"s--t\" and \"ass,\" and adults drink wine with meals. Positive: the film promotes forgiveness, redemption, and teamwork, with Hope van Dyne -- Marvel's first female hero with title billing -- shown as strong and capable alongside Scott's devotion to his daughter.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ant-man-and-the-wasp","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22957393","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":766,"t":"Aquaman","y":"2018","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Underwater origin story has lots of comic book action,\" per CSM. Concerns: extensive fantasy fighting with impalements, drownings, and monster attacks (largely bloodless despite the intensity); scattered profanity (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"d--k\"); adult kissing and a shirtless Aquaman; and a bar scene where a character gets drunk with little consequence. Positive: courage, loyalty, and accepting responsibility for the greater good, with Mera and Atlanna written as capable characters rather than damsels in distress.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/aquaman","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":143,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q22998395","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":767,"t":"Avengers: Infinity War","y":"2018","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Intense violence, strong messages in shocking Marvel epic.\" This is the darkest MCU entry yet, with frequent, massively destructive action including brutal beatings, impalings, and stabbings, plus real, lasting consequences for beloved characters. Language includes a couple uses of \"s--t\" and two aborted f-word attempts, and one scene implies a couple has been intimate. Positive: heroism, self-sacrifice, and teamwork drive the story, with a diverse cast of heroes -- including strong women and a resourceful teenage Spider-Man -- fighting with equal bravery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/avengers-infinity-war","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":149,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23780914","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":768,"t":"Batman Ninja","y":"2018","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Anime Batman time-travels to ancient Japan; lots of action.\" Gorilla Grodd's time machine strands Batman and a roster of DC heroes and villains in feudal Japan for nonstop sword, spear, and cannon battles, plus mild swearing (\"hell,\" \"damn\") and some female characters drawn in revealing outfits with light innuendo. Positive: Batman's courage, intelligence, and willingness to sacrifice for others carry through no matter what century he's in, reinforcing that good wins out over evil.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-ninja","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q44353698","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":769,"t":"Black Panther","y":"2018","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Masterful Marvel film has depth, diversity -- and violence.\" Close-up ritual combat includes bloody wounds, stabbings, and spears and curved knives in play, with more widespread explosive violence than earlier Marvel films. Language is infrequent (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"hell\"), and adults drink socially in the background. Positive: the film promotes teamwork, integrity, and courage, with T'Challa's thoughtful leadership and strong, capable women like Okoye, Nakia, and tech genius Shuri offering standout role models.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/black-panther","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":134,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23780734","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":770,"t":"Teen Titans Go! To the Movies","y":"2018","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Irreverent, immature comedy cleverly mocks superhero genre.\" Expect nonstop cartoonish violence with guns, missiles, and swords, plenty of toilet humor (farts, poop, \"diarrhea\"), mild insults like \"morons\" and \"losers,\" and a couple of brief animated bare bottoms. Positive: the Titans' female members are shown as every bit as capable as the boys, and the film's central message -- that friendship matters more than fame or box-office success -- comes through even when the team's problem-solving leans on chaos over caution.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/teen-titans-go-to-the-movies","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q46392313","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":771,"t":"Venom","y":"2018","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Violent, uninspired comic book tale misses the mark,\" says Common Sense Media, which sets the age recommendation at 14+. Expect intense fantasy violence with slicing, stabbing, and jump-scare fangs from Venom himself, plus strong language (\"s--t,\" one F-word, one use of \"p---y\") and an implied-sex scene between Eddie and Anne. Positive: the film's message that \"everyone has a right to live, human or not\" comes through Anne's forgiveness toward even the most monstrous characters.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/venom","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":4,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":112,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23006268","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":772,"t":"Avengers: Endgame","y":"2019","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Intense but satisfying finale is an epic gift to MCU fans.\" Frequent, intense comic-book violence includes dismemberment, decapitation, stabbing, and destructive explosions, and several beloved characters die in ways that may upset viewers. Language includes \"son of a bitch\" and \"ass\" (even from Captain America), and Thor's heavy drinking as a grief coping mechanism is a recurring subplot. Positive: courage, self-sacrifice, and the idea that \"family is more than pure biology\" run throughout, as flawed heroes become stronger together and choose the collective good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/avengers-endgame","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":181,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23781155","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":773,"t":"Batman: Hush","y":"2019","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"Batman teams up with Catwoman to unravel the identity of Hush, a mysterious new villain who knows all his secrets. Common Sense Media notes cartoon violence throughout -- deaths of major characters, explosions, brutal hand-to-hand fights, gunfire, and a decapitation -- plus language like \"s--t,\" \"bitch,\" and \"goddamn.\" Batman and Catwoman's romance includes kissing and an implied night together, and characters drink socially. Positive: Batman lives by a strict moral code, refusing to kill even a defeated enemy, and the story rewards loyalty and resourcefulness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-hush","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":82,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q63919331","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":774,"t":"Captain Marvel","y":"2019","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Powerful female superhero story has some violence, language.\" Combat mixes fistfights with fantasy weapons like laser scepters and photon blasts, plus explosions and minimal alien blood; all on-screen deaths are extraterrestrial. Language stays fairly mild (\"s--t,\" \"hell,\" \"ass\"), with no real sex or substance content. Positive: Carol Danvers is a fearless, capable lead who is never objectified, and the film's \"you're stronger than you think\" message is reinforced by courageous supporting women like Maria Rambeau and Dr. Wendy Lawson.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-marvel","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23781129","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":776,"t":"Dark Phoenix","y":"2019","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Sophie Turner is best part of intense, dark X-Men finale.\" The trilogy-ender features heavy superpower battles, impalement, alien attacks, and an upsetting death, plus profanity (\"s--t,\" \"damn,\" one \"f---ing\") and party drinking. Positive: the story favors teamwork over vengeance, with Jean's inner conflict, Scott's protectiveness, and Xavier's continued advocacy for mutant acceptance giving the ensemble real emotional weight.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dark-phoenix","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Sci-Fi","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q31188935","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":777,"t":"Justice League vs. the Fatal Five","y":"2019","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Superheroes encounter brutal villains from future; violence,\" per Common Sense Media. Three members of the 31st-century Fatal Five hijack a time-travel capsule to hunt young Green Lantern Jessica Cruz, unleashing continuous explosions, fireballs, gunfire, and swordplay, plus mild profanity (\"hell,\" \"bastard\") and one scene of a character running naked through the streets. Positive: CSM praises the film for portraying Jessica's PTSD and another hero's paranoia with care, showing characters with mental health struggles working toward recovery while the team proves strong, loyal, and brave.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-vs-the-fatal-five","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":77,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q61740835","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":778,"t":"Reign of the Supermen","y":"2019","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Animated sequel with frequent violence and a complex plot,\" per Common Sense Media. Six months after Superman's apparent death, four new \"Supermen\" emerge in Metropolis while Lois Lane investigates, amid explosions, gunfire, alien attacks, and brutal hand-to-hand combat, plus mild profanity (\"hell,\" \"son of a bitch\") and Lois using seduction to gather information. Positive: CSM highlights Lois as resourceful and strong and the Justice League as determined and loyal, with the story affirming that good triumphs over evil and that heroic power shouldn't be underestimated.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/reign-of-the-supermen","genre":["Animation","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":87,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Reign of the Supermen (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":779,"t":"Shazam!","y":"2019","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Superhero comedy is charming, with some scary/violent parts.\" Concerns: car crashes, gunfire, and disintegrating characters, plus the monstrous Seven Deadly Sins killing people in disturbing ways; moderate profanity (\"s--t,\" \"ass,\" \"hell\"); two visits to a gentlemen's club played for comedy; and characters buying beer before switching drinks. Positive: the loving Vasquez foster family models found family and support, and Billy learns to move past selfishness toward gratitude and teamwork.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shazam","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":4393,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q62961936","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":780,"t":"Wonder Woman: Bloodlines","y":"2019","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"This animated origin story sends Wonder Woman from Themyscira into the human world to protect a troubled teenage girl from a criminal syndicate. Common Sense Media flags frequent violence -- bloody deaths, explosions, gunfire, and lengthy hand-to-hand combat -- along with language such as \"bitch\" and \"s--t,\" a kiss, and some revealing costumes. Positive: the nearly all-female cast shows women as courageous, smart game-changers, and the film models that doing right sometimes means taking risks.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder-woman-bloodlines","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":88,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q66764344","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":781,"t":"Superman: Man of Tomorrow","y":"2020","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Graphic violence and imagery in animated origin story,\" per Common Sense Media, this follows a young Clark Kent interning at the Daily Planet while learning to become the Man of Steel. The review flags lengthy fights with firearms, flame, and chains leaving characters bloody and beaten, profanity like \"s--t\" and \"a--holes,\" Superman briefly losing his clothes to flames, and the alien Lobo binge-drinking from a bottle. Positive: the film promotes diversity, though CSM notes even Lois Lane turns manipulative here.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-man-of-tomorrow","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q96419433","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":782,"t":"Superman: Red Son","y":"2020","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"Reimagining Superman's rocket landing in Soviet Ukraine instead of Kansas, this alternate-history tale follows him growing up as a tool of Stalin's Cold War propaganda machine. Common Sense Media notes Superman kills Stalin with heat vision, Batman dies by suicide rather than return to the gulag, and there's schoolyard violence, profanity (\"s--t,\" \"bitch,\" \"hell\"), and Lois Lane shown as a heavy smoker trying to quit. Positive: strong, independent female characters and a thoughtful look at how power can be used or misused.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman-red-son","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q78914620","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":783,"t":"The New Mutants","y":"2020","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Groundbreaking elements, but violent X-Men tale falls short.\" This horror-tinged spinoff includes stories of teens who've killed people (some remorseful, some not), creature attacks, torture scenes, and bloody imagery, plus strong profanity (\"a--hole,\" \"bulls--t,\" \"bitch\"), a bully's racist language, and both same-sex and opposite-sex teen make-out scenes with some shirtless/partial nudity. Positive: an unusually diverse cast across race, gender, and sexuality, with characters confronting fear and trauma through self-discovery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-new-mutants","genre":["Live-Action","Horror","Superhero"],"studio":"20th Century Fox","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:The New Mutants (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":784,"t":"Wonder Woman 1984","y":"2020","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Melancholy DC sequel about redemption has mixed messages.\" Concerns: frequent action violence, including gunplay and a scene where a character's appearance disturbingly deteriorates with blood dripping from his ears and nose; infrequent strong language and sexist catcalling; several passionate kisses and a scene implying a couple has slept together, shown in bed; and social drinking at a reception. Positive: women's skill as warriors and fighters, plus compassion and courage, though the film also suggests appearance affects women's self-worth.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/wonder-woman-1984","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":151,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q33408623","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":785,"t":"Batman: The Long Halloween, Part One","y":"2021","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Violence, smoking, language in noir DC action-mystery,\" says Common Sense Media of this adaptation, where Batman, Commissioner Gordon, and Harvey Dent hunt a holiday-themed killer. The review cites characters shot and killed with a silenced gun, a stabbing, a man pushed down a stairwell, cigarette and pipe smoking, and beer and wine drinking, with infrequent profanity (\"s--t,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"). Positive: the film questions vigilante justice and values teamwork, even as CSM notes its heroes come across as flawed and human rather than simply good.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-the-long-halloween-part-one","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Mystery"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":85,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106453617","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":786,"t":"Black Widow","y":"2021","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Strong women in ScarJo superhero film; violence, language.\" Extensive combat includes knives, punches, and a blunt instrument, plus explosions and a massive avalanche that put characters in peril. Language includes \"bitch,\" \"s--t,\" and \"dammit,\" and characters drink vodka and beer in moderation at gatherings. Positive: the film centers women's independence from those who'd control them, sisterhood, and found family, with Natasha, Yelena, and Melina shown as strong, clever, and powerful especially when they work together.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/black-widow","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":133,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23894626","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":787,"t":"Eternals","y":"2021","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"\"Visually strong but talky MCU tale has violence, sex scene.\" Frequent action against aggressive, goopy-gore monsters is layered with heavier real-world imagery, including references to the bombing of Hiroshima, and main characters die. There's one love scene showing bare shoulders and backs with clearly implied sex, plus adults drinking beer and liquor at gatherings; language includes \"s--t\" and \"ass.\" Positive: sacrifice, unconditional love, and teamwork run through the story, with characters modeling selfless caregiving and compassion even as a few grapple with morally difficult choices.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/eternals","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":156,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23894629","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":788,"t":"Justice Society: World War II","y":"2021","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"The Flash travels back in time and joins Wonder Woman's Justice Society to fight Nazis during World War II. Common Sense Media notes superhero and war violence throughout -- bombs, machine guns, explosions, and hand-to-hand combat -- plus cigarette smoking and a bottle of wine, with minimal language (\"hell\"). Positive: Wonder Woman emerges as the team's clear, capable leader, and the story emphasizes teamwork and standing against tyranny.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-society-world-war-ii","genre":["Animation","Superhero","War"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":84,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q105560151","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":789,"t":"Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings","y":"2021","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Funny, poignant, thrilling MCU adventure; action violence.\" Frequent martial-arts combat features guns, spears, bows, explosions, deaths and injuries, plus scary demon-like monsters in the third act. Language stays occasional (\"s--t,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"), with only light romantic tension between two leads. Positive: courage, heroism, and protecting those you love anchor the story, with Shang-Chi shown as brave, empathetic, and kind, and the film notable for its nearly all-Asian/Asian diaspora cast.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shang-chi-and-the-legend-of-the-ten-rings","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":132,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q65768589","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":790,"t":"Venom: Let There Be Carnage","y":"2021","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM describes this sequel as \"noisy violence and forced comedy in a poor super-sequel,\" recommending it for 14+. Carnage's rampage includes a head bitten off and eye-gouging, an animated flashback depicts child abuse, and language ramps up with an F-word and repeated \"s--t\"; a flashback also briefly shows cartoon nudity. Positive: Eddie and Venom's arc leans on teamwork, showing the pair (unlike their enemies) actually succeed once they stop fighting each other.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/venom-let-there-be-carnage","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":97,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q60498064","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":791,"t":"Batman and Superman: Battle of the Super Sons","y":"2022","la":"11+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"Not on Common Sense Media; per Wikipedia and IMDb's parents' guide, this animated adventure has young Jon Kent and Damian Wayne team up after the alien Starro infects the Justice League and Teen Titans with mind-controlling spores. IMDb notes moderate violence -- punches and kicks with visible blood, aliens bursting from mouths -- plus mild language (a couple uses of \"damn\") and no sex or substance content. Positive: the story centers on two young heroes learning to trust and work with each other despite their fathers' rivalry.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_and_Superman:_Battle_of_the_Super_Sons","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","runtimeMinutes":79,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q114770947","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":792,"t":"Black Adam","y":"2022","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Lots of bashing and smashing in disappointing DC movie,\" says CSM. Concerns: a high body count from electrocution, stabbing, shooting, and destruction, all gruesome but bloodless; sporadic profanity (\"s--t,\" \"bastard,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"); and brief flirting. Positive: the heroes are brave and try to do what's right even when they make mistakes, and the story notably puts the fate of Kahndaq in the hands of its own people rather than outside rescuers.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/black-adam","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q28657013","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":793,"t":"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever","y":"2022","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Epic, women-led sequel is part tribute, part intense battle.\" The film opens with the off-screen death of King T'Challa and processes real grief before Wakanda faces the underwater nation of Talokan, with combat, drowning, and an emotional second death along the way. Positive: Queen Ramonda, Okoye, Nakia, and Shuri lead as strong, smart, and brave role models, and the story favors diplomacy and collaboration over revenge.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/black-panther-wakanda-forever","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":161,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q54860489","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":794,"t":"Catwoman: Hunted","y":"2022","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Female-centered superhero story has violence, some innuendo,\" per Common Sense Media, this anime-style adventure catches Catwoman between Interpol, a global crime syndicate, and Batwoman. The review notes fighting with assault weapons, swords, and steel claws, a character impaled on rebar, mild language (\"crap,\" \"ass,\" \"hell\"), and strong innuendo between Catwoman and Batwoman including a bathing scene. Positive: CSM highlights that the primary heroes and villain are all women in a traditionally male-dominated genre.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/catwoman-hunted","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":78,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q109116363","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":795,"t":"DC League of Super-Pets","y":"2022","la":"6+","ca":"6+","full":"\"Furry cartoon superhero actioner is funny, cute; rude humor.\" Krypto and friends get into plenty of cartoon mayhem -- crashes, explosions, characters hit by cars -- plus bleeped-out profanity, a wisecracking turtle with adult-tinged innuendo, and a subplot involving lab-tested animals; the hero cast includes an engaged lesbian couple. Positive: the film's message that you'll do anything for someone you love, even let them go, comes through the pets' teamwork and self-sacrifice to save the people (and each other) they love.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/dc-league-of-super-pets","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Superhero","Adventure"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q106953528","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":796,"t":"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness","y":"2022","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Twisty, sometimes terrifying MCU film has scares, violence.\" Director Sam Raimi pushes the MCU into horror territory, with jump scares, a body-snatching villain, and graphic depictions of death, burning, and destruction; strong language includes \"s--t\" and \"goddamn,\" and adults drink martinis at a wedding. Positive: the film champions compassion, perseverance, and teamwork, with America Chavez showing real courage and Doctor Strange learning humility and the value of asking forgiveness.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/doctor-strange-in-the-multiverse-of-madness","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Fantasy"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q64211112","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":797,"t":"Morbius","y":"2022","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM sums it up as \"fighting and biting in a by-the-numbers superhero movie,\" rated 14+. Dr. Morbius's vampire-bat serum leads to clawed, blood-spattered violence and a bullying scene where a child is struck with a crutch; language is milder (\"a few uses of s--t\"), and hypodermic needles appear as Morbius injects his formula. Positive: the film does wrestle, if unevenly, with whether Morbius's power is \"a gift or a curse\" rather than treating his new abilities as pure triumph.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/morbius","genre":["Live-Action","Horror","Superhero"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q55405369","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":798,"t":"The Batman","y":"2022","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"CSM calls it a \"confident and mature yet dark, violent Batman reboot.\" Expect intense action violence including killings, dead bodies, brutal beatings, shootings, explosions, and a severed thumb, plus sporadic strong language and disturbing dialogue about orphans and drug addiction (a fictional eye-drop drug with visibly addicted characters). Positive: Batman grapples with the costs of vengeance versus genuinely helping people, learns from his mistakes, and the film critiques how misinformation spreads online.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-batman","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":176,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q61117344","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":799,"t":"Thor: Love and Thunder","y":"2022","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Rescue adventure focuses on love; violence, language.\" Gorr the God Butcher kidnaps Asgard's children, and the opening shows a young girl die of starvation before Thor and Jane Foster (now Mighty Thor) mount a rescue; language includes several uses of \"s--t,\" and there are references to divine orgies and a played-for-laughs nude Thor. Positive: the story promotes teamwork, empathy, and choosing love over guarding your heart, with Valkyrie's bisexuality and Korg's two dads offering LGBTQ+ representation.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thor-love-and-thunder","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Fantasy"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":119,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q65768604","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":800,"t":"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania","y":"2023","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"MCU threequel falls short on humor; violence, language.\" Scott and Hope, with Hank, Janet, and teenage Cassie, get stranded in the Quantum Realm battling Kang and his minions, with large-scale fights, background character deaths, and language like \"holy s--t\" and \"d--k\"; a tavern scene shows aliens drinking mind-altering beverages. Positive: the film promotes forgiveness, redemption, and \"looking out for the little guy,\" with the family working together and showing real courage.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/ant-man-and-the-wasp-quantumania","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":801,"t":"Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom","y":"2023","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Superhero sequel has comic-book violence, creepy monsters,\" says CSM. Concerns: largely bloodless but relentless action against skeletal zombies and clawed, tentacled creatures, plus a torture scene and a character who chooses suicide over capture; mild profanity including one use of \"goddamn\"; and Guinness beer shown in a positive light. Positive: Arthur shows courage and humility in asking a rival for help, with recurring themes of forgiveness, family, and working together against climate change.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/aquaman-and-the-lost-kingdom","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q91226161","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":802,"t":"Batman: The Doom That Came to Gotham","y":"2023","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Violence, drinking in animated Batman origin story,\" per Common Sense Media, this Lovecraftian tale has Bruce Wayne returning to Prohibition-era Gotham to stop a cult from unleashing an ancient evil. The review flags demonic and monster imagery throughout, a character sliced in half, a pickaxe attack, brief nonsexual nudity, hookah smoking, and a character known for binge-drinking wine, with mild profanity like \"son of a bitch.\" CSM found no clear positive messages or role models in this darker, horror-tinged origin story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/batman-the-doom-that-came-to-gotham","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Horror"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":3,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":86,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q117151097","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":803,"t":"Blue Beetle","y":"2023","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Loving family, intense scenes in DC's Latino superhero tale.\" Concerns: intense mech-suit fighting and a disturbing possession-like sequence with screaming, red eyes, and something moving under a character's skin, plus a scene depicting an armed immigration raid; frequent mild-to-moderate language; and an extended kiss with a joke about male arousal. Positive: \"your family is your superpower\" -- the humble, family-devoted hero and his female relatives model intelligence and independence, in DC's first Latino-led superhero film.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/blue-beetle","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":127,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Blue Beetle (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":804,"t":"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3","y":"2023","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Trauma, teamwork at heart of darker MCU threequel.\" This installment is notably darker, with graphic violence (decapitations, blood, skeletal remains) and disturbing flashbacks of animal experimentation and torture on a young Rocket; language includes the MCU's first use of the F-word, and Peter gets severely drunk early on. Positive: the story is ultimately about found family, forgiveness, and moving forward from trauma, with the Guardians showing loyalty and self-sacrifice for one another.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/guardians-of-the-galaxy-vol-3","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":150,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q29226331","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":805,"t":"Legion of Super-Heroes","y":"2023","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Animated superhero origin tale has violence, some language,\" says Common Sense Media of this story, where Supergirl travels to the future to stop a terrorist group from stealing a powerful weapon. The review notes Batman choking a villain to death, another character ripped in half, Supergirl stabbed with a kryptonite knife, occasional profanity (\"s--t,\" \"son of a bitch\"), and ongoing sexual tension with passionate kissing between Supergirl and Brainiac 5. Positive: the film emphasizes teamwork as young heroes learn to value their own gifts.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/legion-of-super-heroes","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":83,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q116919674","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":806,"t":"Shazam! Fury of the Gods","y":"2023","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Funny superhero sequel has action violence, language.\" Concerns: collapsing buildings, monster attacks, impalings, zombie-like creatures, and a terrifying dragon; frequent profanity, including a child character's cut-off \"motherfu--\"; and a party scene with sparkling wine and an implied hangover. Positive: \"the most powerful thing about you is you\" -- themes of found family, teamwork, and courage, carried by a cast diverse in race, disability, body type, and background.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/shazam-fury-of-the-gods","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Comedy"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":120,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q84712809","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":807,"t":"The Flash","y":"2023","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Intense, long superhero adventure explores loss, teamwork,\" per CSM. Concerns: extensive comic book violence with explosions, military-grade weapons, and a fairly high body count, including the stabbing death of Barry's mother and a tense scene of babies falling from a crumbling hospital; frequent profanity including a prominent \"f--k\"; and a comedic scene of young Barry left nude from the waist down after super-speed strips his clothes. Positive: team-building and working together for the greater good, and learning to accept what can't be changed rather than tampering with the past.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-flash","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":144,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q23562553","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":808,"t":"The Marvels","y":"2023","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Teamwork, action violence in fun, woman-centered MCU tale.\" Carol Danvers, Kamala Khan, and Monica Rambeau have their powers entangled and must team up against a Kree revolutionary, with laser-gun and spear battles and a few alarming scenes of planetary destruction; language is mild (\"s--t,\" \"damn,\" \"hell\"). Positive: the film celebrates the strength of female friendship and teamwork, with all three leads shown as brave, empathetic, and responsible, and a real emphasis on family acceptance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-marvels","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":105,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q89474225","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":809,"t":"Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths Part One","y":"2024","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"This first chapter of a trilogy adapting the classic DC crossover mostly follows the Flash as the Justice League faces the android Amazo and a coming multiversal threat. Common Sense Media notes cartoon blood and violence with weapons, guns, explosions, and stabbing, along with language like \"s--t,\" \"crap,\" and \"goddamn,\" plus a married couple kissing. Positive: Barry Allen models teamwork and self-sacrifice, and the film's tagline -- \"the future isn't written until we write it\" -- underscores hope and perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-crisis-on-infinite-earths-part-one","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":3,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":810,"t":"Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths Part Three","y":"2024","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Heroes unite for a universe-saving finale; intense action.\" This trilogy closer is heavier than typical Justice League fare: cartoon violence includes guns, explosions, and stabbings with visible blood, plus intense dinosaur-attack and bar-fight sequences, some profanity (\"s--t,\" \"hell\"), and characters drinking beer. Positive: Supergirl, Superman, and Wonder Woman risk everything for others, and the story leans hard on teamwork, sacrifice, and hope even as the universe collapses around them.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-crisis-on-infinite-earths-part-three","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":98,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths (film)","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":811,"t":"Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths Part Two","y":"2024","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Superheroes fight evil in dark, violent sequel,\" says Common Sense Media of this middle chapter, as the Monitor rallies heroes while the multiverse unravels. The review cites cartoon blood and violence with guns, explosions, and stabbing, including a mind-controlled teen stabbing another with a pitchfork, plus language such as \"damn\" and \"bastard.\" Positive: characters like the Monitor and Wonder Woman model leadership and sacrifice, and the film keeps its throughline of hope and not giving up.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/justice-league-crisis-on-infinite-earths-part-two","genre":["Animation","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Warner Bros. Animation","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":95,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Justice League: Crisis on Infinite Earths","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":812,"t":"Madame Web","y":"2024","la":"12+","ca":"11+","full":"Common Sense Media's tagline is \"action violence in a female-centered Spidey superhero tale,\" recommending age 11+. Characters are shot, stabbed, strangled, and poisoned (with some blood but nothing graphic), and one scene has two characters waking up together in their underwear that turns threatening rather than romantic. Positive: paramedic Cassie's arc centers on protecting vulnerable teens, and CSM highlights the \"power of your mind has infinite potential\" message along with real teamwork among the female leads.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/madame-web","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":116,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q111677117","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":813,"t":"Venom: The Last Dance","y":"2024","la":"14+","ca":"14+","full":"Common Sense Media's tagline calls it \"exposition, explosions in uninspired superhero threequel,\" with an age recommendation of 14+. Alien-monster attacks bring decapitations and blood, strong language includes \"motherf----r\" and repeated \"s--t,\" and Eddie gets visibly drunk in a bar scene. Positive: the film keeps circling back to Eddie and Venom's \"symbiotic\" partnership, framing their bond - however messy - as their real strength.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/venom-the-last-dance","genre":["Live-Action","Action","Superhero"],"studio":"Sony Pictures","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":4,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":109,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Venom: The Last Dance","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":814,"t":"Captain America: Brave New World","y":"2025","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Action violence, swearing in solid, earnest MCU adventure.\" Sam Wilson steps fully into the Captain America role amid an international standoff and a rampaging Red Hulk, with hand-to-hand fights, assassination attempts, and explosions, plus regular profanity including \"s--t\" and \"son of a bitch.\" Positive: the film argues that courage and integrity, not superpowers, define a hero, and that people deserve second chances, with Sam modeling loyalty and doing what's right even under pressure.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/captain-america-brave-new-world","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q112322116","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":815,"t":"Superman","y":"2025","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"CSM's tagline: \"Reboot mixes action violence, charming comic book energy.\" Concerns: large-scale destruction with implied civilian casualties and a shocking scene of a villain shooting an unarmed victim at close range in a game of Russian roulette; moderate profanity (\"s--t,\" \"bitch,\" \"goddamn\"); several passionate kisses between Clark and Lois, plus references to harems and implied sex workers; and Perry White frequently seen with a cigar. Positive: Superman models truth, justice, and using power responsibly, while Lois Lane brings intelligence, bravery, and loyalty to the story.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/superman","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Warner Bros.","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":3,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":129,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q116547790","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":816,"t":"The Fantastic Four: First Steps","y":"2025","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Marvel's First Family gets a retro, action-packed reboot.\" Set in a retro-futuristic alternate Earth, Reed, Sue, Johnny, and Ben face a planet-devouring cosmic villain, with super-powered battles, spacecraft crashes, one character's death (and a later revival), and mild language like \"bulls--t\" and \"hell.\" Positive: the film emphasizes teamwork, sacrifice, and using one's abilities to help others, with Sue Storm shown as intelligent, levelheaded, and fiercely protective as a new mother.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-fantastic-four-first-steps","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Sci-Fi"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":114,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q105105219","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":817,"t":"Thunderbolts*","y":"2025","la":"13+","ca":"13+","full":"\"Trauma, violence in heartfelt MCU antihero adventure.\" A team of antiheroes and former villains, including Yelena Belova and the Winter Soldier, battle a shadowy government threat with intense combat (impalement, shooting), strong language, and frank references to depression, addiction, and past meth use. Positive: the film centers empathy and real connection as ways to cope with trauma and mental illness, with the team learning to support each other rather than fight alone.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/thunderbolts","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":1,"drinking":4},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-12","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q112322474","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":818,"t":"Avengers: Doomsday","y":"2026","la":"12+","ca":"Not on CSM; substitute source used","full":"This crossover hasn't released yet (theaters December 2026), so no Common Sense Media review exists; per Wikipedia and early marketing, the Avengers, Wakandans, Fantastic Four, and X-Men band together against Doctor Doom (Robert Downey Jr.) as the multiverse collapses. Expect large-scale, PG-13-style superhero combat and peril consistent with prior Avengers films, with directors describing a more \"serious and somber\" tone than recent MCU entries. Positive: early descriptions point to themes of teamwork and unity across generations of heroes, though specific content details will need confirming once reviews are published.","srcUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avengers:_Doomsday","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","runtimeMinutes":165,"runtimeSourceId":"wikipedia:Avengers: Doomsday","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":819,"t":"Spider-Man: Brand New Day","y":"2026","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Fourth MCU Spidey movie spins tale of action and emotion.\" Four years after the world forgot Peter Parker, he fights crime alone, facing frequent comic-book fighting and peril with bloody, oozing wounds, plus language like \"s--t\" and \"goddamn\" and a hot-tub scene with suggestive dialogue. Positive: the film's core message is that everyone deserves people to lean on, and Peter learns that isolating himself isn't healthy, with MJ's kindness and Ned's steady loyalty modeling real friendship.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/spider-man-brand-new-day","genre":["Live-Action","Superhero","Action"],"studio":"Marvel Studios","source":"MCUDC","flags":{"violence":4,"language":3,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":145,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q113244935","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
const MOVIES_GHIBLI = [{"num":820,"t":"Castle in the Sky","y":"1986","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Exciting anime fantasy has some violence, peril,\" per Common Sense Media. Expect near-constant peril -- gunfire aimed at the young heroes, cannons, heat rays, and a devastating nuclear-style blast that levels a fortress, plus falls and off-screen deaths -- though nothing graphic or bloody. Positive: Sheeta and Pazu model courage, perceptiveness, and teamwork, and the pirate captain Dola shows that toughness and leadership aren't limited by age or gender.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/castle-in-the-sky","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q498577","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":821,"t":"Grave of the Fireflies","y":"1988","la":"15+","ca":"15+","full":"\"Tragic WWII anime has devastating teen and toddler deaths,\" says Common Sense Media -- and this one earns every word of that warning. Siblings Seita and Setsuko slowly starve after their mother dies of burns from an air raid (her injuries and later her decomposing body are shown), the toddler is seen eating dirt out of hunger, and firebombed streets are littered with corpses; both children die by the end. Positive: it's an unflinching, deeply moving portrait of how war devastates civilians, especially children, built around Seita's fierce, ultimately futile devotion to protecting his little sister.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/grave-of-the-fireflies","genre":["Animation","Drama","War"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":4,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":93,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q274520","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":822,"t":"Only Yesterday","y":"1991","la":"10+","ca":"11+","full":"\"Classic Studio Ghibli drama focuses on Japanese girlhood,\" per Common Sense Media. As adult Taeko reflects on her fifth-grade year, boys tease her about menstruation and try to look up girls' skirts, her father slaps her hard across the face in anger, adults smoke, and there's mild schoolyard romance. Positive: it's a thoughtful, honest coming-of-age story that affirms a woman's independence, with Taeko's curiosity, kindness, and perseverance paying off without needing marriage to feel complete.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/only-yesterday","genre":["Animation","Drama","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1045889","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":823,"t":"Porco Rosso","y":"1992","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Lesser-known Miyazaki has heavy themes, cartoon violence,\" notes Common Sense Media. Expect WWI-style dogfights, machine-gun fire, and grenades (all cartoonish, not gory), plus bar scenes with wine, cigars, mild profanity like \"hell\" and \"damn,\" and some womanizing references. Positive: the film quietly explores how war scars the people who fight it, valuing integrity and humility over glory, and its young mechanic Fio proves her skill despite others doubting her because of her age and gender.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/porco-rosso","genre":["Animation","Adventure","War"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":92,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q498375","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":824,"t":"Pom Poko","y":"1994","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Animated tale has environmental message; peril, sadness,\" per Common Sense Media. Shape-shifting tanuki battle bulldozing developers and each other with cartoon violence, several tanuki are shown as roadkill or starved, three human construction workers die, and the tanuki's frightening monster transformations and drinking scenes may unsettle younger kids (traditional depictions also leave the tanuki's testicles visible, per Japanese folklore). Positive: the film champions empathy for wildlife and the environment, and its tanuki leaders -- several of them female -- show courage, resourcefulness, and self-sacrifice in a story about collective rather than individual heroism.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/pom-poko","genre":["Animation","Comedy","Fantasy"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":118,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q167206","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":825,"t":"Whisper of the Heart","y":"1995","la":"9+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Sweet, romantic coming-of-age anime with strong role models,\" says Common Sense Media. Content is mild: a brief scene of adult smoking, some name-calling like \"stupid\" and \"jerks,\" and an innocent tween romance at the story's center. Positive: Shizuku and Seiji both chase real passions -- writing and violin-making -- and the film models how hard work and determination turn ambitions into achievements.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/whisper-of-the-heart","genre":["Animation","Romance","Coming-of-Age"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":1,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":111,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q842292","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":826,"t":"Princess Mononoke","y":"1997","la":"12+","ca":"12+","full":"\"Epic, compelling, and violent anime classic,\" per Common Sense Media. This is Miyazaki's darkest, most adult film: battle scenes include dismemberment and decapitation, swords, guns, and arrows draw visible blood, a dying boar god decomposes to a skeleton in seconds, and there's mild profanity plus references to former sex workers. Positive: Ashitaka and San both show real courage and conviction, and the film's central debate -- protecting nature versus exploiting it for progress -- is handled with unusual moral complexity, including a villain, Lady Eboshi, who is also shown as compassionate toward society's outcasts.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/princess-mononoke","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Action"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":128,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q186572","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":827,"t":"My Neighbors the Yamadas","y":"1999","la":"7+","ca":"7+","full":"\"Quirky animated comedy follows a family's ups and downs,\" per Common Sense Media. Told in loose comic-strip-style vignettes, it includes a scary moment where a young girl is briefly left behind at a mall, a motorcycle chase with menacing bikers, a father who smokes, mild insults like \"stupid\" and \"shut up,\" and a boy's first-crush storyline that draws teasing. Positive: despite the daily chaos, the film celebrates family resilience, with a witty grandmother, a protective mother, and a caring father showing that imperfect families can still be loving ones.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/my-neighbors-the-yamadas","genre":["Animation","Comedy"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":104,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q1418326","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":828,"t":"The Cat Returns","y":"2002","la":"8+","ca":"10+","full":"\"Imaginative adventure anime has some fantasy violence,\" says Common Sense Media. Haru is nearly hit by a truck early on, and once she's swept into the Cat Kingdom there's cartoonish sword-, spear-, and chain-fighting along with a fall from a collapsing tower. Positive: Haru grows more assertive and self-possessed over the course of the story, declaring that \"nobody decides who I am but me,\" modeling healthy boundary-setting and standing up for yourself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-cat-returns","genre":["Animation","Adventure","Fantasy"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":75,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q51543","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":829,"t":"Howl's Moving Castle","y":"2004","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"\"Charming Miyazaki fairy tale with surreal villains,\" per Common Sense Media. Sophie is cursed into an old woman's body and moves in with the wizard Howl, whose castle is stalked by war planes and unsettling blob-like soldiers; expect a few tense chase and explosion scenes (no blood shown) plus a steady anti-war current about a pointless conflict. There's mild romantic tension and one adult who smokes a cigar, but nothing graphic. Positive: the film rewards compassion over cruelty, treats aging with warmth rather than fear, and follows Sophie's growth from timid to self-assured as Howl learns to put others first.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/howls-moving-castle","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":119,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q29011","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":830,"t":"Tales from Earthsea","y":"2006","la":"11+","ca":"11+","full":"Common Sense Media's tagline is blunt: \"stylish animation isn't enough to save violent adaptation.\" It's the darkest, most violent entry in the Ghibli catalog -- an early scene has a son stab his own father, there's a bloody dragon-on-dragon battle, sword fights that draw blood, and a sorcerer who morphs into monstrous forms. Enslaved young people are shown zonked out on an addictive drug, and drunken palace guards appear elsewhere. Positive: for older kids who can handle it, the story argues that life must stay in balance with nature and that facing death honestly beats fleeing from it, with the heroic wizard modeling loyalty and bravery.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/tales-from-earthsea","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":4,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":115,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q721737","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":831,"t":"Arrietty","y":"2010","la":"5+","ca":"5+","full":"Common Sense Media praises this (released in the US as The Secret World of Arrietty) as a \"deeply felt anime about loneliness and friendship.\" Tiny Arrietty and her Borrower family live hidden in the walls of a house, and the tension comes from close calls with a curious cat and a well-meaning but sickly human boy, including one frightening scene where a Borrower is trapped screaming in a jar. It's gentle overall, with no language or romance and only a passing mention of wine. Positive: the film celebrates the bravery of reaching out for help and shows that friendship can cross even the biggest differences in size and background.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-secret-world-of-arrietty","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Adventure"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":94,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q699835","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":832,"t":"From Up on Poppy Hill","y":"2011","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Billed by Common Sense Media as an \"inspiring, romantic coming-of-age tale about '60s teens,\" this one centers on a Yokohama high schooler running her family's boarding house while her mother is away, and the sweet, awkward romance that develops with a classmate -- complicated by a scare that they might secretly be related. Both teens lost fathers, one in the Korean War, and there's a beer shared at a gathering along with some mild insults. Positive: it champions loyalty and standing up for what you believe, as the students band together to save their clubhouse, and treats young love as sincere rather than trivial.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/from-up-on-poppy-hill","genre":["Animation","Drama","Romance"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":91,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q194726","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":833,"t":"The Tale of the Princess Kaguya","y":"2013","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Common Sense Media calls this a \"beautifully animated Japanese folktale for older kids,\" adapting the classic bamboo-princess legend. A suitor falls fatally while chasing an impossible treasure, a mother is shown breastfeeding (brief, nonsexual nudity), and the back half turns melancholy as Kaguya is pressured into a loveless, status-obsessed life she never wanted -- themes of grief and constrained freedom that can hit hard. Positive: the story insists that children thrive on love and the freedom to be themselves rather than money or rank, with Kaguya's parents and her childhood friend Sutemaru modeling devotion and treating her as an equal.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-tale-of-the-princess-kaguya","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":137,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q888136","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":834,"t":"The Wind Rises","y":"2013","la":"10+","ca":"10+","full":"Common Sense Media describes this fictionalized biography of aeronautical engineer Jiro Horikoshi as \"lovely\" and \"contemplative,\" but aimed at older kids and adults. It includes a terrifying earthquake-and-fire sequence, plane crashes, near-constant cigarette smoking (even beside a dying woman), and a tender adult marriage with implied intimacy; Jiro's wife eventually succumbs to tuberculosis. The film also sits uneasily with the fact that Jiro's elegant planes were built for Japan's WWII war effort. Positive: it's a genuine meditation on chasing a dream with integrity, on partnership and loss, and on engineers turning dreams into reality -- even when the real-world use of that dream is morally complicated.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-wind-rises","genre":["Animation","Drama","Biography"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":2,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":126,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q888131","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":835,"t":"When Marnie Was There","y":"2014","la":"9+","ca":"9+","full":"Described by Common Sense Media as a \"beautifully animated but slow tale about unique friendship,\" this quiet mystery follows lonely, asthmatic Anna as she befriends a mysterious girl named Marnie at a crumbling seaside mansion. There's a scary storm sequence in a decaying silo, an alleged (unconfirmed) knife threat between two girls, some self-directed insults like \"fat pig\" and \"pathetic,\" and adults drinking wine and smoking at a gathering. Positive: at its core the film is about a girl learning she's genuinely loved by the family around her, even without a blood tie, and coming to accept herself.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/when-marnie-was-there","genre":["Animation","Drama","Mystery"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":2},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":103,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q15303700","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":836,"t":"The Red Turtle","y":"2016","la":"8+","ca":"8+","full":"Common Sense Media's \"beautiful word-free drama about a castaway who finds love\" has no dialogue at all. A shipwrecked man's escape rafts are repeatedly destroyed by an unseen force, he lashes out and strikes a giant turtle in anger, and a storm later threatens his family; the turtle-woman he falls for emerges from her shell nude (her hair covers her), and their relationship is implied to turn intimate, evidenced later by their son. Positive: the film is ultimately a wordless ode to companionship, environmental respect, and attentive parenting, with the son growing into a curious, kind kid who cares for his parents in turn.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-red-turtle","genre":["Animation","Drama","Romance"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":2,"language":1,"romance":2,"drinking":1},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":80,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q19840623","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"num":837,"t":"The Boy and the Heron","y":"2023","la":"11+","ca":"10+","full":"Common Sense Media's own warning is right in the tagline: \"breathtaking personal story has self-harm, smoking.\" Grieving Mahito, whose mother died in a WWII hospital fire, deliberately wounds himself with a rock hard enough to draw visible blood, and the fantastical world he later enters is full of unsettling imagery -- carnivorous giant birds, a fish disemboweled on camera, frog-covered figures -- alongside adult smoking and mild profanity. Positive: for kids old enough for the intensity, it's a rich meditation on grief, resilience, and staying open to an uncertain future, with courageous, capable characters (especially its women) modeling perseverance.","srcUrl":"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/movie-reviews/the-boy-and-the-heron","genre":["Animation","Fantasy","Drama"],"studio":"Studio Ghibli","source":"GHIBLI","flags":{"violence":3,"language":2,"romance":1,"drinking":3},"csmRecheckedAt":"2026-09-07","csmRecheckVersion":2,"runtimeMinutes":124,"runtimeSourceId":"wikidata:Q47482560","runtimeVerifiedAt":"2026-09-26"}];
